ADB to Support Animal Production and Animal Health in Cambodia
Welcoming the Prime Minister, Mr. Veng Sakhon thanked the Asian Development Bank for its important role in providing technical assistance, technical training, training and resource development of the Ministry's professional staff and support infrastructure in the agricultural sector.
Minister Veng Sakhon hopes and believes that the ADB will continue to support, strengthen and expand cooperation with the Ministry to jointly develop sustainable agriculture in response to the context of Cambodia's economic growth and the Royal Government's long-term vision for the year. 2030 and 2050.
On this occasion, the Director General of the Asian Development Bank also thanked and highly appreciated the Minister and his colleagues who always provide excellent cooperation with the team of the Asian Development Bank together to implement programs and projects to achieve fruitful results. To farmers and the agricultural sector as a whole.
He added that, following the recommendations of the Minister at the previous meeting, the Asian Development Bank (ADB) has revised and prepared a strategic plan to support Cambodia in the agricultural sector 2021-2023, with the new strategic plan focusing on reform. Via:
* Agricultural modernization, agricultural modernization, agricultural diversification * Planning of zoning * Management and use of pesticides * Quality and safe processing and packaging and lending to communities and small and medium enterprises Complete agricultural production chains to increase value added to producers.
In the field of animal production and animal health, the Asian Development Bank will also support the new program, which is scheduled to be implemented in 2021 to control the movement of animals and human-to-animal and animal-to-human transmission. Domestic animal production.
He added that the ADB team has been actively working with the Fisheries Administration to implement programs to conserve and develop natural resources in the coastal and coastal areas. To achieve all these programs, we need the active and effective participation of the Ministry's professional officials, so we ask the Minister to provide support.
In response, Minister Veng Sakhon once again expressed his deep gratitude for the attention and especially support for the Ministry's reform policy to respond to the current context of economic growth and population. And the future.
