The lawyer for Leang Khun's statement came after a number of media outlets and social media outlets continued to share and accuse the tycoon of having an extramarital affair with Khun Srey Sros, who jumped to his death. Condo building.
The lawyer representing Duke Leang Khun issued a statement with the following content:
I, May Vannady, Member of the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia, ID 599, is a lawyer defending the rights and representing Mr. Oknha Leang Khun, I would like to make the following statement:
Due to some social media and media continued to share unsubstantiated information and propaganda that caused serious damage to the honor and dignity of the family and our company in connection with the suicide case of a woman named Khun Srey Sros (or Sri Nika Facebook Account) which happened on March 11, 2020, we would like to clarify the following content and basis:
1: The death of a woman named Khun Srey Sros, who made the accusation against Mr. Oknha Leang Khun, was confirmed by the competent authorities through an autopsy that she was a real suicide.
3: After dealing with a woman named Khun Srey Sros and finding out the truth, the police also prepared video clip evidence that the woman confessed her mistake and apologized in front of the police and to the tycoon. Compassionate and unwilling to have a long-term problem, the tycoon decided not to debate the matter further and thought that the issue had already been resolved.
4: Until March 11, 2020, after a woman named Khun Srey Sros posted a message and committed suicide, the accusation suddenly reappeared on social media and some media. Attached is a video clip of the woman and some pictures that are documents in the old case and was denied by Khun Srey Sros herself as a slander, threatening to demand money from the tycoon (video evidence to prove).
5: Through this clarification, along with the clear evidence that we presented, along with the confirmation of the competent authorities, we hope that the public will be aware of the facts that have arisen around this issue.
6: We respect the right to freedom of expression as well as the dissemination of information about this case in a professional and responsible manner, avoiding any further dissemination of information that has no clear basis and cause damage to honor and dignity. Of others, this is a criminal offense that can be punished by law.
7: Finally, we would like to express our condolences for this loss, as well as share the grief with the whole family of the corpse with the utmost regret. Minister of Health: Cambodian man infected with COVID-19 virus in Siem Reap is healthy and thanked for the attention of the Royal Government
