Cambodia recognizes more than 60,000 foreigners living legally as immigrants
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Interior has issued a proclamation recognizing 60,279 foreigners, equal to 20,228 families as immigrants who came to live in Cambodia legally, out of 103,738 immigrants, equal to 32 637 families who have applied for recognition in the past.
This was stated by General Dr. Khieu Sopheak, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Interior, at a press conference on the morning of March 12, 2020 on the progress and further direction of the Ministry of Interior organized by the Leadership Unit. The word Royal Government.
Article 10 of the Immigration Law defines a foreigner who is considered an immigrant as someone who has arrived in Cambodia legally to stay for a long period of time or to engage in a profession or other activity related to industry, trade, services or Agriculture.
General Khieu Sopheak also said that the Ministry of Interior had previously confiscated 37,436 illegal administrative documents held by foreigners, equivalent to 20,107 families of 69,957 people.
According to General Khieu Sopheak, there are currently 64 refugees of 8 nationalities, 21 asylum seekers of 6 nationalities and 27 Vietnamese Montagnards.
