Hundreds of thousands of dollars worth of mobile phones were stolen from almost 25 capitals and provinces using scissors to cut zinc and cotton hammocks, including the victims of the theft were cracked down by the Kandal Provincial Armed Forces.
In fact, at the end of 2019 and the beginning of 2020, the crime of breaking the door, piercing the roof of the house, stealing the mobile phone of the trader always occurs in a series in the territory of Kandal province, as well as in some provincial capitals. In particular, this case occurred in Takhmao City, Kandal Province twice:
* Takhmao City:
In all of the above cases, after the incident, General Sam Tola, Commander of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, led the relevant provincial and municipal experts to the scene immediately to intervene, search and arrest. The perpetrators follow legal procedures.
Through careful research day and night, fearless, experienced, willing under the direct supervision of Colonel Touch Inan and the attention of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, the suspects were identified. Name: Tot Tha, Male, 39 years old, Ethnic Khmer, Living in Chong Koh Village, Koh Chen Commune, Ponhea Leu District, Kandal Province.
On March 10, 2020, under the direct coordination of the Kandal Provincial Prosecutor's Office, the specialized forces of the Royal Cambodian Gendarmerie and local authorities confiscated the stolen phone, named Heng Heng 1 (unidentified owner). At Samhan Market in Group 5, Street 907, Bak Touk Village, Sangkat Toul Sangke, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, 69 mobile phones were confiscated. A total of 145 mobile phones were confiscated from the suspects.
In front of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, the suspect, Tot Tha, confessed that he used to use scissors to cut the roof of the house, use a hammock, and go up and down several times to steal mobile phones in Kandal, Phnom Penh and other provinces. More. Separately, the suspect, Sam Oun, confessed that he had actually bought a cell phone from a brand that many times had resold it.
At present, the two suspects and the exhibits of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie have been sent to the Kandal Provincial Court for legal action. He added that the suspect, named Tot, had been imprisoned for stealing property and stealing for many years. Phnom Penh, etc.
Please be reminded that the Military Police of Kandal Province also cracked down on the active activities of looting mobile phones in 2018 in one case, arresting 2 suspects and confiscating more than 44 mobile phones out of nearly 200 lost. .
On behalf of the competent authorities, we request the traders (selling and buying mobile phones) to be very careful in taking care of their property, to have a security camera, to make the sales place strong and to rest near their property, especially in case of theft, to keep Evidence well and complain to the authorities in time to intervene.
