Dr. Kun Nhim confirmed that seven container ships were continuing to enter Cambodia, five to Sihanoukville and two to Ho Chi Minh Port, Vietnam, which will be transported by land to the region. Bavet Special Economic Zone, in which 4 ships have already arrived at the port and sent to the factory.
Speaking to reporters, Dr. Kun Nhim confirmed that "I would like to inform the situation of the restoration of the supply of raw materials for the garment sector ... At the request of the Royal Government, there are seven container ships, "Five to Sihanoukville Port and two to Ho Chi Minh Port, which will be transported by land to supply the Bavet Special Economic Zone."
In addition, Dr. Kun Nhem believes that there will be more ships to come to Cambodia according to the improved situation of China, while China is a country that produces raw materials for Cambodia.
