Cluster munitions clearance project after US $ 2 million grant launched
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Heng Ratana, General Director of CMAC, met with staff and staff on March 12, 2020 and announced the launch of the Operation Information Research and Disposal Clearance Operation Project. Kampong Chhnang Mine Action Technical Institute.
The launch comes after CMAC signed an agreement with the NPA on a cluster munitions research and clearance project, which runs for 12 months (March 1, 2020 to February 28, 2021) with government funding. The United States will support the project with $ 1,600,000.
Mr. Heng Ratana stated that this project will be implemented in some provinces such as Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum, Svay Rieng, Kratie, Stung Treng, Takeo and Prey Veng, with a plan to liberate an area of 19,016,932 square meters, researching an area of about 30 kg. Square meters will use about 230 people.
"Today, the operational force of this project will start its operation from now on," he said. "Thank you to the NPA and the United States Government for providing assistance in clearing explosive remnants of war for the safety of the Cambodian people under the umbrella of peace in the Kingdom."
Taking this opportunity, he also reminded about the fight against Kovid-19, which all officials must overcome the disease of fear, lack of knowledge and deception of the scare group, the use of "Khmer Krama Health Care" must be firm in case If there is a suspicion of a disease, it must be examined and examined at a hospital to find the virus. In the meantime, strict measures must be taken in accordance with the instructions of the Ministry of Health.
