Speaking on the program "Provision of services and updates of various events of the General Department of Taxation" on March 12, 2020 via Live on Tax Facebook, Mr. Kong Vibol said that in the online era is a complex problem of Fiscal administration, both Cambodian and international. Online sellers in Cambodia under tax law are obliged to register taxes.
He continued, "Every economic activity that occurs for 15 days must be registered in accordance with Article 101 of the tax law, and if that income is exempted below 250 million riels, it is not taxable, if 250 to 700 million riels is taxable, but As a small taxpayer, between 700 million riel and 4 billion riel is taxed on average, and from 4 billion riel up is a large taxpayer according to the tax law is taxed and has to declare taxes.
Mr. Kong Vibol added, "I observe that some online sellers, especially lotion sellers, may not be fulfilling their duties and they are doing business with income but not registered to pay taxes." "Therefore, I strongly urge that all sales must comply with tax laws, all economic businesses within 15 days must come to register."
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng urges to increase the efficiency of providing public services to the people
(Prey Veng): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, this morning, March 12, 2020, urged to mobilize to create effective public services, benefits from the development of protection. Equitable social sector for local people.
The remarks of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng were made during the closing ceremony of the meeting to summarize the work results for 2019 and the work direction for 2020 of Prey Veng Provincial Administration and the Royal Government Working Group.
On that occasion, Mr. Chea Somethy, Governor of Prey Veng Province, also reported on the activities of the sub-national working group implemented in 2019, which organized 423 public forums and meetings with a total of 49,042 participants. Of which, received the requests of the people, a total of 559 cases have been resolved, 190 cases have been resolved, 163 cases are being resolved and 206 cases have been sent to the national level.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the hard work of the 13 sub-national working groups of the municipal and district administrations who have worked hard to implement the action plan well, which ensures The needs and requests of the people have improved significantly.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng continued that 2020 is the second year of the implementation of the political program and strategy of the fourth phase of the Royal Government of Cambodia to promote the development of the country to be more developed in all areas. In 2020, we must work together to strengthen our commitment to achieve four key strategic goals:
* First, to continue to resolutely defend the independence, sovereignty and territorial integrity of the Kingdom of Cambodia, as well as to maintain peace, political stability, security, social order and macroeconomic stability, and to promote all rights and freedoms of the people in accordance with the Constitution and the law. In force in Cambodia.
* Second, continue to promote the process of multi-party liberal democracy on the basis of ensuring peace and sustainable development of the nation by linking the democratic process with the rule of law and the preservation of identity. Nation, dignity, traditions, good traditions of the nation and building harmony in society.
* Third: Continue to promote the implementation of the reform programs set out in the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategic Political Program, including decentralization and deconcentration reforms, to create more new opportunities for further economic growth and reduction. Poor, equitable and sustainable.
* Fourth: Efforts to mobilize the efficiency of the provision of public services, the benefits of development, the provision of equitable social protection and the efforts to address the challenges and requests of the people to ensure the participation and People's ownership of all sectors of society. Officials from CamControl, Dry Port and 8 CamControl branches in Phnom Penh confiscated more than 3 kilos of pig's blood and rice and destroyed it after finding borax
(Phnom Penh): Under the guidance of the Director General of CamControl and Chief of Phnom Penh Dry Port Branch, on March 12, 2020, the officers of CamControl Phnom Penh Dry Port and all 8 CamControl branches in Phnom Penh cooperated with the Experimental Officer and The Olympic Market Commission and Chbar Ampov Market Commission have inspected and researched to prevent defective goods that can harm the health of consumers.
