Cambodia-Australia continue to strengthen employment and vocational training
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia-Australia is committed to further enhancing cooperation in the field of employment and vocational training, which was mentioned in a working meeting with Mr. Pablo Chiho Kang, the new Ambassador of Australia to Cambodia. And Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, on the morning of March 12, 2020 at the Ministry of Labor.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng stated that the Cambodian leadership and the Ministry of Labor will be ready to cooperate with the Ambassador to facilitate his diplomatic mission successfully in order to deepen and improve the relationship between Cambodia and Australia.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng also mentioned some of the progress and achievements that the Ministry has worked closely with relevant partners to actively contribute to the development of employment and vocational training in the past, successfully achieving job opportunities and Ensure harmonization between workers and employers.
At the same time, the two sides also discussed cooperation to deepen and further develop the two countries, especially in the field of employment and vocational training.
The Minister also asked the Ambassador to assist in training human resources for more Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training officials.
After the meeting, Mr. Ngoy Rith, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Labor, said that both sides recalled the good relations and memories between Cambodia and Australia, what Australia has helped develop Cambodia's economy in the past.
In relation to the field of employment and vocational training, the Australian side wants to learn more about the field of vocational training, how to make parents and young people more aware to turn to vocational training in Cambodia to respond to The growing market demand of the Cambodian economy today.
He said that Australia has promised to provide scholarships to students and civil servants to continue their studies in Australia. At the same time, Cambodia-Australia will increase cooperation in the exchange of students, professors in the field of vocational training to study, understand and help each other.
At the same time, Australia is a country that helps Cambodia from the effects of asbestos, which Australia is a leader in eliminating this substance, it has a serious impact on our workers when we do not prevent. Cambodia has partnered with Australia to provide technical funding in a partnership to enhance the asbestos awareness capacity for the prevention of adverse health effects aimed at reducing asbestos exposure.
He added that for other issues, Australia will continue to support and cooperate with Cambodia in case Cambodia needs Australia to help.
