In this regard, the development of tourism, especially river tourism, requires the development of clean cities, green cities and clean and green tourism destinations, which are development models that take into account the conservation and preservation of cultural resources, natural resources and the environment in a sustainable manner, that is, development for Preserve, preserve for development by ensuring economic, social and environmental sustainability and balance.
Mr. Top Sopheak urged all tourism businesses in Battambang province to strive to strengthen the quality of its tourism service industry, strengthen the attractiveness, friendly hospitality at the reception and be affordable to be ready to receive tourists. On the occasion of the 6th River Festival.
The Undersecretary of State added that in relation to the concept of green and clean, the Royal Government has launched the "Clean City, Clean Resort, Good Service and Good Hospitality" competition to make Cambodia a beautiful, green and clean tourist destination. Therefore, tourism businesses must also participate in this movement.
