Husband announces search for wife after missing factory in Bavet
(Svay Rieng): A hairdresser living in Po village, Mes Thnak commune, Chantrea district, Svay Rieng province, announced that he was looking for his beloved wife, who went missing after working in a factory in Bavet City and could not return home.
Husband Wang, who works as a barber, described this morning as his wife, Chheng Saray, 40, who works in a factory in Bavet's Mehathen Special Economic Zone.
Before disappearing, the wife went to work as usual and was told that a woman named Sam had borrowed her clothes while packing her clothes for the woman in front of the factory in the morning and then disappeared. After returning to work in the factory, he did not return home in the evening, so he announced his search for his wife on Facebook and asked the media to help spread the word, and he also went to complain to the authorities.
