Water Supply Authority calls on people to use water sparingly to share with suburbs, using 700,000 cubic meters of water per day, but producing only 600,000 cubic meters
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority (PPWSA) issued a new announcement on March 12, 2020, calling on people to use water sparingly to share with other people, especially in areas such as The city has the capacity to produce 600,000 cubic meters of clean water per day, but the demand is up to 700,000 cubic meters per day.
According to the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, currently, the Water Supply Authority has a total of four water treatment plants producing an average of 600,000 cubic meters of clean water per day, but obviously with the growth of Phnom Penh and population growth. The demand for clean water has risen to 700,000 cubic meters per day, leading to a shortage of clean water for distribution, especially in the suburbs during high water demand.
In response to the growing demand for clean water, the company is continuing to build a new water treatment plant in Bak Kheng, which will be able to produce 390,000 cubic meters of clean water per day by 2023.
Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority added, "Considering that the dry season demand will increase, PPWSA would like to appeal to all customers in both Phnom Penh and Takhmao to save water to share. To other customers, especially in the suburbs, please do not use clean water for spraying, cleaning the house, please reduce watering the garden and wash the car.
