Kampong Cham Provincial Governor: A British woman infected with Covid-19 in Kampong Cham has been transferred to a hospital in Phnom Penh.
It should be noted that the Minister of Health, Professor Mam Bun Heng, this morning, March 11, 2020, visited the health of a 65-year-old British woman who was found to be infected with the Covid- virus. 19 Yesterday evening and was hospitalized in Kampong Cham.
Please be informed that at 16:30 on March 10, 2020, the results from the Institut Pasteur du Cambodge confirmed that a 65-year-old British woman was positive for Kovid 19 virus.
The woman with the Covid-19 virus flew from London, England to Hanoi, Vietnam on March 2, 2020 with five people (four British people tested negative). ). They then proceeded from Ho Chi Minh City by ferry to Phnom Penh on March 5, 2020 and arrived in Phnom Penh on March 7, 2020.
The same day before arriving in Phnom Penh, the ship's tour operator was informed that the plane that the British woman was flying on March 2, 2020, had a Vietnamese man sitting next to the British woman. The 65-year-old was diagnosed with the Covid-19 virus in Hanoi, Vietnam.
Arriving in Phnom Penh on March 7, 2020, the five British nationals were sent for medical examination at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital and three samples were taken (with two refusing to take them). Absolutely, he claimed there were no health problems or symptoms. ”As a result, all three were negatively infected with the Covid-19 virus.
The Ministry of Health and the Kampong Cham Provincial Health Department, in cooperation with the provincial authorities, are taking care to examine and take samples from those directly or indirectly affected on all ships for analysis at the laboratory of the Institut Pasteur du Cambodge.
