Ten large companies in collaboration with the National Employment Agency of Sihanoukville will provide nearly 4,000 job opportunities on March 14
(Preah Sihanouk): On March 14, 2020, the National Employment Agency of Preah Sihanouk Province will cooperate with 10 big companies to organize 3 job search forums in Prey Nup District, Preah Sihanouk Province. 799 places. The forum will be held at Prey Nup District Hall from 8 am to 12:00 noon, located in Veal Meas Village, Veal Renh Commune, Prey Nup District, Sihanoukville Province.
According to the announcement of the National Training Committee of the National Employment Agency, obtained by Fresh News on the afternoon of March 11, 2020, this job forum is organized in close cooperation with the Department of Labor and Labor. Preah Sihanouk Provincial Vocational Training Prey Nup District Hall and Preah Sihanouk Provincial Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia (UYFC) in order to:
* First: Create a meeting place that is easy to recruit and apply for all types of jobs.
* Second: 10 large companies, including 3,799 job opportunities and recruitment needs of all types of labor.
* Third: Job seekers in the surrounding areas and provinces can apply and get a wide and easy job.
The following is the announcement of the National Training Committee of the National Employment Agency: In the first two months of this year, Cambodia exported more than 40,000 tons of rice and more than 34 tons of vegetables to Europe.
This was revealed during a working meeting between Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Ms. Carmen Moreno, the new EU Ambassador to Cambodia, to strengthen and expand cooperation between the EU and the Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry; Agricultural fishing on the afternoon of March 11, 2020.
"Remarkably, Cambodia's rice exports to the EU continue to grow proudly in the first two months of the year compared to last year," Veng Sakhon told the EU ambassador. 2019 is an increase of more than 12.8%. "The total output for the first two months of this year was to export more than 41.3 thousand tons of Cambodian rice to the European Union and about 34.5 tons of vegetables."
Minister Veng Sakhon also congratulated her on her support and the appointment of a new EU Ambassador to Cambodia. Some through the Ambassador on behalf of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
He added that in the context of current economic and population growth, and especially in the future, the Royal Government's long-term vision is to transform Cambodia into a high-middle-income country by 2030. The Ministry will reform its policy and shift its focus from agricultural production to food security to production for both domestic and foreign trade.
The Minister hopes and believes that the Ambassador will work to further strengthen and expand cooperation between Cambodia and the European Union and continue to provide support to the Ministry for the benefit of the Cambodian people and farmers.
On that occasion, the Ambassador also expressed her appreciation and appreciation for the progress in all areas that Cambodia has achieved now and in the past.
She also thanked the Minister and the professional staff of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries for their excellent cooperation to the EU working group to achieve many achievements, all of which have been and are helping. For the agricultural sector to grow continuously and considered as an important sector to support Cambodia's economic growth.
