(Kampong Speu): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, chaired a meeting this morning to review the work of the Veterans Association. Disaster of Kampong Speu Province.
The ceremony was also attended by a delegation from the Ministry of Water Resources, Ministry of Agriculture, provincial governors, provincial councilors, commanders of the armed forces, members of the sub-national and local disaster management committees.
According to the report of the Provincial Disaster Management Committee, Kampong Speu province was affected by the drought in 5 cities / districts, damaging 3,167 hectares of rice fields, 34 strong winds, 300 houses and 31 fires. Damaged 27 houses.
In addition, the province also planned to cultivate 113,600 hectares of rain-fed rice, implementing 114,996 hectares, equivalent to 101.23 percent.
On behalf of Samdech Techo, Senior Minister Kun Kim conveyed greetings from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to government officials, the Armed Forces and the people of the whole province.
The senior minister also praised the efforts of the Provincial Disaster Management Committee and the Provincial Veterans Association, which performed their duties well in the event of an incident.
To the Provincial Veterans Association, Senior Minister Kun Kim instructed to maintain good hygiene everywhere and at all times, to eat properly cooked food, not to be overly shocked and to participate in preventing pneumonia caused by Covid- 19 All together.
At the same time, both the Commune / Sangkat Chief as the Honorary Chief and the Chief of the Administration Post as the Commune / Sangkat Branch Chief must continue to do good deeds and strive to cooperate and create all possible opportunities for our veterans to receive various public services.
He added that in the future, it is necessary to inspect and evaluate veterans and their families who are really poor and difficult, and prepare a correct list and send it to the General Secretariat to request the President to provide housing or social land concessions to you.
Ministry of Economy holds meeting with stakeholders on COVID-19
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance on March 11, 2020, organized a meeting with stakeholders on the Master Plan for Combating Respiratory Syndrome (COVID-19) organized by the Ministry of Health in collaboration with World Health Organization (WHO) and to assess the comprehensiveness and financing needs of this plan.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth requested all partners to consider the possibility of providing financial support for the implementation of this master plan according to the priorities and capabilities of their respective institutions, and the rest will be supplemented by sources from the Royal Government's own budget, especially for support. To implement immediate response measures in the first scenario.
Finally, the Permanent Secretary of State expressed his deep gratitude for the spirit of cooperation and participation of all stakeholders and development partners in responding to and preventing the spread of this disease in Cambodia.
Oddar Meanchey Provincial Governor Calls on Citizens to Be Extremely Cautious of Fire Causes
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, called on people throughout the province to be very careful at all times for the causes that can cause fires, such as: stoves, candles, lamps, incense burners, forest fires. Cigarettes, ammunition, fireworks, fuel, electricity, flammable gases and all kinds of flammable materials.
The appeal of the Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province was made on the occasion of his participation in the 5th National Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Day on March 11, 2020, with the participation of Mr. Siprasit, Chairman of the Provincial Council. Deputy Governors, Ladies and Gentlemen, Civil Servants, Armed Forces, Students, Youth Scouts, Red Cross Youth, Youth of the CPPCC and a total of 1,119 people.
According to the report of the Deputy Provincial Police Commissioner, in 2019, there were 3 disasters caused by fire, and in the beginning of 2020, there were 2 disasters, causing some property damage, but the force Authorities intervened in a timely manner.
Mr. Pen Kosal expressed his appreciation and appreciation to the fire brigade of the Provincial Police Commission, the Royal Gendarmerie, as well as the relevant authorities for their good cooperation in caring for the people affected by the fire. Timely and encourage all competent forces to continue to strive to perform their duties better in the cause of our nation and our people.
At the same time, the provincial governor instructed local authorities at all levels to increase educational measures to guide people in their jurisdiction to raise awareness and participate more actively in the fire prevention and fighting movement in their local area, including:
People should be very careful at all times for sources that can cause fires, such as stoves, candles, lamps, incense burners, garbage fires, wildfires, cigarettes, fireworks, electricity, gases, chemicals and flammable substances. Flammable in all kinds.
* The construction of gas and gas stations must comply with technical standards, which must be checked by all relevant skills in accordance with technical standards to prevent risks.
* Must make public the permanent telephone number so that people know and contact when a fire accident occurs.
* The Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Police Unit at the provincial and district police stations must be on duty 24 hours a day and must have vehicles and equipment ready for firefighting intervention in a timely manner.
Senior Minister Meas Sophea calls on men and women to work together for peace and to oppose those who seek to destroy peace
(Preah Vihear): Senior Minister Meas Sophea, Chairman of the Royal Government Assistance Team in Preah Vihear Province, called on women and men to work together to maintain peace and to oppose those who seek to destroy peace.
