(Phnom Penh): The Australian Embassy in Cambodia has expressed its support for the work of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation in the past to raise awareness and provide benefits for people with disabilities.
This support was made during a meeting between Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, and Mr. Pablo Kang, Australian Ambassador to Cambodia, on 11 March 2020 at the Ministry of Social Affairs.
During the meeting, Australian Ambassador Pablo Kang praised the work and national strategic plan on disability, as well as the efforts to reduce disability to all government ministries in response to the UN Convention. On the rights of persons with disabilities.
In response, Minister Vong Soth also thanked the Royal Government of Australia for its continued support and assistance in work related to the disability sector in Cambodia.
On that occasion, the Minister also confirmed to the Australian Embassy that the Ministry of Social Affairs is currently actively working to serve the interests of the people set by the Royal Government.
In addition, the Australian Ambassador confirmed that the Embassy is also monitoring the reforms as well as proposing amendments to the Ministry of Social Affairs' disability law. He sees these reforms in line with the Royal Government of Cambodia's Rectangular Strategy and in line with Australia's ongoing development assistance to Cambodia.
