Cambodian Human Rights Leader Holds a Lecture on "Youth Together to Maintain Peace and Respect for Human Rights" to Raise Awareness in Battambang
(Battambang): Mr. Keo Remy, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, continued to open the lecture on "Youth together to maintain peace and respect for human rights" organized in collaboration with the Cambodian Human Rights Committee and the Battambang Provincial Administration. This morning, March 11, 2020, to raise awareness among local people.
On this occasion, Mr. Keo Remy also thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party for sacrificing everything to exchange peace and freedom for the people of Cambodia. From the Khmer Rouge killing field regime "Pol Pot".
Mr. Keo Remy said that peacekeeping to promote human rights and development is not for one person and no one can take care of it alone, only with the participation of For all Cambodians to continue to maintain peace, political stability, and order that promotes respect for human rights.
Taking that opportunity, Mr. Keo Remy also warned the people in Battambang province that when there is a war, do not hope to live with relatives, families, and when the country is at war, please do not talk about human rights. Therefore, let all the people unite with the Royal Government of Cambodia to maintain the peace that Cambodia is having absolutely.
In addition, Mr. Keo Remy told the people not to compare the democracies of other countries with Cambodia, because the implementation is different according to the social context. In fact, Cambodia is now open to the people living in the country with all the rights set by state law, especially respect for the rights of indigenous peoples, respect for religion, education, care services, welfare and rights. Others, like Cambodians across the country.
