The King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, and the Queen Mother of Cambodia, Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, pay their last respects at a time when the Chinese government is facing a crisis caused by the COVID-19 virus. His Majesty wishes to donate his personal wealth in the amount of 150,000 US dollars to help solve China's problems.
When China contracted the COVID-19 virus, many countries showed discrimination against the people and China by cutting off flights and banning Chinese people from entering their countries. They also decided to evacuate people from China and shut down businesses in China.
In particular, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, not only showed the maintenance of communication, travel and cooperation to fight against COVID19 disease, during the difficult time that is feared for China, Samdech also visited in China, too.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to Beijing, China on February 5, 2020 has led to a great deal of admiration for Samdech Techo Hun Sen's deep feelings for the country and the people of China. They called Samdech Techo a "handsome man walking in reverse."
Hu Zhengyue, Vice President of the Chinese Foreign Affairs Association, expressed his deepest respect for the King, Queen and Prime Minister.
"Cambodia is a true friend of China," said Zhang Jinfeng, a former Chinese ambassador to Cambodia. I am excited almost every day because I, like my Chinese friends, have heard and seen everything that His Majesty the King, Her Majesty the Queen and Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen, on behalf of the Cambodian people, strive to do. "And to the Chinese people in the fight against the virus."
She added, "This is to prove that Cambodia is an iron brother, the Chinese and Khmer friends decided that, but I want to add another phrase, not just iron, but steel." I believe that the virus is deadly, but the struggle will win. "I am convinced that the friendship between China and Cambodia, which has been tested again in this struggle, will always last."
