Minister Tram Iv Tek: Digital literacy is very important for the general population, students and civil servants at all levels
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tram Iv Tek, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, said that digital literacy is very important for the general population, students and government officials at all levels to participate in the economic process and activities in this digital age.
The remarks were made on the occasion of Minister Tram Iv Tek presiding over the closing ceremony of the "Digital Literacy" project, which has trained 1,463 students in recent months. This.
The ceremony, held at the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications on the afternoon of March 10, 2020, was also attended by Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports.
Also present were the Vice President and Board members of the Capacity Building, Research and Development Foundation for Telecommunications and Information and Communication Technology (ICRD-CBRD Fund), as well as representatives of Smart Asiata and students. Lots of crowds.
Speaking at the event, Mr. Tram Iv Tek said, "Digital literacy is very important for the general public, students and government officials at all levels to participate in the economic process and activities in this digital age."
He said that digital literacy training not only covers digital skills, but also the ability to use technology to meet the real needs of work, participation in digital society and self-development.
In this sense, it refers to the ability to find, process, communicate and generate information, as well as the ability to find solutions using technology efficiently, securely and responsibly in response to rapid technological change.
Minister Tram Iv Tek added that the ministry has focused on increasing the digital literacy of the ministry's civil servants. And as a first step, the ministry has been setting up a digital literacy test for civil servants under the auspices of the online system.
He said the statistics from the survey would be used to develop a clear staff training policy aimed at responding to changes in the work environment, especially support for building digital government and the digital economy.
On that occasion, the Minister expressed his support for the digital literacy program, as we really need to increase the capacity of citizens, government officials and students to participate in all social activities to ensure the benefit of technology. Effectiveness and safety.
The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications will also continue to support the development of digital skills with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports by continuing to build high school and secondary technology infrastructure, supporting various training programs using the US Fund.
At the same time, Minister Tram Iv Tek requested the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to examine the possibility of including in the formal education system any programs that the Ministry deems consistent with the education program to ensure the sustainability and effectiveness of the implementation of both programs. All this.
Svay Rieng Provincial Military Commander considers women as an important backbone in the development of family and society
(Svay Rieng): Brigadier General Se Vuthy, Commander of the Svay Rieng Provincial Gendarmerie, mentioned and considered women as an important backbone in the development of family and society that can not be lacking.
This statement was made by Brigadier General Se Vuthy on March 11, 2020 at the March Meeting to Review the Implementation of the Roles, Duties and Work of the Royal Gendarmerie, the Work Direction for April 2020 and to Celebrate the Anniversary Commemoration of the 109th International Day of March 8, 2020 under the theme "Peace, Promoting Gender Equality".
Brigadier General Se Wutty said that the celebration of the International Day on March 8, 2020 is really aimed at improving the living conditions, rights, freedoms, status of women in our society as the military police will continue to support and encourage women to participate. It is the core of the work to help the motherland.
The Commander also commended all officers and deputies for their hard work in the past by cooperating with local authorities and all stakeholders in the province to better protect the security and social order of the people. Appreciation and recognition from the leadership of the Ministry of National Defense, the National Gendarmerie and the Governor of Svay Rieng.
He also instructed all military officers to strengthen the network of information that causes chaos to the society around the province and continue to search for criminals. In addition, take care of the existing equipment and evaluate the building, equipment, transportation.
On that occasion, the Brigadier General, Commander-in-Chief, provided 12 women soldiers, each of whom received a hooded sweatshirt, an embroidered shirt and a budget of 50,000 riels.
