National Reading Day held at Hun Sen Ta Kork High School, Preah Sdach District, Prey Veng Province to commemorate the work of Samdech Sangkhareach Chuon Nath
(Prey Veng): To celebrate the National Reading Day on March 11, 2020, Hun Sen Ta Kork High School, Preah Sdach District, Prey Veng Province, celebrated the National Reading Day at the High School with a reading competition for students.
Through this event, led by Mr. Am Sophal, Principal of Hun Sen Ta Kork High School, with the aim of promoting a culture of reading and inspiring everyone to enjoy reading books again. This National Reading Day is also attended by teachers as well as school management and students at Hun Sen Ta Kork High School and from the Office of Education, Youth and Sports of Preah Sdach District.
Mr. Am Sophal said that the reading competition has students from each class who have been selected for the first prize and will receive an incentive prize. And the students who participated in the competition received some reading books that encouraged them to read more and share with other students in the class.
Please note that Cambodia has designated March 11 as the National Reading Day after a sub-decree was issued in September 2015. This date is set to coincide with the birthday of Chuon Nath, an expert in Khmer literature.
In 2016, Cambodia celebrated National Reading Day for the first time and has been continuing this celebration to this day, especially in Phnom Penh. The purpose of the government in this celebration is firstly to commemorate the achievements and works of Chuon Nath, and secondly to raise awareness of the importance of reading and to improve the reading habits of students, civil servants and the public. Ordinary people.
