Speaking on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Ministry of Interior, General Ke Kim Yan, introduced the following important tasks to be achieved in 2020 as follows:
* First, the Unified Command at all levels must increase the control of the situation at the local level, prevent all activities that attempt to cause insecurity, unrest and chaos to society in all forms, and must jointly prevent the insurgency and the color revolution.
* Second, the authorities and the competent forces at all levels must continue to maintain security, public order, social safety, provide better public services, continue to inspire the people to participate in the implementation of the policy of safe villages and communes to prevent and Suppress crimes, especially drug offenses, both in urban and rural areas under the direction of three do not and one report is not involved, do not intervene, do not exempt and must report all drug cases.
* Third, the provincial and district administrations must continue to promote the development of infrastructure to serve the economic activities, investment, trade, tourism and employment of the people, especially in the agricultural sector, which is a potential sector of the province to increase money. People's income.
* Fourth: Sub-national administrations at all levels must pay attention to solving challenges such as construction, garbage and sanitation, environmental issues and urban order.
* Fifth: Sub-national administrations must pay attention to the important work, councils and governors of provinces, municipalities and districts must increase the sense of responsibility in the implementation of management functions, monitor, provide services and support communes in the implementation. Project to develop and strengthen the capacity to support communes in performing their duties properly in accordance with the principles, procedures and procedures in force.
* Sixth: Sub-national administrations must continue to promote a sense of responsibility and accountability in the management, management and provision of services in the OWSO to ensure that people receive services more easily, quickly, transparently and accountably.
Seventh, the authorities and the armed forces at all levels must strive to promote the protection of territorial integrity, national sovereignty and increase security and public order in the border areas.
