At the same time, the team set up a test of the bottom layer of stone, using wooden sticks to store or raise the stone to match the default, so the team can not move the stone completely to maintain the level. The original height and original position of each rock.
After assembling the first layer up to the third layer and subsequent layers by default, the team has to dismantle the stone until the first layer is removed and replace the laterite, brittle and small, and replace it with new stone. Larger than recommended by UNESCO Ad hoc experts.
Regarding the excavation and research of the temple, Dr. Chea Socheat, an archaeologist from the Department of Temple Conservation in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology, said that the excavation was useful to study the preparation of the temple foundation, the cause of the temple collapse and how. Of temple construction.
Mr. Socheat said that the excavations also found the remains of the hospital's laterite walls, which are generally about 31 meters long and more than 20 meters wide. Parts of the wall are completely lost. It may have been dismantled when the hospital was closed.
