(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Chamkar Mon District called on the people to participate in packing and storing garbage properly to avoid dumping it, which will lead to the flow of sewers, causing congestion of garbage can not flow, especially during the rainy season. Come on.
This call was made while Mr. Theng Sothol, Governor of Chamkarmon District, in cooperation with the Department of Public Works, inspected and led the force to rehabilitate the Boeung Trabek Drainage Canal along Street 105 in Sangkat Boeung Trabek, Khan Chamkar Mon this afternoon, March 10, 2020. .
Mr. Theng Sothol, during the inspection and removal of garbage from the canal, added that in the past, as the district authority, he always educated and instructed the people to pay attention to the proper storage and packaging of garbage by Take into account environmental issues and hygiene in life.
However, there are still a small number of people who regularly dump garbage in the Boeung Trabek drainage canal, which makes it impossible to drain the water to the pumping station. He added that this work can not be achieved without the participation of the people alone.
On that occasion, the Governor of Chamkar Mon District also called on the people living along Boeung Trabek Canal to consider the hygiene issues in their lives by keeping the garbage properly and not throwing it in the sewer canal, which will lead to garbage congestion, especially May affect the health of the family, children and young children, which is easy and harmful to health.
According to the district administration official, in a day, 18 trucks collect garbage from the canal and transport garbage, each of which contains about 5 tons of garbage from the canal to be dumped at the landfill. This work was carried out from last Saturday until the garbage from the sewer.
