General Ith Sarath urges officers to be united as one to keep the peace
(Phnom Penh): General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, urges all officers to be united in maintaining peace in order to continue building and developing the nation. Growing and strong, stable.
The urging of General Ith Sarath took place this morning, March 10, 2020, on the occasion of presiding over the closing ceremony of the 28th Parachute Training Course, the closing ceremony of the 4th Generation Anti-Terrorism Training Course and the opening of the Training Course. The 4th Generation Sea Shark of the 911th Special Forces Brigade at the Parachute Jumping Training Ground in Ktan Roy Area, Thmor Koul Village, Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province.
General Ith Sarath said that on behalf of the leadership of the Ministry of National Defense, he also brought greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Katiprit Bun Rany Hun Sen to officers, deputies, soldiers and military teachers. All participants will also send their condolences to the families of all the soldiers who have made significant contributions to the defense of the country's territorial integrity.
General Ith Sarath also expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the dedication of the Commander, Deputy Commander and all levels of leadership in the 911 Division who have worked together to achieve unity. The division's annual training plan now.
At the same time, General Ith Sarath also recommended and urged the 911 Parachute Special Brigade to continue to pay attention to increase the capacity of human resources to follow the progress in all areas in the region, especially in the field of defense. .
The General also stated that today's training is an appropriate and timely response to the policy of the Royal Government to build high quality human resources to serve the duties of our motherland and To the future. General Vong Pisen Visits Troops in the 3rd Division, 4th Military Region to Celebrate Khmer New Year
(Oddar Meanchey): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, on March 10, 2020, led a delegation to visit and bring food donations from Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense. To support the 3rd Army, 4th Military Zone to celebrate the traditional Khmer New Year that will come in the coming days.
Conversation and gift giving ceremony was held at the 251st Battalion Headquarters in Banteay Ampil District, Oddar Meanchey Province.
On that occasion, General Vong Pisen brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen and Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh to the troops standing in the line area. Face.
The Commander-in-Chief explained to all forces about the political message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, which means "thank you for peace" because there is peace like today, which makes Cambodia prosperous. No fear and live a more prosperous life.
General Vong Pisen also quoted Hun Sen to tell the forces that all people in the world need peace, without peace there is nothing. Seeing the great value of peace, the General called on all forces to continue to maintain peace, protect peace, because there is peace to ensure sustainable development and a prosperous and prosperous life of the people.
On that occasion, General Vong Pisen also praised the heroic example of all forces that have strived to fulfill their duty to serve the motherland with high responsibility for protecting the territorial integrity of the motherland.
