Deputy PM Prak Sokhon Urges Youth to Seize Opportunity as Cambodia Hosts Asia-Europe Summit
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, urged young people to seize the opportunity when Cambodia hosts the 13th Asia-Europe Meeting (ASEM) in November. This face.
The Deputy Prime Minister's urging was made on the occasion of the celebration of ASEM DAY on Cambodia to host the 13th Asia-Europe Meeting in 2020 on the morning of March 10, 2020 in front of Wat Botum Vatey, Phnom Penh. .
Mr. Prak Sokhon said that today's celebration of ASEM Day is a sign of Cambodia's highest readiness and commitment to host the 13th Asia-Europe Summit. In addition to the purpose of raising awareness of the importance of ASEM and all ASEM-related events that Cambodia is organizing this year, this event is particularly relevant to our youth.
The ASEM Summit is a biennial meeting of the Heads of State and Government, the President of the European Council, the President of the European Commission and the Secretary-General of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN). ASEM, held regularly every two years, has become an important platform for partnership cooperation in maintaining peace, stability, social and economic development.
He added that to achieve this goal, Cambodia has set the theme "Strengthening Multilateralism for Joint Growth" for this summit. The theme focuses on a combination of four key perspectives: multilateralism, growth, sustainable development and prosperity, which will contribute to strengthening the Asia-Europe Partnership to ensure that multilateralism leads to inclusive growth. And overall prosperity.
