There is a case of illegal logging in Chrak Laeang waterfall, Krakor district, Pursat province, the community asked the authorities to intervene and search for the perpetrators
(Pursat): There is a report from the natural forest community at Chrak Laeang Waterfall Resort in Chheu Tom Commune, Krakor District, Pursat Province, that a group of criminals illegally cut down trees in the above area. Contrary to the protection efforts of the Royal Government to conserve the remaining forest.
On March 08, 2020, the Krakor District Joint Police Force conducted a search and identified the target of illegal logging and transportation of cut timber in the community area of Chrak Laeang Waterfall Resort. During the operation, the police confiscated some used wood and confiscated a recycling vehicle.
Although the suspect has not been arrested yet, but the subject has been identified as Su Neang, male, 42 years old, living in Khla Krapeu village, Anlong Thnout commune, Krakor district, Pursat province. Presently, the exhibits confiscated by the authorities are being kept at the Krakor District Police Inspectorate for further investigation.
Chrak Laeang Waterfall Resort was established in 2002 with a total area of 660 hectares, managed by the tourism community of Chheu Tom commune, Krakor district. It is located at the intersection of Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Speu and Pursat provinces and is surrounded by wildlife sanctuaries managed by the Department of Environment.
Since its establishment, with the attention of the provincial leadership, especially in recent years, Mr. Mao Thunin, the provincial governor, has worked hard to improve and expand the shops and parking lots. Characteristics for more visitors to provide income to the community.
Separately, Mr. Keo Rattanak, Chairman of the Krakor and Kandeang District Assistance Team, through the Chheu Tom Commune Assistance Team, also provided funding and other means to encourage the team to work with the community to preserve the forest in this area for survival. To the base and to tourists all over the country.
