The 19 communicable diseases in China have disrupted the supply of raw materials from China and disrupted the operation of factories in Cambodia. Heng Sour, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and spokesman, told Fresh News that the shortage of raw materials had led to the suspension of 50 factories, affecting 20,940 workers and 16,183 women.
To address this shortage of raw materials, the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of China, which are closely related countries, have made every effort to find ways to accelerate the import of raw materials to Cambodia. Seven ships began transporting these materials, and one arrived at the port of Sihanoukville on the night of March 9, 2020.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, during the graduation ceremony for Vanda students on the morning of March 10, 2020, emphasized that the seven ships will carry raw materials back and forth until the problems caused by Kovit 19 disease are completed. Five ships will transport goods to the port of Sihanoukville, while the other two ships will transport raw materials to Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam and transport by truck to supply factories in Bavet, Svay Rieng province.
During the graduation ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered that the rush and acceleration of the transportation of raw materials from China to Cambodia is due to the good relations between Cambodia and China. In particular, the comprehensive partnership between the two countries.
"This is a comprehensive strategic partnership between Cambodia and China in which we have access to raw materials to address workers' unemployment and the stability of the production chain serving our exports." Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, who has been named as Cambodia's strong man, further confirmed.
Along with the delivery of raw materials, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also called on the relevant authorities, including the capital-provincial governors to facilitate the transport of goods to the factory as soon as possible. Samdech Techo advised to have a siren to help open the road for trucks in case of obstacles.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen appealed to the competent authorities to facilitate the transport as follows: If you come to Phnom Penh, it is difficult to cross that we are not allowed to cross during the day, also during that day. "And find the leading Saren truck to transport the raw materials to the factory."
Heng Sour said the arrival of raw materials from China helped some of the suspended factories to resume operations. According to Heng Sour, seven factories that had been suspended have resumed operations. These seven factories have a total of 10,103 workers, 9,173 women.
During the graduation ceremony this morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that during the period when Cambodia was in trouble due to the 19 epidemic of Kovit, some factories were in trouble, but some factories were also increasing their activities.
According to Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the French manufacturer of medical clothing brand "Dipong" is increasing its production to supply countries. Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that some countries have ordered up to 2 million copies.
The company also donated 1,000 pieces of protective clothing for the Cambodian medical team.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also revealed that in 2003, when the world was suffering from the disease, the company produced up to 5 million pieces of clothing and supplies to various countries.
