(Phnom Penh): A Vietnamese ceiling worker was found dead after being electrocuted by a paintbrush motor and died one night ago, but due to the victim He was working alone in the house when no one knew.
The body of the above man was found causing a surprise at 7:30 AM on March 10, 2020 in the Aviation Borey, Kbal Damrey 2 Village, Sangkat Kakap II, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
Victim name: La Kimsan, alias Ley, 31 years old, Vietnamese, Khmer nationality, Occupation: Ceiling worker, Residence: 767C, Road Lum, Sangkat Svay Pak, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh. The apartment under renovation is 3 stories high and the owner is Heng Sokly, 31 years old, living in Chrey Kong village, his hometown in Kandal province.
Rin Vichay, a 22-year-old construction worker, resides at No. 26, Lum Road, Phnov Village, Khnes Commune, Mesang District, Prey Veng Province. Then they went home and saw that the victim was working alone, had not yet gone home, and did not know what had happened to him.
At around 7 am on March 10, as he went to work on the construction site of the house above and went up to the third floor, he found the victim lying on the roof of a motorized paintbrush there. When he went to see, he realized that the victim was electrocuted, so he removed the motor and ran downstairs, shouting at them, causing a surprise in the morning.
After receiving the above information, the 2nd Kakap Police Station and the Po Sen Chey District Police went to check the situation and reported to the Technical and Scientific Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police for an autopsy and handed over the body to the family. Take it to the traditional festival.
