Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Urges People to Be More Aware of Fire, Especially in the Dry Season
(Kampong Cham): In the celebration of National Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Day this morning, March 10, 2020 in Chakrey Village, Ou Svay Commune, Kampong Siem District, Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, reminded the people to increase Be careful not to catch fire because this season is the dry season, which makes it vulnerable to fire.
According to the Governor of Kampong Cham Province, according to the report of fire incidents in 2019 and in the first quarter of 2020, there were 49 fires in Kampong Cham province, killing one person and injuring several others. Two people burned 57 houses and damaged a total of more than 800 million riels, compared to 2018, an increase of 17 times.
At the same time, Mr. Un Chanda requested the people to pay special attention to the fire, this is another priority for all of us, because if there is a fire, the damage is really large. Unpredictable, as a proverb says (Su ab die, do not die, sink the boat in the middle of the river, do not let the house fire).
Lt. Gen. Em Kosal, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Cham Province, said that in order to prevent accidental fires, the competent authorities must implement the following plans: firearms, explosives and fire control plans must be carefully managed and instructed to the specialized offices and municipal police inspectorates. - The district should be prepared in advance to provide timely relief.
In particular, in the market area, it is necessary to organize order for vendors, stalls, to check the electricity lines and have enough water nearby, there are pumps and pipes to be ready in case of fire.
