(Phnom Penh): US President Donald Trump has sent an official message to Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen outlining the reasons and consequences for postponing the ASEAN-US Summit scheduled for March 2020. This is due to the spread of Kovid 19 disease.
"Unfortunately, we must postpone this summit because of the global risks posed by the outbreak of the new coronavirus," Donald Trump said. "I believe we can all agree by focusing our attention now on coordinating a global response that protects and ensures the health and safety of our people."
"Even though we have to postpone this special summit, our team has come up with a number of initiatives to highlight the relationship between our countries," he said. We will continue to launch many of these major programs, and we will continue to look for opportunities to implement them in the coming months.
The President is confident that ASEAN leaders will be able to convene this special summit in the near future.
