Director of the Department of Counter-Terrorism and Transnational Crime: We must value women as mothers of the world and work together to prevent violence against women
(Phnom Penh): The Department of Counter-Terrorism and Transnational Crime on March 10, 2020, celebrated the 109th Anniversary of International Women's Day on March 8, 2020 under the theme "Peace, Promoting Gender Equality". Under the chairmanship of Major General Thou Saroeun, Director of the Department and Mrs., as well as the participation of the Deputy Director of the Department and female police officers, a total of 56 people visited the Department.
On that occasion, the Major General of the Department said that the March 8 campaign is a global event that the United Nations General Assembly has declared as the day to organize the International Day for Women's Rights and World Peace in 1977.
He added that peace is an important element for ensuring the sustainability of development while stepping on the path of building and developing in all areas under the shadow of peace, which makes the Cambodian people happy. Peace, political stability and economic growth in reducing poverty.
He stressed that women have the same rights as men, women can also lead the country, in the world there are women as leaders, so we must value women as mothers of the world.
He also called on officials at all levels to take measures to prevent any violence, especially sexual violence at the grassroots level, and this is one of the topics raised by the Ministry of Women's Affairs this year. This is also 2020.
