Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presenting Diplomas to Vanda Institute Students
(Phnom Penh): About 3,458 students of Vanda Institute, 2,954 females, successfully graduated and received their degrees this morning, March 10, 2020. The graduation ceremony was presided over by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
Students graduating this morning include associate degree, bachelor and master's degree graduates in the 2018-2019 academic year. The students who received this degree include 30 undergraduate students of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, 23 females.
The following are the key remarks made by Samdech Techo Hun Sen during the graduation ceremony for Vanda Institute students:
* To begin the conversation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen presented a new uniform with a krama. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this was the uniform of the 19th Kovit disease. Samdech Techo added that even though the 19 Kovit problem is over, Samdech still uses it.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen congratulates all graduates. But Samdech Techo also reminded all students to continue to develop their capacity to respond to the development of society.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminds professors to strive to find new ways to improve the quality of education.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that no one hires people with just a degree and no ability.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the market economy has no emotions, only losses and gains.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the current situation is full of challenges that require reform and capacity building.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Ministry of Health is taking care of a man who is suffering from Kovit 19 in Siem Reap.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in Cambodia, there were only 19 cases of Kovit, only two cases: a Chinese man in Sihanoukville and a Cambodian man in Siem Reap.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on those who have been in contact with 19 men with Kovit in Siem Reap to come for a health check-up.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Ministry of Health is looking for people with a history of contact with Japanese men and Cambodian men with Kovit 19.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech encourages health precautions but prohibits discrimination against Siem Reap residents.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that all entrances and exits to Cambodia need to increase medical examinations to fight HIV 19.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on people with health problems to hurry to check their health.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech has no right to forbid people from being frightened, so Samdech does not prevent people from rushing to buy other goods.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen agreed with Mr. Khieu Kanharith that if Cambodians are afraid of traffic accidents such as Kovit 19 will reduce road deaths.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked critics of the quality of Cambodian medicine that if they do not believe in the Cambodian medical system, which country to believe in medicine, because when the disease 19, they are not allowed to enter their country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen orders Svay Sitha's Rapid Reaction Unit to report to the world 19 cases of measles three times a day.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that no matter what the trend, we must work together to fight HIV 19.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reiterated his call not to take fear and discrimination as a basis in the case of Kovit 19, that is, to choose for oneself.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that excessive fear will lead to disaster.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that mobile phone detectors continue to be used to monitor fraudulent activities.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen told the provincial governor to make it easier for trucks to transport raw materials to the factory as soon as possible.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this afternoon, 1,000 sets of "Dupong" medical uniforms will be handed over to the Ministry of Health.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that millions of "Dupong" medical uniforms were made in Cambodia and exported abroad.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that 60 containers of raw materials from China have arrived in Cambodia. Samdech Techo considers this as a coordinating effort of China as a comprehensive strategic partner of Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that fear must be turned into an opportunity to protect oneself by paying attention to hygiene.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has prepared a budget of $ 800 million to $ 2 billion to solve the problem of 19 cases of Kovit epidemic.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has stated that several international meetings have been canceled, with some meeting in Vientiane, Laos next week unclear.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government is ready to provide tax exemptions to factories affected by the suspension of the 20% preferential tariff system from the European Commission.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reiterates that Cambodia does not trade Cambodia's sovereignty and independence for European preferential tariffs.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that those convicted of treason must be punished when the verdict is issued. Samdech Techo confirmed that this time the punishment was not in Trapeang Phlong, but in another place.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the salary increase for civil servants on April 1 will be done as scheduled, including the pre-New Year allowance.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the recording of phone calls to listen to corrupt activities continues. Samdech Techo confirmed that this recording was not only for Cambodia, but also for other countries.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call for joint efforts to fight Kovit 19 and also to cooperate with neighboring countries.
Unlike in other countries, most patients who die of the new coronavirus in the UK are elderly and physically ill.
