On the first day of the operation, the police checked the alcohol on more than 1,000 drivers in Phnom Penh, and found more than 49 people drunk
(Phnom Penh): On the first day of the operation, the police checked more than 1,000 drunk drivers in Phnom Penh and found 96 drunk people. This is according to the report of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, which was received by Fresh News on the morning of March 10, 2020.
Of the 96 alcoholics, 49 were referred to the Office of Road Traffic with an alcohol content of 0.40 (12 car drivers and 37 motorcycle drivers), the report said. And 47 were educated at places with alcohol levels below 0.25 (31 car drivers and 16 motorcycle drivers).
It should be informed that the operation to control driving under the influence of alcohol on the night of March 9, 2020, led by Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner. Last night's operation took place in Khan 7 Makara, Sen Sok, Daun Penh, Dangkor, Chamkarmon, Chroy Changva and Khan Kambol.
According to the new Article 77 of the Road Traffic Law, anyone who drives a vehicle while under the influence of alcohol with an alcohol content of 0.40 mg per liter of air or from 0.80 grams per liter. Blood and above is fined 200,000 Riels for motorcyclists, tricycles or tuk-tuk drivers, 400,000 Riels for light vehicles and 800,000 Riels for heavy vehicles.
Drunk drivers who have already been fined once but continue to commit misdemeanors within six months of the previous fine will be sentenced to one to six months in prison and fined. 800,000 to 4 million riels.
