Raw materials for the first leg of textile and garment sector have arrived at the port of Sihanoukville!
(Preah Sihanouk): As planned, the first ship carrying raw materials to serve the textile and garment sector arrived at the port of Sihanoukville on the night of March 9, 2020.
On March 9, 2020, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, announced that the Chinese government has prepared seven ships to transport raw materials to supply factories in Cambodia during the 19-crisis Kovit crisis. Some factories in Cambodia are forced to suspend work due to lack of raw materials.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen claims that the first leg of a Chinese ship carrying raw materials from China to Cambodia arrived at the Cambodian port on March 9, and the second leg will arrive today and will arrive. Next.
Also yesterday, the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia reaffirmed the Chinese government's commitment to assisting Cambodia in dealing with a shortage of raw materials for the garment and footwear sector in Cambodia.
The Chinese embassy confirmed that the first ship that arrived at the port in Sihanoukville was the first to carry more than 60 containers of textile and garment materials, while other ships carrying other materials will arrive in Cambodia in the future, which will help Cambodia's losses. Fall to the lowest rate.
