Rural Development Bank celebrates International Women's Day on March 8 under the theme "Peace, Employment, Gender Equality"
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Monday, March 9, 2020, Mr. Kao Thach, Director General of the Rural Development Bank and Ms. Sour Sok Kim presided over the program. Celebrating the 109th Anniversary of International Women's Day on March 8 under the theme "Peace, Employment, and Gender Equality" with nearly 90 staff members participating.
Over the past decade, the number of rural development bank staff has increased from 54 to 114, of which the number of female staff has increased from 11 to 23% to 36 to 32%. Total number of employees.
He said that in order to promote gender equality, the management of the Rural Development Bank also provided opportunities for female employees to participate in all activities of the bank and provide some key positions, which increased the number of female leaders in the bank to 32%. He is confident that in the following years, the growth of the bank's female staff will increase.
On that occasion, the Director General expressed his appreciation and gratitude to all employees who have worked hard to fulfill their roles and perform their duties with results, results and high sense of responsibility.
Through this day, the Director General also requested all employees to be aware of gender issues, have a spirit of solidarity, cooperate and work together to make the Rural Development Bank sustainable.
