The Ministry of Commerce issued an appeal to traders selling goods in Cambodia, please keep the price of goods the same, do not raise prices!
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce on March 9, 2020 issued an appeal to traders who sell goods in Cambodia to maintain the same price on the market without raising prices.
The Ministry of Commerce's call comes after the Cambodian Ministry of Health announced the discovery of the Covid-19 case of a Cambodian man in Siem Reap. Increase the price of goods such as face masks, alcohol, hand wash and some other essential goods, these activities can cause serious social unrest.
