(Phnom Penh): "People's Congress" is a program created during the Sangkum era to be a direct meeting between the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk and the people to listen to all the problems of the people and put Issue remedial measures. Nowadays, it is rare to see the use of face-to-face meetings between officials and citizens to listen and resolve such issues.
Mr. Mao Thunin considered meeting, listening and solving problems directly with the people as an adaptation and incorporation into the well-being of the people in his province.
In Pursat Provincial Hall, every Monday at the beginning of each week, in a large meeting hall, many people often sit in a chair opposite the Governor of Pursat, Mr. Mao Thunin, accompanied by some other officials. Mr. Mao Thunin said that he chooses Monday and Thursday of each week to meet, listen and solve problems for the people. But if Monday or Thursday is busy, move to another day instead.
The governor of Pursat province confirmed that "this mechanism. This mechanism I usually remove two or three days a week, every Monday morning. So, if he comes on Monday and he comes in trouble on Tuesday, we can inform him on Thursday, and if he comes on Friday, we will raise him on Monday. ”
People in trouble were intercepted from all over Pursat province to seek direct solutions from the provincial governor on various issues related to their daily lives. Some people have land disputes, some people have debt problems, some people have family disputes and some people are cheated. There are also disputes in the temple between the monks and the pagoda committee.
People who came to seek a solution from Mr. Mao Thunin learned about his help through the villagers and some learned through his own announcement in meetings as well as during Go to the basics.
During the search for a solution, Mr. Mao Thunin called the troubled people to sit down one by one and asked them to describe the problems they encountered, while some officials accompanied him to record all the problems raised by the people. . He then decided what to do and how to deal with it. Do you have to go directly to the problem area or let the authority be the district governor or the commune chief to solve it? In other cases, he has to go to the district and commune to find a solution.
The provincial governor confirmed that "all the work that they always come to meet at the provincial hall is not a big problem. Most of them have disputes, lack of roads and bridges, as well as land issues related to the transfer of inheritance from parents to children. We incorporated him as a member of his family, we settled as a family, and we took the legal mechanism to prepare a letter or settlement according to the law to him.
Land issues are also a hot topic in Cambodia today. Pursat province before Mao Thunin took control also had many land disputes. Over the past five years, Mao Thunin has settled more than 400 land disputes, and now land disputes are less common.
"In the past, the mechanism we have used seems to have been reduced," he said. In Bong province, for the past 5 years, there have been more than 400 cases of all kinds. State land and people, community and people, company land, investment with people or company with people, people and people. "This land issue is not just about the people with the company or between the company and the people." This is the additional confirmation of the provincial governor.
In relation to land disputes, it is also said that some land disputes are difficult to resolve because they belong to influential or powerful people. For Mao Thunin in his province, there are no unresolved land disputes, as he stands by the principles of law and justice.
In addition to establishing a mechanism to provide opportunities for people to meet and describe problems in order to find solutions directly, in his capacity as Governor of Pursat, Mr. Mao Thunin led the development of Pursat to emerge many notable achievements. During his five years in charge of Pursat province, Mr. Mao Thunin also contributed to improving the lives of the people in the province.
The achievements of the efforts to lead and manage Pursat province, Mr. Mao Thunin received the love, satisfaction and support of the people in the province. Some people have said that they are lucky to have a good governor like never before and do not want this governor to leave.
