National Road 55 can be said to be the first national road in Cambodia to be built flexibly up and down and intersecting the high ridges of the Cardamom Mountains. In addition to splitting through the mountains, National Road No. 55 also splits through the forest, small, large, high, low, green, creating a landscape like a painting becomes food for the eyes, very attractive to all travelers. Cross on this road.
This development has not only helped the people in the mountainous areas to prosper, but also the people living in Veal Veng district have become more and more prosperous. For example, Ms. Kang Kim Hourn, who lives in Veal Veng district and has a restaurant to receive tourists, said that in the past she always sat waiting to hear the sound of cars and motorbikes crossing this road from time to time, but now she does not need to listen. Sounds like this no more.
Of course, where there is a road, there is hope and development. Most of the people living on this road are engaged in growing various crops, so the presence of this road facilitates the transportation of agricultural products to the market. In addition, due to the attractiveness of the streets and natural beauty, forests, mountains and waterfalls also attract tourists. Facilitating the transportation of agricultural products and attracting tourists has improved the lives of the people.
National Road No. 55 is more than 182 kilometers long, passing through three districts, including Bakan, Phnom Kravanh and Veal Veng districts, to the rocky border. In addition to inspiring development on the rocky border, National Road 55 is built with modern technology and standards set by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, as well as companies. China, the builder.
Achievement National Road 55 Not only did the governor of Pursat see the value of the Cambodian-Chinese friendship, but the people of Pursat also highly valued the Cambodian-Chinese friendship. They expressed their appreciation for this achievement and expressed their gratitude to the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia as well as the Government of China.
