According to the authorities, the suspect was named Thi Vannak, alias Thi Siv, 25 years old, residing in Trapeang Cham village, Po Ty commune, Sithor Kandal district, Prey Veng province, occupation: fishing worker in Sihanoukville.
He was arrested in connection with the murder of another victim, who was killed and dumped into the sea in Sihanoukville. At 10:00 on March 3, 2020, the bodies of the victims were found floating in the water around Koh Rong.
After receiving this information, the Prey Veng Provincial Police Commission immediately ordered the police force of Sithor Kandal District Police Inspectorate to monitor the suspects until they received specific information, then the authorities of Sithor Kandal District Inspectorate arrested the suspects. Sithor Kandal District Police Inspectorate immediately at 16:45 on March 7, 2020.
The community is nicknamed the "Eight Corners Forest Community" and is actively working to conserve wildlife such as wild boars, wolves, wolves, peacocks, especially endangered reptiles, under special protection from the community.
In the dry season, the community faces major problems such as water shortages and wildfires.
Mr. Soeun Lay, President of Pram Bei Mom Forest Community, said that this community forest was established in 2003 with a total population of 678 families (2,269 people (1,372 women)) to manage the 937 hectares of community forest. A kind of degraded mixed forest.
He said that today there are 16 forest and wildlife patrols in the community, patrolling day and night, volunteering since 2003.
He called on NGOs, the private sector and philanthropists to continue to support and support the community to continue to be more active and strong in protecting wildlife and forests for the benefit of the people and future generations.
The eight-corner community forest was recognized by the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries on April 3, 2018 and the community forest agreement was signed on September 10, 2018 with the support of the Forestry Administration.
Dr. Keo Omalis, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Forestry Administration, considered this forest community to be the most exemplary community for Cambodia to be able to take care of the endangered forest and wildlife on its own, without relying on any assistance. All.
He said that although the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries is not indifferent to the livelihood of the community, it always mobilizes philanthropists, donors and other organizations to help the rest of the community.
He added that in the future, the Forestry Administration plans to develop the area into a tourist attraction for wildlife viewing and research.
Please be informed that the community forestry in Cambodia started in 1994 and is currently receiving interest and support from all relevant circles, including national, international development partners, civil society and local communities.
Currently, under the coordination and support of the Forestry Administration and the participation of local authorities, development partners have established a total of 636 community forests covering more than 510,000 hectares of forest in 21 provinces, 99 districts, 312 communes, 954 Village.
The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has issued a proclamation on the establishment and management of a total of 494 community forest areas covering more than 440,000 hectares of forest land for the purpose of managing, conserving and developing forests sustainably and benefiting. Equity and improve living standards to contribute to reducing poverty and for the future of the next generation.
