Understand the law: the vow
(Phnom Penh): Men or women who are already married in accordance with the legal conditions of the Kingdom of Cambodia can not register a new marriage (civil) or jointly (have sex) with a person other than their spouse. Break the old marriage bond.
In the actual social situation, some people still have the misconception that men and women who have lived together, whether married or not, are often called "spouses" and can not share services with other people or It is not possible to get married again. This understanding of the legal meaning is not correct unless you have registered a legal marriage of the Kingdom of Cambodia to become a legal couple.
In addition, if the spouse commits adultery, it is considered a crime and shall be punished according to the law in force. Therefore, to better understand what adultery is and to what extent should the person who committed adultery be punished?
Therefore, this week, Fresh News' Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation, brings up the topic of "conspiracy" and shares it with all students:
Pursuant to the 2006 Law on Monogamy, which was enacted to ensure the protection of dignity and to promote harmony, happiness in the family and mutual respect between husband and wife in accordance with the Constitution, the supreme law of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
