Missing girl abducted in Ratanakkiri province's Kon Mom district was found and returned to her family
(Ratanakkiri): After a busy search under the direct command of Brigadier General Thao Yen, Commander of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Gendarmerie, Kon Mom District Local Gendarmerie on the night of March 6, 2020, brought the daughter of the family of workers of "Hang Anh" Company. Kon Mom District Military Office to wait for the guardians to take home.
It should be noted that the above family has a father named Yav Yoeung, 60 years old, a wife named Heng Loun, 61 years old and a daughter named Yoeung Srey Nith, 15 years old, who were abducted from the house by the suspect named Nget, a worker of the same company. February 23, 2020 ago.
According to the description of the girl, Yoeung Srey Nith told the local military officer in Kon Mom district that when he ran away from home with Nget, he hid at the house of a friend named Dip for two days in Sesan district. Stung Treng Province. Until the 25th, the two of them took a taxi from Stung Treng Provincial Bus Station to hide in Kratie Province (U Khang Pros).
Using professional rules, the military officer contacted the man's family on a regular basis to send the two of them home with various promises. On the 27th, they appeared at the base of the Sre Pok bridge, close to the woman's house in the company "Hang Anh", but two hours later, the suspect named Nget seemed to be afraid of the military arrested and rode. The motorbike ran back to the house named Dip in Stung Treng province and then continued to hide in Kratie province again.
However, because the male relatives were afraid of legal problems and the use of professional rules by the military officers, the suspect's relatives persuaded the girl to return home alone, saying that the suspect, Nget, did not come with her.
After questioning local military officers in Kon Mom district and with the permission of Mr. Ngin Pech, the Ratanakkiri Provincial Prosecutor handed over the girl, Duong Srey Nith, to her guardians and bring her back to her home. As for the victim, Nget is waiting for the order from the higher level and the prosecutor of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Court to take further action. Cambodian Community Support Fund Association Organizes General Assembly and Targets 2020
