Minister of Women's Affairs Joins International Women's Day on March 8 to Encourage Women Teachers and Civil Servants in Kambol District
(Phnom Penh): To celebrate the International Women's Day on March 8, the 109th Anniversary of 2020, Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs, presided over a meeting with female police officers and teachers on the morning of March 7, 2020. And more than 400 civil servants in Sangkat and Khan.
The 109th International Women's Day on March 8, 2020, was held under the theme "Peace, Promoting Gender Equality", highlighting the important role of peace in society. In particular, this peace has contributed to the promotion of women's rights and freedoms and to help women have a higher value in society.
The ceremony was held at Kambol District Hall with the participation of Mr. Khim Sun Soda, Kambol District Governor and his wife, Mr. Deputy Governor, Deputy Director of Ban Khan, a female civil servant of Sangkat Khan. And primary and secondary school teachers throughout Bol district.
Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi stated that the Prime Minister praised the Ministry of Women's Affairs, the National Council of Cambodia for Women, relevant ministries, the private sector, civil society and all national and international development partners who have contributed to the improvement of living conditions, rights, status, roles and well-being. Women and children and the provision of quality and effective assistance to victims of violence.
Ms. Ung Kantha Phavi brought the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which called on all relevant ministries, institutions, development partners, civil society, the private sector and all compatriots to implement the following seven key points:
* First, we must pay attention together by giving priority to increasing the number of women in leadership positions in various fields and at all levels.
* Second, we must work together to strengthen law enforcement and expedite the trial of convicted women. Manage the use of the Internet across the country effectively to prevent many issues related to violence, exploitation of women and girls on the Internet and various social media that disrupt social order.
* Third, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports must instruct all ministries and institutions to implement discipline and provide opportunities for girls at all levels, especially parents to educate their children to have good morals in society.
* Fourth: To continue to invest in the education of girls at all levels, especially in science and technology to keep up with the advanced technology of society.
Fifth, the Ministry of Culture, the Ministry of Information and all media must continue to strengthen and promote the social morality, values of Cambodian women and families through the creation of educational programs that reflect the identity of Cambodian women, especially through the dress with dignity and Characteristics of a Khmer woman.
* Sixth: Together to prevent the spread of new HIV and to not discriminate against women, beer promoters, including LGBT people.
