Reduce spending by ministries and institutions to save money to fight the spread of severe respiratory illness (COVID-19) and prevent negative impacts on the national economy.
According to the new circular, in 2020, all ministries and institutions are required to implement:
Manage staff expenditures very strictly by applying the new recruitment policy equal to the number of retirees, that is, maintain the number of civil servants, military and police as in 2019.
Save 50% on overseas mission expenses for all ministries and institutions except the Council of Ministers, Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Ministry of Commerce to 25%.
* Save 15% on office supplies in all ministries and institutions.
* Reduce the cost of information technology equipment and supplies by 15% in all ministries and institutions.
* Save 13% on fuel and lubricants for all ministries and institutions.
* Suspend the purchase of vehicles for administrative work of all ministries and institutions, except for the purchase of fire trucks, ambulances, etc. to meet the need to provide public services.
