Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong sends congratulatory message to Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen on the occasion of the 109th Anniversary of International Day, March 8, 2020
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong and Mrs. Borey Hor sent a congratulatory message to His Excellency Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross on the occasion of the 109th Anniversary of the International Day of March 8, 202 under the slogan "Thank you for peace" To continue to develop the motherland in all fields in a sustainable and prosperous manner and to promote gender equality and environment.
Please be informed that the celebration of International Women's Day on March 8 is held every year around the world to commemorate the struggle and heroic example of women in demanding freedom and freedom from oppression. In Cambodia, the rights of both men and women were lost during the Democratic Kampuchea regime of the Pol Pot genocide.
The rights and freedoms of the Cambodian people, as well as women, were restored after the brutal regime of Pol Pot was overthrown on January 7, 1979. From the day of liberation until now, the Royal Government of Cambodia has always paid attention to the promotion of women, creating the slogan "Women are the backbone of the national economy."
By paying attention to promoting and promoting women's rights, more and more Cambodian women are working in government ministries and institutions. Women have been playing a vital role in boosting the national economy by working in the garment and footwear sectors. In this sector, 90% of the workforce is women.
