Please be informed that on March 6, 2020, the Ministry of Health and Siem Reap Provincial Authority held a meeting to focus on preventing the new situation that is happening in Siem Reap after a Japanese man was Announced the infection of Kovid 19 a few days ago after he left Siem Reap.
After receiving information about the 19-year-old Kovid infection in the Japanese man, the Ministry of Health and Siem Reap provincial authorities immediately took immediate action by taking four people with direct contact, who were working with the patient. In order to monitor their health, another 40 people were also advised to pay more attention to their health.
According to the police report, the four people who worked with the Japanese man infected with Kovid 19 were working directly in the room with the patient for many hours, but the Japanese man who was infected Extremely vigilant about health issues, since the outbreak of Kovid, he has tightened and protected the health of the company by having employees wear masks and wash their hands regularly.
However, to date, there is no official confirmation as to where the Japanese man crossed the Kovid 19, but he returned to Cambodia on February 16, 2020. February 21: Traveled to the Philippines until February 28, left the Philippines for Siem Reap, passed through Bangkok until the night of March 3, then left Siem Reap for Nagoya, Japan. Pass through Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam.
