Cambodia, Laos agree to continue to work on three important issues related to security
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Interior of Cambodia and the Ministry of Public Security of Laos have agreed to continue to implement three important tasks related to security. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Interior on March 6, 2020 on the results of the three-day working visit of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior in Laos.
During the working visit, Sar Kheng met with Lao Minister of Public Security Vilayla Khamphong, and the two sides signed a memorandum of understanding on cooperation for 2020. Attention to continue to perform some important tasks, including:
* Continue to urge the border authorities of the two countries to cooperate to facilitate the entry and exit of people across the border and mutual trade to serve the needs of development and improvement of people's lives. Citizens living in the border areas, as well as cooperating to solve problems or other phenomena for the people in time to continue the peace and have a high level of understanding.
* Continue to cooperate in taking strict measures to prevent and suppress drug offenses across the borders of the two countries, as well as to exchange information and experiences related to drug offenses, especially to promote the establishment of drug-free villages, communes and schools in Border area.
* Continue to push for strict measures to prevent and crack down on illegal border crossings, as well as continue cooperation in border management and cooperation to resolve various issues peacefully, based on the principles of mutual respect, independence and sovereignty.
On the occasion of the meeting between the two sides, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng invited the Minister of Public Security of Laos to lead a delegation to visit Cambodia at an appropriate time to attend the meeting to evaluate the results of the implementation of the 2020 Memorandum of Cooperation and sign The minutes of the 2021 cooperation of the two ministries.
General Vong Pisen leads a delegation to visit and inspect the work of the engineering force at Phav base
(Kampong Cham): On the morning of March 6, 2020, General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, led a delegation to visit and inspect the work of the Engineering Force based in Phaov Commune, Batheay District, Kampong Cham Province.
On that occasion, General Vong Pisen conveyed greetings from Samdech Techo Chea Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit and Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense. The lieutenants and soldiers of the Engineering Force, who have worked hard, physically and mentally, to take responsibility for the historic mission to serve the nation in the past.
General Vong Pisen recalled the sacrifice of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to fight for national liberation from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot and highlighted the vision of the Royal Government that led the Cambodian navy towards peace and progress.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen: In 2020, Cambodia has made progress in reducing the gender gap should be proud (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, said that the efforts of the Royal Government to raise The promotion of gender equality and empowerment of women is highly valued by the World Economic Forum's 2020 rankings, which Cambodia is proud to have made progress in reducing the gender gap.
This statement was made on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen presiding over the celebration of the 109th International Women's Day on March 8, which was held at Koh Pich Center, Phnom Penh this morning, March 6, 2020. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that "the Royal Government's efforts to promote gender equality and empower women are highly appreciated through the World Economic Forum's 2020 rankings, which Cambodia has received. "Progress in reducing the gender gap should be proud: down from 112 in 2016 to 89 in 2020 out of 153 countries."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is recognized as a country where women are actively involved in the economy and the promotion of women's health, and the highest participation rate of women in the workforce is 79%, 65% of business owners are Women Although most of these businesses are micro and micro enterprises.
In addition, the Prime Minister emphasized that in the field of education, Cambodia has gender equality at the primary and secondary levels, and the gender gap at the secondary and tertiary levels has been gradually reduced. In recent years, the number of female students at the upper secondary level has increased both in quantity and quality. The result of female students who got A grade in the high school exam was around 50%.
Samdech Techo stated that women and girls are more likely to have access to education both inside and outside the system, in which they are encouraged and supported to acquire new knowledge, skills and technologies, especially education. Science, technology, engineering, creative arts and mathematics in line with the evolution of technology and the labor market.
In response to all forms of violence against women and children, the Royal Government has developed mechanisms, laws, policies, national action plans, the provision of multidisciplinary services and other measures with the participation of relevant institutions, including civil society organizations, to assist Victims of gender-based violence. This is an additional confirmation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Meanwhile, the Royal Government has increased the budget for the National Council of Cambodia for Women by 500 million Riels per year to help women and girls victims in seeking justice services through the establishment of Samdech Techo Sen Lawyers in all capitals. The 25 provinces to help find justice services for the poor, women and girls affected by violence in a timely and effective manner.
