Samdech Techo Hun Sen Introduces 7 Measures to Respond to the Challenges of Private Sector-Social Development Partners (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, sets out seven measures to Respond to the current challenges that the partner organizations for social development, civil society, the private sector and all citizens must focus on together.
The seven measures taken by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of presiding over the celebration of the 109th International Women's Day on March 8 at the Koh Pich Center this morning, March 6, 2020 include:
* First, all leaders of ministries and institutions must continue to increase the number of women in leadership positions at all levels.
* Third, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports must instruct all educational institutions to strengthen the implementation of discipline and to communicate with parents and guardians of students on a regular basis. Parents and guardians should pay attention to educating their children, boys and girls, study hard, have a moral culture, non-violence in the family and in society.
* Fourth: Continue to invest in the education of girls at all levels, especially in science, technology, engineering, creative arts and mathematics to keep pace with the progress of science, technology and innovation.
* Fifth, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, the Ministry of Information and all media, both public and private, must continue to strengthen and promote social morality, the values of Cambodian women and families, as well as increase good educational programs that reflect the values of Cambodian women, traditions and culture. More broadly and consider the impact and dignity of people, especially the values of women and girls.
