Gameweek 5 consists of 9 matches of the 5th Svay Rieng Cup 2020 Season
(Svay Rieng): This season Svay Rieng Cup has 51 teams participating, 107 matches, running for 4 months from January to May 2020, with sports teams from 8 districts Throughout Svay Rieng province.
A total of 1,500 players and officials participated. The competition will be held at 2 pitches: Svay Rieng High School for the group stage and the Svay Rieng Provincial Stadium will play the main round.
All sports teams must have Cambodian players aged 16 and over, a team with a maximum of 23 members and a minimum of 17 members, and each team can bring 3 players from outside the province. And 20 are residents of Svay Rieng province or place of birth in Svay Rieng province.
It should also be noted that the Svay Rieng Cup has been established for 5 seasons from 2015 to the present, with the initiative of Mr. Dy Vichea, Vice President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia and President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia in Svay Rieng.
The purpose of the Svay Rieng Cup is to create sports activities for the benefit of the youth, as well as the people in the province have the opportunity to participate in sports for health, friendship and solidarity, away from drug use and other atrocities. ⁇.
Ministry of Tourism Celebrates International Women's Day on March 8 at Phnom Da Cultural and Historical Tourism Resort, Takeo Province
(Takeo): The Ministry of Tourism celebrates the 109th anniversary of the International Women's Day on March 8, 2020 under the theme "Peace, Promoting Gender Equality". Done on March 05, 2020.
The ceremony was presided over by Ms. Nhek Sim Thong Khon, Honorary President of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development, Ministry of Tourism, and Ms. Hun Dany, Secretary of State and President of the Women's Association of the Ministry of Tourism, and was attended by female officials of the Ministry at both the national and lower levels. National Authority, Tachi Yai Chi forces, a total of more than 300 people.
Speaking at the event, Ms. Hun Dany mentioned that the reason why the Ministry chose this resort to celebrate:
The first is to "thank for the peace" and highlight the value of peace that has transformed Cambodia from an ashes of national division into a country of peace, freedom, democracy, the rule of law and strong development in all areas, as well as free participation and Equal rights with countries in the region and the world, especially gender equality, have been continuously promoted with remarkable positive results.
Third, to promote and promote local tourism as a contribution to improve the lives of the people in accordance with the will and high recommendation of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo, who wants the Cambodian people to divert their travel destinations in the country. Rather than going on a tour abroad.
Fourth: Participate in creating job opportunities and income for local people.
Fifth, to strengthen the bonds of solidarity, friendship and brotherhood between women officials at all levels, both at the Ministry-Capital and Provincial levels, to help each other and share experiences with each other.
She added that although today we commemorate the rights of women, we also welcome the participation of men. Gender equality is a key factor in ensuring the sustainability of peace and development.
She stressed that women are an important and necessary contributor to ensuring the effectiveness of the environment and the long-term sustainability of peace. Gender equality and empowerment of women and girls is an agenda that the Royal Government of Cambodia strongly focuses on and encourages them to become a driving force to actively contribute to development and A strong backbone of the economy and society.
