This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Celebrates the 109th International Women's Day on March 8
(Phnom Penh): On Friday, March 6, 2020, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen presided over the celebration of the 109th Anniversary of International Women's Day on March 13, 2020. Koh Pich Center.
The rights and freedoms of the Cambodian people and women were restored after the brutal regime of Pol Pot was overthrown on January 7, 1979. From the day of liberation until now, the Royal Government of Cambodia has always paid attention to the promotion of women, creating the slogan "Women are the backbone of the national economy."
* The following is the history leading up to the celebration of International Women's Day on March 8:
This radical movement had a profound effect on women workers in Germany, a large industrialized country at the time. In Germany at that time appeared three famous young women, Clara Shekkin, a German, and Roska Lumpur, a Polish, who had joined forces with Grupe Skaya (Lenin's wife) to inspire the movement. International Secretary to lead the women's movement.
In 1910, the 17th International Women's Conference was held in Copenhagen, the capital of Denmark, to mark March 8, "International Women's Day," a day of great solidarity for women workers around the world for the rights and freedoms of democracy. The slogan is "Work eight hours a day", "Equal pay, equal pay", "Protect maternal and child health".
Since then, March 8 has become International Women's Day, commemorating the struggles of women workers around the world who strive to liberate women by demanding equal rights for men and women.
It is because of the hard work and perseverance of all the hardships of the past 100 years that women in the world now have the opportunity to enjoy equal rights in some form of humiliation. This brilliant result has greatly reduced violence and discrimination against women who are often considered the weaker sex.
In 1980, the Second World Conference on Women was held in Copenhagen, Denmark, to review the progress and implementation of the action plan set out in the first conference, and to discuss topics such as education, employment and employment. Health.
In 1985, at the end of the Women's Decade, the third conference was held in Nairobi, Kenya to review and evaluate the achievements of the Women's Decade and to adopt a progressive strategy for women's growth in 2000.
These are the strategies and solutions of women that are always practiced peacefully through expression only. The result that women achieve is the provision of adequate equal rights and human values, that is, nothing more is required.
If we compare the history of the International Women's Day on March 8 with the birth of the United Nations, we see that the history of the International Day of March 8 was born before the United Nations and also before human rights.
However, today in Cambodia, there are national and international laws, such as the United Nations Universal Declaration of Human Rights, the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination against Women, and the Constitution of the Royal Government of Cambodia. In Chapter 3 on rights, even inequality between men and women, discrimination against women, abuse of women, and domestic violence remain.
That is why our Royal Government and a large number of NGOs are working diligently to bring all these issues to the attention of all men and women, to help women achieve justice in exercising their rights and to exercise their rights. Reduce, prevent and eliminate the above problems that occur in women. Hun Manet's Second Daughter Wins 1st Place in Asia and World Class Math Competition
