Ministry of Environment Presents Certificate of Environmental Peace to Chip Mong Bank
(Phnom Penh): On the evening of March 5, 2020, Chip Mong Bank received a Certificate of Merit from the Ministry of Environment.
The awarding ceremony was presided over by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Mr. Chuob Paris, Deputy Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the National Council for Sustainable Development.
Chip Mong Bank is the first commercial bank to implement environmentally friendly practices by reducing the use of paper, creating digital systems, facilitating customer banking operations, setting up offices that are comfortable and hygienic for employees, and engaging. Implement sustainable financial principles.
Mr. Oknha Leang Meng, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Chip Mong Bank, said that receiving this certificate of environmental friendliness really made him and all the colleagues of Chip Mong Bank excited and happy that the bank has been praised by the Ministry of Environment. And this achievement comes from the efforts of all leaders and colleagues.
He added that Chip Mong Bank uses the latest industry-leading digital technology 4.0, which uses electronic, paper-saving technology to help protect the environment, reduce deforestation and reduce carbon emissions. CO2).
At the same time, on behalf of Minister Say Samal, Mr. Neth Pheaktra expressed his appreciation to Chip Mong and thanked Chip Mong Bank for its consistent respect and good environmental performance until receiving this award.
