(Svay Rieng): Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, called on women to work together to maintain peace in order to develop the nation and ensure gender equality.
Ms. Men Sam An said this during a meeting with women of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development in Svay Rieng province during the celebration of the 109th anniversary of the International Women's Day on March 8, 2020 under the theme "Peace, Promote Equality Gender ”at Svay Rieng Provincial Hall on the afternoon of March 5, 2020, with the participation of a large number of female members.
"Peace and political stability are essential foundations for a government to be able to focus on socio-economic development and the well-being of its people," Men Sam An said. If peace is lost, everything, including gender equality, will be lost. "So peace is an important element for ensuring the sustainability of development."
She added that, in fact, after achieving complete peace throughout the country due to the win-win policy initiated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia has changed and grown steadily, taking a confident step on the path of development in all areas. Towards a brighter future.
Under the shadow of peace, political stability and high and stable economic growth of an average of more than 7% during the past decade, Cambodia's poverty has been reduced to 10% today and the unemployment rate. About 0.3% and Cambodia is expected to become the new economic tiger in Asia.
