(Central): The case of three-star military officer Leng Bunsrey (aka Hun Bunsrey) who was accused by two citizens of defrauding thousands of dollars was sent to the Criminal Office by the criminal police of Ang Snoul District Police Inspectorate. Light level of Kandal Provincial Police to proceed with the procedure. The Kandal Provincial Police Office of Minor Offenses will send the case to court soon.
In response to this case, General Leng Bunsrey completely denied the allegations and claimed that he did not know the two individuals who accused him and asked for specific evidence.
The inspector said by telephone that immediately after receiving the complaint, the expert summoned the three stars for clarification at the end of February, but the person did not follow the summons but appeared. Chea Kimsen contacted the authorities, claiming that Mr. Leng Bunsrey, also known as Hun Bunsrey, did not know anything.
The inspector said that because the person refused to come as summoned, the expert prepared the case of Mr. 3 star Leng Bunsrey to the Office of Minor Crimes of the Kandal Provincial Police under the pretext of accusing him of breach of trust.
According to the story and the complaint of the people, the senior military officer promised with them to join the army for $ 5,000, but the victim asked to come down to $ 3,500 and Another promised to end the land dispute for $ 10,000, but the victim asked for only $ 2,000, but in the end the three stars did not keep their promise.
The first victim: Mab Vannak, male, 28 years old, resident of Rong Village, Yuth Samaki Commune, Oudong District, Kampong Speu Province, cheated Mr. 3 Star Leng Bunsrey (aka Hun Bunsrey) in early 2019. The second victim: Las Sok Ken, a female resident of Trapeang Chheu Neang village, Peuk commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province, cheated 3-star Leng Bunsrey (aka Hun Bunsrey) during the middle of 2019.
In this regard, the victim, Mab Vannak, described to the media that he knew Mr. Pkhay 3 Leng Bunsrey through the name Noun, who lives in Ang Snoul district. Noun was then brought to meet with the three stars to help enlist in the military for an agreed price of $ 3,500.
Believing in the names of Noun and 3-star Hun Bunsrey, who claimed to be relatives of the nation's top leaders and had many factions who wanted to work in any institution, the victim agreed to hand over $ 3,500. Give 3 stars Hun Bunsrey to his house in Ang Snuol II village, Peuk commune, Ang Snuol district, Kandal province.
General Leng Bunsrey told Fresh News on March 5, 2020 that he would like to dismiss the allegations because he did not know the two individuals who accused him. The general also asked for specific evidence because he was not involved in the slightest, and the media that came down from him also asked for professional requirements because he did not act as alleged.
