In addition, the Cambodian Embassy in Japan on March 5, 2020 confirmed the status of a Japanese national infected with the new coronavirus, or Covid-19, who was screened when leaving Cambodia for Japan via Vietnam. . This is according to the letter from Mr. Ing Rachana, the Cambodian Ambassador to Japan, who made a report to Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia.
Siem Reap Provincial Administration will apply restrictions on construction sites that have been pre-licensed and demolished.
(Siem Reap): Siem Reap Provincial Administration From 2020, the provincial authorities will strengthen the legal mechanism to control the quality of construction that has been completed before the permit is issued and will be demolished. This was confirmed by Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap.
At this point, Samdech Pichey Sena said that urban development such as construction issues such as garbage, environmental issues and urban order, cooperation with development partners, etc. are priority issues that all sub-national administrations must pay attention to solve. Challenge by improving management measures and re-learning the technical characteristics of landfills to protect the environment.
Mr. Tea Seiha also said at the meeting that the Siem Reap provincial authorities will start implementing the restriction mechanism on better construction management. For any construction built in 2018-2019, the provincial authority will assign a professional officer to inspect the quality and technique. If it is found that the construction is correct, the provincial authority will issue a permit to continue the construction.
From 2020 onwards, the strictest measures will be implemented. Any construction that is built before the permit is issued will be demolished, even if it is 30% or 50% completed. The reason why the authorities are doing this is to strengthen the implementation of the construction law and improve the quality of construction to ensure the safety of workers and people. Video inside)
Sihanoukville CamControl Officers Continue to Inspect Goods at Shopping Markets and Supermarkets Around Theater in Sihanoukville
In fact, on Wednesday, March 4, 2020, CamControl Sihanoukville Branch, with Mr. Bun Chamroeun as the Acting Branch Manager, in cooperation with the local authorities, continued to promote the quality and safety of food in commercial markets and supermarkets around the city. Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province.
According to the Sihanoukville CamControl official, during the inspection, some food samples were taken for preliminary testing, including shrimp, fresh squid, dried fish, cooking oil, mixed vegetables, meatballs, sausages and pickles to find banned chemicals. Harm to the health of the people.
