(Svay Rieng): Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, stated that Buddhism has played a role in educating Cambodians to be moral, dignified, and well-behaved. It is through this education that immoral acts can be avoided in human society, thus creating a credible culture of peace.
This statement was made by Ms. Men Sam An on the morning of March 5, 2020 at the ribbon-cutting ceremony and the inauguration of the achievement at Wat Chin Ves, also known as Wat Chak Va, which cost $ 163,900 in construction in the village. Banteay Kraing, Banteay Kraing Commune, Kampong Ror District, Svay Rieng Province.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Ouk Samvithya, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director of the National Social Security Fund, and Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province, as well as more than 1,000 government officials.
Ms. Men Sam An addressed a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who are always in love All nations will help solve all kinds of problems everywhere in Cambodia.
Ms. Men Sam An stated that Samdech Techo has set out a social protection policy to facilitate and solve the difficulties of workers, such as raising salaries, providing benefits to workers during childbirth, the establishment of the National Social Security Fund. Reducing the price of water, electricity and raising the salaries of all types of civil servants and the armed forces.
She added that the Prime Minister also considered the salaries of factory workers who were stuck and did not work during the supply of raw materials when the COVID-19 Coronavirus invaded. The government pays 20 percent, while factory owners pay 40 percent.
Ms. Men Sam An called on people to protect themselves, regular hygiene is the best option to get rid of all kinds of diseases, including COVID-19. We must work together to maintain peace and development by maintaining security, order, strengthening safe villages and communes at the local level, and working together to preserve the achievements of the Royal Government that have been provided for the benefit of future generations. More.
At the same time, she also reminded the Svay Rieng Provincial Health Department to continue to pay more attention to providing health education services, disease prevention and health services to local people in their respective jurisdictions. Time and efficiency.
