(Phnom Penh): The daughter of a police officer working in the Technical and Scientific Police Department of the Ministry of Interior, who was arrested by the police on suspicion of violence against a girl student at Chumpouvorn School, raised ten fingers to appeal to the court and the Ministry's leadership. Justice asked for his father's release, claiming that his father had not beaten him, only arrested and detained the children.
Mr. Chhum Saveth is a widow with two children and a police officer working in the Police Technical and Scientific Department of the Ministry of Interior. Detained.
At that time, he only arrested and detained the group of children, did not use any violence, but later called the school police to bring to the police station.
Finally, she asked the authorities to release her father, who was innocent, and came back to take care of her and her sister to give them warmth as before, because she was the only father who did not have a mother like children. No more. The two sisters raised ten fingers and begged the leaders of the Ministry of Justice and the court to help her father return home to give them warmth.
The incident happened on March 3, 2020, when the youngest daughter called her father for help during a school dispute. He immediately arrested and detained the group of children, but was accused by the students of beating other schoolgirls until the local police arrested and sent them to court.
Some female students were also injured in the incident.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kun Nhim, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise, confirmed that the revenue collection of the General Department of Customs has decreased slightly in February 2020 due to Kovid 19.
In a press conference held by the Royal Government Spokesperson on the morning of March 5, 2020 on the progress and further direction of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Mr. Kun Nhim also claimed that the impact on customs revenue for February. Caused by three other factors as well.
According to figures released by Kun Nhim, customs revenue in January collected more than $ 250 million more than planned, but for February collected $ 235 million, less than planned.
The top sources of revenue in 2019 were vehicles and machinery, earning $ 1,693.7 million, an increase of nearly 50%; The dollar grew by nearly 14 percent and commodities, including construction materials, collected $ 984 million, an increase of about 14 percent.
3,560 pigs from Kampong Thom farm were screened before being distributed in the domestic market
(Kampong Thom): In order to improve the well-being of the people, the Production and Veterinary Office of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampong Thom Province inspected pigs at pig farms before distributing these pigs for distribution. Resale in markets across the country.
In fact, on March 4, 2020, Mr. Tan Meng Chhang, Director of Production and Veterinary Office of Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Agriculture, led a working group in cooperation with CP Company to inspect Mr. Ngy Kim Pov's pig farm in Okorki village, Chreab commune, Santuk district. There are 6 pig farms with 3,560 pigs.
"The inspections found that all 3,560 pigs were healthy and an animal health assessment was conducted so that farm owners could apply to the province's one-stop shop before being transported to the market," he said. .
At the same time, Mr. Tan Meng Chhang praised Mr. Ngy Kim Pov's farm for taking into account the well-being of the people and promoting more pig farming to supply the local market, reducing imports from abroad on the advice of Samdech Techo Hun The Prime Minister of Cambodia. A young man who shared pornographic images and videos on the Telegram social network was arrested by the Anti-Technology Crime Department.
(Phnom Penh): Under the strict order of General Santibandit Neth Savoeun, the National Police Commissioner, the Police Force of the Department of Technology Crimes, in cooperation with the forces of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, arrested a young man who posted and shared pornographic pictures and videos. Telegram social network.
The Prime Minister stated that such live leads to sexual abuse of women in today's society and can lead to rape cases. Samdech Techo Hun Sen's order was made at a recent meeting of the National Council for Women.
