Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court Holds a Meeting to Summarize 2019 Work Results and Work Orientation for 2020
(Phnom Penh): Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court held a meeting to review the work results of 2019 and work direction for 2020 on March 3, 2019, which was composed of the President of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court, Mr. Vice President. Judges, prosecutors, deputy prosecutors, bailiffs, clerks and clerks, secretaries, deputy secretaries, secretaries and all contracted officials of the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court.
This is the annual meeting that shows the work results for the whole year 2019 of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court, Prosecutor of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court, Bailiffs of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court and Secretariat of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court, as well as work directions for 2020 of each institution.
Mr. Sok Kalyan, President of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court, stated that the results of the work in 2019, the judge handled criminal investigations, criminal cases, civil cases (cases of lawsuits, defense cases, cases). Civil non-litigation) and a total of 2,178 cases of forced enforcement.
Thus, in 2019, a judge handled a total of 217 cases, and this number is not uncommon compared to the results of the judges' annual working days.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court has set the work direction for 2020 in response to the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategic Policy, the third phase, related to legal and judicial reform, such as increasing and strengthening cooperation with relevant institutions to be effective. Work for the common goal: "Together for justice" and "Love justice is love for peace" and so on.
(Kampong Chhnang): The project to improve National Road No. 5 from Prek Kdam to Thla Mam, Pursat Province, with a total length of 135.24 km, has completed 15% of the construction and as of March 2020, this project is scheduled to be completed. In March 2022 to facilitate freight traffic and ensure the safety of people's travel.
Mr. Misunori Misunisi said that the scope of the project focused on the improvement of National Road (from km 31 + 370 to km 171 + 200, with a length of 117.97 km), widening two lanes. To 4 lanes, the park divides the road into 3 meters with steel dividers dividing the road and many other safety equipment. The rural part is usually 23 meters wide and the urban part is 28 meters wide.
The project has built 2 new bridges, renovated 13 old bridges and replaced 18 old bridges, and built 115 box drains and 212 round drains by installing LED light poles at major intersections and towns. Also.
Dun Vandy Reagan, project manager for the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, said the National Road 5 improvement project would develop into an ASEAN highway, part of the Southern Economic Corridor and walkway. An important role in linking local activities.
He said that the project to improve National Road No. 5, Prek Kdam Thla Mam, the southern part, which connects Phnom Penh to the Thai border by improving the condition of this road, will build a new bypass in Udong and Kampong Chhnang to reduce the impact and Facilitate traffic without congestion. Especially to contribute to the growth of the economy in Cambodia and development, as well as attract international tourists.
On this occasion, Mr. Dun Vandy Reagan requested that some crooks always steal materials at the construction site, please stop stealing activities because the construction of this road to allow people to use. So far, he said, about 2,000 cones have been stolen from the side of the road around the construction site, with a budget of about 20,000 dollars.
Please note that the project to improve National Road No. 5 from Prek Kdam Thla Mam, Pursat, southern part, with a total length of 135.24 km, was built in April 2018 and will be completed in April 2022 in collaboration with Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA).
