Senior Minister Kun Kim: Disaster management is not just for the Disaster Management Committee, it is for inter-sectoral and multi-sectoral work.
(Battambang): Disaster management is not just for the Disaster Management Committee, but it is a multi-sectoral and multi-sectoral work that requires inter-ministerial-institutional coordination at all levels. This is what Senior Minister Kun Kim said at a meeting to review the results of disaster management and work of the Cambodian Veterans Association in 2019 and the work direction for 2020 in Battambang province on the afternoon of March 4.
General Kun Kim outlined some important tasks as follows:
A: Disaster management:
1: Strengthen the capacity of sub-national disaster management committees
2: Hold information on the occurrence of disasters and timely dissemination to the people to avoid and reduce damage in advance
3: Increase water use management for both agricultural work and for future use
4: Partners and development partners, please cooperate with the Disaster Management Committee at all levels, and from next year there will be a forum to meet with cooperation partners.
5: Must continue to learn from the work experience of the past year, because obviously the results have significantly reduced the impact of both floods and droughts, we were well prepared last year.
B: For the work of the Veterans Association:
1: Meet local veterans and take measures to help those in need and continue to build houses for poor members
2: Take care of the health of the veterans at night because they are old and the commune chief and postmaster must help send him to the hospital on time.
3. It is necessary to mobilize philanthropists to help veterans.
4: To manage the land given by the state to the Veterans Association, prepare to clear and prepare to build houses for the homeless.
