According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Siem Reap tour guide expresses satisfaction and is ready to serve local guests
(Siem Reap): According to Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen, who encouraged tour guides in Siem Reap to be ready to serve guides to local tourists once again, although the service to international guests is a bit better. The tour guide in Siem Reap has already expressed his satisfaction and is ready to serve local guests.
The congratulations of the Head of Government were made during a meeting with Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, who led a special working group of the Ministry of Tourism to introduce the measures of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Tourism. National tourism sector during the Covid-19 crisis to staff, tour operators and tour guides in Siem Reap on the evening of March 2, 2020.
Recently, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, also mentioned the Royal Government's measures several times around the promotion of tourism during the Covid-19 crisis, in which Samdech Techo also spoke. Let tour guides in Siem Reap be ready to serve guides to local tourists and Cambodians visiting Siem Reap, while international tourists visiting Cambodia continue to decline.
On that occasion, he said that due to the Covid-19 crisis, trade wars and other problems caused by external factors, Cambodia has not been able to receive international tourists as expected in 2020. The Ministry of Tourism estimates that the number of international tourists will drop by about 1 million, while Thailand estimates that the country will face a drop of about 6 million international tourists.
The Minister continued that if the relevant parties do not help each other to implement the measures of the Royal Government and the measures of the Ministry of Tourism to solve the obstacles ahead, the number of tourists in Cambodia will decrease by about 40%, but if the relevant parties join together to overcome This barrier has reduced the number of tourists from only 10% to 15%.
According to Minister Thong Khon, although Cambodia is facing these crises, by 2025, the number of tourists in Cambodia will increase by about 25%, according to the forecast.
Unfortunately, at the end of 2019 until the beginning of 2020, the world experienced the new Covid-19 crisis, which caused the global tourism sector to run a deficit, in which Cambodia could not escape this problem. The Royal Government of Cambodia and the Ministry of Tourism have put in place measures to encourage more domestic tourism movements.
