During the closing ceremony of the Ministry of Health on the afternoon of March 4, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that although all the workers were temporarily suspended, they still received 60% of their salaries. Of that, factory owners provide 40 percent and the state provides 20 percent.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "As of yesterday, the workers who had been asked to suspend about 20 factories had lost more than 18,000 workers and three hotels in Siem Reap with nearly 300 workers." "People who, apart from the factory owners, give 40 percent, the state has to give 20 percent."
Please be informed that Mr. Heng Sour, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, said that during March 2020, about 200 factories in Phnom Penh faced closure due to lack of imported raw materials. From China due to Covid-19 problem. Of the 200 factories facing this, about 160,000 workers could be laid off.
In order to immediately address all these challenges, the Royal Government of Cambodia has used all means to cooperate with the Chinese side as a supplier of raw materials, so that the Chinese government prioritizes the supply to Cambodia, which creates the conditions for This shortage of raw materials is short-lived. This is according to Mr. Heng Sour.
Heng Sour pointed out that the disruption of the production chain in China is really affecting the production chain in the whole world, especially in Asia. He said that even Japan and Korea have suspended some of their production lines due to lack of raw materials or semi-finished products, which are always accepted from China.
