The decision to reduce spending by ministries and institutions up to half of the annual expenditure was made by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to help the Cambodian economy affected by Covid-19.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the reduction of spending in ministries and state institutions allows the state to collect about $ 400 million back.
The announcement of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's firm decision was made on the afternoon of March 4, 2020, on the occasion of the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of the old year 2019 and the work direction of the new year 2020 of the Ministry of Health in Sokha Hotel.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also stated that the cost of salaries for civil servants has not been reduced, which is related to the current monthly expenses of Cambodia to spend more than $ 400 million.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister stated that some unnecessary expenses have been reduced to save money to help the national economy, which has prepared a budget to help the health sector and some other sectors that face urgent problems. At the same time, Samdech Techo will wait to see which ministers implement this economical method, do not wait for the Prime Minister to decide.
Separately, for the investment project of the Royal Government which has not yet opened the construction site, Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to suspend the construction site until the Covid-19 disease is completed, except for the foreign-funded construction site with the Cambodian contribution. To have the site open.
Please be informed that the 2020 budget law, the total expenditure of the state budget or the total expenditure of the national budget is planned to be about 8,223 million USD, of which the current expenditure of the state budget is about 4.888 million USD and 2: the expenditure of the state budget is about 3.335 million USD. Dollars.
