Key Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Occasion of Closing the Meeting of the Ministry of Health
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Wednesday, March 4, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the closing ceremony of the 2019 Annual Meeting. And set the work direction for the New Year 2020 of the Ministry of Health. The closing ceremony was held at Sokha Hotel.
The following are the main remarks made by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of closing the meeting to review the work and raise the work direction of the Ministry of Health:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen commends leaders, civil servants and health workers across the country who have worked hard to implement the Royal Government's health policies and programs and achieved proud results, especially the results of the provision of health education and prevention services. Illness, medical examination and health care for the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the health sector has been making significant progress in improving the health status of the people with the development of the social health screening system in line with the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategic Goals at all stages.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that all capital-provincial administrations must cooperate with ministries, institutions and stakeholders to reorganize the institutional structure, roles and functions of health units at the sub-national level and to maintain the operation of the Capital Health Units. Province as usual. In particular, there should be no disruption to the health care delivery process that affects people's access to health services.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Ministry of Health must review, adjust and define the roles and functions of ministries and health units under the national level in order to implement transparently and accountably between the national and sub-national levels with a high sense of responsibility. .
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Capital-Provincial Administration must make efforts to mobilize financial support, materials and techniques from various institutions and stakeholders, using the discretionary resources of the Capital-Provincial Administration to provide health services to local people in their respective jurisdictions. Body on time and efficiently.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that currently the private health sector in Cambodia has been growing remarkably fast, especially the provision of examination and treatment services.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government encourages the establishment of partnerships between the public health sector and private health services, especially the provision of health services to the people in a timely and effective manner.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminds the Ministry of Health and Sub-National Administration to continue to strengthen the implementation of health laws and regulations through existing mechanisms at the national and sub-national levels or new mechanisms to ensure that private health services provide health services. Accurate in accordance with the standards, technical competencies, quality standards and professional ethics.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urges doctors, health workers to continue to raise awareness about the use of new medical technologies in the diagnosis and treatment of high-tech medical devices, new generation drugs and new therapies. Help doctors diagnose, treat, and care for patients more accurately and effectively.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the choice of fear is not a good choice, but the courageous choice to know how to urinate, regular hygiene is the best option, and the urgency of all kinds of diseases.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that all institutions reduce spending by 50 percent, except for three: the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the Office of the Council of Ministers, the Ministry of Commerce reduced by 25 percent.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the reduction of expenditures in the ministries and state institutions made the state collect $ 400 million back.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech will see which ministers start implementing this plan.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that more than 18,000 workers lost their jobs after some factories asked to suspend work.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that by now the woman who is said to be sick has arrived home and no longer has health problems. Samdech Techo stated that this is a clear demonstration for the quality of Cambodia's health and also to provide justice to Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen raises the idea not to shake hands to welcome when meeting to prevent Kovit 19. Samdech Techo confirmed that the tradition of Khmer people to greet each other is to say hello.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen tells bodyguards not to prevent people from welcoming Samdech during a road inauguration in Pursat next week.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen encourages the use of krama to prevent Kovit 19.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the people for not choosing fear and discrimination.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces that in 2020, Angkor Sankranti will be re-organized.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on people to visit the River Festival in Battambang next weekend.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen raises the idea of considering various sponsorships in case of people with coronary heart disease.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Kovit disease is attacking more developed countries than less developed ones.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that despite the need to reduce costs, the increase in salaries and support for armed forces officers during the New Year and Pchum Ben will not be canceled.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen to prevent people from burning forests, chasing rabbits, finding turtles and throwing wildfires, leading to forest fires.
