(Phnom Penh): After a strong reaction from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the performance of the Royal Ballet in Singapore, which is different from the traditional Khmer culture and insults to the royal family, on March 4, 2020, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts Has issued a new press release instructing those who bring the Royal Ballet or Khmer Classical Dance to perform internationally must first ask permission.
The Ministry of Culture stated, "The Ministry would like to recommend the organizations, associations, arts groups that will organize the Royal Ballet or Khmer traditional dance to perform internationally abroad, please cooperate closely with the Ministry by providing reports. A summary of the vision, purpose, place or environment in which the Royal Ballet or the Khmer Classical Dance is performed to avoid inappropriate images affecting the value of art and national honor.
Please be informed that during the celebration of National Cultural Day under the theme "Youth for National Culture" at the Koh Pich Exhibition and Convention Center on the afternoon of March 3, 2020, Samdech Techo reacted strongly to the performance of the Royal Ballet of Cambodia. In Singapore, which violates the traditional Khmer culture.
This reaction came after Samdech received a video posted on Facebook regarding the Royal Ballet performance organized by a Malaysian, a Singaporean, in collaboration with some Cambodians.
