Foreign Ministry Releases Results of Cambodia-Bangladesh Joint Commission Meeting in Dhaka
(Phnom Penh): The first meeting of the Cambodia-Bangladesh Joint Commission was held on February 27, 2020 in Dhaka, Bangladesh. The meeting was co-chaired by Ms. Ath Sophea, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, and Mr. M. Diza Rielam, Member of Parliament, Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of Bangladesh.
The two sides agreed to fully implement all the agreements signed between the two countries to promote bilateral cooperation and to maintain regular high-level visits and exchanges between the two countries' parliamentary friendship groups. Both.
Both sides agreed that naming the streets in a prominent area in Dhaka and in Phnom Penh in the name of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King of Cambodia, and in the name of the Father of Bangladesh, Bangladesh Bandu Sek Muji Buraman has significant significance for further strengthening ties between Cambodia and Bangladesh.
