This afternoon, Samdech Techo Hun Sen closed the meeting to review the work of the old year and raise the work direction of the new year of the Ministry of Health
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Wednesday, March 4, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the closing ceremony of the 2019 Annual Meeting. And set the work direction for the New Year 2020 of the Ministry of Health. The closing ceremony was held at Sokha Hotel.
Health work is a priority and necessary work of the Royal Government of Cambodia to improve the well-being of the people. Poor health will also affect the nation's economy and development.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, has paid the highest attention to the health sector since the liberation of the country from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot. In order to improve the health sector, the Royal Government has dropped the highest national budget into the health sector on its annual recurrent expenditures. In 2020, more than $ 400 million of the national budget will be released for use in the health sector.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also chaired the closing of the annual meeting of the Ministry of Health to take this opportunity to provide some recommendations and advice to doctors in order to improve the health system of Cambodia.
Although Cambodia's health sector is currently not as strong as in neighboring countries and there are still some challenges, it is seen that the sector is much better than in the past of Cambodia. Doctors rely on cents for scratching the air. Currently, the Royal Government has deployed health centers to all communes throughout the country to ensure the rescue and improve the well-being of the people.
Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, said that the one-and-a-half-day meeting reviewed the report on the achievements and progress of the health sector in 2019 and discussed and exchanged views on key topics to assess progress, identify challenges and opportunities to address These challenges aim to improve the provision of health services and strengthen the health system by 2020 and beyond.
The Minister of Health also said that the meeting noted the level of satisfaction of patients who came to use referral hospitals at all levels and at health centers nationwide more than 80% in the fourth quarter of 2019 . This is a good sign of the results of the efforts of health workers in all fields, especially doctors, to improve the quality of management and quality of health services.
According to the Minister, the growth of the use of health services is in line with the investment of resources to expand service coverage and improve service quality. The supply of medicines and medical equipment is tailored to the basic needs.
In 2019, 38.5% of the total Cambodian population was covered by the Equity Fund and the Social Security Social Security System. The cash support program for pregnant women and children under two years of age, which started on June 1, 2019, is an effective investment by the Royal Government to improve the health of women and children in poor families.
According to the Minister, the meeting also noted that along with the progress made in the health sector, there are still some major challenges, including: the trend towards a society with more elderly people and the burden of non-communicable diseases. Chronic illness, the emergence of new infectious diseases and the resurgence of existing infectious diseases have increased the demand for health care services, which requires the health system to strengthen its ability to respond effectively.
