TIKA was established in 1992 with the aim of providing technical assistance to developing countries in the fields of economy, trade, culture, technology, education and social development through the development of projects and programs.
TIKA is headquartered in 60 countries, cooperating in more than 150 countries, with a focus on technical cooperation for the development of human resource institutions. TIKA also finances infrastructure projects such as irrigation, sanitation and transportation projects, as well as the construction and renovation of schools, hospitals, architecture and humanitarian assistance.
Minister of Commerce Visits Kampot Pepper Plantation of La Plantation
