Preah Vihear Provincial Administration inspected the location of the pile of wood that the authorities cracked down on and instructed to store and measure properly
(Preah Vihear): At noon on March 4, 2020, Mr. Ko Sum Bunsoeut, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province, on behalf of Mr. Prak Sovann, Provincial Governor, led the relevant officials to inspect the location where the authorities cracked down on an illegal timber warehouse. In Bos village, Promeru commune, Tbeng Meanchey district, Preah Vihear province.
Mr. Kor Sum Bunsoeut told Fresh News Agency that the actual visit to the location of the pile of wood that the authorities cracked down on was in order to encourage the authorities who worked hard to crack down and also want to know the exact number of The number of trees, because there is some information that the authorities have cracked up to 200 to 300 cubic meters. When he actually inspected, he saw that the pile of wood that was suppressed was only about 20 to 25 cubic meters.
The Deputy Governor instructed the authorities to continue to work hard to crack down on this natural resource crime by following the orders and instructions of General Sao Sokha, Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Chairman of the Committee. National Commission for the Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes and Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province and Chairman of the Provincial Unity Command, without making any exceptions.
Mr. Kor Sum Bunsoeut also evaluated and thanked Brigadier General Kang Sao Kun, Commander of the Preah Vihear Provincial Gendarmerie, for leading the force in cooperation with Forestry Administration officials to crack down on the illegal pile of wood. At the same time, he also instructed the Forestry Administration to transport the wood to store and measure properly.
(Kampong Thom): On March 4, 2020, Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, and his wife presided over the celebration of the 109th Anniversary of the International Women's Day, March 8, 2020 under the theme "Peace, Promoting Equality". Gender ”with the participation of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development, the Deputy Director of the Department around the province, the commander of the three forces and the mayor / district.
On that occasion, Mrs. Lum Kuntheary, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province and President of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development, read a message from Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia in Freedom, Dignity and Happiness under the theme "Peace Promoting Gender Equality ”to the ceremony.
Mr. Sok Lou said that the celebration of International Women's Day on March 8 every year aims to commemorate the courage and efforts of women ancestors around the world for the rights, freedom and equal role of men and women in society.
More importantly, this day provides an opportunity for all of us today to reflect and celebrate the achievements made in promoting women's participation in all aspects of society, including economic, social, cultural and political.
On that occasion, he stated that on behalf of the leadership, I would like to support the theme "Peace, Promoting Gender Equality", highlighting the values of peace and thanks to the peace that the Royal Government of Cambodia has been maintaining peace. Long live the future.
In addition, under the distinguished leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Cambodia has strengthened cooperation in maintaining world peace and stability and cooperating with neighboring countries to build the region. The border is an area of peace, friendship, cooperation and development.
Before concluding, Mr. Sok Lou thanked the Department of Women's Affairs for organizing this event and commended the Women's Association for Peace and Development of all relevant institutions that have contributed to support humanitarian work, capacity building, rights, status, role, welfare. Women and the prevention of violence and the peaceful settlement of disputes.
Taking this opportunity, Mr. Sok Lou presented flowers as a souvenir to the sisters who participated in the 109th anniversary of the International Women's Day on March 8, 2020 in happiness.
