Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced that in his role as Prime Minister, he could not accept such a royal dance performance in Singapore, with Apsara dancing behind a Singaporean Malaysian, Om Am. "What is more serious is that this person is a Malaysian and has just become a Singaporean citizen, and has seriously attacked the Royal Palace," he said.
The reaction took place during the celebration of the National Cultural Day under the theme "Youth for National Culture" at the Koh Pich Exhibition and Convention Center on the afternoon of March 3, 2020, after Samdech received a video posted on Facebook related to Royal Ballet performance organized by a Malaysian, a Singaporean in collaboration with some Cambodians.
"If you pray for the Kingdom of Cambodia, you must find a suitable place and it is not possible for Cambodian dancers to sit and dance behind the person who is the teacher," he said.
However, for this issue, Samdech stated that this is not a conflict between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Singapore, it is focused only on this Malaysian-Singaporean, with the conspiracy with some Cambodian individuals.
