The following are the main remarks made by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the National Cultural Day on March 3:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen, may this day remain immortal in the hearts of all Cambodians with a patriotic conscience and a spirit of love for national art and culture.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen, May there be good internal unity and cooperation to help each other among the young people of Cambodia, who are the successors of the shift with a high sense of responsibility, to preserve the cultural heritage of Cambodia to be stable and lasting. Forever.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised and appreciated the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, the Inter-Ministerial Commission, as well as all working groups that have worked hard and actively cooperated to organize national cultural events every year with new innovations. Highlight the works of Khmer ancestors who have left a rich cultural work, which is an invaluable heritage for future generations.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the motto "Thank you for peace" and development in all areas with high economic growth in the last two decades makes the cultural sector proudly develop rapidly. .
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the celebration of the National Cultural Day every year for the past 20 years reflects the glorious civilization of the Khmer capital in the Angkorian era.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the celebration and remembrance of the Khmer ancestors in the National Culture Day is a mechanism to promote the transfer of knowledge and technical skills in arts and culture, cultivate courage, conscience, love of national art and culture to all compatriots.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommends nine recommendations to the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and relevant stakeholders to continue the work of preserving and developing the tangible and intangible culture in a transparent manner. The nine recommendations include:
Fourth, I would like to support the cooperation of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and the Ministry of Information, which has made the Cambodian film industry has been growing remarkably by setting a golden hour for the broadcast of Khmer films. In the past. At the same time, local authorities at all levels must cooperate to facilitate the provision of locations in their territories to facilitate the process of filming and production of all kinds of films.
Fifth, to continue to cooperate with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, to inspire the activities of all Cambodian embassies and consulates abroad, to organize regular Khmer cultural events every year to promote national culture with the strengthening of cultural policy, and to inspire Let the Cambodian community abroad participate in organizing the National Cultural Day program in a solemn and comprehensive manner.
Sixth, to work closely with local authorities at all levels to effectively preserve the traditions, customs and places of worship of indigenous peoples as part of our nation's long-standing culture. .
Ninth: I would like to express my appreciation for the participation of some philanthropists such as Lok Chumteav, Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An, Lok Chumteav Mao Malay, Ke Kim Yan, Lok Chumteav Sieng Chanheng and Lok Chumteav Suy Siphan, as well as many other philanthropists who have contributed their own financial resources. With the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts to preserve some ancient temples and temples in the past.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen Requests Artists and Writers to Immediately Stop All Forms of Serious Violations of the Law on Copyright and Related Rights by Taking Songs, Films, Pictures and Literary Works Literary and other cultural works, both inherited and non-inherited, are reproduced without the permission of the copyright holder or the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts.
