Malaysian Ambassador vows to cooperate with Cambodia in mine action
The Ambassador of Malaysia expressed his appreciation for the relations between Cambodia and Malaysia and expressed his appreciation and congratulations for Cambodia's strong progress.
At the same time, the Ambassador also expressed his congratulations to the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister for its success in the field of mine action by clearing humanitarian mines to provide safe land to the people and Reducing the risk of landmines and explosive remnants of war.
At the same time, the Ambassador expressed his commitment to cooperate with Cambodia in the field of mine action, and the Ambassador will strive to mobilize resources from the Royal Government and Malaysian civil society to contribute to the relief of people with disabilities due to landmines and Explosive remnants of war.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Senior Minister expressed his pleasure and deep gratitude for Malaysia's commitment to cooperate with Cambodia in the field of mine action. The Mine Authority will continue to work closely with the Malaysian Embassy in Cambodia.
