The Royal Government sets three main goals to modernize Cambodia's industry from labor-intensive to industrial-based
(Phnom Penh): The Economic and Financial Policy Committee, a staff of the Royal Government of Cambodia, has set out a vision to promote and modernize Cambodia's industry from labor-intensive to industry-based by 2025, setting three main goals.
The three main goals are:
Goal 3: Strengthen the management and development mechanism of small and medium enterprises by promoting official registration from 80% to 90% by 2025, in which 50% to 70% have good corporate governance with a list Accurate accounting and balance sheet.
The "Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025" launched by the Royal Government of Cambodia is a new economic growth strategy of Cambodia, focusing on the reform of economic structure through economic diversification, strengthening Competing and improving the productivity and skills of the Cambodian workforce.
The implementation of the Industrial Development Policy in 2017 and 2018 has made significant progress based on the achievement of the above three goals and four measures, including:
In addition, in order to strengthen the work efficiency and proactive thinking, the Council for the Development of Cambodia, in collaboration with development partners and relevant ministries and institutions, will prepare a conceptual framework for monitoring and evaluation of the mid-term, which is scheduled to take place in the first half of 2021.
This framework will provide guidance for the preparation of a mid-term progress report that can reflect gaps in achievement and expectations, and in particular provide good lessons and experiences as input for adjusting certain methods and measures to Achieve better results in the last half of the term.
(Phnom Penh): A shocking incident occurred when a police officer from the Ministry of Interior was told by his daughter that he had a fight with a student at the same school, and suddenly arrived at the school and assaulted two female students at Chompouvorn School caused injuries and beat the scouts who came to stop more.
After causing trouble, the police officer, along with his eldest daughter, who went to beat the two students, was also arrested by the Chaom Chao police station. The incident happened at 8:50 AM on March 3, 2020 in Hun Sen Chumpouvorn High School in Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The second female student, P.P., also described that the man, a police officer, mistakenly thought that she was an ally of S.J. In fact, she had never had an argument or knew his daughter. Prior to the incident, she and two friends were carrying irrigation equipment to the storage area when the police officer and her daughter arrived and did not ask for anything. Only once.
After the arrest of the 3rd Chao Chao Police Station, the police officer denied that he had beaten the two female students and did not know who beat them, but when the chaos broke, he entered. To restrain only.
He also did not know the victim and did not touch or hit her. However, the police have now decided to detain the man along with another daughter, P.P., while the daughter, P.P., has not been arrested. His girlfriend beat the two female students and injured them.
