(Phnom Penh): A handful of people have been using social media to distort the truth about the case of Kovid-19 virus with the intention of sabotaging and destroying the well-being of the Cambodian people as they arrive across the country. At present, no one has been born or infected with the virus.
Deliberate sabotage for political gain or to destroy the well-being of the people throughout the country has been retaliated against by Phnom Penh Governor Khuon Sreng, requesting health officials, schools, educational institutions, local authorities and stakeholders to Disseminate factual information Respond to the situation that in its locality control no one is born or infected with this virus yet, do not be afraid without consideration.
Mr. Khuong Sreng's proposal was made on the evening of March 2, 2020 at the closing ceremony of the Phnom Penh High School Championship for the 2019-2020 academic year at Chea Sim High School in Boeung Keng Kang. He stressed that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has no reason to hide the truth of Kovid 19 while the world is very concerned.
He added that the Royal Government, through the Ministry of Health, has also introduced preventive measures, such as washing hands frequently with soap or alcohol before eating or touching the nose. On the other hand, if you have the flu, wear a mask to prevent it from spreading to others around you.
He also urged schools in the capital to continue to pay attention to improving the school environment, food safety and establish adequate hand washing facilities with soap or alcohol to encourage students to be careful not to eat. Unhygienic food, do not drink any drink that is too sweet, especially to spread the announcement of the Ministry of Health to students and parents to know to participate in the protection.
In connection with this ceremony, Mr. Khuong Sreng stated that the vision of building a Cambodian society with peace, political stability, security and social order, sustainable development and equity requires people to have high knowledge, deep culture, decent living and living in harmony. Both in a national society and a sustainable family society.
Mr. Khuong Sreng also called on students and athletes to pay more attention to training better in knowledge, wisdom, spirit, cooperation and health, especially to continue to win for the school and the whole country in the future.
Morocco, France invite Cambodia to French-speaking regional peacekeeping conference in April
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Morocco and the Government of France have written a joint letter inviting the Royal Government of Cambodia to attend a conference on peacekeeping in the French-speaking region to be held in April 2020. .
"The main purpose of the meeting was for the ambassador to deliver the invitation letter of the visiting Moroccan foreign minister," said Ny Sam Ol, director general of the EU, Africa and the Middle East. "Together with the French Foreign Minister, we invite Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon to attend a French-speaking regional peacekeeping conference."
"This is a forum that Morocco, as well as France, really want the Deputy Prime Minister to share to share what Cambodia has done to contribute to peacekeeping in the French-speaking region," said Ny Sam Ol. As in the whole world. "The deputy prime minister will also meet with the Moroccan foreign minister to discuss bilateral issues on regional as well as international issues."
During the meeting, the ambassador also said that Morocco appreciates Cambodia's policy of harmonizing religious harmony because Morocco is 90 percent Muslim. He said that there was a lot of harmony in Cambodia and suggested that the model that Cambodia used to do should be presented at the conference as well.
Separately, Deputy Prime Minister Prabhukhon responded by thanking Morocco and France for the invitation. He said that he was happy to participate in the program, but had to wait for the final decision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The Deputy Prime Minister also said that Cambodia's peacekeeping force from 2006 to the present has sent about 6,500 people to nine countries. Cambodia has sent a significant number of women compared to other ASEAN countries.
The head of the diplomatic corps said that among ASEAN countries, Cambodia is the country that sends the most troops to keep the peace, ranking third and women second. He added that if he was allowed to attend the conference, he would meet with the Moroccan foreign minister and discuss various issues and bilateral relations to boost cooperation as well as promote free trade and tourism. Culture and education.
However, in the event that it is necessary to travel abroad, government employees must strictly adhere to the measures to prevent and control the spread of the disease imposed by the host country, and upon return must comply with the measures imposed. By the Lao Health Authority. Lao authorities have urged the public to be wary of fake information about COVID-19 and to trust only official and reliable sources.
To date, no cases of COVID-19 infection have been reported in Laos, while neighboring countries such as Thailand, Cambodia and Vietnam all have cases, but one case in Cambodia and 16 cases in Vietnam have been cured. In Thailand, there were 43 cases, of which 31 were cured, 11 were still in hospital and one died.
Are there any tourism events in Siem Reap that tourists can enjoy in 2020?
(Siem Reap): In order to promote the growth of tourism to Siem Reap and to encourage more stays in the province, the Royal Government of Cambodia has set up national, regional and international meetings and cultural and artistic tourism events. Religion, sports, food in Siem Reap-Angkor from the beginning of the year until the end of 2020 and in the years to come.
These events were presented at a meeting to disseminate measures of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Tourism to promote national tourism during the Covid-19 crisis to employees, tour operators and tour guides in Siem Reap on the 2nd. March 2020 at the Regency Angkor Hotel under the chairmanship of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism.
Those meetings and events include:
The World Tourism Organization (UNTWO) Senior Officials Training Program for Asia-Pacific, which will be organized from April 29 to May 2 by the Ministry of Tourism.
* Khmer New Year and the upcoming "Siem Reap Sankranti" event will be held from 13-16 April by the Siem Reap Provincial Administration in collaboration with the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, APSARA Authority and the Ministry of Tourism. .
* Regional Meeting on the ASEAN Mechanism for the Evaluation of Previous Studies, to be Held May 18-19 by the Ministry of Tourism.
* Regional Meeting on Updating ASEAN Tourism Community Standards to be Held from 23-24 June by the Ministry of Tourism.
* The 2nd International Conference on Food Tourism, which will be held from 14-17 July by the Ministry of Tourism.
* The second "Sunrise at the Top of Angkor Wat" event will be held on September 20-23 by the Ministry of Tourism in collaboration with the Apsara Authority and the Siem Reap Provincial Administration.
* Royal Water Festival, Floating Lanterns and Moon Worship, which will be held at the end of November by the Siem Reap Provincial Administration.
