(Preah Sihanouk): On the afternoon of March 3, 2020, a delegation of the Senate led by Mr. Kong Sarach, Chairman of the Ninth Committee of the Senate, led a working group to inspect the progress of the restoration of five major streams in Sihanoukville. Encourage and appreciate the efforts of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport in rehabilitating canals in Sihanoukville.
Please be informed that as of March 2020, the rehabilitation of 5 major streams in Sihanoukville with a length of 29,791 meters has been restored, with a length of 16,670 meters, equivalent to 55.96%, while the remaining length of the Ministry And cooperate with local authorities to expedite the restoration work before the rainy season arrives.
Accelerating the restoration of some important streams in Sihanoukville aims to prevent and prevent flooding due to the upcoming rainy season, as well as to prepare a canal system in the city. This should be attractive and hygienic as planned.
Mr. Ouk Savuth and his family brought $ 20,000 after the funeral of his mother to the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): $ 20,000 as a suffix from the 7-day and 100-day anniversary ceremony dedicated to Kosal Buoy Tong, the mother of Mr. Ouk Savuth, Prosecutor General of the Court of Appeal who passed away. To the next world, on Wednesday, January 29, 2020, Mr. Ouk Savuth and Ms. Try Eng handed over to the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia on Tuesday afternoon, March 3, 2020.
The funds were handed over to Dr. John Narith, Director of the Secretariat of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia, and in the presence of Professor Kisanti, Director of Kantha Bopha Hospital.
Mr. Ouk Savuth stated that the current contribution to the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia is in accordance with the words of Mrs. Buoy Tong, in order to support the operation of Kantha Bopha Hospital, which needs to spend money to help diagnose and treat patients. Cambodian children.
Prof. Dr. Kisanti, Director of Kantha Bopha Hospital, said that in one day, Kantha Bopha Hospital, both in Phnom Penh and Siem Reap, has an average of more than 3,000 Cambodian children come for outpatient consultation, of which 15% About 500 people are hospitalized due to serious illness, and the department spends about $ 42 million a year to support the hospital's operations.
Dr. John Narith expressed his deep gratitude to Mr. Ouk Savuth and his family for their generosity.
It should be noted that Kantha Bopha Hospital was established in 1992 to provide free medical examination and treatment services for Cambodian infants, children and women.
