(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Economy and Finance (MEF), this morning, March 3, 2020, chaired a meeting of the Ministry's leadership to review and discuss Two documents: 1: Draft "Sub-Decree on Public Investment Management" and 2: Draft "Detailed Action Plan for Implementing the Strategy on Public Investment Management System Reform 2019-2025".
The above two important draft documents were prepared by the technical team of the EAC. According to the strategy on the reform of the public investment management system 2019-2025, which was approved by the Royal Government on October 22, 2019 and announced to be implemented at the plenary session of the Council of Ministers on October 25, 2019. Presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Both drafts were submitted to the ECCC Internal Technical Dialogue. Several messages and technical consultative workshops with relevant ministries and institutions and development partners, as well as relevant departments / units under the Ministry of Economy and Finance, have already been discussed and decided today.
In general, the "Sub-Decree on Public Investment Management" aims to define the essential principles and systems of public investment management, including:
In particular, the "Detailed Action Plan for the Implementation of the Strategy for the Reform of the Public Investment Management System 2019-2025" is a tool to assist in monitoring, monitoring, and evaluating the progress of the implementation of the Strategy for the Reform of the Public Investment Management System 2019-2025. Quarterly and annually - 2025, which clearly defines: key performance indicators, implementation time frame, and responsible units.
