(Battambang): A pesticide warehouse in Battambang province, which smells toxic to the neighbors, was instructed by the Department of Environment on March 3, 2020, with the warehouse owner agreeing to dismantle it. Within one week from the date of signing this contract.
Mr. KOT Boran, Director of Battambang Provincial Department of Environment, said that after receiving the notification from the people, the Department of Environment sent a professional officer to inspect the warehouse location in Kampong Krabei village, Svay Por commune, Battambang city, Battambang province.
According to the director of the Battambang Provincial Department of Environment, the current situation is that the old pesticide depot has been suspended and stored since 2012. During the inspection, the professional team found the storage and storage of some old materials that have expired and have a moderate odor due to lack of intensive care.
He said that according to the owner of the warehouse that the death toll was not true.
To resolve this complaint, the Battambang Provincial Department of Environment requires the owner of the pesticide warehouse to clean and pack old pesticides and pesticides in the current warehouse in an orderly and clean manner. The warehouse owner must manage the warehouse thoroughly.
In the face of this measure, the owner of the pesticide warehouse, Long Ken, promised to clean and pack the old pesticide equipment and pesticides in the warehouse before March 15, 2020 and to ensure the management of the warehouse. Excellent quality ensures proper application of techniques to reduce odors from storage and ensures that waste is disposed of at appropriate locations.
Mr. Boran said that if the warehouse owner does not comply, the business owner will face the law.
