Delegation from the General Department of Taxation attends a seminar on the Multilateral Partnership Program organized by the Australian Tax Administration in Sydney, Australia
The workshop was attended by leaders of the tax administration and relevant officials from 14 countries, including Cambodia, Australia, Fiji, Indonesia, Japan, Kenya, Malaysia, New Zealand, Papua New Guinea, the Philippines, Singapore, Thailand, Uganda and Vietnam.
The purpose of this workshop is to discuss and share experiences and knowledge related to strengthening revenue collection management and revenue collection measures as well as future measures, focusing on key topics such as:
5: Shadow Economy: Focus on the shadow economy in Australia, study and launch effective measures and the results of the measures taken by the Australian Fiscal Administration to respond to the economy. Shadows.
Through this workshop, the delegation of the General Department of Taxation gained new experiences and ideas that the member countries have implemented, achieved good results, and exchanged experiences on a number of key points of interest and goals. The form that the General Department of Taxation has been implementing.
It is noteworthy that the implementation of the reform of the General Department of Taxation as a whole is on the right path, that is, some of the implementation directions are within the framework that developed countries have been implementing, and some of the reform directions are also in the context. With the overall attention of the member countries as well.
