Taxpayers tell taxpayers to separate the business situation from 2019 to 2020 by paying income tax correctly and on time
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation, on March 3, 2020, urged all enterprises that taxpayers should be separated from the business situation in 2019 from the internal situation. 2020 by fulfilling the income tax obligation for 2019 properly and on time.
Mr. Kong Vibol made the remarks during a seminar on "Annual Income Tax Obligations and E-Filing Business Tax Management System and New Billing Rules" at Sofitel Phnom Penh. Phukitra.
Mr. Kong Vibol mentioned the situation of the effects of Covid-19 respiratory disease on tourism, as tourists were afraid to travel and some flights were closed and the garment sector was closed due to lack of raw materials. Most of the raw materials are imported from China, as some factories in China have not yet reopened.
During today's workshop, Mr. Kong Vibol delivered a keynote address on tax administration reform and modernization, improvement and improvement of taxpayer services and solutions to the problems and concerns raised by the sector. Private with the following main content:
* Improve the rules and implementation of income tax through Proclamation No. 098 MEF.PrK dated 29 January 2020 on the income tax received from all stakeholders in order to solve concerns and problems Challenges raised by the private sector.
* The audit procedure was amended by Proclamation No. 270 MEF.PrK dated 13 March 2019, with no overlapping or overlapping audits, the period of taxable years shall be revised and deducted. Reduce the risk of serious misconduct, select an e-commerce audit based on risk and clear judgment, and reduce interest rates from 2% to 1.5%.
* Propose the private sector to reform its governance to contribute to strengthening fiscal compliance and contribute to national development, while the General Department of Taxation has been continuously reforming and modernizing the tax administration.
* Tax service agencies must continue to strengthen their professional performance, avoid negligent closure of enterprises or conspiracy to evade taxes, and the General Department of Taxation will work with the National Accounting Council (NAC) to take strict action. For tax service agents who do not comply with the profession or commit in violation of tax laws and regulations.
* Encourage enterprises to study, understand and strengthen the use of the online filing management system (E-Filing), which will be implemented from June 1, 2020 and implement the new monthly tax declaration form. For taxpayers.
* The National School of Taxation has a tax training course to contribute to strengthening tax knowledge and the practical implementation of the system, and taxpayers can register online.
Today's workshop disseminates new work progress and measures that have been put in place and planned to be implemented soon in order to strengthen the provision of services to taxpayers as well as respond to and address challenges that Mentioned by the private sector include:
* The new invoice rules clearly define the method or method of using the invoice correctly to ensure the efficiency and transparency in the collection of taxes and duties by the General Department of Taxation, Notification No. 3218, dated 06 February. 2020 on the implementation of Prakas No. 723 MEF.PrK dated 14 August 2019 to facilitate the use of this new billing rule.
* Annual Income Tax Obligations During the tax filing season from January to the end of March 2020, remind all enterprises to submit timely and accurate income tax returns in 2019 and disseminate On the content of Prakas No. 098 MEF.PrK dated 29 January 2020 on income tax.
Phnom Penh Governor Leads Officials and Authorities to Inspect the Condition of Stung Meanchey Market
(Phnom Penh): Due to the condition of Stung Meanchey Market, which is known to have been built since the 1960s, made of wood, tile, until now, it is very dilapidated, which can cause danger to traders as well as people. Go shopping in this market.
Faced with this problem, the Governor of the Board of Governors of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, this morning, March 3, 2020, led professional officers and Meanchey district authorities to inspect the situation in Stung Meanchey to repair this market.
The Governor of Phnom Penh confirmed that on behalf of the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority, as the mother and father of the people, they have always considered the well-being and hardships of the people.
"At this time, the old Stung Meanchey market, which has been built since the 1960s, is seen to be dilapidated and could endanger traders and residents while it is raining or windy," he said. Therefore, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration plans to renovate this market.
However, Mr. Khuong Sreng confirmed that the project, if the traders have objections to the renovation, the authorities will not repair. But if the people, the traders, have more support than the non-supporters, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will do a better job of keeping the default completely.
