The National Assembly accepts the draft law renaming the Ministry of Industry and five other draft laws (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): National Assembly President Samdech Heng Samrin on Tuesday morning, March 3, 2020, chaired a meeting of the Standing Committee. Of the National Assembly to review a number of draft laws proposed by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The meeting decided to accept six draft laws for review and study, including the draft law on changing the name of a Ministry of Industry, to submit to the National Assembly specialized committees for review and report to the National Assembly Standing Committee.
The six draft laws that the National Assembly has decided to study now are as follows:
1: Draft Law on the Approval of the Treaty on the Transfer of Prisoners between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam to the National Assembly's Committee on Legislation and Justice And report back to the National Assembly Standing Committee.
2. The meeting approved the handover of the draft law on the establishment of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation to the National Assembly Committee on Legislation and Justice, in collaboration with the Committee on Public Works, Transport, Telecommunications, Post, Industry, Mining, Energy, Trade, Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction of the National Assembly. And report back to the National Assembly Standing Committee.
3- Draft Law on the Approval of the Treaty on Legal Aid in the Criminal Field between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam to the Legislative and Justice Committee of the National Assembly for review in collaboration with the Foreign Affairs Committee International cooperation, propaganda and information of the National Assembly and report to the Standing Committee of the National Assembly.
5: Draft Law on the Approval of the Third Protocol on the Amendment of the ASEAN Comprehensive Investment Agreement to the Commission on Public Transport, Telecommunications, Post, Industry, Mining, Energy, Trade, Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction of the National Assembly for review in collaboration with the Agricultural Investment Planning Commission Rural development, environment and water resources of the National Assembly and report to the National Assembly Standing Committee.
6. Draft Law on the Approval of the Second Protocol on the Amendment of the ASEAN Comprehensive Investment Agreement to the Commission on Public Works, Transport, Telecommunications, Post, Industry, Mining, Energy, Trade, Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction of the National Assembly. Rural development, environment and water resources of the National Assembly and report to the National Assembly Standing Committee.
