Minister of Tourism Disseminates the Measures of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Tourism to Employees and Guides in Siem Reap Affected by the Covid-19 Crisis
(Siem Reap): The Ministry of Tourism has organized the dissemination of the seven measures of the Royal Government on tourism support solutions to employees, tour operators and tour guides in Siem Reap province, which affected their jobs and occupations during the crisis. Covid-19, which caused a drop in tourists in Cambodia as well as in the world.
Minister Thong Khon read and explained the 7 measures of the Royal Government as follows:
* First: Exemption of monthly taxes on all types of hotels and guesthouses (State in charge of substitute tax) registered with the General Department of Taxation and have business activities in Siem Reap for a period of four months from February. Until May 2020. The hotel and guesthouse business is still obliged to file a tax return and use the online system to manage value-added tax (E-VAT) every month during this tax exemption period.
* Second, do not conduct a full audit for the year 2020 for enterprises in the hotel and guesthouse sector that are registered with the General Department of Taxation and have business activities in Siem Reap.
* Fourth: Increase the efficiency of joint travel by land, sea and air, especially with neighboring countries (Bangkok-Siem Reap and Ho Chi Minh-Siem Reap), especially by bus or private car by facilitating effective settlement. Challenges that arise at border crossings and other related issues.
* Fifth, the Ministry of Tourism and relevant ministries and institutions must launch campaigns to organize activities and attractive events in Siem Reap, such as Angkor Sankranti (2020), traditional religious festivals, sports programs, concerts, film screenings and fashion shows. Origin to attract national and international tourists.
* 6th: Keep the ticket price for Angkor area the same, but add the number of days for each type of ticket, tickets for 1 day can be accessed for 2 days, tickets for 3 days can be accessed for 5 days and tickets for 7 days can be entered Watch 10 days to attract more tourists to stay in Cambodia.
Minister Thong Khon suggested that in the absence of such tourists, hotel and guesthouse owners who want to renovate their location can now implement their plans when more tourists return to their places. They are ready.
He encouraged the above stakeholders not to despair or fear losing their jobs and careers due to the Covid-19 crisis and to believe and participate in the implementation of the 7 points of the Royal Government for unity. Overcome this obstacle.
