This afternoon, Samdech Techo celebrates National Cultural Day on March 3 under the theme "Youth for National Culture"
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Tuesday, March 3, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the celebration of the 3rd National Cultural Day. 22 held under the theme "Youth for Culture".
In conjunction with the celebration of the National Cultural Day on March 3, which took place at the Koh Pich Center this afternoon, there will also be the closing ceremony of the 6th National Youth Art Festival and a solidarity dinner with artists.
"Culture" is a branch of civilization related to the training of knowledge, wisdom, history, tradition, art, science, literature ... to grow. In particular, the Committee on Culture and Fine Arts defines culture as the cultivation of knowledge, wisdom, history, and human way of life in order to adapt to the environment and social development through science or the arts.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen is a leader and a Khmer son who has taken the utmost care to preserve and promote national cultural values. Samdech Techo Prime Minister is always invited to participate in the National Cultural Day on March 3 every year.
Seeing that young people are an important driving force in preserving and promoting this national culture, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has set March 3 as the National Cultural Day under the theme "Youth for Culture" every year.
Please note that the celebration of National Cultural Day aims to encourage people, especially young people to participate more actively in the following essential points:
* Promote the consciousness and spirit to participate in the transfer and acceptance of knowledge, skills, techniques, arts and culture to promote the preservation and development of national culture as well as multiculturalism of ethnic communities in Cambodia to be stable and stable, which is the mechanism of national unity, harmony and Peace of the society.
* Increase awareness of the true value of the national culture, which is an inexhaustible resource with high energy to contribute to socio-economic development by increasing services and cultural products for trade and tourism destinations.
* Encourage participation in research and understanding to compile and preserve all documents of all kinds of cultural heritage in their locality and disseminate them widely.
* Promote the use of cultural potential to contribute to the development of the national economy and reduce poverty of the people in order to increase employment and opportunities for all people, especially young people to strive to develop quality new cultural works.
* Encourage the responsible participation of young people in the preservation and development of national culture in a sustainable and peaceful manner, regardless of political affiliation, religion or color.
