Mr. Un Chanda continued that for the registration of plots of land of the officials of the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Land Survey for the first two months of 2020, there seems to be a delay due to the number of plots collected for registration. In the past two months, more than 5,000 plots have been issued and more than 2,000 plots have been issued, which is not 10 percent of the 60,000 plots planned for 2020.
