Ministry of Women's Affairs issues important messages to promote the 109th Anniversary of International Women's Day March 8, 2020
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Women's Affairs on March 3, 2020 issued important messages to promote the 109th Anniversary of International Women's Day, March 8, 2020 under the theme "Peace, Promoting Gender Equality" .
1: Thank you Samdech Techo Prime Minister for leading Cambodia to peace 2: Thank you for peace that makes the country prosperous 3: Together to maintain peace, ensure gender equality and environment 4: Invest in gender equality for development Sustainability 5: Women together to maintain peace for national development 6: Peace, gender equality.
The Ministry of Women's Affairs is a national mechanism for promoting the status of women in Cambodia. The Ministry was established to lead, coordinate and promote efforts for gender equality and women's empowerment in Cambodia.
The Ministry of Women's Affairs acts as a catalyst for advocacy to encourage ministries, state institutions, civil society and the private sector to integrate gender equality into their policies and programs.
The Ministry of Women's Affairs is also responsible for monitoring and evaluating the effectiveness of the implementation of government policies and programs aimed at achieving gender equality. The ministry originated from the Secretariat of Women's Affairs, established in 1993.
The Secretariat was replaced by the Ministry of Women's Affairs in January 1996 and later renamed the Ministry of Women's Affairs and Veterans from 1999 to 2004. When the new government was formed in July 2004, the ministry was renamed the Ministry of Women's Affairs.
In February 1999, the Ministry of Women's Affairs and Veterans Affairs published for the first time a five-year National Strategic Plan on Gender Equality and Women's Empowerment (Rattanak I Plan 1).
Court Detains 3 of 9 Defendants in Land Arrest in Sangkat Samrong, Khan Prek Pnov, While Sar Thavy, Undersecretary of State for the Ministry of National Defense
(Phnom Penh): The Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Pich Vicheathor, on the morning of March 3, 2020, issued an order to detain three people, including: Long Dara, 35 years old, and Long Ros. Male, 40 years old, and 3: Poch Then, male, 52 years old. Six other defendants are currently being remanded in custody by the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
