(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, said on March 2, 2020 that the cultivation of reading habits is important that parents and stakeholders must pay attention to promote.
This statement was made on the occasion that Dr. Hang Chuon Naron chaired a press conference on the organization of the 5th National Power Day under the theme "Reading, Cultivation, Research and Innovation" at the Ministry of Education.
Minister Hang Chuon Naron stated, "Cultivating reading habits is an important issue that parents and stakeholders must pay attention to, especially in schools across the country, both public and private, by establishing libraries in all schools with enough books. For students to read.
In fact, the National Reading Day in 2020 is set for March 11, which is the birthday of Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Choun Nath, to be celebrated every year.
This year's theme is "Reading, intellectual development, research and innovation" to promote to the public and stakeholders to support the development of reading habits, promote reading culture and promote reading and writing in Cambodia.
Minister Hang Chuon Naron said that this day is celebrated from the sub-national level to the national level in collaboration with relevant ministries, authorities, authorities at all levels, development partners and other stakeholders.
The minister said that reading is started from the first grade, so in order for children to enjoy reading, parents need to send their children to kindergarten, cultivate reading habits at home and set up a home library by providing a variety of books for children. Read it when they are at home.
In addition, in order to disseminate widely and with the participation of all circles, the Ministry has set March 6-8, 2020 to inaugurate and exhibit 104 books at the Institute of Technology of Cambodia open to the public.
On March 6, there will be a workshop on reading the first day, aimed at promoting and promoting reading habits from an early age, with presentations by expert speakers. March 06-15 "Let's read every day" campaign aims to cultivate reading habits, promote reading culture and promote reading and writing.
On March 08-10, there will be a competition and announcement of the winners of the essay reading, recitation, poetry and composition, as well as interpretation competitions on the topic: the role of literature in society, the role of Kampuchea Sorya magazine in promoting Khmer literature and Composing in the digital age.
