The 33-meter-long golden pole, hundreds of years old, is worshiped at Wat Samrong Sen to ask for happiness
(Kampong Chhnang): The flagpole, as the elders call it, is a golden tree that is thousands of years old, 2 ounces in size and 33 meters long, which people found in the flagpole lake almost 10 years ago. The district kept it in Wat Sen Serey, called Wat Samrong Sen, for worship.
Wat Samrong Sen is located in Samrong Sen Village, Samrong Sen Commune, Kampong Leng District, Kampong Chhnang Province. Since the golden flag was kept in the pagoda, people from near and far have believed that it is sacred and have come to pray for the fulfillment of various purposes and for their well-being. They even helped to build this Samrong Sen pagoda. There has been progress so far.
The chief abbot of Wat Samrong Sen, Yeon Yan, said that he had been living in Wat Samrong Sen for more than five years. In the past, some people in Phnom Penh, some in Kampong Chhnang and other provinces came to pray for the help of the golden tree, and some of the people who came to pray were able to offer offerings and some also offered music. Pin Peat to the palm tree above.
In particular, every major festival such as Pchum Ben, Kathina, Khmer New Year, etc. Also, the villagers and local elders always offer Thai music to the hand of Thkol Meas to wish good fortune to their children and to their villages. Those who come to pray and offer offerings have always come to participate in the construction of the pagoda, so far, Wat Samrong Sen has developed many satisfactory achievements.
But when the villagers made offerings and brought them from the lake to the land, the loose flesh of the tree broke down and rotted away, leaving only the essence of the tree. The locals also took the ancient flag and kept it in Wat Samrong Sen to worship and celebrated for 3 days and 3 nights in the pagoda to ask for happiness for the villagers.
(Prey Veng): A fire broke out in a motorbike repair house near Karndet Market at 12:45 on March 2, 2020 at Chambok village, Prasat commune, Kampong Trabek district, Prey Veng province. The fire injured three people and damaged a large amount of property.
