Cambodia finds 150 out of 500 species of wild orchids
(Siem Reap): Through the "Sok An Phnom Kulen Hair Research and Conservation Center" at the foot of Kulen Mountain, Banteay Srei District, Siem Reap Province, officials have been able to find and breed about 150 species of wild orchids while in the country. Cambodia is estimated to have up to 500 species of pollinators.
Cassava is a large species of plant with more than 25,000 species, of which more than 10,000 species are found in the tropics. Every year, hundreds of new species of wild coral are discovered and named after their scientific nature.
In Cambodia, natural resource researchers have documented about 300 species in the wild. This is a very small number compared to neighboring countries studied earlier, such as Thailand with more than 1,500 species, Vietnam with more than 700 species and Laos with more than 500 species.
This "Sok An Phnom Kulen Kesor Research and Conservation Center" is to commemorate the precious merits of the soul of Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An in the cause of nation building, protection of natural resources, conservation of biodiversity and conservation of human cultural heritage and the promotion of tourism in Cambodia.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, said that the establishment of this research center will provide many benefits, such as: Preservation and restoration of local wildlife, collecting live hair samples, recording and inventory for study. Research and provide scientific knowledge and information on wildlife for the next generation and theme parks.
According to a Vietnamese government statement, the construction of the center, located in the center of Hanoi, will be completed by the end of 2022 and will employ between 2,200-3,000 people in Vietnam. Samsung has also invested about $ 600 million to build another research and development center in Ho Chi Minh City.
Samsung is the largest foreign investor in Vietnam with a total investment of more than $ 17 billion, which will be invested in eight factories and two research and development centers, while this huge investment will create job opportunities. More than 160,000 places for Vietnamese people. Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Inaugurates a 5,000-Meter Concrete Road in Prey Chhor District
