After receiving the recommendation from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Ministry of Tourism, which is in charge of this work, disseminated and developed a strategic plan to help promote as well as restore the challenge of declining the number of tourists caused by the coronavirus or Covid-19 in China.
On the morning of February 2, 2020, Mr. Tith Chantha, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, during a press conference organized by the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit on "Progress and Future Directions of the Ministry of Tourism", confirmed that the measures taken by the Ministry Issued and recommended by Samdech Techo Hun Sen will improve the situation of tourism.
Mr. Tith Chantha noted that although the number of foreign tourists visiting Cambodia has decreased, but all activities and destinations are still alive. He considered that during this period of decline, it is also an opportunity for Cambodia to organize better tourism destinations.
He added that the forthcoming measures are to alleviate what is happening now, as the ministry has not yet been able to conclude that it will boost tourism in 2020, as the coronavirus has now affected the market. The biggest tourist destination for Cambodia is China. He said Chinese tourism is the number one market for Cambodia.
According to the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, the most declining destinations are Siem Reap and the coastal areas, especially in Sihanoukville, where in the first two months of this year, the number of foreign tourists decreased by about 15 percent. .
Separately, for the four main measures that have been implemented in 90 cases, including:
* First: Promote domestic tourism activities, including domestic and foreign tourists in Cambodia. The conference supports the development and implementation of incentive tour packages with facilitation of public and private tour packages at tourist destinations, and supports affordable local entertainment tickets, the establishment of events and measures to actively promote With the participation of all media channels.
* Second, measures to promote the development of tourism products, infrastructure, support and better tourism services, as well as promote investment activities, both public and private, in order to strengthen, expand and make Cambodia's tourism destinations more vibrant in the eyes of national and international visitors.
* Third: Attracting visitors from neighboring countries, regions and internationals who are not severely affected (including Cambodians living abroad) by measures to control, prevent and ensure visits without fear of threats. Covid-19 or other negative cases, as well as the use of those viewing opportunities to help expand Cambodian tourism promotion, as well as the docking of the Westerdam, is allowed to enter the famous Cambodia.
* Fourth: Measures to alleviate the hardships of the tourism industry, especially in Siem Reap, Sihanoukville, are urgent and urgent, which the Congress is satisfied to support and cooperate with the Royal Government.
Recall that in 2019, Cambodia's tourism sector continued to grow, receiving a total of 6.6 million international tourists, an increase of 6.6%, while domestic tourists traveled across the country. More than 11.5 million people, an increase of about 2%.
