(Siem Reap): Mr. Kong Vibol, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the General Department of Taxation, explained that the duty of hotel and guesthouse owners to file tax returns is a data collection measure by the General Department of Taxation, which is the state's specialized staff. Disclosure of the Royal Government's expenditure on the four-month tax exemption for the hotel and guesthouse sector.
Mr. Kong Vibol stated that the tax exemption is the purpose of the Royal Government to help the tourism sector in Siem Reap to continue its sustainability and as an opportunity to set the price of services to attract tourists.
Mr. Kong Vibol's explanation was made during a seminar on tax facilitation measures to reduce the impact on the hotel and guesthouse and real estate sectors, as well as to promote the annual income tax. The online tax declaration and new billing rules were held at Sokha Hotel, Siem Reap on March 2, 2020.
He said the tax exemption was to help reduce the impact of the Covid-19 epidemic, which has severely reduced Chinese tourists. However, despite this exemption, hotel and guesthouse owners are still required to submit their tax returns, as has been the case in the past.
Mr. Kong Vibol stated that for the date of 2020, we will not have a full audit, and with this non-audit, let the private sector as taxpayers use the obligation to file tax returns in good faith with each other. Contribute together for national economic growth.
Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province, expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for the Royal Government's measures on monthly tax exemptions for hotels and guesthouses and the real estate sector, as well as revenue promotion. Annual E-Filing in Siem Reap is registered with the General Department of Taxation for four months from February to May 2020.
