ERCP techniques are commonly used to diagnose and treat pancreatic and biliary tract diseases, including: Gallstones, gallbladder inflammation, or narrowed bile ducts caused by pancreatic or intestinal tumors.
Previously, all of the diseases mentioned above were treated by surgery to remove stones or intestinal obstruction with the bile duct, which took a long time to treat and had many side effects.
* No abdominal surgery: Patients undergoing treatment do not need surgery * No side effects or severe pain after treatment * No worries about incisions, wounds do not heal or stick to the gut like abdominal surgery * Relaxation Hospital treatment is short, which does not significantly affect daily performance.
Therefore, patients who have or suspect that bile duct problems can come for consultation and treatment by ERCP technical doctor at Preah Ketomealea Hospital safely and with high confidence.
Bek Trabek Canal is about 60% complete
