Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Occasion of Graduation Ceremony for 1,589 Asia-Europe Students
(Phnom Penh): On March 2, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presented diplomas to 1,589 Asia-Europe University students, including 616 women, after they successfully graduated.
The graduation ceremony took place at the National Institute of Education. Students who receive this degree include associate degree, bachelor's degree, master's degree and doctoral degree.
The following are the main remarks of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of handing over diplomas to Asia-Europe students:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised and appreciated the progress of Asia-Europe University.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen encourages public and private institutions to continue to pay attention to strengthening the quality of education.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the quality of education is still a key point to pay attention to the education sector.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the study must be done for life, not a bachelor's degree, master's degree or doctorate and must walk on the chest.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that living in a society requires constant monitoring of various issues in society, both in the country and in the world.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanks Asia-Europe University for providing scholarships for Samdech. From the academic year 2003-2004 to the academic year 2019-2020, Asia Europe University provides 1253 scholarships to Samdech.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in one month, Samdech donated money and rice to poor students at 5 universities totaling more than 5,000 USD.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the postponement of the US-ASEAN Summit in the United States, only the United States can confirm the real reason.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the United States did not attend the full meeting with ASEAN for three consecutive years.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the postponement of the US-ASEAN meeting led to Samdech rescheduling the program to go abroad as well.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed hope that Malaysia will have political stability while the country's politics are in trouble.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that countries in the ASEAN region all have their own problems, but for Cambodia, the problem is purely law enforcement.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said it was ridiculous for commentators that Cambodia had a political crisis.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that there is a politician, Samdech is easy to use. This includes amending the constitution from two-thirds to 50 plus one for the winning political party to lead the government.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he supported Donald Trump's decision to postpone the US-ASEAN Summit.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on people to protect themselves to get good health.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that self-defense is a matter, but do not choose to be overly fearful.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he did not choose to be detained for 14 days upon his return from China to avoid causing undue fear to the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that according to the data of the World Organization, in a year, no less than 250,000 people in the world die from the flu.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in Sihanoukville, two factories had more than 300 workers suspended due to lack of raw materials for production.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on those who like to travel abroad, please turn to visit in the country, to get to know all the entertainment places in the country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodians visiting Angkor should use tour guides to understand the history and provide jobs for guides.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested the Ministry of Tourism to consider this issue. Samdech Techo added that this is not a coercion, but a joint effort to help tour guides.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers the actions of the Mongolian Prime Minister, who detained himself and his delegation after returning from a visit to China, a mistake.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call on people to adhere to the principles of hygiene.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call on celebrities to appear on television not to be too sexy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks those who criticize Samdech Roeung to call on people not to wear sexy clothes to look at the law on human trafficking and the law on the traditional culture of Cambodia.
