This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen hands over diplomas to 1,589 Asia-Europe students
(Phnom Penh): Monday, the 9th day of the month of Phalkun, in the year of Kor Ek Sak, B.C. 2563 On March 2, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will present diplomas to 1,589 Asia-Europe University students, including 616 women, after they successfully graduate.
The graduation ceremony took place at the National Institute of Education. Students who receive this degree include associate degree, bachelor's degree, master's degree and doctoral degree. Dr. Duong Leang, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Asia-Europe University, said that the graduating students this morning included 22 scholarship students of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
Education is the leading sector among the four priority sectors, including: human resources, water, roads and electricity for the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. In order to promote education for excellence, the Royal Government of Cambodia has opened up opportunities for the private sector to invest in education.
Dr. Duong Leang said that Asia Europe University was born out of the professional training at the certification level through Asia Europe in 2002.
With the strong support of the Royal Government and the trust of the students, the school has gradually developed into a university. From the 2005-2006 school year to the 2017-2018 school year, there were a total of 56,208 vocational and graduate students (23,157 females). This number includes the winning students who must receive a degree now.
The President of the Board of Directors of Asia-Europe University confirmed that most of the graduates are employed. Of these, master's and doctoral degrees are 100% employed, 89% are bachelor's degree and 73% are associate's degree. Students also claimed that 53.08% of jobs were in skills, 44.31% in non-skills and 2.61% in self-employment.
In addition, to meet the real needs of the society and the development trends of the region and the world in the fourth industrial era, Asia-Europe University has implemented a digital management and education services (Digital).
