The driver of the Mercedes, Long Lundy, a 35-year-old military man living in Moul village, Dangkor commune, Dangkor district, pulled out a shotgun and fired at a Corolla tire. Police arrested and transferred to the Phnom Penh Gendarmerie by the military.
According to the traffic police, a drunk Corolla driver was driving in the same direction as a Mercedes driven by a man who hit the back of a Mercedes, causing damage to the left rear and did not know why. The driver of the sedan pulled out a pistol and fired, breaking the wheel immediately.
The police said that the police force stopped the military man and removed the firearm, while the two vehicles were measured and stored at the Chamkar Mon District Inspectorate and handed over to the Phnom Penh Police Force for legal action in the case of a firearm explosion on a public road.
