A safe vegetable stall in Preah Vihear province has been opened to help farmers sell more
(Preah Vihear): In order to promote the production of all kinds of vegetables by farmers, as well as to provide customers with confidence to buy safe vegetables, the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Vihear Province and the Chey Sen District Administration have opened a safe vegetable stall to Let farmers increase sales.
The official opening of the vegetable stall was held on February 29 in the presence of Mr. Peng Trida, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture and Mr. Ros Heng, Governor of Chey Sen District in Saang Commune, Chey Sen District.
Mr. Peng Trida said the opening of the safe vegetable stall was aimed at increasing the volume of local safe vegetable sales, helping traders to expand their business even better.
He said that if they want to buy local safe vegetables to eat, of course, they will come to buy at the booth there, because they believe that the stall of farmers sell safe vegetables, natural vegetables grown by local farmers without using chemical fertilizers. .
Mr. Peng Trida added that this safe vegetable booth is the second booth of the Aspay program after the first booth built in Chep district.
He said that in 2020 and the following year, the Aspire program of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture plans to expand the construction of vegetable stalls to other communes and districts with vegetable business clusters throughout the province, in collaboration with collectors and other traders to expand Market safe vegetables grown by local farmers throughout Preah Vihear province.
At the same time, the director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture also called on people to encourage farmers who grow natural vegetables by buying vegetables at safe vegetable stalls for everyone's health.
