Preah Vihear provincial authorities promise to build achievements for people who have lived in the forest for many years in Chep district
(Preah Vihear): In order to keep a satellite village with people living in the forest for many years near the town, today the Preah Vihear Provincial Authority led by Mr. Ko Sum Bunsoeut, Acting Governor of Preah Vihear and Mr. Sok Santara On February 29, 2020, the governor of Chhep district led a team to inspect the location of the village to find out the geography and living conditions.
Mr. Kor Sum Bunsoeut informed the people that due to the peace factor, the people have been able to live in peace and be able to earn a living easily and in accordance with the law, while the country has developed in all areas. From downtown to remote rural areas, such as in Preah Vihear province.
He continued that under the guidance of Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, today, together with the Governor of Chhep District, he led the relevant authorities to inspect the living places of the people in this satellite village to study the geography and living conditions in general. The aim is to develop a satellite village in this forest close to the town of Chep district.
In addition, the visit is to check the progress of the construction of a school building with 3 classrooms measuring 6 meters by 21 meters, supported by the Chhep District Administration, the Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports and the World Vision Organization in Chhep. At the same time, Senior Minister Meas Sophea donated money and materials to the teachers and students there.
Originally, this village was inhabited by about 10 families, but now there are 33 families with a total population of 134 people, including 72 women. After receiving many requests from the people living in this satellite village, the provincial authorities will develop this village to be closer to the town to facilitate the lives of the people.
