The inauguration ceremony was presided over by General Ke Kim Yan, Member of Parliament for Banteay Meanchey and Mrs. Mao Malay Ke Kim Yan.
On that occasion, General Ke Kim Yan recalled the brutal regime of genocide from 1975-1979, this 261-year-old pagoda was destroyed, no different from the pagodas that were demolished by the Khmer Rouge Pol Pot. Go to build a cooperative kitchen and this church is used as a rice barn.
He said that Buddhism, the state religion, had just survived and flourished after the liberation on January 7, 1979, under the efforts of the CPP leadership to rehabilitate and develop it. Prosperous prosperity of the lives of the Buddhists.
