The community forest was established in 2003 with a total population of 678 families (2,269 people (1,372 women)) to manage the 937-hectare community forest, which is a degraded mixed forest. Community forestry received a proclamation from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries on April 3, 2018 and signed a community forestry agreement on September 10, 2018.
This community forest is a beautiful plateau and mountain landscape and rich in wildlife resources, wild pigs, wolves, especially rich in reindeer and a huge potential for eco-tourism.
He said that due to the success of the eight-corner forest community, the Forestry Administration of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has always promoted community livelihoods by mobilizing to help this community for the benefit of Cambodia's 16 million people. Anyone can come and see the wildlife here.
