Mr. Soeun Lay, President of the Eight Forests Community Forest, stated that today there are 16 forest and wildlife patrols in the community, patrolling day and night, volunteering since 2003 to protect wildlife.
He also called on NGOs, the private sector and philanthropists to continue to support and support the community to continue to protect wildlife and forests more actively and vigorously for the benefit of the people and the next generation.
