Mr. Chea Vuthy welcomed the visiting delegation to Cambodia as the whole of China is taking strict measures to combat the new Covid-19 respiratory disease and informed the delegation of Cambodia's commitment. Condolences to Chinese friends in all circumstances were confirmed during the Prime Minister's visit to Beijing on February 5.
He briefed the delegation on the immediate impact of the shortage of raw materials on the garment and footwear industry, a large number of investments from the People's Republic of China, and the short-term impact of the suspension. One of the tax concessions under the EBA to various sectors.
He informed the delegation of the urgent measures of the Royal Government of Cambodia to counter the above impact and brought the request of the Prime Minister to the Chinese government to facilitate the supply of raw materials to factories in Cambodia. Encourage Chinese investors to continue investing in Cambodia, promote the opening of the Chinese market to Cambodian products and strive to complete the negotiations on the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement as soon as possible.
