Opinion: Strict law enforcement, do people respect the law?
(Phnom Penh): Traffic accidents are becoming a major concern for Cambodia today, as road accidents claim the lives of many Cambodians during the war. The report shows that in 2019, nearly 2,000 people were killed on the streets and more than 6,000 were injured in more than 4,000 traffic accidents.
The accident rate in 2019 was found to be higher than in 2018. Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Road Safety, has decided to declare 2020 as the year of emergency to effectively prevent and reduce traffic accidents on this road.
According to the report, the problems that led to the increase in traffic accidents were that the infrastructure system did not respond to the growth of vehicles on the road, some places were damaged or lacked signs, lack of control on the sidewalks and sidewalks caused the road to be built. Traffic is getting narrower.
People's sense of law is still limited, they are more afraid of the police than they are of the law, the capacity of law enforcement officers is still limited and the quality of work is not yet responsive to requests due to lack of means, equipment and operational materials. These are also factors that lead to accidents.
Although the problem leads to more accidents, there is an assessment that if the driver's awareness of traffic rules and the spirit of law enforcement are strengthened and enhanced, it may contribute to the prevention and reduction. Road accidents.
Drivers in Cambodia are seen as having a limited sense of law and order while driving. Some drivers on the road continue to use the wrong lanes, some continue to violate the speed limit, and some in places where it is forbidden to overtake, such as curves, they still overtake.
The use of night lights is still incorrect. Some drivers use headlights that cause excessive light, disturb the driver in the opposite direction, and can even lead to accidents.
In addition to the problems mentioned above, the factors of vehicles, overweight transport, bulky transport are all the causes of traffic accidents.
Strengthening the driver's law-abiding spirit, ending the traffic of illegal vehicles and transporting heavy loads on the road is one of the reasons to help prevent and reduce the high rate of traffic accidents that are becoming a concern of the Royal Government. Currently.
In order to encourage drivers to increase their awareness of the law and eliminate illegal processing vehicles, illegal transport and bulk transport, traffic police officers on the road are the main players. Traffic police officers are those who are assigned duties by law to stop and fine all drivers and vehicles that violate the law.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, during the closing ceremony of the Ministry of Interior on February 20, 2020, supported the amendment of the traffic law to severe fines for illegal drivers to the point of revocation. Driving more often for offenders.
There has been much applause for the idea of imposing severe penalties on illegal drivers. Along with amending the law to severely penalize drivers, enforcing traffic police officers' enforcement of the law is also needed.
If the law on fines is stricter, but the enforcement of traffic police officers remains lax or loopholes will lead to the driver's law-abiding spirit remains less effective.
While traveling on the road, there were many cases of collusion between the driver and the traffic police officer who enforced the law, and finally the offending driver was allowed to continue his journey.
This is one of the few cases I have encountered while traveling on the road. The above example would like to draw the attention that in order to increase the spirit of respect for the law, reduce the number of illegal vehicles and transport bulldozers on the streets more effectively, it is necessary to constantly shoot the effectiveness of law enforcement officials. .
Authorities send 3 people involved in land theft case in Prek Pnov to court
(Phnom Penh): Police of the Minor Criminal Bureau of the Ministry of Interior's Criminal Department on the afternoon of February 29, 2020, sent a group of three suspects, one of whom was identified as 35-year-old Long Dara, who was arrested. On February 27, 2020, involved in the theft of 22,900 square meters of land located in Samrong Tbong village, Sangkat Samrong, Khan Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh during 2018.
The suspect, Long Dara, further confirmed to the authorities that Poch Then was the nominee to buy the land for Sar Thavy, and that for the $ 150,000, Long Dara received Sar Thavy from Lok Kheng through a Canadia Bank check. .
Long Dara confessed to the authorities that the land he sold was owned by Mr. Phaen Phalla, with Mr. Sar Thavy ordering him to sell it to Poch Then. All documents related to The land was bought and sold by Oum Pheakdey.
The three suspects, including the ringleader Long Dara, are currently being investigated by the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
Mr. Khuong Sreng advises students to pay attention to health issues and study hard to become good students
(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng and Ms. Chea Sina Khuong Sreng, this morning, February 29, 2020, were invited to the Oral Health Education Program of the Samdech Techo Association of Volunteer Youth Doctors.
The ceremony was held at Phum Thom Primary School in Sangkat Ponhea Pun, Khan Prek Pnov, with 500 children attending the Oral Health Education and Dental Examination Program.
On that occasion, in addition to oral health, Mr. Khuong Sreng and Mrs. brought the gifts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to give to these 500 students, each of them received a penny book. Also comes with two boxes of toothpaste.
Mr. Khuong Sreng on that occasion also advised all students to pay attention to health issues by taking a bath, brushing their teeth, washing their body thoroughly before coming to school to pay attention to learning to become Be a good student, a good friend, because your nephews are the successors of bamboo.
It should be noted that for this program, there are three main points that require children to apply to strengthen children's oral health, including: To brush your teeth with toothpaste containing fluoride 2. Once a day, avoid foods and drinks that are high in sugar, see your dentist regularly for dental care.
For oral health examination, care is divided into 3 levels depending on the needs of the child, including:
* Level 1: Oral health check-up and protective cream (Sylvester Diamond Manure) to help stop the growth of tooth decay * Level 2: Children can get a toothpaste without scratching and closing. Protection on the back teeth * Level 3: Advanced treatment that includes touching the front teeth, treating teeth and removing severely damaged teeth.
It should be noted that on that occasion, Mr. Khuong Sreng and Mrs. also supported the construction of 5 toilets and one washroom to Phum Thom Primary School.
