National Bank of Cambodia raises awareness about the use of financial services to the public
(Koh Kong): Mr. Kith Sovannarith, First Deputy Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that the Royal Government as well as the National Bank of Cambodia want to see the Cambodian people, especially those who use all financial services to receive official financial services. Quality and control of clear laws and regulations.
He said that in order to raise public awareness about the use of financial services, the National Bank of Cambodia organized a dissemination workshop on "Microfinance in Cambodia" organized in Khemarak Phoumin, Koh Kong Province, a western province bordering Thailand. On February 28, 2020, after working in Mondulkiri for 2020.
This workshop aims to raise awareness of the use of financial services to the public.
He said that people who are using informal financial services must turn to financial services in a system that is properly controlled by the National Bank of Cambodia.
He said that the remittances of customers about 15.4 trillion riels (equivalent to 3.7 billion US dollars) to the past progress reflects the joint efforts. Achievements also depend on the support of the Royal Government of Cambodia and under the direct supervision of the National Bank of Cambodia.
Mr. Kith Sovannarith added that currently 59% of the adult population in Cambodia has access to official financial services, of which 17% is provided by banking institutions, 42% is provided by non-bank financial institutions such as microfinance institutions and institutions. Provide payment services.
He added that the cooperation from all relevant departments of the province in this workshop is now the most important and necessary part in contributing to the long-term development of the financial sector in line with the rectangular strategy of the Royal Government. Help people who use financial services get out of debt.
He added that at the same time, the Deputy Governor also proposed that microfinance institutions as well as private banks in the city should provide convenience and promptly to those who apply for a loan with valid documents that are legally recognized. From commune and municipal authorities.
Four Ministries jointly issue an inter-ministerial prakas on the establishment of an inter-ministerial inspection team in the manufacturing and tourism industries
Heng Sour, spokesman for the Ministry of Labor, confirmed to Fresh News that the release of this inter-ministerial proclamation is in line with the spirit of the results of the 18th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum on March 29, 2019. At the forum, the Prime Minister set out a 15-point package of sharp reform measures to facilitate business, strengthen competitiveness and promote Cambodia's economic diversification.
Mr. Heng Sour added that the integration of the four inter-institutions is a continuous reform of each ministry, which in the last five mandates of the Royal Government is integrated many units in each ministry into an inspection team. One of the Ministry. In this sixth mandate, we move from the integration of the internal units of each ministry into a single inter-institutional inspection team.
This integration will reduce the interruption of time for enterprises to receive inspection delegations, as previously each institution conducted different inspections, sometimes the subject of inspections were similar. From April onwards, when inspecting an enterprise, we only visit once a year, and when we visit, we will visit all three institutions together in each sector.
