Will officially open on March 7, 2020. Sokha Hotel's huge new project "Treasure of Heaven" has been investing in the international hotel industry since 1997.
The company organized the groundbreaking ceremony for the housing development project on Bokor Mountain on March 7, 2020, with the participation of Mr. Chea Sophara, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, as well as the participation of the people. In Kampot province, including many investors, and this participation to get to know this project better, especially to get the first investment opportunity.
Sokha Hotel is one of the leading hospitality companies in the Kingdom of Cambodia and a concessionaire for development investment in Monivong Bokor National Park.
Monivong Bokor National Park is only about 189 km from Phnom Penh and is located near major infrastructure such as: Kampot Tourism Port, Sihanoukville Deep Sea Port, Railway, and Sihanoukville International Airport. .
There are many major roads that can be accessed to this Bokor development area, such as National Road No. 3 and the expressway that is being built and expanded, which is scheduled to be completed in the near future, as well as roads. National Road 4 and Road 41, which are the main national roads for travel to the area today. In addition, it is possible to travel there by helicopter.
It should also be noted that the groundbreaking of the third Crown Estate project focuses on potential development projects in finance, transportation, trade, tourism and housing construction. In addition, the company welcomes local and foreign investors who are interested in investing in this large third project.
It should also be reminded that Monivong Bokor National Park has big potential that attracts investors to invest in Borey Morakot Thansur, Borey Amret Thansur and Crown Estate, which will be officially launched from March 2, 2020 at the sales headquarters: 2nd floor, Sokimex Building, No. 22, Kramuon Sar Street, Sangkat Phsar Thmei 2, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh.
Monivong Bokor National Park is a very attractive natural area full of beautiful forests, waterfalls, waterfalls, valleys, streams, flowers and exotic plants, as well as natural rocks that look like animals or temples. In addition, it is also considered a sacred place for worship, prayer and meditation.
The historical relics left to this day include: Sla Khmao Royal Palace, King Sisowath Monivong Royal Palace, former Bokor City Hall building, nearly 100-year-old hotel building, former casino building, temple He healed animals, Catholic temples, Wat Sampov Pram, etc. Leaders of Buddhist students and students of Sihamoni Raja University visited some historical sites in Prey Veng province.
Mr. Nguon Sdech Pheakdey said that the purpose of this study tour was to understand the history of the continuous development of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Minister, as well as to show the living conditions of the people in the provinces. And what is important is that all ordinary students have studied the culture, civilization of the Phnom Kingdom and more new knowledge.
It should be noted that in the program, there was also a presentation on the key points of the experts, including Dr. Seng Vansay, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, and a presentation by Dr. Lawyer Dr. An Sam Ath.
