(Phnom Penh): On Friday, February 28, 2020, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, invited Samdech Sokun Vary to irrigate the three Deputy Prime Ministers. The King has just ordered a new appointment.
The irrigation ceremony of Preah Sokun Vary is held at Wat Mony Sovann called Wat Champouk K'aek. The three deputy monks who will be irrigating Sokun Vary today are: Samdech Preah Pothivong Amlim Heng, Samdech Preah Sang, the first deputy director, Samdech Preah Vanrath Noy Chrek, the second deputy monk and Samdech His Excellency Vongsa Muongra, Samdech Preah Sang, the third deputy director.
It should be noted that the three monks were appointed by the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, and appointed as the first, second and third deputy monks on February 12. 2020 ago.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen starts his speech on the occasion of inviting Preah Sokun Vary to irrigate 3 Deputy Chiefs at Wat Champouk K'aek on the morning of February 28, 2020
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Senior Minister Him Chhem, Minister of Cults and Religions, was hospitalized.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that there are many religious conflicts in the world. Thus, governing a state requires religious harmony as well.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen noted that the monks of both the Mahanikaya and Dhammayut sects are in harmony with each other today, while in the past there was some tension.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that all religions in Cambodia were destroyed during the genocidal regime.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that monks have an important role to play in helping to explain to Buddhists to participate in maintaining peace.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the stability of religion depends on the beliefs of the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks to check whether the funny sermon is correct or not? Samdech Techo proposes to put in place preventive measures during the annual meeting of monks.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that monks can run out of food if Buddhists have a lack of livelihood.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen noted that in the field of Buddhism today there is a great progress, which shows that the lives of Buddhists are also better.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that when the empire went astray, the Buddhist side also perished.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the empire and the Buddha must go hand in hand, that is, the empire grows and the Buddha grows. In this sense, Samdech Techo stated that the Buddha Chakra has a very important role in helping to preserve the empire.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the territory of Kandal province, such as Lvea Em, etc., will be cut into Phnom Penh in the near future.
The joint commitment between the leaders of the two countries' parliamentary friendship group was made at a bilateral meeting between the two sides on February 27, 2020 at the Lao National Assembly building in Vientiane, while Chea Van Det led the delegation. Delegates to pay an official and friendly visit to Laos from 24 to 28 February 2020.
During the bilateral talks, Mr. Chea Van Det emphasized that the traditional friendship, solidarity and good cooperation between our two countries, Cambodia-Laos, have had diplomatic ties since 1956.
The Chairman of the Delegation was very pleased to see that the traditional friendship, solidarity and cooperation between our two countries have been continuously accumulated for the benefit of the country's sustainable development and peace and stability. Region and world.
He added that the strengthening and expansion of cooperation between the two countries 'parliamentary friendship groups will bring further progress in strengthening the bonds of solidarity between the two countries' legislatures. Recently, Mr. Bun Nhong Vorachik, President of the Kingdom, paid a state visit to Cambodia on February 9, 2020.
Mr. Chea Van Det strongly believes that under the brilliant leadership of the party, with Mr. Bun Nhong Vorachik as President, Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit, Prime Minister and Mrs. Panya Toto, President of the Lao National Assembly, will achieve new achievements in Develop the country to become a developed country, the people have the right to decide the fate of the nation on their own.
Mr. Say Thong Keo Duong Dy congratulated the success of the 27th Annual Meeting of the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum hosted by the National Assembly of Cambodia in Siem Reap in January 2019.
He also asked the Cambodian side to maintain and promote the traditional relations and good cooperation between the two countries to the younger generation.
Mr. Say Thong Keo Duong Di continued that he also recently led a Lao parliamentary delegation to visit Cambodia in 2019. During his visit to Cambodia, he attended the hearing and paid a courtesy call on Dr. Nguon Nhel, First Vice President of the National Assembly and also discussed with Dr. Pen Panha, Chairman of the Legislative and Justice Committee of the National Assembly of Cambodia.
Mr. Chea Van Det praised the Lao National Assembly and the Lao government for leading the country to development in all areas, making the people live in peace and decent living. Regarding the relations between the two countries, especially the relations between the National Assembly of Cambodia and Laos, the Chairman of the Delegation emphasized that Cambodia and Laos have a long tradition of solidarity.
