This morning, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit watered Preah Sokun Vary to give water to 3 monks
(Phnom Penh): On Friday, February 28, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, watered Sokun Vary. Presented to the three Deputy Prime Ministers, who had just been appointed by the King.
This Sokun Vary Irrigation Ceremony is one of the many traditional Khmer Buddhist traditions, one of the many ancient Khmer traditions that Khmer ancestors left to their descendants to pass on to them. This custom originated a long time ago and continues to this day.
+ Biography of the three deputy monks
- Samdech Preah Pothivong Amlim Heng: Samdech Preah Pothivong Amlim Heng, Preah Chao Athikar Wat Monisovann, also known as Wat Champouk K'aek, was born on Thursday, October 21, 1965 in Roka Kong commune. Roka Kong 1, Muk Kampoul District, Kandal Province. Mother's name is Ton Cheav Ly, father's name is Am Sok. Samdech's parents are a pure family of farmers and a family with a right view, popular in the village.
Samdech Amlim Heng has 7 siblings, 3 brothers and 4 sisters, of which Samdech is the third child in the family.
Later, Bhikkhu Am Lim Heng was invited to stay at Wat Monisovan, called Champouk K'aek, until today, which is ruled by the Chief Inspector named Ke Yan. After being invited to stay at Wat Thmey, Bhikkhu Amlim Heng paid close attention to his efforts to study Dharma and Discipline in both Kantha Thurak and Vipassana Thurak in the presence of Master Seng Heng and was well received. Very much from the abbot and his own teacher.
At school age, Noy Chrek was sent by his parents to study arithmetic at Wat Krous Primary School, Samrong Commune, Ponhea Leu District, Kandal Province. Seeing the poor family, Venerable Ind Panho Ten Chuon, the chief abbot of Wat Tep Rainsy, Prek Taten commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province, asked Noy Chrek to take care of the children.
After the genocidal regime was overthrown on January 7, 1979, Antith Noy Chrek returned to the gates of the Dharma as a monk in 1986 and lived at Wat Chan Borey Vong, Samrong Commune, Ponhea Leu District. Kandal province to the present.
With a deep understanding of both secular and moral, Samdech Preah Vanroth Noy Chrek has fulfilled his duty to participate in the promotion of Buddhism to the fullest capacity to get the role and duties in Buddhist studies and many Buddhist works. Until February 12, 2020, he was appointed by the King as the second Deputy Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Samdech Preah Odom Vongsa Muong Ra: Samdech Preah Odom Vongsa Muong Ra, Deputy Inspector General of the National Inspectorate of Buddhist Studies and Preah Chao Athikar Wat Moni Prasidh Vong, was born on February 23, 1962 in Kampor Village, Prek Pnov Commune, Ponhea Leu District, Kandal Province. There is a father named Muong Chu, there is a grandfather named Hem Lai. Samdech Muong Ra has 4 siblings, 3 brothers and 1 sister. Samdech is the third child.
As a young man in 1977, dissatisfied with the genocidal regime, Muong Ra left his family and joined the people of the Eastern Zone and other patriotic elites to fight for national liberation from the genocidal regime. In 1978, he joined forces with the United Front for National Salvation to overthrow the genocidal regime.
After the genocidal regime was overthrown, on April 19, 1979, Muong Ra decided to build a pagoda. After the construction of Preah Phnos, Bhikkhu Muong Ra participated in the study and efforts to contribute to the revival of Buddhism after being completely destroyed by the genocidal regime.
Seeing the merits and achievements of Samdech, in 1994, Samdech was appointed as Preah Samuh Anukon, Ponhea Leu District, Kandal Province. In 1997, he was appointed Preah Dhammathor Anukon, Ponhea Leu District, Kandal Province.
In 1999, Samdech was awarded the title of Preah Sorn Rainsy, King of the Honorary Council, Advisor to Samdech Preah Akka Moha Sangkha, King Tep Vong of the Mahanikaya of the Kingdom of Cambodia. In the same year, Samdech had a deep knowledge and Pali language, Samdech was ordained as a priest for the ordination of children.
In 2001, Samdech was awarded the title of Preah Vinay Samvor, Royal Committee of Chatva. In the same year 2001, Samdech has done a good job in performing his duties. In 2001, Samdech was also appointed Preah Dhammathoron, Ponhea Leu District, Kandal Province.
From 2010 to the present, Samdech Muong Ra has been appointed as the Secretary to the present. And is a Buddhist supporter in charge of the Council of Buddhist Discipline and Administration.
In 2019, Samdech Muong Ra, representing Cambodian monks, led a procession of pilgrims to the territories of the five countries, beginning their journey from Cambodia to Thailand, Myanmar, Laos and Vietnam. In 2020, Samdech was appointed as the third Deputy Chief of the Board of Priests in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
In addition to his work in Buddhism, Samdech Preah Udomvong Kittibandit Muongra is a talented architect with high creative talent. Apparently, the achievements that have been under construction in Wat Moni Prasidh Vong are his own creative works. Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit will irrigate Preah Sokun Vary to present 3 Deputy Chiefs
