The Chinese man was treated by the Royal Government of Cambodia and returned to China. Apart from this case, there are no other cases of coronary heart disease in Cambodia. Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin: Japan has made significant contributions to Cambodia's economic development after the end of the civil war
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Bin Chin, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Office of the Council of Ministers, stated that Japan is an important partner that has contributed to the development of the Cambodian economy in all areas since the end of the Cambodian Civil War.
The Deputy Prime Minister said: "From the peace process in the early 1990s until Cambodia has developed as it is today, it is inseparable from the precious development assistance of the Government of Japan and the people of Japan. .
Under Japan's cooperation on industrial construction, infrastructure development to improve people's livelihoods and good governance, as well as focus on human resource development and participation in resolving crises and problems, Deputy Prime Minister Binh Minh said. Challenges in Cambodia that have contributed to Cambodia achieving an average annual high economic growth of 7.7 percent over the past two decades.
Mikami Masahiro, Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia, recalled that the previous Heisei reign was 31 years. This reign began when Japan actively participated in Cambodia's peace process and continued its support for the reconstruction and development of Cambodia based on liberal, multi-party democracy.
Mikami Masahiro said that during that time, Cambodia-Japan relations were strengthened, and the Japanese government was committed to making every effort to strengthen and expand bilateral relations in the new era of Reiwa. And cooperation established during the Heisei era.
