The following is a statement from the Ministry of Economy on the call for people to be vigilant: Two Cambodian universities have received the European Union's "University Innovation Project in the Asia-Pacific Region"
The project brings together 16 education and research institutions, eight of which are in the Asia-Pacific region (two in Cambodia: the University of Health Sciences of Cambodia and the Institute of Health Sciences of Cambodia and six universities in Vietnam). These institutions will benefit from the results of this project.
EU partners with scientific research centers and universities in France, Germany and Belgium will provide hands-on experience in university governance, training on change management and risk prevention. The French Higher Education Agency (AUF) is responsible for co-ordinating, coordinating and managing the administration and finances of the project.
The PURSEA project aims to strengthen the governance capacity of eight higher education institutions in the Asia-Pacific region by defining and implementing strategic plans in context and focusing on three goals.
Develop the necessary methods and means for developing strategic plans for the development and development of operational plans for partner universities. The main outcome to be expected is a strategic plan for innovative development or enhancement of each partner university and operational plan.
Implement priority action plans in each partner university, formulate project components, and lead change. Expected outcomes of this step include priority plans selected and implemented, as well as project components (governance and management).
Develop tools to exchange and disseminate local expertise by developing strategic plans as well as university governance and management processes. The expected tool is the creation of a web page for communication and exchange of project results between the university and interested individuals.
To achieve these goals, the exchange of knowledge, support and expertise between project partners will be established through various workshops and trainings to be held in Vietnam, Cambodia, France and Belgium.
Of these 10 work packages, the second package, 3-4-4-5-6, is essential for the project because it involves the development of a strategic plan directly for the development and implementation and action plan. Points 7-8 are necessary to change and require the training of staff of universities in the region to ensure quality and risk management. Items 1-9-10 are for the implementation, management and dissemination of project results.
