Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng calls on the judiciary to expedite the prosecution of drug traffickers and those involved in this crime
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, on the afternoon of February 27, 2020, called on the judiciary to expedite the trial to prosecute drug traffickers and stakeholders after the crackdown by the judicial police force. Yes.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng made the remarks while co-chaired by Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An, Minister of National Assembly Senate Relations and Inspection and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Phnom Penh. Of Phnom Penh Capital Administration.
In addition, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also called on the judiciary to prosecute those involved in drug trafficking in a fair and just manner in order to give confidence to the people and reflect the joint efforts of the authorities. Day and night crackdown to eradicate drugs in Cambodia.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated, "I continue to call on the judiciary to speed up the trial of those involved in drug trafficking and other drug-related offenses that we have cracked down on in the past in a timely manner, otherwise we can "To adversely affect the people's faith in the fight against drugs."
At the same time, the Minister of Interior also emphasized that the competent judicial police, especially the Ministry of Interior, were always ready to cooperate with the judiciary if any evidence was needed to place additional charges against the perpetrators.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said that in the last two years, the authorities have confiscated more than 1 ton of drugs intended to be distributed in Cambodia. Samdech claimed that if it could not be confiscated, it would be used for distribution in a large part of Cambodia and the other part to go abroad.
At the same time, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said that so far, the number of suspects and defendants involved in drug crimes has increased, which resulted in more detainees as the total number of detainees increased. 30,000, but only 8,000 have been convicted, less than a third. King issues Royal Decree terminating Mon Ramadi from the post of Secretary of State of the Ministry of Information
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, on February 27, 2020, issued a Royal Decree terminating the position of Mr. Mon Ramadi from the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Information.
The termination of Mr. Mon Ramadi was done under the obeisance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Letter to readers: Bids for timber have been quietly cracked down on crime, and now they are ready to allow the construction of sawmills and shredders on the crime scene.
(Phnom Penh): Sources from an expert leaked at a delicious noodle table next to the Forestry Administration said that in January, they conspired to auction the timber that the commission cracked down on in Tbong Khmum, Kratie and Mondulkiri provinces. The mosquito nets were already silent at the time, as it was claimed that the company of "Oknha Chey", a well-known timber trader, was able to bid by daring to pay high tea prices.
It is said that the location where the company bid for timber from the state to set up a sawmill and cut wood is at the location of the forest crime company, which has been cracked down on by the Natural Resources Crime Commission in the past five companies in the middle. Forest in Mondulkiri province.
The informant whispered that at the time of the auction, the auction company was scheduled to remove all the timber from Mondulkiri province within 60 days so that there would be no more "sleeping mats" cases like in the past, but now if Allow the bidding company to set up a sawmill and cut wood at the location of the offending company in the middle of the forest. .
Therefore, the Minister of Agriculture, please help check and prevent the plan to run a request to establish a sawmill and cut wood that can be auctioned in the middle of this forest.
