Ministry of Tourism: Travel through affordable travel cards, reduce costs by 20-30% compared to self-travel
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has introduced the implementation of affordable travel card system for students, professors, government officials, employees, athletes, workers and people who want to travel in the country, which can reduce costs from 20-30. % Used compared to personal travel.
This affordable tour aims to promote the sustainable and responsible growth of domestic tourists by encouraging them to travel at least once a year, promoting the diversification of tourists to existing destinations. Fewer tourists and new tourist destinations contribute to the tourism sector and national economic development and link tourism activities to environmental, social, cultural and humanitarian education to local communities.
This affordable travel voucher offers a wide range of benefits such as safety, budget, travel security and high reliability, ease of time and decision making, make it easy to find destinations and reduce costs. From 20-30% used compared to direct travel.
Please be informed that some tour companies as well as the Ministry of Tourism have already sold a lot of tour packages at reasonable prices. In fact, during the 6th River Festival in Battambang, the Ministry of Tourism has announced the sale of 3 nights 4 nights tour packages. Days also include Battambang, Banteay Meanchey and Siem Reap.
At the meeting to review the work of the Ministry of Tourism, held from 26-27 February 2020, the conference fully supported the launch, promotion and implementation of affordable travel ticket mechanism. COVID-19 infection in Singapore rises to 96 after 3 new cases found, but 66 cases are cured
According to a statement from the Singapore Ministry of Health on the same day, four more patients were allowed to leave the hospital after they were fully recovered. So far, 96 COVID-19 cases have been reported in Singapore, but 66 have been cured and 30 are still in hospital.
