He also informed the Prince that he would consider doing this work in collaboration with Mr. Hun Manet himself. In other areas, he informed the Prince that he would pay attention to the Japanese government to consider cooperation on cooperation, especially the work of the Blue Hat Army in training both in the country as well as abroad.
In relation to this disaster management work, he informed the Prince that Japan intends and considers to promote this cooperation with the Cambodian Army. He hoped that the two countries' relations would continue to expand in many areas, especially in the field of defense.
Samdech also highlighted the history of cooperation in this framework, and especially in other frameworks where Cambodia and Japan have always cooperated.
Samdech Techo stated that he would like to see further cooperation between the armies of the two countries, especially the Cambodian Army and the Japanese Army, especially in the exchange of information, participation in Fight against terrorism, etc., and especially in the training by the prince wants to see Japan participate in training human resources, especially the Cambodian army.
