Anti-Technology Crime Force cracks down on Nigerian after Instagram scam victims
The scammer sent pictures of clothes, cell phones and some money and told them that the luggage had been sent, and then contacted the victim to identify him as a courier at the airport with the goods from Dubai. He came to receive it by requiring the payment of shipping and administrative fees and the excuse for the victim to send money through the Wing agent, but did not find any materials to send to the victim.
The Anti-Technology Crime Department's specialized forces conducted a search and identified the suspects.
Then, on February 25, 2020, at 16:40, the specialized force of the Department of Technology Crime Prevention conducted a search operation and arrested HAMADOU ABDOU, a Nigerian national, in front of the house 13E30 Street. 185 Group 07, Village 02, Sangkat Tumnup Teuk, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, Phnom Penh, and bring the suspects to the Department of Technology Crimes and build a case to be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action.
