The French Embassy will host the second "Art Tour" in the Embassy Park on March 7
Nine well-known artists, including eight Cambodians and a Frenchman, were invited to create their own imaginative works of art for public display. With colorful plants and large trees in the shade, the works of art on display in different parts of the park seem to be creating a calm, romantic conversation with nature.
With different talents, most artists choose trees to associate with their artwork. Ms. Eva Nguyen Binh, French Ambassador to Cambodia, believes that in addition to the decorative features, these trees have become the real characters of this exhibition.
She said: "Through the design of the artist, these trees have become a living thing with beautiful colors that we have to take care of as a shelter and a witness to the memory. "These trees seem to be the stationary objects that give meaning to life."
Cambodian Red Cross Distributes Donations to Pregnant Women, Newborns and Health Center Staff at Kdol Daun Teav Health Center
On that occasion, Dr. But Kim Sean brought the words of Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who sent a message of sympathy to all people, especially pregnant women and women with small children who participated in this program. Dr. thanked Ms. Prum Vanna, Member of the Provincial Branch Committee, for reading the message of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to his compatriots on the occasion of the National Day of Maternal, Child and Child Health.
Dr. But Kim Sean urges all pregnant women and young children to comply, including:
1: All pregnant women should go for a health check-up, consult with a midwife at a health center or hospital near your home on a regular basis to receive all preventive services regularly as directed by a specialist. And voluntarily perform blood tests to check for HIV and syphilis status to rule out both disability and mother-to-child transmission.
2. Go to give birth at a health center or hospital with a properly trained midwife.
3: Please go for postpartum health check, both mother and baby and get 11 vaccines as prescribed by your doctor.
4: Feed the baby exclusively from the time the baby is born until the baby is 6 months old and provide all kinds of nutritious supplements (porridge, all ingredients), along with continuing to breastfeed until the child. Must be at least 2 years old.
5: Take the baby to the hospital immediately when you see any danger signs of respiratory disease, diarrhea or other infectious diseases, and take the baby or young children who are thin or do not gain weight at all to consult and receive. Hospitalized.
At the same time, Dr. emphasized the importance of setting the National Day for Maternal, Infant and Child Health on February 21, while Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen was honored by the United Nations as a national outstanding figure of the Joint Action Plan. United Nations Secretary-General for the Health of Women and Children, 21 February 2011.
Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association: For more than 2,000 years, it was only during the Techo Sen era that China became a friend of steel.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association has noted that in the history of more than 2,000 years, only in this Techo Sen era, the relationship between Cambodia and China has become a true steel friend and Promoted this friendship from the leadership to the people and spread from the city to the countryside.
This talk was given on the morning of February 27, 2020 at the National Defense University by Dr. Chea Monirith, President of the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association.
He highlighted the background and progress of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and China, which began on July 19, 1958 by His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk and President Mao Zedong, and the legacy of this relationship extends beyond bilateral relations. To a comprehensive strategic relationship and steel friendship by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Xi Jinping, President of the People's Republic of China.
Mr. Chea Monirith highlighted that more than 60 years of diplomatic relations between the two countries have provided many benefits, in fact, economic development, trade, infrastructure in Cambodia are all indispensable to the contribution of Chinese friends to Cambodia.
In addition, Mr. Chea Monirith expressed his friendship in times of emergency and hardship, which was clearly demonstrated through Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to China in early February 2020, along with a historic message. Many of Samdech Techo's issues related to COVID-19 and the relationship between the two countries.
Lt. Gen. Va Monin, Vice Chancellor and Director of the Postgraduate Training Center, expressed his appreciation for the research work of Dr. Chea Monirith, which was presented to the current undergraduate trainees, including: Thousands of years of Cambodia-China relations 2- The biography of Mr. Chiv Ta Kwan 3- Cambodia-China relations during the reign of King Norodom Sihanouk 4- Khmer philosophy in the Funan period.
(Phnom Penh): At the Closing Ceremony of the Meeting of the Ministry of Tourism held at the Sokha Residence Hotel in Phnom Penh on 27 February, the Royal Government of Cambodia, through Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance and Representative of Samdech Techo The Prime Minister also announced five recommendations to the Ministry of Tourism to implement the work direction in 2020 and next year.
The five recommendations include:
* First, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth has set 2020 as the base year for the start of sustainable and quality tourism development to promote tourism development. In addition to the measures issued by Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the Ministry of Tourism must promote the implementation of the action plan for 2020-2021 for tourism development in Siem Reap.
In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth requested the Ministry of Tourism to prepare a master plan for tourism development for Phnom Penh and surrounding areas towards 2030 in line with the reputation of "Phnom Penh: the World Capital of Tourism and Culture" to increase tourism products. More rich for tourists to visit and stay longer.
* Second, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth supported the strategy of diversifying tourism from cultural-historical tourism sites to ecotourism and coastal areas with high vigilance, specific development strategies and certain institutional mechanisms.
In this regard, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth requested the Ministry of Tourism to promote the preparation of a master plan for tourism development in Cambodia's coastal areas towards 2030 and to complete the master plan for tourism development in Kep province 2020-2035 to ensure the prestige of "Cambodia is a beach "The most beautiful sea in the world."
In addition, the Ministry of Tourism must strive to complete the tourism development master plan of Mondulkiri province in order to participate in the protection of natural resources, local culture and traditions and make the people in the local community have jobs and benefit from tourism activities.
* Third: Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth called on relevant ministries, institutions, the private sector and all citizens to join in promoting the local tourism movement in connection with the patriotic spirit in the direction of "patriotism, know the land". In order to make this movement a driving force in the tourism sector, the Ministry of Tourism must prepare a strategic plan to promote domestic tourism in 2020-2030.
Fourth, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth requested the relevant institutions, the private sector, the people and development partners to seize the opportunities of the fourth generation industry for tourism business.
Fifth, the Ministry of Tourism must lead and strengthen good governance in the tourism sector, which is a mechanism to support and develop sustainable tourism.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth requested the Ministry of Tourism and the Capital-Provincial Tourism Development Commission to cooperate with relevant ministries and institutions to study and establish a permanent joint forum for each priority tourism area to enable all stakeholders to "think together". To work together and take joint responsibility "and to strengthen the structure of the Capital-Provincial Tourism Development Management Committee effectively.
Meanwhile, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth also requested that all tour operators have a code of conduct and a professional code for tourism, while tourists also have a code of conduct and code of conduct for travel to Cambodia.
Senior Minister Meas Sophea: The public forum wants to find out about the concerns and requests of the people to solve together
(Preah Vihear): Senior Minister Meas Sophea, Chairman of the Preah Vihear Provincial Government Working Group, said that the public forum held today was to understand the concerns of the people on many issues related to livelihood. On a daily basis, the people do not have access to public services and some other issues that are the policy of the Royal Government's political program.
This statement was made by the Senior Minister on the occasion that he led the Royal Government working group to help Preah Vihear province, Preah Vihear provincial authority, director of relevant departments around the province and Tbeng Meanchey district authority, commune chief, commune council and many other people on February 27, 2020, in the area of Bak Kam pagoda in Chhean Mok commune, Tbeng Meanchey district.
Senior Minister Meas Sophea said that this public forum is to listen to the opinions of the people. This is your opportunity for the Royal Government's working group to explain and clarify some issues that are the questions of your parents. On the other hand, there are clearly suggestions such as some shortcomings related to the implementation of the policy of the Royal Government or some needs in the village-commune of parents and siblings.
Through this forum, requests will be addressed, and the resolution will be divided into levels of resolution, such as commune-level, provincial-level and national, depending on the size of the problem. The senior minister said that currently the whole of Preah Vihear province is very developed.
The senior minister stressed that "all these problems are due to the correct leadership of the Royal Government for many terms, and this Royal Government is led by the Cambodian People's Party, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister."
"So far, the country is completely peaceful, or it can be said that peace covers the whole of Cambodia under a win-win policy, no separatist zone, no territorial division as before," he said.
The Senior Minister praised our people who have the courage to speak out on the challenges as well as some suggestions. Through today's public forum, he will accept the problems and requests of the people to solve as soon as possible. Announcing the appointment of some civil servants at the Department of Agriculture, Commerce and Labor in Kampong Thom Province
(Kampong Thom): On February 27, 2020, Kampong Thom Provincial Administration held a ceremony to announce the inauguration of civil servants in the structure of departments and units around Kampong Thom Province under the chairmanship of Mr. Chhun Chhon, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province. More than 300 Deputy Governors, Chiefs, Deputy Heads of Departments, and Armed Forces participated.
In the announcement, three officials were transferred to work in the agricultural sector more effectively, such as public health, managing the movement of cattle, cattle, beef to good quality before selling in the market in Kampong Thom.
Mr. Tan Meng Chhang was reassured by the leadership of Kampong Thom Province to be the Director of the Kampong Thom Provincial Production and Veterinary Office, replacing Mr. Chan Panhavan as the Director of the Office of Agricultural Legislation, and Mr. Samrith Kruy as the Deputy Director. Office of Agro-Industry.
Mr. Sok Loo, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, requested the Chairman of the Municipal Council to find out more about the regulations. Samdech Techo said that the provincial governor, like the sub-national prime minister, is responsible for all areas, including the expertise of departments, units, until all command forces agree and must understand the leadership and management of each place from their roles and responsibilities.
He continued that as the Chairman of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command, he instructed the new Chief of the Office and the appointed officers to respect the role, work hard to perform effectively and quality for the health of the people, cooperate and internal unity. Better and do your best to serve the people to get better results.
It should be noted that the announcement of the position has 4 units, including:
* Citizens' office * Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries 13 people * Department of Labor and Vocational Training 2 people * Department of Commerce 2 people.
Senior Minister Kun Kim inspects the site of a cigarette factory building that was destroyed by fire in Por Sen Chey district
(Phnom Penh): At 1:15 am on February 27, 2020, a fire broke out at a cigarette factory along Wat Prey Sop Road, Sre Chumrov Village, Sangkat Choam Chao 2, Khan Por Sen Chey, Phnom Penh. Rescuers helped put out the blaze nearly an hour after the fire.
After receiving this information, on the morning of February 27, 2020, Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Deputy Chairman of the Disaster Management Committee, led officials and local authorities to inspect the site of the fire, which caused a lot of property damage.
According to a report from local authorities, the factory building was built of galvanized iron, measuring 50 meters by 70 meters, and caused a fire in a cigarette factory, but did not spread to neighboring houses.
For the above firefighting operations, the rescue force includes:
* 20 vehicles of the Office of Fire Prevention and Extinguishment of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police * 3 vehicles of the Ministry of Interior * 3 vehicles of Unit 711 "Ng 70" * 1 vehicle of the Cambodian Brewery Company. A total of 27 fire trucks.
