Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Introduces Increased Deployment of Night Traffic Police
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Road Safety, recommended to increase the deployment of traffic police forces, night patrols and increase the installation of security cameras on the road and control. Check the driver of the truck for drugs as well.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also expressed his pride in the attitude of most police officers who do a good job. Before concluding, the Prince also expressed his support and encouragement for the increase of traffic education on traffic issues in addition to tightening the law as a priority.
The introduction of this new measure by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng to traffic police officers was made on February 27, 2020 on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the January 2020 Road Safety Inspection Meeting held at the office. Ministry of Interior.
For the work ahead, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stressed that all traffic police officers must continue to strictly abide by the law on road traffic, with Samdech noting that passengers are now very afraid of the police. In fact, during the day, when the police work a lot, they wear helmets and obey the law a lot, but at night, when the traffic police force is not strong enough, they break the law a lot, especially not wearing helmets.
Regarding the amendment of the Law on Road Traffic, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng urged the public not to have any doubts about this issue, as the social situation, especially the traffic situation in Cambodia, is evolving from year to year, which in principle requires Amend the law to address recent issues.
In that, the Prince also recommended to discuss the inclusion of ways to reduce traffic accidents on the road already in the road construction bidding, to be determined in the Law on Road Traffic when amended.
Kandal Provincial Land Department calls on residents of 2 villages in Prek Ambel commune, Saang district to come and check the names and verify the plot data within 15 days
(Kandal): Kandal Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs has called on the people who own land plots in Sampan Krom and Prek Ta Teav villages, Prek Ambel commune, Saang district, Kandal province to come and check the names and verify the plots data correctly. In the next 15 days from February 27 to March 12, 2020.
Mr. Prum Chat, Deputy Director of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Kandal Province, made this kind of appeal during the public posting of systematic land judgment documents in Prek Ambel commune, Saang district, Kandal province this morning, February 27, 2020. In Wat Prek Ambel.
The Deputy Director of the Department said that this posting is very important for the people who have land in both villages to check and verify the plot data correctly, and in case of misspellings, land size or land boundaries, people and people. Stakeholders may object to the posted data.
The protest will last for 15 days from the date of this posting until March 12, 2020, during which time the administrative committee and cadastral officials will be on duty every day, both on holidays and on public holidays. To wait to explain the data, receive complaints, resolve complaints and disputes.
After posting for 15 days, we will get the correct data to issue the certificate of ownership of real estate (hard title) to the people, which contributes to reducing land disputes, reducing poverty.
Mr. Nhim Vandin, Governor of Saang District, said that the posting of the judgment now reflects the high attention of the Royal Government under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Raise living standards, welfare and reduce poverty, as well as contribute to the strengthening of justice and social stability.
He said that in implementing the systematic land registration procedures, we used advanced techniques, including aerial photographs, automatic machine measurements, as well as data storage and computerized cadastral mapping.
It should be noted that in Sampan Krom village, Prek Ta Teav village, Saang district, Kandal province, there are 1,630 plots of land that have been posted to the public, including 797 plots in Sampan Krom village, 833 plots in Prek Ta Teav village, and the International Women's Day in Cambodia reports. Gender gap in Cambodia has been significantly reduced
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training this morning, February 27, 2020, celebrated the International Women's Day on March 8, the 109th anniversary of 2020, by presenting the report of the World Economic Forum on the gender gap in Cambodia. Has been significantly reduced from 112 in 2016 to 89 in 2020.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng emphasized that gender equality is a key factor in ensuring the sustainability of peace, the environment and the long-term sustainability of peace. Gender equality and empowerment of women and girls is an agenda that the Royal Government of Cambodia strongly focuses on and encourages them to become a driving force to actively contribute to development and A strong backbone of the economy and society.
Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 for Employment Growth, Equity and Efficiency The National Strategic Development Plan 2019-2030 and Cambodia's Sustainable Development Goals set out to promote gender equality and empower women and girls as separate priority areas. As well as work in other priority areas.
In response to the promotion of gender equality, the Ministry of Labor has integrated gender work into the Strategic Plan for Employment Development and Vocational Training 2019-2023 in the fourth program of the fifth strategy, the seventh activity cluster, and has developed a strategic plan for gender mainstreaming in the sector. Employment and Vocational Training Phase 4, 2019-2023, also shows the Ministry's commitment to participate in promoting gender equality.
This classification is based on four main factors: first, increasing women's participation in the economy, second, gender equality in education, third, women's health status, and fourth, gender equality. Public and political decision-makers. Mobile customs forces seize four heavy machinery imported from Vietnam without permission in Ou Raing district, Mondulkiri province.
(Mondulkiri): A mobile customs force led by Mr. Preap Karath, in cooperation with the National Gendarmerie, seized four heavy machinery imported from Vietnam without permission at Pouleh village, Dak Dam commune, Ou Raing district. Mondulkiri Province.
The operation was also attended by the Mondulkiri Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Lor Sokha, in cooperation with the Joint Customs Force in Area 6, and coordinated by Mr. Heang Sopheak, Deputy Prosecutor and Representative of the Mondulkiri Provincial Prosecutor's Office.
During the operation, the driver of the injection was arrested and handed over to the police.
The youth forum will take place on the National Television of Cambodia on April 22, 2020 with the interpretation of 5 student speakers from Panha Cheat University and 5 speakers from Western University.
As part of this campaign, on the morning of Thursday, February 27, 2020, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, presided over the opening ceremony. Orientation course for about 100 students of Panha Cheat University.
On that occasion, the First Deputy Secretary-General brought the remarks of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who sent a message of remembrance and highlighted the purpose of the celebration of May 8 as an opportunity to:
1: Demonstrate the achievements of the Cambodian Red Cross in alleviating the suffering of the most vulnerable victims with transparency and accountability, as well as disseminating the Red Cross Red Crescent Movement, international humanitarian law, roles and responsibilities. National Association.
2. Identify what are the global and national challenges that, as a national association, must fulfill in order to solve those problems or crises and disasters.
3. Raise funds to find resources to support humanitarian operations to help the most vulnerable and vulnerable from year to year.
At the same time, she stressed the importance of organizing a youth forum as an opportunity to give young people the courage to discuss, express their views, interpret the meaning, content and questions asked by the committee and know how to work in a team.
Please be informed that the Cambodian Red Cross will continue to disseminate the "May 8 Preparatory Campaign" to 5 other university students in Phnom Penh on a regular basis.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth tells customs and tax officials to study the possibility of opening luxury shops in tourist areas
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, has instructed the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia in collaboration with the General Department of Taxation to study the feasibility of opening a place for selling luxury goods and outlets. ) In major tourist areas and towns to attract investment in this area.
At the same time, while Cambodia has been facing some major challenges, including: the slowdown in global economic growth, the partial suspension of the EBA and the spread of the Covid-19 virus, which has affected Seriousness to the supply chain of raw materials, he advised for the direction to continue in 2020, emphasizing a number of work, including:
1: Continue to strengthen good governance in the institution by adhering to the four approaches of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the five approaches of Samdech Techo Prime Minister: mirroring, bathing, scrubbing, treatment and surgery.
2. Promote compliance with the private sector by providing trade facilitation to highly compliant businesses, but must take strict action against businesses that commit crimes.
3. Take measures to facilitate the import of raw materials for the production of investment projects both inside and outside the SEZ, especially when the supply chain resumes after being temporarily suspended due to the outbreak of Covid- disease. 19.
4: Continue to expand and update the customs automation system and promote the full implementation of the second phase of the one-stop-shop system.
5: Continue to pay attention to strengthen the efficiency and speed up the work of verifying customs duties, classification of goods, and rules of origin, and assess the impact on customs revenue caused by various reasons to take measures to compensate for revenue. Appropriate.
6. Encourage the completion of the preparation of information technology strategy documents of the General Department of Customs and prepare a clear expenditure plan for the medium and long term.
7. Continue to implement the measures taken by the Royal Government in the past and prepare to implement the new package of measures of the Royal Government under the jurisdiction of the General Department of Customs to be effective.
8: Promote the completion of the policy of importing used cars.
Dr. Kun Nhem, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, said that for 2019, the total revenue of about 3.215 million US dollars, an increase of 30% compared to 2018 and exceeded the plan. About 42.7%.
He said that the revenue collected by the General Department of Customs in 2019 was the highest in the past 20 years in the context of tax incentives, both in terms of investment incentives and priority sectors, as well as the implementation of trade agreements. Serey has been steadily increasing from year to year. Minister of Agriculture recommends 7 points to promote the development of modern agriculture
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, this morning, February 27, 2020, presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work results in 2019 and the work direction for 2020 of the General Department of Agriculture. The meeting was held at the Ministry of Agriculture.
At the closing ceremony of the meeting to summarize the work results in 2019 and the work direction for 2020 of the General Department of Agriculture was attended by Mr. Chea, the leader of the Ministry under the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of the Capital-Province and about 500 officials of the General Department. .
Mr. Veng Sakhon expressed his appreciation and appreciation to the General Department of Agriculture, as well as civil servants and the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of the Capital-Provinces for their diligent performance in performing their duties. In the past year, which has achieved positive results, despite still facing challenges from severe natural disasters.
According to the assessment of the expert unit, in 2019, the agricultural sector achieved a real GDP growth rate of 4% of the agricultural sector. Agricultural sub-sector achieved around 13.7%, similar to 2018, but exports increased. Although the growth of production of some crops has slowed slightly, some strategic agricultural crops as well as exports have maintained high growth, such as cassava, vegetables, bananas, yellow beans, mangoes, turmeric and cashew nuts.
At the same time, the Ministry maintains its pride in the quality of Cambodian rice, which is still competitive and has gained international prestige for four consecutive years, especially Cambodia's fragrant fragrant rice, Phkar Romduol rice. Recognized as good quality and delicious in the world.
In addition, we have negotiated to open the market and expand the volume of exports of major crop products, which is in the process of negotiating a protocol on phytosanitary requirements for the export of fresh mangoes and Pailin lentils to the Chinese market. Enterprise and completion of protocol on phytosanitary requirements for export of fresh mangoes to the Republic of Korea and Pailin lentils for the Thai market.
In order to continue to promote the development of the agricultural sector in a modern way and in a new scope and speed, competitiveness, sustainable climate change and innovation, he further reminded some recommendations for implementation. Continue:
First, to continue to prepare and strengthen the professional implementation of the strategic framework, policies and legal documents that serve the management of crop production, quality control of crops and agricultural inputs, management and use of agricultural land. Good agriculture and organic farming standards.
Second, we must continue to promote the research and development of refined crop production techniques and plant varieties that are of good quality, resistant to climate change, and have high added value.
Fifth, to strengthen and expand the capacity of the National Agricultural Laboratory to analyze and evaluate the quality of agricultural inputs (fertilizers, pesticides), soil quality and pesticide residues in agricultural products, soil and water, in close cooperation with all relevant partners. All.
Sixth, to strengthen measures to protect crops, sanitation and phytosanitary by monitoring, evaluating, forecasting and interventions to eliminate pests on crops, monitoring and registration of farms, good agricultural practices, strengthening mechanisms to prevent the spread of pests and restrictions Restrict the import of substandard and unsafe agricultural products that affect local crop production, public welfare and for export.
Seventh, continue to strengthen the efficiency of laboratory and laboratory services by equipping pesticide waste analysis equipment and phytosanitary inspection services to enhance export competitiveness by promoting phytosanitary testing services closer to consumers. Convenient as well as launching regional phytosanitary services, such as applying for computer monitoring and developing e-Phyto systems.
