Minister Mam Bunheng: Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital Tbong Khmum worth about $ 50 million, reached 45% and will be completed by the end of 2021
(Tbong Khmum): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bunheng, said that the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital, Tbong Khmum, worth about $ 50 million, will be completed by the end of October 2021.
This statement was made by the Minister of Health on the occasion of Mr. and Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, together with Mr. Keo Vannak, Director of the Provincial Health Department, inspecting the progress of the construction process of this hospital on the morning of February 27, 2020.
On that occasion, Minister Mam Bunheng thanked the Chinese government, people and Chinese companies for their support in promoting health care in Cambodia.
In addition, the new hospital will be a regional hospital covering the population in Tbong Khmum and some of Kratie, Ratanakkiri, Stung Treng and Mondulkiri provinces, and so far the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital Tbong Khmum is 45% completed. The Ministry of Health will strive to strengthen the knowledge, skills and techniques of doctors to provide health services to people in Tbong Khmum province with high efficiency.
45% of the construction progress, including:
Please be informed that this Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital Tbong Khmum was built on March 1, 2019 with the inauguration of the construction site under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and will be completed by the end of October. 2021, built on an area of 24,300 square meters on a total area of 55,815 square meters. This project is built in 40 months. The new large hospital needs an additional 456 specialized staff.
