Arrested a thief driving a car to act in Thmor Koul district, Battambang province, today sent the suspect to court
(Battambang): The police force of Battambang Provincial Police investigated and arrested a suspect and sent him to the Provincial Court on the morning of February 27, 2020 for aggravated theft (robbery of property) after On February 26, at Prakeab village, Rong Chrey commune, Thmor Kol district, Battambang province.
He confirmed that on February 23, 2020, the victim rode a motorcycle from work to rest in the rented house in the above point, when he arrived at the rental house, the victim got off the motorcycle. Locking the door, a gray Highlander car drove up next to the victim, got out of the car and hit the victim on the jaw, causing the victim to swell, bruise the jaw and rob the property. The victim was left in a gray handbag.
The suspect acted and got in the car and escaped.
Currently, the specialized office has built a case to be sent to the provincial court to deal with the procedure. Senior officials of the Ministry of Rural Development advise officers to reach out to villages and communes so that people can understand how to eat clean, drink clean and live clean in daily life
