General Vong Pisen Receives General Yu Asaguro, Commander of the Japanese Land Self-Defense Forces
(Phnom Penh): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF), met with General YUASA GORO, Commander-in-Chief of the Japanese Army Self-Defense Forces, on the morning of February 27, 2020. Lead a delegation to pay a working visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Commander-in-Chief requested the Commander-in-Chief of the Japanese Army Self-Defense Force to strengthen information cooperation as well as non-traditional cooperation, help train young soldiers for shifts, and expand exchanges between the two countries' armies. Both, too.
In response, General Yusas Guro expressed his pleasure to pay his first visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia, seeing that Cambodia's economy is growing and developing remarkably rapidly. He attributed all this to Cambodia's peace and political stability, which are key factors in economic growth.
General Yusas Guro has promised to bring Cambodia's proposals to the attention of the Japanese leadership to examine the possibility of enhancing the Cambodian defense sector, especially the capacity of the United Nations peacekeeping force. Is actively helping to train this skill.
