Asia-Europe Parliamentary Partnership Meeting Organizing Committee Summarizes Past Performance and Continues Orientation
The meeting was chaired by Dr. Nguon Nhel, First Vice President of the National Assembly and Chairman of the Organizing Committee of the 11th Asia-Europe Parliamentary Partnership Meeting, with the participation of the Chairman, Vice-Chairman and members of the Services to the Commission and professional officers of the General Secretariat of the National Assembly, the Senate, representatives of ministries, other relevant institutions.
Mr. Leng Penglong, Secretary General of the National Assembly and Chairman of the National Secretariat of ASEP11, reported to the meeting on the results of the work done in the past, including the work, content, documents and preparation of services such as hotels, transportation and so on.
He pointed out that after months of preparation, now is the time to start practical work, such as booking a hotel for a meeting place and a delegation car. The contents and format of the invitation letter of the foreign delegation to the meeting and the welcome message of the President of ASEP11 were submitted to the management for consideration and decision.
The Asia-Europe Parliamentary Partnership Meeting is one of the meetings of the Royal Government Asia-Europe Summit. This year, the Royal Government of Cambodia will also host the Asia-Europe Summit.
The 11th Asia-Europe Parliamentary Partnership Meeting, hosted by the Cambodian Parliament, will be held under the theme "Strengthening Parliamentary Partnership for Peace and Sustainable Development." Fifty-three ASEP members, 51 of whom are members of parliament and two partner organizations, are scheduled to attend the meeting in Cambodia.
After discussing many issues, especially the procedures and principles of ASEP, Dr. Nguon Nhel advised all members to continue to work hard in all aspects in a thorough and responsible spirit for the benefit of the whole nation. .
Please be informed that the Asia-Europe Parliamentary Partnership Meeting Organizing Committee will hold a meeting to review the work and set the direction for implementation once a month.
