(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Professor Mam Bunheng, said that for the third year in a row, from the end of 2017, the number of deaths from malaria was zero and the number of cases has dropped.
This statement was made by the Minister of Health on the occasion of the opening of the meeting to review the work results of 2019 and set the direction for 2020 nationwide of the National Center for Malaria Control, Parasitology and Bacteriology on February 26, 2020.
Minister Mam Bunheng continued, "The work to eradicate malaria is a very difficult task because it is a part that requires our officials and partner organizations to go directly to explain and guide the people in the community. And follow the instructions. In that, the Royal Government also continues to supply various materials that are in short supply, such as mosquito nets, spraying medicine to the people to prevent mosquitoes when entering the forest.
Minister Mam Bunheng said that in order to ensure the achievement of malaria eradication indicators in Cambodia in 2020 and 2025, we would like to encourage partner organizations representing donors, technical advisors and development partners to fully coordinate and cooperate with each other. Possibility with the National Center for Malaria Control, Parasitology and Bacteriology.
In addition, high-risk populations, such as migrants and forest dwellers, must be targeted to provide preventive measures to prevent the spread of disease and to provide health services to diagnose and treat diseases as soon as possible in order to prevent the spread of the disease. This disease.
(Phnom Penh): A cigarette factory was destroyed by fire until the building completely collapsed in less than an hour.
The fire was located near Prey Speu pagoda in Sre Chumrov village, Sangkat Choam Chao II, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh at more than 1 am on February 27, 2020.
Residents living near the factory said that at more than 1 o'clock in the morning, they saw the flames coming out of the factory in less than 20 minutes, the fire was fully burst, combined with strong winds, making the fire worse and burning until The factory building collapsed completely at 1:50 a.m. the same day.
The fire at the cigarette factory did not spread to nearby homes.
As of 6:00 a.m., the fire was still burning and authorities were using an excavator to help the fire brigade put out the blaze, with the extent of the damage and the cause of the blaze still unknown.
