Speaking at the meeting to review the results of the General Department of Customs and Excise today, Dr. Kun Nhim stated that "what is within the jurisdiction (Customs) is to find ways and implement measures to facilitate. "Maximum procedures to complete the removal of goods from customs, especially raw materials for the garment sector and the assembly of other commodities."
The Director General of the Customs and Excise of Cambodia stated that the main duties of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia are the core of collecting taxes into the national budget, while the Customs also has the duty to provide trade facilitation.
Dr. Kun Nhem further stated that the Customs has done a lot of work, all of which is in its regular action plan, while some of the work has been completed by the Customs and some of the work is still going on, especially in the challenging facilities. Recommended by the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
He added that if necessary, the Director General of the Customs and Excise of Cambodia will also coordinate with stakeholders, including autonomous ports, transport companies, etc., which we may extend the administrative hours so that the goods arrive immediately can be released. Goods leave the port, shipped to the factory immediately.
Please be informed that the Ministry of Economy and Finance on February 25, 2020 yesterday issued an official letter to the General Department of Customs and Excise to implement the Royal Government's measures to effectively reduce the logistics and transportation costs. Of the businessman.
The Ministry of Economy and Finance has instructed the General Department of Customs to carry out some urgent work as follows:
1. Adding green lane treatment to the import of raw materials, garments and parts and components for the production of investment projects, by maximizing customs clearance procedures and procedures. If necessary, the General Department of Customs can carry out subsequent compliance verification measures, including post-import audits.
2: Collaborate with the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia to discuss with the Association of Freight Forwarders and Customs Brokers to find a solution on transparent fees. In case of finding any concrete, inflated or fraudulent evidence, legal action shall be taken.
3. In order to implement the first point effectively, the General Department of Customs must cooperate and coordinate with stakeholders such as the Autonomous Authority, International Ports and Shipping Companies, etc. to ensure that the provision of this feature is smooth and consistent. Each cell, if necessary, can agree to extend the administrative time to carry out the work as soon as possible.
