Deputy Prime Minister instructs the Council of Jurists to continue to improve the quality of work to be more effective, contribute to the justice sector in the process of strengthening the rule of law (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Honorary Legal Officer Dr. Bin Chin, Permanent Deputy Prime Minister, Minister in Charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers and Chairman of the Council of Jurists, advised the Council of Jurists to continue to strengthen the quality of advice and input to contribute to ensuring respect and Maintain the principles of legal security and legal coherence in line with the political and socio-economic developments of Cambodia.
This instruction was made at the meeting to review the work results for the year 2019 and work directions for implementation in 2020 at the Friendship Palace, Office of the Council of Ministers on February 25, 2020 in order to maintain the legal value and long-term implementation. To contribute to the justice sector in the process of strengthening the rule of law in line with the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy Phase 4.
He also encourages further personal capacity building through research and development efforts and sharing experiences to increase legal awareness.
Please be informed that in 2019, the Council of Jurists helped review and advise on a total of 173 draft laws and other legal documents in 531 meetings, including 28 draft laws. 7 draft royal decrees, 55 sub-decrees, 24 draft decisions and 59 other documents.
At the same time, the General Secretariat of the Council of Jurists also helped to prepare 24 draft Royal Kram proclamations for promulgation of laws. 66 times and coordinated the work of 18 parliamentary questions and answers.
Through this work, it shows that the Legislative Council has achieved a lot of work results for the Royal Government on legal aspects and other relevant aspects in order to ensure more effective performance in 2020.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Wants to Ship Garments from China to Cambodia by Air to Prevent Factory Closures (Video inside) (Banteay Meanchey): While some factories in Cambodia are short of raw materials imported from In the face of the temporary closure of China, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, told the Chinese side that he wanted to send the fabric by air directly to Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's remarks were made this morning, February 26, 2020, on the occasion of the inauguration of National Road No. 58, the Cambodian-Thai border ring road, more than 174 kilometers long, connecting Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province to Samrong City, Oddar Meanchey Province, together with Mr. Wang Vinthean, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Sixty percent of the fabrics in Cambodia are taken from China, so I hope that HE Wang Vintian will contribute to help the Government of the People's Republic of China ship." "China can do it, and Cambodia can do it if some of the fabrics have to be airlifted to save the closure of factories in Cambodia."
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Samdech thinks that this proposal is possible because the Chinese side has a lot of Chinese planes, so only the option of air transport can save Cambodian workers from factory closures due to problems. Lack of this raw material.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen claimed that during this period, for factories that have a lot of raw materials left, it is not a problem, that is, the problem for factories that have only a few raw materials left. At this point, the prince pointed out that the raw materials transported by ship are still continuing to transport, but only add means, while Cambodia may also rent a plane to transport this raw material.
The Prime Minister stressed that now China should not be in trouble, if China is in trouble, other countries will be in trouble as well as car parts in China, and if not can be removed. Make some countries start to suspend the same production chain.
Apart from the industrial sector, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that another problem is shaking tourism in the world, because 100 million Chinese tourists a year visit abroad. Therefore, hotels and restaurants that used to receive Chinese tourism will face a shortage of guests.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that even Cambodia, while Cambodia does not block Chinese tourism, but China is careful when leaving, so only the Cambodian tourism sector for Chinese tourism fell to 90 percent and hope that Chinese friends will resume Chinese tourism later. Because China is discriminated against in other countries, but not in Cambodia.
Therefore, after the Chinese economy and the stabilization of the coronary heart disease, Chinese tourism will focus on Cambodia, this is where we need to see the relationship, and the decision not to close flights, not to evacuate Cambodian students and citizens in China. In Cambodia, the prince thinks that it is not just a normal right, it is a great right.
