ACLEDA Bank Plc. Will be the first commercial bank in Cambodia to list the first publicly traded securities on the CSX. The Bank plans to issue 8,751,391 new equity shares and 13,127,086 existing shares to the public.
He added that the bank will officially start booking building and invite investors and the public to set the share price of the bank between 15,000 riel to 17,400 riel per share. The final share price will be determined by the price set by the investor in the book building process, which will take place from 3 to 14 March 2020.
Dr. N. Channy added that after the Book Building phase is completed, all investors and the public will be invited to participate in the subscription phase to purchase the bank's shares at the final share price from March 23 to April 4. 2020.
He added that the bank expects to list on the Cambodia Securities Exchange by the end of April 2020. As the first commercial bank to be listed on the CSX ACLEDA Bank Plc. Will be a model bank for other banks in the banking and finance sector to use the Cambodian capital market to raise capital.
Dr. In Channy stated that the proceeds from the IPO will be used to develop digital banking services and for the general business purposes of the Bank.
He added that the IPO of ACLEDA Bank Plc. Will be considered as a "IPO" that encourages investors, individuals and the general public to participate in the IPO. According to its financial capacity. We have worked with banks to develop a preferred stock distribution method for individual investors who purchase 1,000 shares or less.
He stressed that the IPO is a golden opportunity for individual investors to become the most reliable and financially stable shareholders of the bank in Cambodia.
After the outbreak of bird flu in Vietnam, the governor of Kandal province ordered officials at all ports to take care to prevent and prevent the import of all kinds of birds
(Kandal): Dr. Mao Phirun, Governor of Kandal Province, ordered the relevant officials at all border crossings of Koh Thom and Leuk Dek districts bordering Vietnam to increase attention to prevent the spread of bird flu, such as restrictions. Tighten at the gates to the side.
