Samdech Sar Kheng Closes a Meeting to Summarize the Work Results of 2019 and Raise the Work Direction for 2020 of Battambang Provincial Administration and the Work of the Royal Government
(Battambang): In the morning of February 26, 2020, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior and Chairman of the Battambang Provincial Government Working Group, presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work results for 2019 and work directions. 2020 of the Battambang Provincial Administration and the work of the Royal Government in Battambang.
The ceremony was also attended by members of the Royal Government, Senators, National Assembly delegates from the Ministry of Interior, working groups of the Royal Government, localities, municipalities, districts, communes, leaders, civil servants, forces around the province, commune chiefs, commune chiefs, students, more than 1,000 students.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Provincial Governor, read out the report on work activities in 2019 and proposed the direction of work in 2020, as well as the work of the Royal Government to help the whole province of Battambang. Inauguration of National Road No. 58
(Phnom Penh): National Road No. 58, a 174-kilometer-long border ring road between Cambodia and Thailand, connecting Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province to Samrong City, Oddar Meanchey Province, was completed and officially inaugurated on February 26, 2020. This road on the territory of the former battlefield in the painful history of Cambodia took almost 4 years to build with a budget of nearly 123 million US dollars.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a keynote speech with the following key points:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the people of Banteay Meanchey for supporting Samdech, supporting the CPP and voting for the CPP.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech is very happy to join the people in the process of all nations, especially the quest for peace and end the flames of war in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech will not end his position by 2023, but will continue to hold the position of Prime Minister until 2028 and the following year.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the people who voted for Samdech to continue to lead the country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that National Road No. 58 achieved two important goals at the same time. The two goals are to turn the former battlefield into a development zone and to transform the border area into a border of peace, friendship, cooperation and trade.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he was proud to contribute to the people of all parties involved in ending the war and reuniting after the divisions in the past.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that Banteay Meanchey province in the past was ruled by four sides, but due to the win-win political power, this territory became a single Khmer-controlled area under the Royal Government and the same armed forces.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the unification of Cambodia from many parties to one party is not normal. Samdech Techo Prime Minister stated that this lesson of national unification can not be taught to other nations, but a source of pride for the Cambodian nation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the construction of National Road 58 has released more than $ 4 million for demining and unexploded ordnance.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that those who commented negatively on relations with China were wrong.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked and highly appreciated the Chinese government, despite the problems, but did not cancel the road construction project in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen tells the Chinese ambassador that he wants to transport fabrics, which are the raw material for making clothes from China, to Cambodia by air.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he does not want China to suffer, because if China suffers, other countries will suffer the same.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech had discussed with the Prime Minister the opening of the O'Neang Gate to connect the economic zone in Cambodia with Thailand.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminds the people of the former battlefield in Banteay Meanchey province that peace is very valuable and must be maintained together.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that as long as the CPP continues to lead the Royal Government, no tax will be levied on farmland.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanks China for helping to build roads and bridges across the river. Currently, more than 3,000 kilometers of roads have been completed and are being built and bridges across many rivers have been built.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced that Cambodia needs the help of all friendly countries, and if there are many countries to help Cambodia, China is also happy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen wonders why analysts see the advantages of China helping Cambodia and analyze the attack only Cambodia deals with China.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia does international politics with all countries, does not capture one country and abandon other countries like some negative analysts.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that during a trip to the provinces in 2016, Samdech helped build a school in Banteay Meanchey province worth nearly 30 million US dollars.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that condos priced under $ 70,000 are not required to pay stamp duty like buying an apartment.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces that he will promote Mr. Sokpheap from the Under Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense to the Secretary of State.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that many Cambodians who were divided from the past have been working together.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced that he will not exempt those who carry out separatist activities and will not give foreigners the opportunity to interfere in Cambodia's internal affairs.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the Ministry of Economy, the Ministry of Public Works, stakeholders and the people for working together to achieve National Road 58.
A total of 406 people were tested positive for COVID-19 on Tuesday, while a total of 52 patients died the same day. Also in 31 provinces and regions across China.
(Phnom Penh): Minister of Agriculture Veng Sakhon on February 25, 2020, presided over the awarding ceremony of the Outstanding Agricultural Community 2020 and the Recognition Ceremony of the Cambodian Agricultural Community Alliance.
Mr. Ngin Chhay, Delegate of the Royal Government of Cambodia, in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture, reported to the meeting on the organization of the Cambodian Agricultural Community League and the process of selecting the best agricultural communities, giving winners and selection exam subjects.
The Minister commended the five agricultural communities that won this year and highly appreciated the responsible efforts of all stakeholders, especially the General Department of Agriculture, which cooperated in organizing Important events right now.
He also thanked the German government and people for their continued support for agricultural development.
He stated that the Ministry has organized four outstanding agricultural community competition programs since 2015 so far, with agricultural communities being given the opportunity to participate in farmers' conventions to compete among outstanding agricultural communities to win annual prizes. .
The Minister stated that the Ministry has taken care to encourage farmers to organize agricultural communities in order to maintain the sustainability of activities after the project is completed, properly registered with the Ministry, have a clear leadership structure, have economic activities to serve farmers as Members will have a self-governing governing mechanism, an administrative structure, finances, as well as partner units and state institutions.
In this regard, he requested that DGRV continue to cooperate with the General Department of Agriculture to draft a national policy on the development of agricultural communities, as well as to support the Alliance of Agricultural Communities to function well in order to participate in the development of agricultural communities. In the future.
In the meantime, in order to provide input for the Coalition of Cambodian Agricultural Communities and the 5 Outstanding Agricultural Communities, the Minister provided some recommendations for basic implementation as follows:
First, the leaders of the agricultural community alliance must strive to fulfill their duties and roles well in order to serve the real interests of the members in order to make progress for the agricultural community. Make more efforts to become a model farming community for the benefit of farmers.
Second, to strengthen the institutional capacity, conduct external audits regularly to run smoothly, transparently, accountably, sustainably, and find business partners to enter into agricultural production contracts. Need to strengthen and expand more business capacity to become a strong agribusiness enterprise.
Third, the Capital-Provincial Department needs to update the agricultural communities and monitor and evaluate to know exactly how many agricultural communities are functioning well or stop working? If it stops working, the registration certificate must be revoked. Encourage other farming communities to become agricultural communities and be successful in their development process.
Fourth, strive to strengthen the structure and business to become a modern agricultural enterprise by establishing management mechanisms and continue to liaise with the Rural Development Bank and Agriculture and other financial institutions to provide credit.
Fifth, ask the development partners to continue to help develop the farming community further by taking them as key players in the project to help the farmers through the transfer of technology to connect with all stakeholders through the "public-private-development partners and Community.
Please be informed that for this year, the 1st place winner: went to Tasou Meanchey Agricultural Community, 2nd place: Our District Development Agricultural Community, 3rd place: Borey Aphivath Agricultural Community, 4th place: Anh Rong Samay Thmey Agricultural Community and 5th place: Samros Kampong Lpoua Agricultural Community. .
Based on the actual needs, this year, the Ministry decided to give the five winning agricultural communities a budget to be used according to the needs of their communities, which are in the order from 01 to 05, as follows: 16 million Riels 10 Million riels, 8 million riels, 6 million riels and 4 million riels, as well as commendation cards.
(Phnom Penh): National Road No. 58, a 174-kilometer-long border ring road between Cambodia and Thailand, connecting Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province to Samrong City, Oddar Meanchey Province, was completed and officially inaugurated on February 26, 2020. This road on the territory of the former battlefield in the painful history of Cambodia took almost 4 years to build with a budget of nearly 123 million US dollars.
The Minister pointed out that this national road was built in accordance with the level 3 road standard of the technical standard of the People's Republic of China, with a total road width of 12 meters, double-layer pavement (DBST) 10 meters wide. This road has 47 connecting bridges with a total length of 1,574 meters.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol stated that National Road No. 58 is a strategic road for national defense and economic development and tourism, located along the Cambodia-Thailand border, connecting the physical, institutional and people-to-people contacts between Banteay Meanchey and the provinces. Oddor Meanchey and with other capitals and provinces.
The Senior Minister emphasized that complete peace throughout the country has transformed the areas on both sides of the national road, which used to be battlefields and minefields, into areas rich in fertile land, with large numbers of people living and engaged in agricultural business. And rice fields, especially rice and many other agro-industrial crops such as cassava, corn, soybeans.
(Phnom Penh): According to a report from Fresh News Agency, until more than 8 pm on February 25, 2020, the fire of people's houses near Chroy Changvar Bridge in Daun Penh district, Phnom Penh has been completely extinguished. After the police, all institutions work together to save.
According to the report, the fire destroyed 12 houses, while the police used 46 water trucks and more than 100 water trucks to completely control.
However, in this social disaster did not cause any people to be injured. The cause and extent of the damage have not been confirmed by the authorities yet, because research is underway.
