The following is the letter from the Minister of Health: The Royal Government team visited Phnom Sampov commune, Banan district, brought donations to the back of the house to visit 5 patients and their families.
(Battambang): In the afternoon of February 25, 2020, Mr. Hem Theng, the Royal Government Working Group visited Phnom Sampov Commune, Banan District, led the colleagues to bring donations.
Visit the backyards of 5 sick patients and their families and help restore a canal to pump water to save rice in 3 villages.
Mr. Hem Theng said that seeing that 5 families were struggling to make a living, 3 families, the commune guards, had recently died and two others, a village chief and a deputy, had fallen ill and were living in poverty. Then, he led his colleagues to visit and distribute gifts to each family: 50 kg of rice, 3 boxes of noodles, 2 cans of orange juice, 5 boxes of fish and 200,000 Riels.
Mr. Team Leader would like to express our condolences to the families of the deceased and send a message to those who are sick to take good care of their health and recover as soon as possible to be healthy and able to work as before.
On that occasion, Mr. Hem Theng also helped to build a 230-meter-long canal to pump water into people's rice fields for 3 villages and to install 7 bicycles with a 1-meter diameter drain for use in the dry season until the next rain. This.
The families of the dead and the patients raised their hands to thank the team, always aware of the well-being and help the people in time so far.
After completing the work of serving the people, he also donated money to encourage the Phnom Sampov commune council and the 10 sub-village chiefs, each of whom received 50,000 Riels, as well as a solidarity meal this evening.
