(Phnom Penh): During a bilateral meeting between Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, and Lieutenant General Le Quy Voeung, Deputy Minister of Police of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, on the afternoon of February 25, 2020 at the office. The Ministry of Interior has pledged to further strengthen bilateral cooperation in preventing and cracking down on drug crimes along the two countries' borders.
Both sides stressed that the drug problem along the border between Cambodia and Vietnam is still a serious concern, so in order for the crackdown to be more effective, it is necessary to communicate frequently and effectively. As soon as possible so as not to affect the lives between the people of the two countries along the border.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said that in the past, the police forces of the two countries have cracked down on and arrested a large number of drug suspects while they were doing so.
However, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated that until now, although the global problem of drugs has not decreased, Cambodia is still highly committed to the prevention and suppression of this drug.
