Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh Makes 4 Recommendations to the National University of Cambodia to Achieve the Vision of the 2020 Curriculum
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, at the Closing Ceremony of the 2019 Training Course and Opening Ceremony of the 2020 Course, set out four recommendations to achieve the vision for the 2020 course of the National Defense University. To be continued.
The four recommendations made by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh include:
* First, the University Council of the Ministry of National Defense shall hold regular meetings quarterly, semi-annually and annually to monitor the conduct of training, retraining and retraining of officers, students, trainees effectively and as an experience. For continuous work performance.
* Second: For officers, the management, military personnel must pay attention to continue to deepen the reform, including the soft structure, such as roles, duties, capacity building, improve the quality of work in all areas responsibly and effectively. Develop human resources in line with today's advancing digital technology, in response to the organization's need for information technology in the era of the Fourth Industrial Revolution.
Continue to pay attention to strengthen and expand good cooperation with friendly countries to help build infrastructure, develop human resources, provide scholarships, study visits, exchange of experiences, organize training courses at home and abroad, give lectures, share knowledge and ideas. Strengthen the capacity of human resources to be professional, smart, modern technology with strategic ideas.
Pay attention to allocating various policies of the Royal Government, Ministry of National Defense to military officers, officers, staff, students and trainees to be transparent, effective, accountable and efficient through regular open economic announcements.
* Fourth: For students and trainees who complete all courses must strive to continue to improve their understanding and to use this knowledge in their unit better. Continue to collaborate with other participants to form a joint network to gather additional inputs for performing tasks in accordance with the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy and the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Reform Plan.
