This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presented Diplomas and Certificates to Nearly 600 Royal Students of Administration
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, February 25, 2020, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, presented diplomas and certificates to 575 students of the Royal School of Administration, 105 females. People after successful graduation.
In addition to awarding diplomas and certificates to graduates in today's program, Samdech Techo Prime Minister will also announce the opening of training courses for students of the 11th generation of senior officials, interns, senior officers, administrative officers, intermediate officers and general staff. 461 people, including 92 women.
The Royal School of Administration is about 50 years old. This school is the main school for the training of agents of public administration, in charge of one of the main functions is to recruit, train and train civil servants who must serve the administration of the Kingdom of Cambodia, actively participate in state reform and become non-partisan. The bias of change is the guarantor of the pluralism and peace of the people and a pillar of the country's modernization.
The Royal School of Administration has completed the mission of training and developing human resources and professionals with high skills and professional conscience to assist in the implementation of the mission of good governance, improve the quality, transparency of work and provide services to the people more effectively.
From 1992 to 2019, the school trained 13,055 female and 2,830 female trainees, including senior civil servants, intermediate students, kramakar students, senior civil servant trainees, and intermediate trainees.
Currently, the school is training 461 students, senior officers and interns, senior officials, administrative officers, middle officers, junior officers, 92 females.
Dr. Pich Bunthen, Minister of Public Works and Chairman of the Royal School of Administration, said that the Royal School of Administration has continuously strengthened and expanded the effectiveness and quality of the training program by continuing to deepen the reform of leadership. Management, training and recruitment of senior staff, student officers, kramakars, interns, senior officials, middle officials.
He said that after the Royal School of Administration was transferred to the Ministry of Public Works in October 2013, the school has continuously reformed its management and operations to ensure the effectiveness of training. And continue to promote research related to the public sector.
