He noted that in recent decades population growth, urbanization, agricultural prosperity, development of transport, energy and other sectors, along with climate change, have put severe pressure on forest resources, wildlife and biodiversity. Agriculture pollutes the environment due to wildfires, global warming, affecting human life, animals, homes, especially the forest community itself.
Once again, through this forest fire truck, the Minister hopes and strongly believes that this means will directly benefit the forest management unit at the local level and also provide Cambodia with more new technologies and experiences for the work. Effectively prevent and reduce wildfires.
At the same time, the Minister instructed the leaders of the Forestry Administration, relevant departments and community forests to take care to use and maintain this vehicle effectively, targeted and long-lasting.
