A group of international newspapers intervene to research Cambodian tourism to spread to the world
(Phnom Penh): Eight world-renowned media delegates from the European Union visited Cambodia to study the potential of tourism in order to spread the word to the world and tourists. Cambodia is already in need of additional advertising partners.
The visit took place from 16-24 February 2020 in the main tourist destinations, including: Siem Reap, Sihanoukville, Kampot, Kep and Phnom Penh.
The above delegation arrived in Cambodia at Siem Reap International Airport and discussed the recent developments and maintenance work of the temple, as well as the future development plans of Siem Reap with the Cambodian side.
The next day, the media delegation started a tour of the forest to study, explore and take pictures of some of the temples in the Angkor area and visit the elephants in Prey Kulen.
The delegation visited various exhibition centers and NGOs located in Siem Reap to learn about Khmer art, culture and civilization.
During the visit, the journalists also went to learn about Khmer food, with a detailed presentation on the name of Khmer food and how to cook delicious food at famous restaurants in Siem Reap.
On February 19, a group of journalists left for Sihanoukville, a coastal region of Cambodia, with the aim of capturing beautiful Cambodian beaches and world-class five-star resorts, as well as gaining experience. Stay on some of Cambodia's islands.
The delegation continued to visit some of the famous resorts of Kampot and to explore the world-famous Kampot pepper plantations.
Phnom Penh, the economic, commercial, political and heart center of Cambodia, was the final destination of the press delegation's visit, taking beautiful photos of famous tourist destinations and exploring their daily lives. Vendors in some markets, as well as visit the various tourist destinations, which appeared beautifully highlighted by colored lights illuminating Phnom Penh at night.
