(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, February 25, 2020, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, will present diplomas and certificates to 575 students of the Royal School of Administration. 105 women after successful graduation.
The students who will receive their degrees and certificates tomorrow include the 10th generation of senior civil servants, the 8th generation of kramakar students and the 2018 interns. Samdech Techo Prime Minister always presides over the awarding of diplomas and certificates to the students of the Royal School when they graduate to provide advice and recommendations to the students who are civil servants to strengthen the effectiveness of their work.
In addition to handing out diplomas and certificates to graduates in tomorrow's program, Samdech Techo Prime Minister will also announce the opening of training courses for the 11th generation of senior officials, trainees, senior officers, administrative officers, intermediate officers and kramakars. A total of 461 people, including 92 women.
