The Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs' reaction came after a number of foreign media outlets and institutions speculated that Cambodia may have allowed passengers carrying the coronavirus to leave the Westerdam cruise ship, a move that would increase the spread of the coronavirus globally.
However, on the way back to the country among the 145 passengers who left Cambodia in the third leg to pass through Malaysia, the country's Ministry of Health announced that it had discovered a new coronavirus on a woman. An 83-year-old American who entered Cambodia aboard the Westerdam.
It should be noted that the permission of the Royal Government of Cambodia to ship Westerdam, which sailed in the middle of the sea for almost two weeks, has been highly respected and appreciated by many countries and foreign institutions in the world.
The decision of the King of Malaysia is in accordance with Article 43 of the Constitution, which also states that the Acting or Interim Prime Minister will hold office for a maximum of 10 days until the Council of Ministers. As well as the new Prime Minister to be elected. In addition, the King also ordered the police force to maintain order and security throughout the country.
