General Kiet Chantharith: Immigration police continue to work with the Ministry of Health to control the Covid-19 virus
(Phnom Penh): General Kiet Chantharith, Director General of the General Department of Immigration, said this afternoon, February 24, 2020, that all immigration police continue to cooperate closely with the Ministry of Health. Check visitors for new coronavirus or Covid-19 and so far no suspects have been diagnosed with the virus.
Speaking to the media after attending the closing ceremony of the training course on the implementation of the program budget, General Kiet Chantharith confirmed that the international police, both land, air and water, are cooperating with officials of the Ministry of Health at all times to prevent and control all People are coming and going in search of new coronavirus, as this deadly virus has caused great concern in the world, especially in China.
General Kiet Chantharith pointed out that after the outbreak of the new Coronavirus, or Covid-19, the number of tourists at some ports decreased slightly due to the suspension and delay of some flights. However, it does not seriously affect Cambodia.
To date, the Coronavirus, or Covid-19, has killed thousands of people in China and other parts of the world, and has infected more than 70,000 people worldwide. In Cambodia, this is not the case, but the Ministry of Health and relevant institutions continue to take care to prevent this virus.
Missing car in Phnom Penh 5 years ago found in a garage in Kandal province, 4 provincial police forces joined forces to crack down on a suspect
(Kandal): Police in four provinces, including Kandal, Prey Veng, Kampong Cham and Mondulkiri, have joined forces to arrest a car thief who stole his car in Phnom Penh five years ago and found it in a car repair garage in Phnom Penh. Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province, while the suspects fled to hiding and escaped from one province to another.
Through the cooperation between the four provincial police to provide information to each other, finally on February 23, the police targeted the arrest in Prey Veng.
The victim is Theng Sovathdy, car owner, 38 years old, selling car parts, address: 80A, Street 156, Sangkat Phsar Depot 1, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh. The arrested suspect is Ly Phean, 45 years old, a taxi driver, residing in Ta Kao village, Samrong commune, Svay Antor district, Prey Veng province.
Kandal Provincial Police narrated the story that on August 18, 2015 at 2:00 AM, the victim left his car in front of the house when an unknown person stole the victim's car left in front of the house. Gone. After the car went missing, the victim went to file a complaint at the Depot Market 1 administrative police station, but was not found.
On February 19, 2020, at 12:00, the victim found his car in the car repair shop of Mon Sokim Heng brand in Kandal village, Sanlong commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province by changing the license plate Phnom Penh 2C-2067. After seeing his car, the victim came to file a complaint at the district police inspectorate for the authorities to search for the suspect.
Police said that under the guidance of the Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner, as a result of the four-day investigation, the provincial and district police authorities cooperated with the Prey Veng and Mondulkiri Provincial Police to arrest the suspect named Ly. Plan to continue to follow the procedure.
