Senior Minister Kun Kim Tells Leaders and Officials in Kampong Cham Province to Continue to Visit the Living Conditions of Families of Veterans Still in Need
(Kampong Cham): In the afternoon of February 24, 2020, General Kun Kim held a meeting to summarize the results of disaster management and the work of the Veterans Association in Kampong Cham province, with the participation of representatives of relevant ministries, institutions around the province and A total of 323 officials from communes, sangkats, cities and districts.
With the care and support of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the National Committee for Disaster Management, relevant ministries and provincial authorities responded in a timely manner and significantly reduced the death rate.
The General also stressed that according to the legal documents on sub-national disaster management at all levels, care must be taken to strengthen the capacity and structures ready for the upcoming flood season to ensure the provision of emergency response services. Urgently to the people, especially the most vulnerable, in a timely manner without leaving anyone behind.
The General continued that in order to achieve this better, it is necessary to cooperate with all stakeholders, especially the Cambodian Red Cross and relevant ministries, because the work of disaster management is not the work of the National Committee for Disaster Management alone. But it is the duty of all relevant institutions.
