Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued, "If Britain wants to make a free trade agreement with Cambodia, Cambodia always welcomes. We do not have any objections, and Britain has come to us to support the partnership between Britain and ASEAN. Also. "Cambodia will definitely support Britain to become a full-fledged partner with ASEAN, because it has a sectoral and multi-sectoral partnership. We want Britain to be a full-fledged partner with ASEAN."
Samdech Techo said that the desire for Britain to be an ASEAN partner because Britain is also one of the five permanent members of the UN Security Council. ASEAN needs to have a consensus and Cambodia will discuss with other ASEAN partners to provide support for the ASEAN-UK partnership as Britain leaves Europe.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that the free trade agreement with China is expected to be achieved in November 2020.
Please be informed that Cambodia's trade relations with the United Kingdom are growing from year to year. In fact, in recent years, the trade volume between the two countries has increased to more than 1 billion dollars, while Cambodia's exports outnumber British imports to Cambodia.
In the first half of 2019, the trade volume between Cambodia and the United Kingdom amounted to $ 466 million, of which Cambodia exported $ 450 million to the United Kingdom and the United Kingdom imported $ 15 million to Cambodia.
In 2018, the trade volume of the two countries was $ 1.083 million, of which Cambodia exported to the United Kingdom $ 1.018 million, while the United Kingdom brought only $ 65 million to Cambodia.
Cambodia's exports to Britain include clothing, footwear, bicycles, rice and other agricultural products.
