Samdech Techo Hun Sen's decision to allow the Westerdam cruise ship to dock in Cambodia has led to different perspectives. Many people, including those on board, were amazed and saw Samdech Techo's decision as a humanitarian gesture. However, some people assessed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen saw the political gain and attracted support to allow this giant American cruise ship to dock.
Samdech Prime Minister also said that Samdech does not need to use humanitarianism to please or buy encouragement from any country. "I do not need to use humanitarian means to buy anything. "But if they see that it is good, they give their support as a good reason."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed his regret that the BBC reporters who looked down on the humanitarian spirit of Samdech as well as the people of Cambodia. Samdech Techo considers the opinion of this journalist to be dirty.
The Prime Minister said, "I do not think that those who claim to be educated in the country are dirty and look down on the humanitarian spirit of a small country. I'm just pointing you out that your brain is bad, but you are lucky to be born in a rich country. But your brain is not sure that it is better than the brain of the Cambodian people. "Only Cambodians were born in poor countries."
The Prime Minister called the BBC's morale part of an inhumane act and did not have the heart to save lives.
Surprisingly, Samdech Techo Hun Sen not only allowed the ship to dock, but also went to greet you aboard on 14 February, the day of human love in Europe with roses. Even more so.
Allowing the Westerdam, which had 1,455 tourists and 802 crew members to dock, and Samdech Techo Hun Sen's face-to-face reception received the highest level of admiration and admiration from the passengers on the presidential ship. Donald Trump, the United States, the nations on board, and the leaders of many other international organizations.
Samdech Techo's decision to save the people on this ship led the people of the world to appreciate for the people of Cambodia as a nation full of humanitarian heart and love for humanity.
