(VOVworld) - Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia Neav Chanthana, on behalf of the Co-Chairs of the ASEAN High Commission and the Central Bank of Malaysia, chaired the 19th ASEAN High Commission Meeting in Hanoi, Vietnam.
The meeting was attended by senior representatives of the Central Bank of ASEAN Member States, the Asian Development Bank (ADB), the ASEAN Plus Three Macroeconomic Research Bureau (AMRO), the ASEAN Secretariat and the ASEAN Financial Integration Committees.
The purpose of this meeting is to discuss the progress and direction of work within the framework of ASEAN integration and related work supporting ASEAN financial sector integration to report to the upcoming ASEAN Central Bank Governors Meeting.
Topics discussed include:
According to a report by the National Bank of Cambodia, ASEAN economic growth is projected to slow from 4.9% in 2019 to 4.5% by 2020 due to the spread of coronavirus (COVID-19). There may be risks to the local economy in the medium term and have a significant impact on services, investment and consumption.
A senior NBC official said that in response to this impact, a number of policies have been put in place, such as maintaining inflation, increasing government spending, improving labor and technology, and financing spending. With the spread of the virus, increase infrastructure and connectivity in the ASEAN region.
