As a small developing country in Southeast Asia with a population of about 16 million, Cambodia has suddenly turned the world to the most attention and the major international media and television. Also interested in writing and speaking loudly.
How the Malaysian authorities are responsible for this is an issue that I would like to set aside. But what I want to say now is the positive impact on the national and international framework that Cambodia derives from the sharp decisions of Cambodian leaders in the fight against the Covid-19 virus. Positive effects in the national framework include:
First, the decisive decision of the Prime Minister Hun Sen has been admired by Cambodians of all walks of life, who consider it to be the most intelligent decision that was not expected because this decision. In the end, it brought great honor for our nation and people.
Second, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's message also prevented social unrest on the new Corona issue. Since the Prime Minister sent a message to the masses, there has been fear, especially the unrest, rising mass prices, etc. The national economy has been stabilized, livelihoods have been maintained, and social business activities have been normalized, while people's awareness of how to protect themselves through the practice of sanitation has been steadily improved day by day.
Third, while not panicking, Cambodians are closely monitoring the evolution of the Covid-19 virus in the world, which gives them a better understanding of how to protect themselves and its effects. On the world economy, including Cambodia.
In fact, shortages of materials and raw materials imported from China to supply factory production lines have forced industries in some Asian and European countries to close for a while, while the transport and tourism sectors in those countries have also suffered. Serious side effects.
Cambodia received full points from China after Prime Minister Hun Sen traveled to Beijing to show solidarity in times of emergency. Recently, Cambodia has also received medals from the United States and other major countries, as well as many world organizations in the humanitarian work to save the ship Westerdam.
At the same time, Cambodia has become a model for the world in resolving humanitarian crises and combating discrimination and as a symbol of solidarity in times of emergency, and especially respect for human rights, starting with the right to life.
Therefore, through this discipline, we can also measure the ability of our leaders and can continue to trust this strong man as a leader who can lead the future of our nation and people to prosperity. No one can compare.
