(Phnom Penh): On February 24, 2020, this is the 41st anniversary of the reunion between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen after the overthrow of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Through the official Facebook page of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia wrote an article reminding the suffering, despair, loss of wife and children and requesting that no more painful things happen on Cambodian soil.
The following is the full text of Samdech Techo Hun Sen:
I should remind that after not being able to ask permission from the brutal commander to bury the body of the child and take care of his wife who had just given birth, I was forced to travel with this commander to Peam Chiling commune, Tbong Khmum district (at that time Established as Peam Chiling District). We rested and worked there one night and one morning. In the afternoon we returned to the unit, passing through Memot District Hospital where my wife was staying.
One thing I should remember is that around mid-February 1979, I had a dream that my wife Rany was on the other side of the creek where the deep water could not walk to each other. Waking up at 5 am woke me up from a dream. I woke up, I was crying and could not find an explanation for this dream that Rany was alive or dead.
Kampong Ror district authorities call on residents to be vigilant during the dry season as fire engulfs 60 hectares of rice fields in three communes
(Svay Rieng): According to the report from the people in Kampong Ror district, on February 23, 2020, there was a case of fire in the rice fields in 3 communes: Samley commune, Khseth commune and Svay Tayan commune in Kampong Ror district, Svay Rieng province. About 60 hectares surprised the people and local authorities to help completely extinguish the fire at about 4 pm this afternoon.
