(Phnom Penh): Residents of Prey Tea village, Sangkat Choam Chao 3, Khan Por Senchey, 35 families, representatives of 145 families, protested again this morning, February 23, 2020, against the construction and sale of land in dispute between them. The 91st Airborne Battalion borrowed land from their village and refused to repay it.
The people claim that the dispute has been resolved by the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to divide the land into three parts to end the dispute. But with only two days to go until the land was handed over, the working group set up by the Ministry of National Defense withdrew and stopped measuring.
The gathering of their 35 families now does not want to find a solution, just want the working group set up by the Ministry of National Defense to follow the notes of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
According to the villagers, during 1987, the 91st Air Defense Brigade borrowed more than 9 hectares of Solidarity Village land from them as a temporary military base and promised to return it to them. When the villagers need it. Until 2002, they demanded the return of land to distribute to the children in the village where the family separated to live, but the military refused to return.
Only then did they protest to reclaim the land and make them and the above unit, which had General Sok Pang as the commander of the 91st Army, then confronted each other so much that there was a series of interventions by Relevant authorities and institutions, including the Ministry of National Defense.
However, this story is not over yet, it is still dragging on until now, while the fort border has been narrowed to take the land for sale and the land around the fort has been sold by the military, especially General Sok Pang, his wife and children His nephews all took ownership of the disputed land and abused it all. This is according to additional information from the protesting people.
Residents stated that after the conflict escalated, the Ministry of National Defense submitted a request for the distribution of more than 9 hectares of land, which is in a long-running dispute to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, and Samdech issued a note "059" dated February 9, 2017 Agreed to divide the land into 3 parts at the request of the Ministry of National Defense to end this dispute.
Citizens stated that then, on February 14, 2017, the Ministry of National Defense issued a decision No. 099 Sorn 2017 to establish a working group, including:
* First: Inspection Department of the Ministry of National Defense as Chairman * Second: Engineering Department of the Ministry of National Defense as Deputy Chairman * Third: Representative of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces General Command as a member * Fourth: Representative of the Army Command as a member * Fifth Representative of the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority as a member to measure and divide the land in accordance with the Prince's note.
After the agreement was reached, only two days later, the team withdrew and did not implement, and the reason for not resolving it remains a mystery until now.
