(Kandal): Saang District Governor Mr. Nhim Vandin campaigned to inspire all people to love the environment, participate in public hygiene and pack garbage properly for good health.
Mr. Vandin made this statement when he led government officials, teachers and students to educate business people on cleaning, sanitation, environment and littering in public places on 23 February. This 2020.
Mr. Nhim Vandin said that in order for our Saang district to be clean, it is necessary for all of us to start cleaning the environment in homes, schools, markets, pagodas and other public spaces, and store and pack solid waste properly. By adhering to the slogan Saang, we are clean, Saang, we are beautiful, start from all of us, a clean village brings health and happiness together, clean our village.
The district governor said that the Saang district administration has taken responsibility for the management of solid waste in the town, but there are still many challenges in providing this service, including: lack of space for storage. Put the waste in some commune areas. Private sector investment in solid waste management services is not yet widespread and in-depth.
Law enforcement for offenders dumping solid waste in public places is not yet strict. Changing people's attitudes towards taking responsibility for the waste they have created, rather than participating in waste reduction, packaging, proper waste disposal and not yet taking responsibility for paying waste management fees.
The district governor called on the people to stop littering in public places, to pack solid waste properly to enhance the beauty of the district, our dignity as a good example for the next generation to follow.
