The Cambodian Girl Scouts Association held a ceremony to commemorate and swear in new members under the theme "Diversity, Equity, Integration"
Ms. Sin Serey, the General Commissioner of the Association, stated that the Girl Scout Movement is a purposeful and fun activity for girls and young women, it is an informal education that provides opportunities for girls and girls to try out various activities so that they can have Self-confidence and interest in social issues. The Women's Scout Movement is a non-governmental, non-partisan, non-religious, non-racial, non-racial movement.
The Cambodian Girl Scouts Association is a non-governmental organization that aims to improve the education of girls and young women to become good citizens. The association has a mission to help develop the energy of girls and young women to become good citizens who are responsible for themselves, their families, their communities and their country.
Ms. Pech Chanmony, who participated in the handkerchief ceremony to become a member of the Cambodian Scouts Association, expressed her excitement, joy and pride to join the Cambodian Girl Scouts Association. Commitment to continue to lead with the support and encouragement of older leaders for the cause of social activities of the Cambodian Girl Scouts Association.
Recall that the history of the Cambodian Girl Scout Association dates back to the French colonial period, but its activities were cut off by two decades of war and re-established in 1996 at the request of the World Scout Association (WAGGGS) delegation, Ms. Leang Meng Ho. 16 people and organized for the Asia-Pacific Training Commission, established the committee and organized the NGO Association Month with the Ministry of Interior on May 17, 1997.
In 1999, the first executive committee was set up after training by the executive committee in Bangkok. In August 1999, the association received a certificate from the World Scout Association (WAGGGS) to become a member. On December 7, 1999, His Majesty King Norodom Monineath Sihanouk accepted the request of the Executive Committee as the Honorary Chairman.
Currently, the Cambodian Girl Scouts Association has 4,501 registered members in Phnom Penh, Kampot, Kampong Speu, Battambang, Takeo, Kampong Thom, Kandal, Prey Veng and Siem Reap provinces. The Cambodian Girl Scouts Association participates in national and international events for young women and girls. Drugs harm you and your family! Nationwide drug crackdown for February 22: 21 cases cracked, 54 arrested
