(Kandal): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, this morning, February 22, 2020, led a delegation of the Ministry and the technical working group under the supervision of a bicycle to inspect the quality of National Road No. 21 and have a friendly visit. People in 12 villages in Prek Sdey commune, Koh Thom district, Kandal province.
Inspection of National Road No. 21 by Senior Minister Sun Chanthon to ensure strong quality and longevity after detecting some irregularities related to quality after construction and advised the construction company, technical advisor and technical officer The Ministry must focus on quality first before the official launch.
After cycling to check the quality of National Road No. 21, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol met and greeted people in 12 villages in Koh Thom district, Kandal province, who were waiting to be greeted with a friendly smile. And eating solidarity food with a happy atmosphere as well.
The purpose of this meeting and visit is to connect the national leaders and the local people, especially to find out about the daily life of the local people. In fact, in Koh Thom district, there is a lot of development in the field of road infrastructure, in which each commune has a maze of concrete roads.
Addressing the people waiting to receive him, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized the importance of peace under the right leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and called for unity to maintain the peace achieved. With this difficulty to survive to continue to develop the society to grow even more. Ministry of Education to launch "Children learn, children know" on February 24
The "Learning Kids" program was developed through the experience and participation of stakeholders based on evidence from past research studies at the primary level in the past. The production of all packages in this program is supported by the US Aid, the Global Partnership for Education, UNESCO, UNICEF and many other NGOs.
The elementary reading and math kit for the elementary level of the "Learning Kids" program includes textbooks for teachers and teaching and learning materials for use in Khmer language and mathematics for first and second grade students. These will complement the existing Khmer text-reading textbook.
All first and second grade teachers will receive training and guidance on these new methods. After the training, they will receive help from coaches, pedagogical advisors on this new teaching method.
The math kit is being piloted in Siem Reap and plans to expand to other areas next year. To ensure the improvement of the quality of primary education as a whole, the Ministry will expand the implementation of the "Learning Kids" program to all primary schools throughout the country and integrate it into teacher training programs at primary school teacher training institutions throughout the country.
Through this program, the Ministry believes that at the primary level, all Cambodian children, including children with disabilities, will receive better development of Khmer language and mathematical skills for a solid foundation for further education at the next grade level. More.
First graders will learn basic skills such as reading letters, spelling to read words, reading sentences and simple texts, and writing. To learn math, children need to learn numbers, shapes, geometry and the basics of calculation.
