Mr. Kun Kim Visits a Safe Place for Evacuation in the Rainy Season and Inspects a Riverbank Construction Site in Kratie Province
(Kratie): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, visited Kratie province on February 22, 2020 to review the arrangements for safe evacuation. Flooding during the rainy season and inspect the riverbank construction site in Kratie province.
During the visit, Senior Minister Kun Kim stated that Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit always pay attention to the disaster work that Kate has in the future and at all times, so be prepared and prevent in advance. Is the best factor.
The senior minister urged the National Committee for Disaster Management and the Cambodian Red Cross to cooperate with local authorities to help resolve the situation immediately.
Senior Minister Kun Kim also requested the local authorities to help maintain this safe place and prepare roads and plots for people to prepare clean water, toilets ready for floods during the rainy season.
Mr. Kun Kim also instructed the authorities to pay close attention to vulnerable families such as the disabled, children, women and the elderly and to help protect this safe place from encroachment.
After inspecting the safe haven to evacuate people during the rainy season, Senior Minister Kun Kim also inspected the construction site of the river bank in front of Kratie Provincial Hall.
The river bank in front of Kratie Provincial Hall collapsed last season with a length of about 200 meters. Currently, the team is rebuilding this bank, but without repair in the coming rainy season, this bank will continue to collapse and may even break the riverside road.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister thanked the working group of the Ministry of Water Resources for their diligent efforts to build this bank.
