(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment has expressed regret over the repeated violations of the Prey Lang Network members, whose network is not properly registered and even violates the law on protected areas. This is the statement of Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment on February 22, 2020.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra considered the illegal actions of Prey Lang community networks and some civil society organizations as not a good example for community networks, associations, NGOs. The move also encourages Prey Lang community networks as well as some civil society groups to learn to apply the law and to abide by the law in force, to avoid conflicts with the law under the pretext of liberty.
Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment Neth Pheaktra emphasized that the Ministry of Environment provides close cooperation to communities, associations and national and international NGOs that are legally recognized and registered with the Ministry of Interior or have an agreement. With relevant ministries.
Currently, 19 community protected areas in the four Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary areas, including Kampong Thom, Kratie, Stung Treng and Preah Vihear provinces, which are members of local communities and are legally recognized, are cooperating. Together with the Ministry of Environment, patrol to prevent natural resource crimes.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment pointed out that the Ministry of Environment provided cooperation to the Prey Lang Network in accordance with the spirit of the Forum on Natural Resource Management and Conservation in August 2016, but the Prey Lang Community Network, which operates illegally, is dishonest. In collaboration to protect and conserve natural resources.
He also suggested that organizations such as Equitable Cambodia, especially Peace Bridge and Danmission, which have no jurisdiction and have not signed a memorandum of understanding with the Ministry of Environment, should stop their illegal activities in protected areas and After the Prey Lang network continued to operate illegally.
He said that if these organizations want to cooperate and participate in conservation work with the Ministry of Environment, it is welcome and should request a formal legal procedure rather than working illegally beyond their jurisdiction, which raises suspicions of dishonesty. In carrying out its work.
At the same time, the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment expressed regret that the Prey Lang Community Network tried to act illegally and distanced itself from the collective leadership of natural resource management and conservation with the relevant institutions.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra reminded that the Ministry of Environment together with the protected area community throughout the country, the provincial authorities of Prey Lang area organized a camping and tree planting program in Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary on 14 and 15 February 2020 under the theme Valentine's Day, environment and nature, with a total of more than 500 participants.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment called on the Prey Lang Community Network to respect the law and asked NGOs to strictly abide by the Law on Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations to avoid conflicts with the law.
