Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen Recommends 5 Points on the Occasion of Celebrating National Mother, Baby and Child Health Day
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and National Outstanding Member of the Joint Action Plan of the United Nations Secretary-General for the Health of Women and Children, made five recommendations to the people, especially women. Pregnancy and maternal health care for women and children for 1,000 days.
The five recommendations for celebrating the National Day of Maternal, Infant and Child Health under the theme "Future Health of Cambodian Children" on February 21, 2020 include:
1: All pregnant women should go for health check-ups, consult with doctors and midwives at the health center, hospital near home regularly at least 4 times according to the time and the doctor's advice. All preventive services, especially voluntary blood tests to check for HIV and syphilis to work together to eliminate mother-to-child transmission.
2: Please give birth at a health center or hospital with a well-trained midwife.
3: Go for health check-up after delivery, both mother and baby, take your child to be vaccinated against 11 diseases at regular intervals, monitor the health and growth of the child until the child is two years old.
4: Breastfeed exclusively from the time the baby is born until the baby is 6 months old and provide all kinds of nutritious supplements (porridge, all ingredients) along with continuing to breastfeed until the baby is. At least 2 years old.
5: Take the child or baby to the hospital immediately when you see any danger signs of respiratory disease, diarrhea or other infectious diseases and take the baby or young child who is thin or does not gain weight at all. And receive hospital treatment.
More mothers and children are now better able to access maternity and postpartum care, more babies are being delivered by skilled birth attendants, and more children are getting adequate immunizations. Samdech Kittipritthbandit praises the Royal Government of Cambodia for bringing peace to the motherland and achieving many achievements in the past year
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and National Outstanding Member of the Joint Action Plan of the United Nations Secretary-General for the Health of Women and Children, expressed his gratitude for bringing peace. To the motherland of Cambodia and expressed great appreciation to the Royal Government of Cambodia for achieving many achievements in the past year.
Especially with this progress, Cambodians have more opportunities to earn higher incomes and benefit from the Royal Government's social protection policy, which has helped civil servants to receive health care benefits. Consultation, treatment, receive maternity support, help each family be happy.
The remarks of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen were made in a congratulatory message on the National Day of Maternal, Newborn and Child Health on February 21, 2020 under the theme "Future Health of Cambodian Children".
