Kampong Leng farmers are harvesting more than 7,000 hectares of dry rice and some of the rice is sold to support their families
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Sok Rin, Director of Kampong Leng District Agriculture Office, on the evening of February 21, 2020, said that so far, farmers in Kampong Leng district have harvested more than 7,000 hectares of dry rice on the total land area. Which produced 7,600 hectares on a total plan of 10,800 hectares per hectare, harvested from 4 to 5 tons. The current market price of rice per kilogram is from 650 riel to 680 riel.
Ms. Saing Yun, a farmer in Thmor Rieng village, Chronok commune, Kampong Leng district, was drying rice. There is no monthly rain, which makes the rice in some rice fields dry, yielding only 4 tons per hectare, if there is enough water per hectare can yield more than 5 tons.
The price of rice sold per kilogram is only 650 riel to 670 riel, while the price of renting a rice harvester per hectare is 260,000 riel if he pays off the bank debt that he borrowed to rent a tractor and plow. After harvesting, he left enough rice to eat throughout the year.
Meanwhile, a driver of a rice harvester in Kang Kep village, Chronok commune said that this year's rice harvest in Chronok commune was less than last year due to less farmers than previous years due to lack of water. Farming is a rainy month with little rain, while in the dry month this year there is no rain at all, which makes the rice in the field is dry and lose some yield.
Mr. Taing Sarun, a farmer in Kang Kep village, said that although this year the farmers in the commune were less productive due to the hot weather, no rain and the rice was slightly cheaper than last year. Happy because the country is peaceful, the people have the right to abundance, can do business freely, including in all localities, there is development in all areas.
Separately, in Chronok commune, the Royal Government has built a red gravel road from Chronok commune to Kampong Thom province, which is convenient for farmers to transport agricultural products to sell as well as buy materials from Kampong Thom market to use locally. .
