(Phnom Penh): The Honorary Minister of the Cambodian Red Cross, Ms. Khuon Sodary, Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross, on behalf of the President of the Cambodian Red Cross, Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, presided over the closing ceremony of the 2030 Strategic Development Workshop on Providing Humanitarian Services Closely and Up-to-date. Time for vulnerable people.
The workshop on February 20, 2020 was attended by leaders, members of the Central Committee, 25 branches, capitals, provinces, representatives of the International Federation, representatives of the International Committee of the Red Cross, Head Office, Youth Advisers and Red Cross of Cambodia. 134 people.
Ms. Kittisangha Bandith brought the recommendations of Samdech Kittipritthbandit, Chairman to the workshop, especially the Branch Committee and Branch Executive Team, such as:
* Continue to pay attention to enhance the ownership of branches - sub-branches in institutional development and strengthen - expand the strength of volunteers and youth of the Cambodian Red Cross throughout the country.
* Must pay attention to the implementation of the roles and responsibilities of the Board of Governors in good governance, provide support to the executive team at all levels and strengthen internal unity to facilitate, consult, consult and solve problems together. Good team spirit, share information with each other, exchange experiences together for success together.
* Always remember that humanitarian missions are large and must be done on a regular basis to respond to the needs of vulnerable people and are a task that cannot be achieved by any individual, group or country alone. Yes.
* Maintain and develop the skills of local community volunteers to participate more actively in the study of vulnerability analysis, assess the basic needs of the community and the vulnerable, as well as increase the capacity of volunteers to plan and Manage work according to already trained skills.
* Develop an annual operational plan and budget to ensure that sufficient time is available for community-based vulnerability assessments, with the participation of community beneficiaries, volunteers, sub-branches, and CRC youth. Red.
Please be informed that on the occasion of closing the conference, four perspectives and pillars were achieved: the legal basis and structure, the quality of services of the Cambodian Red Cross, the sustainability of services, the development of the core sector, and the seven values of transparency and accountability. , Trust, Recognition, Readiness, Environment, Efficiency / Effectiveness and Commitment.
