Health officials call on parents of children with birth defects to be treated immediately to avoid disability
(Phnom Penh): Professor Chhoeun Vuthy, Director of Surgery at the National Children's Hospital, called on all parents and guardians of children born with paralyzed children to be treated immediately to avoid children with disabilities in the future. This treatment is free.
Professor Chhoeun Vuthy continued that if these children are left untreated for many years, it will be difficult for us to treat or even lead to surgery. "Therefore, newborns who are crippled need to be treated immediately, can be cured and can walk like normal people, if left for many years difficult to treat or even reach surgery."
He added that according to statistics, each year in Cambodia, more than 400 children are born with paralysis, a large number that requires better treatment if not treated. Children with disabilities will be discriminated against in the family and in society.
Furthermore, according to the research, there is no real cause that causes the child to be born crippled, but one of the main reasons that cause the child to be born crippled is the malnutrition of the mother in During pregnancy, there are various diseases because most of the children are born crippled in low- and middle-income families.
The director of surgery at the National Children's Hospital called on parents to bring their children to be treated immediately so that their children can walk and participate fully in society if they receive the right treatment. Parents must follow the doctor's instructions, and on the other hand, the treatment of children with birth defects is free of charge by the Ministry of Health.
Dr. Nhep Angkabos, Director of the National Children's Hospital, confirmed that deafness is a disease that occurs from birth to children and that deafness can cause children to be disabled if they are not treated properly. .
He said that in the past, the surgical department of the National Children's Hospital has cooperated well with partner organizations to open many training courses for doctors so that they have new knowledge and skills in treating deaf children. Highly effective in reducing the risk of children developing disability.
