National Council of Cambodia for Children Meeting to Study and Research on Child Sexual Exploitation Online
(Phnom Penh): The General Secretariat of the National Council of Cambodia for Children (NCCC) held a meeting on the morning of February 21, 2020 to announce the composition of the inter-ministerial technical working group to review and comment on exploration studies. Child sex on the internet in Cambodia.
The meeting was chaired by Ms. Nhep Sopheap, Secretary General of the Secretariat of the National Council of Cambodia for Children, with the support of APLE and the participation of technical working group members from relevant ministries, institutions and relevant partner organizations.
It should be informed that this meeting was held for the purpose of:
* First, to inform the composition of the inter-ministerial technical working group to review and comment on the research on sexual exploitation of children on the Internet in Cambodia, established by Resolution No. 203 NCC dated 25 December 2019
* Second: Update on the initial situation analysis on child sexual exploitation online in Cambodia
* Third: Ask for support and approval of the process and action plan for the survey on the prevention of the dangers of sexual exploitation of children online.
