(Kandal): Kandal Provincial Police launched an investigation operation to arrest a suspect in the case of threatening to hack and distribute nude photos in public at a factory in Prek Chrey Village, Dangkor Sangkat, Dangkor District, Phnom Penh on the afternoon of the 20th. February 2020.
A police official told Fresh News in Kandal province that the operation was carried out by the Kandal Provincial Police's light criminal police under the direct command of Brigadier General Chhoeun Socheat, Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner, and was coordinated by prosecutors. Provincial Court.
According to the authorities, the suspect, M. Oun, 40 years old, currently lives in a rented house in front of the Prek Chrey factory in Prek Chrey village, Sangkat Dangkor, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh. The 22-year-old victim lives in Kandal Steung district, Kandal province.
Police officials said that during 2017, the victim knew and worked in a factory with the suspect in Prek Chrey village, Sangkat Dangkor, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh. Later, the victim and the suspect had a love affair until they lived together, and the suspect always took nude photos of the victim in his cell phone.
In 2019, the victim found out that the suspect had a wife and two children, so she asked to separate, but the suspect refused. Until December 27, 2019, the victim was engaged to her fiancé.
Embarrassed and having to pay a bribe to the fiancé after the fiancé asked to resign, the victim also filed a complaint with the Kandal Provincial Police Office to intervene to arrest the suspect and take action. By law.
After the police received a complaint from the victim, they immediately investigated and arrested the suspect in a factory in Phnom Penh and build a case according to the procedure. Senior Minister Sun Chanthol: The Ministry is ready to build a deep-sea port to transport goods directly from Cambodia to the United States (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, on February 21, 2020, confirmed that the Ministry is preparing to build a 17-meter deep water port at Sihanoukville Autonomous Port to transport goods directly from Cambodia to the United States.
The confirmation of the Minister of Public Works and Transport was made at a press conference organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government of Cambodia at the Office of the Council of Ministers on the morning of February 21, 2020.
Mr. Sun Chanthol stated that the construction of the deep-water port up to 14 and a half meters was made so that about 93 percent of large ships sailing in the Asia-Pacific region can land when Cambodia builds this port.
Mr. Sun Chanthol claimed that today Cambodia can transport goods from Phnom Penh to the port of Singapore or Hong Kong, which makes it more expensive, so the Ministry of Public Works is studying with JICA, a Japanese international cooperation agency to build a water port. Deep so as not to rely on other countries' ports, that is, to allow cargo ships to come and go directly.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, National Road No. 10 is very important because it was built from Samlot district, Battambang province, through Veal Veng district, Pursat province, through the Osom Chak area to Koh Kong province. Therefore, the goods in that area, the Cambodian agricultural products that want to be transported abroad, no longer need to go through the Thai port of Lam Chambang, we transport directly from Battambang, Banteay Meanchey, Pailin to the port of Koh Kong.
According to the Ministry of Public Works, National Road No. 10 has a total length of 197 km, connecting from Samlot area, Battambang province, connecting with a corridor to Pursat province, then to Koh Kong province and down to Sihanoukville along National Road 48.
The border ring road will be a major freight route from some parts of western Cambodia to Cambodia's ports. National Road 10 will be built with credit from China.
