The questions that we, the Khmer people, have to ask to all of them are:
Do you want freedom for people to walk naked on the streets - Freedom to take pornographic pictures, post on Facebook - Freedom to commit genocide across the country and freedom to insult each other is called democracy or not?
It is remembered that when the Royal Government initiated the drafting of the law against insulting the King, the same group strongly opposed Lampa on the grounds that the law was to restrict freedom and reduce space. Democracy in Cambodia.
At this point, I still remember that some human rights organizations have been accused by the public of being anti-theft organizations. The reason is that in the event of a burglary or robbery, the human rights body does not care about the owner of the property that was shot dead or injured, but instead protects the thief for fear of being harmed.
Turning to pornography, they may not be aware that anyone today is blindsided by some of the women online shopping. Public opinion only urges the government to take serious action in this regard.
In such a situation, as the leader of a country that has an obligation to abide by the spirit of the Constitution, I notice that Prime Minister Hun Sen has always reminded, exhorted and issued a series of measures to protect the good culture and traditions of our nation.
At this point, I would like to express my strong support for Prime Minister Hun Sen's principled position, which states that "Cambodia continues to walk the path of liberal multi-party democracy in the manner of Cambodia."
That is right, because Cambodia really has its many unique and distinctive features in terms of geography, history, politics, especially the features of the culture, traditions, Khmer traditions of our Cambodian women.
In fact, the opposition to the good traditions of the nation under the pretext of democracy, human rights and freedom is nothing but in order to turn Cambodia into anarchy.
Over the years, I have noticed that the words freedom and democracy have been used by these groups as an excuse and a shield to trample on the law and violate public order forever. Freedom and democracy are used to protect the culture of painting and insulting them. And now freedom and democracy are being used by the same group to prevent further atrocities.
Therefore, the Cambodian people should know the face and name of this group clearly, because the real purpose and actions of this group are not to help protect the dignity of Cambodian women, nor to protect the freedom, democracy and human rights. Nothing.
At the same time, the Cambodian people also know and understand more clearly that there is no one but Prime Minister Hun Sen, who has always stood strong as a defender of peace, defending national sovereignty, defending true social stability and especially defending the honor, dignity and traditional culture. And the traditions of our nation and our Cambodian women.
