Samdech Techo Hun Sen Introduces 8 Priorities to the Ministry of Interior and Sub-National Administration (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on February 20, 2020 Issue 8 priority tasks to the Ministry of Interior and sub-national administration at all levels, pay attention and work hard to be effective in 2020 and the years to come.
The launch of this priority work took place on the occasion that Samdech Techo Hun Sen closed the meeting to summarize the work results in 2019 and the work direction for 2020 of the Ministry of Interior at the Ministry of Interior.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order for Cambodia to solve all the challenges in a timely and effective manner in 2020 and in the years to come, on behalf of the Royal Government, Samdech would like to provide guidelines on some important work that the Ministry of Interior and Sub-national administrations at all levels must pay attention to achieve the following:
First, to maintain peace, stability, public order and social security, strengthen business confidence in investing and doing business in Cambodia, ensure complete security for all national and international events organized in Cambodia to prevent Terrorism, transnational crime, money laundering and terrorist financing.
Second, the Unified Command at all levels must continue to actively promote the implementation of the policy of safe villages and communes in order to encourage the people's movement to join the competent forces in preventing and suppressing illegal drugs, theft, murder, armed robbery. Gambling, human trafficking, sex work, logging and illegal land grabbing, fishing offenses, mining and illegal sand mining and illegal checkpoints
Fourth, it is necessary to continue to improve measures to control various subjects related to immigration in order to participate in the prevention of terrorist networks, transnational crime, in order to strengthen national security and social order by increasing the thorough and effective management of immigrants in accordance with Law.
Sixth: Continue to pay attention to training, capacity building for civil servants, national police force and sub-national administration officials to provide new professional skills, knowledge and practical skills, especially social services, administrative services Security and public services are fundamentally relevant to the daily lives of the people in a transparent, accountable and efficient manner.
Eighth, we must continue to strengthen the relationship between the Royal Government and people from all walks of life, and increase grassroots activities to address people's challenges and requests appropriately and in a timely manner.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "I would like to express my appreciation and appreciation for the leadership of the Ministry of Interior, the National Police Force, civil servants and all levels of administration at the sub-national level who have worked together to achieve achievements. Many should be proud of in 2019. "I am confident that the Ministry of Interior will continue to strive for new achievements in 2020 and beyond."
Due to these challenges, on behalf of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has set out four main strategic directions to be achieved:
First, to continue to detach and maintain peace, independence, national sovereignty and territorial integrity, security, social order and macroeconomic stability, as well as to promote all rights and freedoms of the people in accordance with the Constitution and the laws in force in Cambodia.
Second, continue to promote the process of multi-party liberal democracy by ensuring the peace and sustainable development of the nation, national identity, dignity, good traditions of the nation and building harmony with all nations in In our society.
Third, continue to educate the people to clearly understand the implementation and exercise of rights and freedoms by jointly defending the Constitution, defending the King, defending the monarchy or the Constitution and the political system in Cambodia, and strictly enforcing and promoting the implementation of the law. And equal.
Fourth, to deepen the effectiveness of reforms in all areas in line with the motto "Internal reform, increase external friendships in an independent spirit" and the approach of "mirroring, bathing, scrubbing, healing and surgery."
