Ministry of Economy instructs officials to pay attention to health care and prevent various infectious diseases
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance on February 20, 2020, issued a notification on the promotion of health care and prevention of various diseases in order to prevent the risk of the spread of viruses and other infectious diseases. There is a possibility.
The announcement of the Ministry of Economy, obtained by Fresh News today, states that the Ministry would like to inform all leaders and civil servants to cooperate in implementing the following measures:
1. Increase vigilance and care for personal health by washing hands frequently with alcohol, for example, and other protective measures in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health regarding the epidemic situation of infectious diseases and Self-protection as well as timely treatment.
2: Monitor regularly or its symptoms that are abnormal or suspicious in any way. In case any officer has a fever or related suspicious symptoms, he / she must go for a medical examination immediately by notifying the unit to ask for permission to take leave according to the actual case.
3. All units must promote the prevention of infection in a proactive spirit by regularly providing equipment and materials to prevent infection, such as hand washing alcohol to serve the use of their respective units.
(Kampong Thom): Senior Minister Kun Kim said that the humanitarian activities of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, by allowing the US cruise ship Westerdam to dock in Cambodia has become a world-shaking event.
Mr. Kun Kim said this during a meeting with members of veterans in Kampong Thom province on February 20, 2020 at the Kampong Thom Military Operations Area Headquarters. In this meeting, Mr. Kun Kim mentioned the participation of Samdech Techo in the fight against the crisis caused by the disease "COVID19".
In front of veterans, Kun Kim told them that because of the high level of concern about the disease, many countries have left 41 people, or 2,257 people, stranded across the ocean. . But in the end, this unspecified cruise ship was allowed to enter Cambodia by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to help those on board return to their homes.
The ship Westerdam docked at the port of Sihanoukville on February 13, 2020. The docking in Cambodia made the tourists on the ship very excited and happy. Samdech Techo Hun Sen's human gestures have led to a lot of international acclaim.
Mr. Kun Kim stated, "Samdech Techo Hun Sen's decision to allow all tourists to park in Cambodia has made the world know our people as a nation full of humanity, a good nation." "Samdech Techo has brought pride for our Cambodian people."
Mr. Kun Kim continued, "Cambodia was previously known for its genocidal regime, which was a brutal regime." "But in recent years, our Cambodia, our people, has been known through Samdech Techo Hun Sen as a nation with the highest tolerance, virtue and generosity."
Please note that after being allowed to dock at the port of Sihanoukville, tourists and crew on board are highly regarded by the Cambodian authorities. They were warmly welcomed by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen directly.
On February 20, 2020, many tourists disembarked and flew from Cambodia to their home countries.
