They are also arranging entrance inspections, setting up national laboratories for testing, advising on infection prevention and control, implementing case management, as well as providing operational and logistical support if necessary. The Westerdam incident is a case in point.
"It is a very important time for us to respond to the problems that lie ahead of us," he said. Viruses are not limited to one country. Many countries are facing this problem. "How can we talk about respect for human rights if even the right to life is not respected?"
