(Tbong Khmum): General Samrith Dy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, and this morning, on February 19, 2020, inaugurated the roof of the temple, school and inauguration of achievements in Wat Sovanmoly called Wat Koki Chrab in Lneang commune, Tbong Khmum district. Tbong Khmum province is worth more than 90,000 dollars.
General Samrith Dy said that when the country is as peaceful as it is today, Cambodia has the opportunity to do everything, including the ability to build national development and improve the lives of the people to grow rapidly.
General Samrith Dy recalled that after the day of liberation on January 7, 1979, the Royal Government overcame all innumerable obstacles, went through all stages, all kinds of tastes in the cause of rebuilding and defending the motherland. Over the last 20 years, the country has developed at a rapid pace leading to significant economic and infrastructure growth.
The General appealed to the people that it is necessary to maintain lasting peace at all costs so that Cambodia has sufficient opportunities to continue to build and develop the society and protect the achievements achieved for the benefit of the motherland and the people to live in peace. Going forward.
General Samrith Dy also expressed his deep gratitude to the Buddhists at the foot of Koki Chrap pagoda who have jointly built many achievements in the pagoda as a way to promote Buddhism, because the pagoda is the main basis for spreading the Dharma and Dharma that plays an important role in educating the body, speech, and mind for all people to achieve happiness, prosperity and harmony in the family and society.
