(Kratie): According to the report, on the afternoon of February 19, 2020, a fire completely engulfed two houses and one house on one side, shocking the people and the authorities. For example, the authorities are intervening to put out the fire by using several fire trucks in Chhney village, Chhlong commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province.
Chhlong Toran, Chhlong District Police Inspector, confirmed that the incident occurred due to electric shock when the owner of the house was not at home, and in the incident of the fire, four fire trucks helped to extinguish the fire by taking the car of the police. Two vehicles from Kratie province, one vehicle from Chhlong district inspectorate and one vehicle from Krouch Chhmar district, Tbong Khmum province.
The inspector said that the joint police force and the authorities intervened to put out the fire by using four fire trucks to completely extinguish the fire.
The Royal Government provides funding to help restore water canals in Svay Rumpear commune, Kampong Leng district to irrigate more than 2,000 hectares of farmland, People thank Samdech Techo and the Ministry of Water Resources
Mr. Soeng Son, Chairman of the Water Management Committee in Talat Village, said that in this area, every year, dry farming is always short of water because the old canal is dry and shallow, which people can not restore, and every year. Damaged some rice fields and dried up many hectares of sugarcane.
But in 2020, at the request of the people, the head of the Royal Government also dropped the budget to help restore this canal, which is 2,700 meters deep and bigger to bring water from Stung Ta Kuon to irrigate more than 2,000 hectares of people's farmland. The canal has also become an easy way to transport rice to their base.
On behalf of the people, I would also like to thank the Head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, and the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, led by Minister Lim Kean Hor, for always thinking and paying attention to all issues. The hardships of farmers everywhere, especially the lack of water.
Separately, the manager of You Sarith Company, which is the contractor to rehabilitate the canal, said that the project to rehabilitate the canal is 2 meters wide at the bottom, 8 meters wide at the mouth and 2,700 meters long, and to date, the company has rehabilitated the canal. 40% and will probably finish this project by mid-March.
On the evening of the 18th, Mr. Sok Rin, Director of the Kampong Leng District Agriculture Office, also said that the canal rehabilitation plan is funded by the commune fund and the budget of the head of the Royal Government through the Aspay program (a program to promote new agricultural techniques). Resilience and climate change).
Mr. Sokrin stated that the project to rehabilitate the canal is very important to the farmers in Svay Rumpear commune, who used to have a shortage of water every year, but now they are no longer worried because Hopefully, when the canal is rehabilitated, their rice fields will have a high yield, which will be able to harvest the family's supply easily.
