(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on February 19, 2020, issued a press release stating that the Royal Government of Sweden and UNICEF have announced the launch of a partnership project to support quality education. And the environment in Cambodia.
According to the Ministry of Education, with funding from the Swedish government, the $ 8.3 million partnership will be implemented over a four-year period (2020-2023) to provide direct support for priority reforms and programs. In the field of education, as set out in the Strategic Plan for Education 2019-2023 of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
This partnership will contribute to the achievement of Cambodia's sustainable development goals, such as goals related to the quality of education and environment, gender equality, as well as health, nutrition, clean water and sanitation in schools that benefit boys and girls, especially children. It's difficult to reach their full potential.
