Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng: 2020 should not allow drug cases to recur in entertainment clubs
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, this morning, February 19, 2020, issued a strict order that in 2020, drug cases will not be allowed to return to bars and clubs.
At the opening ceremony of the annual meeting of the Ministry of Interior, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng noted that until now, in the entertainment clubs or large bars in Phnom Penh, there is no distribution or use of drugs for a while Recently, the police cracked down continuously.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated, "Regarding the drug problem, we will continue to do so, even though so far we have cracked down on large-scale crimes in Phnom Penh through bars, large clubs, no distribution of drugs. "It's addictive, but it remains a mess that we must continue to crack down on, and this year 2020 will prevent the recurrence of the use of big bars to distribute drugs."
Nevertheless, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng continues to issue orders to the Cambodian National Police, especially the Cambodian National Police, to make efforts to crack down on drug offenses at the local level, as this crime must not be allowed to spread. No. According to Prince Sar Kheng, if the drug case continues to spread, it will lead to difficulties in management.
Prince Sar Kheng also claimed that the drug problem, as we all know, has greatly affected many other areas.
It should be noted that in 2019, the authorities (police and military) cracked down on more than 9,000 drug trafficking and use cases, detained more than 20,000 people and confiscated more than 720 kilograms of drugs.
For all kinds of drugs, the police confiscated more than 720 kilograms and 913 small packages, nearly 100 kilograms of dried marijuana and 94,441 plants.
