Human Rights Committee decides to provide lawyers for women in detention at Second Correctional Center whose 5-month-old child died of severe pneumonia
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Human Rights Committee (CCHR) has decided to provide a free defense lawyer to a detainee with a small child at Correctional Center 2 (M2), where a 5-month-old baby girl died at the hospital. Severe pneumonia. This was confirmed by Mr. Chin Malin, spokesman for the Cambodian Human Rights Committee.
The decision of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee was made after receiving various media reports published on February 18, 2020 on the death of a 5-month-old baby girl on January 26, 2020, living with her mother. At the Second Correctional Center (M2) at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital due to severe pneumonia.
2: The prison monitors and sends the baby to be treated carefully, without any negligence, but because the baby's condition is too serious to save and the prison is really sorry for the death of This baby.
3. The Cambodian Human Rights Committee found that the detainee did not receive sufficient information regarding her legal right to defend herself without a lawyer.
4: The Cambodian Human Rights Committee decided to provide the defense attorney at the request of the detainee free of charge and to participate in all court proceedings to protect the rights of detainees legally and request that detainees He is also on bail.
Samaki Rainsy Primary School, Svay Teap District, is in need of school buildings, and the Ministry of Education is looking for donors to help build more buildings.
(Svay Rieng): Samaki Rainsy Primary School in Svay Teap district, not far from Svay Rieng provincial town, is currently facing a severe shortage of school buildings.
According to Mr. Ou Chhorn, Director of Samaki Rainsy Primary School, which is located next to Samaki Rainsy Pagoda in Prey Samphor Village, Sambour Commune, Svay Teap District, Svay Rieng Province, the school already has 3 school buildings, 2 equal to 8 The other room has 3 rooms with more than 400 students studying every day, one of which is the office and library.
He added that due to the increase in the number of immigrants, most of whom are factory workers' families with young children of school age, the overcrowding has resulted in a severe shortage of school buildings as well as classrooms. Arranged for some students to study under the monk's hut.
However, the principal, deputy principal, teachers, as well as parents of students at Samaki Rainsy Primary School, please call on benefactors and leaders to provide more support so that the school can build another school building to The students studied properly.
