Minister Veng Sakhon Makes Five Recommendations to Ensure the Process of Decentralization and Deconcentration in Agriculture
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, this morning, February 19, 2020, presided over a workshop on "Examining the Progress and Dissemination of Decentralization and Deconcentration in Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries." "Fishing" organized at the Ministry of Agriculture.
The workshop was attended by the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, Advisor to the Royal Government Delegation, the Head of the Unit and the Capital-Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, a total of more than 250 members.
Mr. Kuy Marindy, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Working Group for Coordinating and Implementing the Implementation of the Decentralization and Deconcentration Reform Program, read out a summary report on the progress made by the Working Group:
1: Organized the management structure of decentralization and deconcentration reform at the central level administration with the relevant units and the Capital-Provincial Departments of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
2. Prepared legal documents on decentralization, transfer of administrative functions, administrative services to the OWSOs of the Capital, Provinces and to the OWSOs at the sub-national level.
3: Prepared, coordinated and updated the functions of administrative services (agriculture), application forms, procedures, conditions, links, list of primary functions in agriculture to simplify the provision of administrative services at the sub-national level.
4: Prepared the relevant legal documents on the decentralization of the transfer of resources, including (people, budget, property) linked to the function and the transfer of ownership to the municipal-district-Khan administration.
Minister Veng Sakhon, on behalf of the Ministry and himself, praised and appreciated the team that has worked hard to fulfill its duties with care in the implementation of work activities for the past year and also joined in the celebration. The achievements of the team are as positive as in the previous report.
The Decentralization and Deconcentration Reform Program aims to establish management systems and structures to promote democratic development at the sub-national level and ensure the provision of effective, transparent and accountable public services to meet the needs of local people.
He added that it is true that decentralization and deconcentration reforms are reforms that affect all sectors, both institutional and work management in each sector, because these reforms require the transfer of functions and resources, both human and Financial resources.
In order to make this reform process smoother, it is necessary to increase the leadership, coordination between decentralization and deconcentration reforms with other reform programs, including financial management reform, public administration, law and justice, and Sectoral reform programs aim to ensure that the reform programs are peaceful, interconnected, and support each other effectively and efficiently.
In order to ensure the effective and timely implementation of the process of decentralization and deconcentration reform in agriculture, forestry and fisheries, the Minister has made some recommendations as input for leaders and officials at all levels. Classes for basic practice are as follows:
First, it is necessary to discuss and explain the reasons in detail about the strengths, weaknesses and the direction of implementation in the current context.
Second, to prepare policies, strategic plans, technical standards and service standards as a basis for orientation to the municipal, district and khan administration in the implementation of the tasks assigned by the Ministry and to coordinate the support work of the functions that are delegated related to technical capacity. And monitor and evaluate the provision of administrative services that have been delegated to sub-national administrations.
Thirdly, all units under the Ministry and the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of the Capital-Province shall consult and cooperate on some necessary tasks with the municipal-district-khan administration to ensure the efficiency of public service delivery and Basic development.
Fourth, make efforts to liaise with all relevant development partners to increase opportunities as well as strategic planning, decentralization and deconcentration reforms in response to changes in the current situation.
Fifth, to improve the discipline and working methods of civil servants at all levels to be better and to be able to coordinate and cooperate closely so that this disagreement does not adversely affect the work efficiency and performance. The work direction of the Ministry, especially the Royal Government.
