(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kun Nhem, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, said that the first forum on Cambodian Customs organized by the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce in collaboration with the General Department of Customs will help Promote private sector trade facilitation.
The statement of the Cambodian Customs was made during his presidency of the first forum on Cambodian customs at the Phnom Penh Hotel, which was also attended by Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce.
A press release from the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, obtained by Fresh News on 19 February 2020, quoted Dr. Kun Nhim as saying, "His Excellency Dr. Kun Nhim emphasized the importance of this forum in contributing to "Promote trade facilitation as well as increase the compliance of the private sector by mainstreaming the private sector on topics related to customs techniques and customs clearance procedures."
The forum was attended by key private sector members, professional officials of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, and 150 participants from relevant enterprises.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng noted the importance of the Customs-Private Sector Partnership, which was established in 2010, and praised the ongoing measures taken by the General Department of Customs and the Cambodian Customs to improve the business environment in Cambodia.
The forum was also presented by Customs and Excise officials on customs clearance procedures prior to arrival, e-payment, classification of goods and implementation of preferential tariffs under the framework. Free trade, as well as discussions on issues related to the implementation of these procedures.
