(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh advised the 14 district governors to pay close attention to the inspection work at large construction sites, especially high-rise buildings and without proper permits to ensure safety and avoid construction of non-technical constructions. That can cause problems eventually.
The introduction of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh made in the meeting on improving the quality and safety of construction sites in Phnom Penh on the afternoon of February 18, 2020, with the participation of relevant authorities, including the governor of 14 districts. .
Mr. Khuong Sreng also urged the district authorities to inspect all construction sites in their locality, especially high-rise buildings that have had problems in the past and collapsed cranes to carry materials up to the construction site. Lead to danger to people traveling on the road.
The Capital Governor also stressed that all construction sites in Phnom Penh must ensure the quality of construction, safety of passengers passing through the site and be properly fenced in accordance with construction technical standards, especially workers are not allowed to rest. Absolutely on site at the end of each working hour.
According to the statistics of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction of Phnom Penh, in Phnom Penh from 2005 to 2019, which was completed and under construction from 5 to 40 floors, there are about 1292 buildings.
This discussion meeting was held to remind construction owners to make sure that their construction must ensure quality, safety and follow the correct technical standards.
