(Siem Reap): The General Secretariat of the National Council for Social Protection under the chairmanship of Mr. John Narith, Secretary General of the National Council for Social Protection, on 18 February 2020, organized the Second National Workshop to Disseminate the “National Protection Policy Framework”. Society 2016-2025 ”to the relevant departments in Siem Reap.
Mr. John Narith stated that the dissemination workshop on "National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025" reflects the construction of the protection system in Cambodia, and would like to address Mr. Pin Prak, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap and the participants. All those present at this workshop, as well as GIZ, provided cooperation and support in organizing this important workshop.
He continued that with the vision of transforming Cambodia from a low middle income country to a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050, the Royal Government strongly recognizes The role of social protection system development.
He added that in the spirit of ensuring the income security of the people, the Royal Government has set a long-term vision for the development of the social protection system, which is to build a social protection system that is environmentally friendly, effective and financially sustainable as a tool to reduce And prevent poverty, vulnerability and inequality.
According to Mr. John Narith, the National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025 is a key document reflecting the social protection system in Cambodia, designed to set strategic goals for the development of programs to provide protection, reduce economic and financial vulnerabilities. People's stuff refers to the promotion of social welfare and unity, as well as the reduction of poverty to the maximum.
He stressed that the "National Social Protection Policy Framework" is considered as a roadmap for the relevant ministries and institutions to organize and perform their duties and functions more effectively. The presentations in this workshop will focus on the content and approach of implementing the original document as a core policy.
