(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Puthivuth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, said on February 18, 2020 that the digital economy is a major sector for Cambodia and ASEAN as a whole, and according to recent research. The size of the digital economy in ASEAN is expected to reach $ 200 billion over the next 10 years.
On that occasion, Secretary of State Sok Puthivuth said that the Royal Government of Cambodia recognizes the rapid growth of technology as well as marketing and the economy in the field of information and communication technology.
"The digital economy is a key sector for Cambodia and ASEAN as a whole, and recent research has shown that the size of the digital economy in ASEAN is expected to reach $ 200 billion in 10 years," he said. "Next year, e-commerce will be worth about $ 88 billion."
"While the information and communication technology sector brings many new opportunities, it also opens up many vulnerabilities to all of us," he added. Globally, cyber threats and attacks are becoming more complex and the impact is even greater. Cambodia may also suffer from that threat.
In addition, the government's Internet network has been hit by viruses, data breaches and modifications of information on websites. In addition, we have also suffered from DDoS attacks that disrupt the Internet in Cambodia.
At the same time, Mr. Sok Puthivuth stated that Cambodia needs to respond to the challenges of security, information and communication technology to be ready to travel to the digital economy in the near future.
Mr. Sok Puthivuth hopes and believes that this workshop will contribute to the Royal Government's efforts to achieve the goals set out in the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 of the Government of the 6th Mandate of the National Assembly in the Second Rectangle. The third economic diversification defines "preparation for the digital economy and response to the fourth generation industrial revolution."
