Citizens in Land Dispute Intervene through One Khmer Party Write Letter of Thanks to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for Providing Justice in Land Dispute
(Phnom Penh): Through the only Khmer party of Mr. Kem Rithisit, the younger brother of Mr. Kem Ley, on February 18, 2020, Mr. Sun Bantol, who has a land dispute with Tycoon Lim Taleng, wrote a letter thanking Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who gave him justice in a land dispute with Tycoon Lim Taleng.
Mr. Sun Bundol also thanked Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, for leading the team to further investigate Mr. Bundol's case in Banteay Meanchey province.
According to the announcement of the One Khmer Party, Mr. Sun Bantol filed a complaint of intervention to the delegation of the One Khmer Party, which is a member of the Supreme Advisory Council on July 22, 2019. A working group of delegates from the Khmer Rouge Party visited Tuol Pong village, Sangkat Phsar Kandal, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province on August 14-15-16, 2019.
On December 30, 2019, the party delegation received Notification No. 1900 dated December 24, 2019 by the Office of the Council of Ministers and the letter of mission of the Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection dated January 08, 2020. Signed by Dr. Huot Hak.
On January 14, 2020, Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An led a working group to further study the case of Mr. Sun Bundol in Banteay Meanchey Province, and on 18 February 2020, Mr. Sun Bondol was 100% fair. In the case of a land dispute, Duke Lim Taleng agreed to end the land dispute and reimbursed Mr. Sun Bantol permanently.
ACLEDA Bank of Cambodia and Bank of Thailand Launch QR Code Cross-Border Payment System
The public can purchase goods and make cross-border payment transactions using their own currency by scanning a QR code. The electronic payment system will provide convenience to tourists and merchants, as well as boost the currencies of both countries.
Cambodians traveling to Thailand and Thais traveling to Cambodia can make QR payments without having to carry cash or exchange money from our national currency to a foreign currency.
Dr. In Channy, President and CEO of ACLEDA Bank Plc., Said, “The National Bank of Cambodia has selected three banks in Cambodia, including ACLEDA Bank Plc. Domain.
He added that with the availability of financial technology, ACLEDA Bank Plc. And SCB Bank have been selected to collaborate to support cross-border QR payments. SCB customers can make payments in Cambodia through QR Code Cambodia and ACLEDA Bank Plc. Customers can make payments in Thailand via QR Code Thailand.
In addition, Thailand is one of the most attractive destinations in the world. The partnership with SCB Bank, the largest commercial bank in Thailand, will expand our cross-border QR payment network. Integrating the technology of digital leading bank ACLEDA Bank Plc. And SCB Bank, we are confident that our partnership will bring many benefits to local travelers.
He said that inter-transaction payment through QR system is very important because Cambodia is a popular destination for Thai tourists traveling to: Siem Reap, Sihanoukville and Phnom Penh. There are more than 47 million digital mobile app users in Thailand, of which SCB will have more than 10 million users in 2019.
