(Siem Reap): IDC Cambodia, a leading provider of telecommunications infrastructure services in Cambodia, has successfully deployed the first new carbon antenna towers in Siem Reap, reaffirming its commitment. For the design and innovation of sustainable infrastructure.
The first new carbon antenna tower was built based on two main benefits: to expand the communication network more widely and better and to reduce the impact on the environment in the community, which reflects the IDC is highly committed to sustainability and innovative solutions.
He said the new structure was lightweight and was installed on the roof of a building about 15 meters high. These structures can be installed on the roof without being fitted and attached to the building and do not affect the building as we do with steel structures. It can be installed in just a few hours and it fits the needs of the city plan.
To date, the company has deployed a total of 35 structures constructed from innovative replacement materials and equipped at a total of 1,394 locations with renewable energy.
Please note that IDC (Cambodia) is an independent company established in 2013. IDC (Cambodia) is currently expanding its operations to date and directly manages and operates 3,600 antenna towers throughout Cambodia.
IDC (Cambodia) Co., Ltd. provides services and solutions from start to finish on telephone network infrastructure services, including: antenna tower rental, construction of new antenna towers, power supply, network connection, telephone service and maintenance services on its broadcasting stations. Phone company. The joint cooking event between famous chefs in Cambodia and Singapore has been praised by national and international guests, and it is really delicious!
