Two MFIs merge into one microfinance institution to become bigger and stronger
(Phnom Penh): WB Finance Microfinance Institution Limited and Urie Finance Cambodia Plc. Merged into a single microfinance institution under the name "WF Finance Private Limited" and acquired Approved by the National Bank of Cambodia and the Ministry of Commerce.
The merger is another giant step for WB Finance to make it bigger and stronger, with a stake in Uri Bank, one of the largest commercial banks in Korea.
WB Finance offers a wide range of financial products and services, including savings and loan services, mobile banking and money transfer services. All accounts of Uri Finance MFI clients will be transferred to WB Finance under the same terms and conditions.
"This merger process would not have been possible without the dedicated efforts of the management and staff of both institutions, our venture bank team and our significant support," he said. National Bank of Cambodia, Ministry of Commerce, authorities, clients, partners and other stakeholders.
"We truly thank and appreciate the clients of both institutions for their continued use of our financial products and services, and in the near future we will be a thriving financial institution," he added. With the people of Cambodia by providing financial support, developing new products such as loans for government employees and the development of a series of social programs.
"This is another milestone for WB Finance after the sale of its stake in Uri Bank in 2018 and is now merged with Uri Finance. "One of the best microfinance institutions in Cambodia, and we have completed the process of integration smoothly and comprehensively, focusing on this process."
She added that WB Finance will continue to provide financial services to Cambodia across 25 provinces through its 136 branches, providing financial products and services to meet the needs of customers with adherence to its mission of becoming an institution. Leading finance that provides economic potential for Cambodia's growth.
Please be informed that WB Finance Microfinance Institution Private Limited and WB Finance Microfinance Institution is a deposit-taking institution licensed by the National Bank of Cambodia and a family member of Uri Bank, a leading commercial bank in Korea.
WB Finance has been providing financial services to Cambodians for over 20 years, offering a wide range of financial products and services, including loans, savings, remittances and mobile banking. By the end of 2019, WB Finance had total assets of US $ 377 million and a total loan portfolio of US $ 336 million.
Ministry of Land Management: 5 affordable housing projects have been implemented in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction announced on February 17, 2020 that under the National Policy on Housing and the Policy on Incentives and the Establishment of a National Program for Affordable Housing Development, Five affordable housing projects are underway in Cambodia.
The five affordable housing projects include two in Phnom Penh, two in Kandal and one in Banteay Meanchey. Homes that are private will be sold for $ 30,000 or less.
It should be noted that on the afternoon of February 17, 2020, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, also inspected the progress of Affordable Home Development's affordable housing development project, which is one of the five projects. Leu is located in Koh Kor village, Rokar Khpos commune, Saang district, Kandal province, about 8 km from Takhmao city.
The project covers a total area of 23 hectares with 2,457 houses with an investment of about 73 million US dollars. So far, the company has sold 1,088 houses, accounting for 44% of the total number of houses, of which more than 23% are government employees. The company has completed the construction of 603 houses, plans to hand over the houses to customers during the Khmer New Year and plans to complete the construction of the entire project before the end of 2020.
(Phnom Penh): According to the three sub-decrees of the Royal Government on the functions and structure of the municipal, district and Khan administration, the Ministry of Tourism has transferred some of the functions, resources and administrative services to the municipal, district and Khan administration to decide on the provision of services. The public involved in tourism is getting closer to the local people.
Undersecretary of State Duong Virak said that in the past, the Ministry of Tourism has transferred 18 functions and administrative services to the OWSO in all Capital-Provincial Administration Halls, and then 10 more administrative services were provided. Delivered to OWSOs in all district, municipal, and khan administrations throughout the country.
He added that the functions and administrative services provided by the Ministry of Tourism to the municipal, district and khan administration include: licensing services, tourism, guesthouses (from 8 rooms down), room rental services, restaurants for rent, restaurants, transportation, karaoke shops. Massage and tourism management.
Mr. Duong Virak added that, however, all the functions and administrative services that the Ministry has transferred to the Capital-Province, Municipality-District-Khan Administration need more training for sub-national officials to be confident and have High responsibility, effective.
