Director of the Royal School of Administration forbids trainees to send substitute students
(Phnom Penh): Speaking at the Leadership Development Training for Reform, Mr. Youk Bunna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Function and Director of the Royal School of Administration, stated that each training course is very important and therefore requires all participants to participate directly. Do not assign others to participate instead.
The training course mentioned by Mr. Youk Bunna took place in two shifts, including the morning shift and the afternoon shift, from February 17-28, 2020. Each shift has about 40 participants from 30 ministries and institutions (3 participants from one ministry and institution) start from 8: 30-12: 00 for morning shift and from 2: 00-5: 30 for Afternoon shift at the Cambodia-Singapore Cooperation Center, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Youk Bunna continued that the Ministry of Civil Service and the Singapore Institute of Civil Service, with the Royal School of Administration as its staff, have organized leadership development training for this reform in order to make the leadership trainees better able to Lead officers and units in the rapidly evolving facilities as they are today.
On that occasion, the Secretary of State stated that this training course requires all participants to be present at least 80% to be considered successful graduates and can obtain a certificate of education.
Mr. Youk Bunna highlighted the background that made this training course possible because with the support of the Embassy of Singapore in Cambodia agreed to support the capacity building project for the leadership, Director General and Deputy Director General of the institution. Implemented by this project are the Singapore Civil Service Institute (CSC) and the Royal School of Administration.
On November 4-8, 2019, the CSC Working Group and the Royal School of Administration began interviews with the Secretaries of State and Undersecretaries of State from nine ministries, and meetings with relevant officials: the Director General, the Deputy Director General and the Chairman - Deputy Head of Department.
Samdech stated that after a thorough medical examination of some tourists who did not have positive signs of Kovid 19 virus (Corona), the Royal Government of Cambodia has now allowed 500 tourists to stay temporarily at Sokha Hotel in Phnom Penh to Arrange for a plane ticket from Cambodia to their home country.
