Angkor Heritage Living is part of the tourist attraction outside the temple
(Siem Reap): Apart from the famous temples, Angkor Park still has a lot of living heritage called intangible heritage, such as customs, traditions, rituals, prayers, religions, as well as crafts and daily lifestyles that the people of Angkor have adhered to and Executed for generations.
On the occasion of the 25th anniversary of the establishment of the APSARA Authority, Mr. Hang Pov, Director General of the APSARA Authority, said that these are all things that tourists want to see, want to know and want to explore about the heritage outside the temple.
Village arrangements, traditional handicrafts, ox-cart transportation are all additional products for experienced tourists and bring them to see the way of life of the Cambodian people in the past. Angkor.
He added that at present, some traditions that people in other areas have forgotten or not paid much attention to, and the people of Angkor are still continuing to practice, such as shaving ceremony, ascension ceremony, rain ceremony, soul call ceremony, etc. .
The Apsara Authority, which is responsible for managing and developing the Angkor resort, is paying close attention to these traditions, ensuring that these traditions can survive forever and attract more tourists.
It should be noted that the Angkor area or Angkor resort, which was registered as a World Heritage Site in 1992, has a total area of 401 square kilometers, which includes 91 archeological sites, archeological sites, the environment and human communities.
