(Kampong Thom): After seeing the poor living conditions and lack of shelter of a family of veterans in Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, arranged to build a house for veterans. This picture.
Chuon Veth, a disabled man with four children and eight grandchildren in his care, is a veteran who is struggling and receiving kindness from Samdech Kittipritthbandit to provide a house for shelter. Currently, Mr. Chuon Vet is building a house for living in a size of about 4 meters by 6 meters. But due to lack of livelihood, the construction process has stalled.
After examining the difficult situation, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen decided to ask Senior Minister Kun Kim to build this house for Mr. Chuon Veth until it is ready and expand from 4 meters by 6 meters to 6 meters by 7 meters. Also.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, in addition to managing the construction of a house for the veteran, also provided an additional 4 million to the veteran to pay for land injection and medical treatment for his son.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, on behalf of the Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, expressed his deepest gratitude and appreciation to Samdech Kittipritthbandit for always taking care of the well-being of the veterans and resolving all difficulties.
After receiving the kindness from Samdech Kittipritthbandit, Mr. Chhuon Veth and his family were very happy and could not find anything to compare with. Mr. Chuon Vet said that Samdech Kittipritthbandit was his living God who came to help solve difficulties and provide shelter for him and his family.
The disabled veteran said that he and his family will remember for the rest of his life the virtuous and compassionate gestures and compassion of Samdech Kittiprittbandit.
With this incomparable joy, Mr. Chhuon Vet raised his hand to pray to the sacred objects according to the Governor to take care of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as his beloved sons and daughters and grandchildren. Better to lead the development of the Cambodian nation more prosperous and a cool shade for the Cambodian people.
