Please be informed that on 12 February 2020, the European Commission (EU) issued a decision to cut parts of the EBA. According to the private sector, partial cuts in the preferential tariff system amount to about $ 140 million on 40 Cambodian products.
GMAC says employment in these sectors, supported by the EBA, now exceeds 750,000 and contributes to lifting millions of Cambodians out of poverty. Most of the workers are women who take care of the family, take care of the health and well-being of the children and provide direct income to more than 20% of the families in Cambodia.
GMAC urges the European Commission and the European Parliament to reconsider this decision, taking into account the values of the program, which was implemented almost 20 years ago instead of development, poverty reduction and dignity. Of work. "The EBA program is a clear success in Cambodia in achieving these goals. Partial withdrawal of this program will only lead to job loss and poverty."
