He claimed that since the process, the school management has been trying to mobilize philanthropists to develop the school in order to make the school more prosperous and increase the trust of parents or guardians of students in the school. . Ministry of Rural Development presents 15 work directions for implementation in 2020 (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chan Darong, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Rural Development, said that the Ministry has set 15 work goals for implementation in 2020.
Speaking at a press conference on "Updates and Progress of the Ministry of Rural Development" organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government of Cambodia on the morning of February 17, 2020, Mr. Chan Darong said that the Ministry has set out an action plan for the implementation of the group. Jobs and professional officers under the following supervision:
1: Continue to actively implement the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 to be more active for the rural development sector to contribute to achieving 7% economic growth and reduce poverty to below 10%.
2: Continue to develop the capacity of civil servants and develop institutions to better improve the work of the Ministry.
3. Research new technologies to build climate-resilient rural roads.
4: Study, project and implementation of construction, maintenance and repair of rural roads, bridges and all kinds of artistic structures must be carried out in a timely manner with quality, aesthetics, resilience to climate change and must give priority to the project in accordance with the necessary And budget availability.
5. Encourage all units that implement direct financing projects and cooperation projects with development partners on construction, maintenance and repair and all kinds of artwork to have quality certification of samples, materials and raw materials from the laboratory of the Ministry of Rural Development.
7. Collect data on roads, bridges, sewers, water supply systems and toilets in rural areas as a basis for the preparation of a master plan for consistency.
8. Promote the registration of indigenous peoples to the maximum. Promote the development of indigenous peoples to stand out as in other areas, in terms of physical infrastructure and essential public services, and preserve the good traditions, languages spoken in each community.
9. Increase rural water supply services to achieve 90% of the target by 2023 as stated in the Strategic Plan for Rural Development 2019-2023. Continue to coordinate between all stakeholders on water supply work through the distribution network.
11: Prepare to amend Sub-Decree No. 51 on the Organization and Functioning of the Ministry of Rural Development, Sub-Decree No. 141 on the Establishment of the Steering Committee for the Control of Weight-Lifting Vehicles and Sub-Decree No. 197 on Network Forage Land Management National roads and railways.
12. Develop a national policy on rural road development and update technical standards on the construction, rehabilitation, maintenance and repair of rural roads and artistic structures.
13. Promote rural economic activity and entrepreneurship to support increasing household income by raising livestock, fish, crabs and beekeeping to help prevent risky migration. Promote the implementation of mobile training programs.
14. Strengthen and expand good cooperation with private sector partners and friendly countries to mobilize new financial, technical and technological resources to support rural development.
15. Collaborate with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to develop procedures and methods for developing a master plan for road development, design and project prioritization. Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi: Most women in prison are involved in drug offenses
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs and Chair of the "Cambodian National Council for Women", emphasized that most of the women currently incarcerated in prison are involved in drug offenses.
According to a report by the General Department of Prisons of the Ministry of Interior, more than 3,000 women are currently incarcerated out of an estimated 36,000 inmates.
The Royal Government of Cambodia issued a circular in June 2019 requiring the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and the Ministry of Women's Affairs to continue to examine the feasibility and increase vocational training programs to create job opportunities and improve health and hygiene. For female prisoners. This was further confirmed by Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi
In addition, the Cambodian Human Rights Committee also inspected the human rights situation in prisons and three correctional centers and investigated and resolved cases involving women in prisons through the provision of legal services.
According to the National Anti-Drug Authority, in 2019, both police and military police cracked down on more than 9,000 drug trafficking and use cases, detaining more than 20,000 people and confiscating more than 720 kilograms of drugs. Of the more than 20,000 detainees, more than 1,000 were women.
General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, emphasized that Cambodia continues to face drug problems due to the problem of drug production in the world.
At the same time, the Secretary-General also stressed that it is always the most difficult thing to deal quickly with such infectious diseases, but for China has responded very strongly and very interestingly. The death toll from the new coronavirus (COVID-19) in China has risen to 1,770, and the number of infected people has risen to more than 70, authorities said on Monday morning. 000 people.
