On that occasion, Mr. Phan Chanthul reached out to the Principal of Hun Sen High School, Tep Nimmith City, Pailin City and all teachers to continue to provide additional skills to Scout students to better understand the tools provided. In particular, to participate in the maintenance of long-term protection to strengthen the technical ability of playing music better.
(Phnom Penh): A delegation of the Cambodian Cement Industry Association (CCMA) led by Mr. Oknha Leang Meng, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Association, on February 17, 2020, led the leaders of the Cement Industry Association of Cambodia to discuss and pay a courtesy call. With Mr. Ty Norin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Mines and Energy.
Mr. Put Chantarith, Secretary General of the Cement Industry Association of Cambodia, confirmed to Fresh News that the purpose of the courtesy call and discussion was to inform the Ministry of Mines that there are five companies for the Cement Industry Association of Cambodia. Each requires 30 megawatts of electricity, so the total power required is 150 megawatts.
In this courtesy call and discussion, Mr. Oknha Leang Meng, on behalf of the Cement Industry Association of Cambodia, requested the Ministry of Mines and Energy to provide sufficient electricity to the Cement Industry Association of Cambodia to have sufficient capacity for its cement production process. This is according to Mr. Put Chantarith.
Ministry of Labor Spokesperson: Even without EBA, Cambodia will always make improving the working conditions of its workers a priority
(Phnom Penh): While there has been criticism of the EU's recent decision to withdraw parts of the EBA from Cambodia, Heng Sour, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, stressed that despite With or without the EBA from the European Union, Cambodia has already decided that improving the working conditions and freedoms of workers is always a priority of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Heng Sour made this statement during a consultative meeting on the joint plan of the Better Factories Cambodia (BFC) project held at the Cambodiana Hotel on February 17, 2020.
According to Heng Sour, when Europe decided to withdraw parts of the EBA, it was not because Cambodia did not provide conditions for workers' work or freedoms to professional organizations, but because of political issues that some countries required Cambodia to comply with. Their foreign policy. However, they should not link working conditions to politics.
"Cambodians demand justice, Cambodia does not want to be the best, but ask for equality in decision-making and common sense of what Cambodia is trying to do," he said.
He claimed that Cambodia had prepared a package in response to any impact on Cambodian trade due to unfair decisions. With or without the EBA, the Royal Government of Cambodia has already determined that improving working conditions, respecting workers' freedoms is a priority, and therefore Cambodia is linking trade to working conditions.
Ms. Ong Sona, who was originally just a teacher, said that until today, it is not easy, there are many obstacles, both sales and collection, distribution representatives. However, because N.N.P products received a lot of support from customers and consumers, and also received encouragement and encouragement from her own husband, she decided to invest exclusively in N.N.P products in Siem Reap.
