Ministry of Tourism to open offices in cities, districts, Khans required for tourism
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has requested the decision of the Ministry of Interior to keep the existing tourism offices in some cities, districts and Khans and to open more tourism offices in cities, districts and Khans with great potential and necessary for tourism while It is estimated that all cities are essential for tourism.
Mr. Duong Virak said that during the discussion on the draft sub-decree on the state structure of Ban Krong Srok Khan (3 different sub-decrees), the Ministry of Tourism had made a request to the Ministry of Interior to keep the existing tourism office in Towns, districts, Khans, that is, please save.
For other cities, districts, and Khans, one of the essentials for tourism and there is no tourism office yet, please create more new tourism offices.
The Undersecretary of State said that the sub-decree on the structure of the state, municipality, district and Khan has clearly stated that it allows the Ministry of Tourism to make a request to the Ministry of Interior if any city, district or Khan has tourism potential and needs to establish a tourism office to open a new tourism office. In that district.
According to the assessment of the Ministry of Tourism, all cities in Cambodia have all the potential for tourism, but in order to establish a tourism office, that office must have a line of accountability to its mayors, districts and Khans.
He said that the difference is that in the past, tourism offices had to have a direct line of accountability to the capital-provincial tourism department or directly to the Ministry of Tourism, but now does not do so to open tourism offices in cities, districts, Khans, that office must have a straight line of accountability. To the governor of that district. People prefer to eat vegetables on the water than vegetables grown on the ground because it is safe
(Kampong Chhnang): Farmers who grow safe vegetables on water in Boeung Leach village, Sethy commune, Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province confirmed that most people now prefer to eat vegetables grown on water rather than vegetables grown on the ground because they think about safety. Health Although vegetables grown on water are more expensive than vegetables grown on the ground. On the other hand, vegetables grown on water taste better and crispier than vegetables grown on land.
However, after being instructed by the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries on growing vegetables on the water, he took the time to learn how to grow vegetables on the water, as he had visited Vietnam for an internship. That growing vegetables on water is of the utmost importance to the well-being and health of consumers, and consumers also like to make the market price more expensive than vegetables grown on land.
On the other hand, the Department of Agriculture and Kampong Chhnang Provincial Authority have established a community market in Toul Kralanh Village, Sangkat Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Chhnang City for farmers who have organized a community to produce chemical-free agricultural products to sell to customers who like to eat vegetables and fish. Which has no chemicals.
Since the opening of this community market, there have been more and more customers buying chemical-free agricultural products, and the community market also sells agricultural products such as chicken, duck, fish, beef, pork, vegetables, garlic, fertilizer, turmeric, etc. . With no chemicals.
This is according to Mr. Chan Darong, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Rural Development, speaking on the occasion of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit held a press conference on "Update and Progress of the Ministry of Rural Development" this morning, February 17, 2020 at the Office of the Committee. Minister.
Mr. Chandarong stated: "People in rural areas, please participate in the construction of toilets and use toilets for everyone to end the defecation that leads to infectious diseases. "Ourselves, our families and our society."
He also urged officials in the capital and other provinces to pay close attention to this work, focusing on education, outreach and construction of toilets and toilets.
Mr. Chandarong also requested the people to contribute to the maintenance and proper use of the achievements provided by the Ministry of Rural Development, such as development partners and philanthropists, such as wells, ponds for good long-term use and Let them consider those achievements as their own.
He also instructed people to save water for proper use and boil water before eating. In addition, please wash your hands with soap or ash after leaving the bathroom and before handling food to eat.
The spokesman also urged residents to help prevent overweight vehicles running on the rural national road network by providing information to the relevant authorities. At this point, he claimed that the Ministry will cooperate with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to prepare procedures and methods for developing a master plan for road development, design and project prioritization.
Please be informed that by the end of 2019, about 80% of the rural population will have access to latrines and 65% will have access to clean water, while Cambodia has launched a plan to achieve the goal of rural people having access to clean water and 100% sanitation. 2025.
Ms. Men Sam An Holds a Meeting to Summarize the Work Results of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development and the Women's Movement
