This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen chaired a meeting to review the work of the "National Council of Cambodia for Women"
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, February 17, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will chair a meeting to review the work results in 2019. And set the work direction for 2020 of the "National Council of Cambodia for Women" held at the Peace Palace.
The "Cambodian National Council for Women" has Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk as its honorary president and Samdech Techo Hun Sen as its honorary vice president. Since 2006, the leadership of the "Cambodian National Council for Women", chaired by Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs, has held regular meetings once a year under the chairmanship of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The meeting was held to monitor and monitor all activities and implementation of some recommendations on the work of the "National Council of Cambodia for Women" in contribution to the Royal Government to promote rights, freedoms, status, special role, to participate in resolving all work. Women's priorities.
Women are considered by the Royal Government as an important backbone to promote national economic development. Through regular meetings of the "Cambodian National Council for Women", a number of recommendations have been reviewed and put forward to promote women's rights and develop women's capacity, especially to promote women's activities in social affairs.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has always paid close attention to women's issues. Women's rights are better promoted and on an equal footing with men in society, and more women are included in leadership roles and decisions in ministries and institutions.
In fact, in Cambodia's top institutions, both the legislature and the executive, more and more women are being included in leadership roles. The National Assembly, Ms. Khuon Sodary, was elected Second Vice President of the National Assembly.
In the executive branch of the government of the sixth mandate, Ms. Men Sam An has been appointed Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly Senate Relations and Inspection, Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi has been appointed Minister of Women's Affairs, and Ms. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture. And fine arts. In addition, many women have been appointed Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, Director General, Deputy Director General ... and provincial governors.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also showed more attention to women by providing support services to women civil servants and members of the armed forces and women workers in the industrial sector.
In 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to provide a policy to provide workers with a maternity allowance of about 400,000 Riels for those who gave birth, 1,800,000 Riels for giving birth to twins and 1.2 million Riels for mothers 3 twins. In addition, workers are entitled to three months of maternity leave with a 120 percent wage rate.
In addition, in 2019, the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to provide a subsidy of 760,000 Riels to women in poor families during childbirth from pregnancy to two-year-old children.
Along with education, female students are also seen as encouraging and facilitating their higher education.
However, every year in this work review meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen always reminds all women to strive to increase their capacity through study efforts.
For example, on February 14, 2020, when they met Samdech Techo, Samdech presented a souvenir with a krama and a rose in the sense of sincere love without discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion That. We see that all the tourists showed such happy faces that some of the American brothers cried, hugged the prince, or some bowed to the ground, expressing their excitement that they had escaped death.
Cambodia is just as scared as any other country. But what Cambodia adheres to is the spirit of humanitarian values, saving lives on board, and all kinds of measures to protect its people. In other words, "Cambodia does not adopt the spirit of fear of selfishness by choosing to push this ship to float in the middle of the vast ocean without islands." This is the "value of Cambodia."
