Minister Thong Khon Inaugurates Achievements in Wat Tang Kork worth More Than 90,000 USD and Receives More Than 16 Million Riels
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Baray and Taing Kork District Assistance Team, Kampong Thom Province, and Ms. Nhek Sim Thong Khon, on February 16, 2020, inaugurated many Buddhist achievements at the pagoda. Samdech Choat Nhan called Wat Tang Kork, which has a total value of more than 90,000 dollars, as well as received more than 16,100,000 Riels from Buddhists and other philanthropists.
Wat Samdech Choat Nhan, also known as Wat Taing Kork, is a pagoda located in Taing Kork Village, So Yong Commune, Taing Kork District, along National Road 6. This pagoda is 179 years old and was first built on an area of 34.88 square meters from 1841-1970 under the handiwork of Prince Chuon Nath.
Mr. Hak Mong Huot, Governor of Tang Kork District, said that during the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime, Wat Tang Kork, as well as the whole of Cambodia, suffered a lot of destruction until after the liberation on January 7, this old pagoda was built. And there are monks living again until today.
On that occasion, Minister Thong Khon expressed his request for the people, civil servants, teachers and students to have a strong position and confidence in the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to continue to lead. The development of the nation for the progress of development.
He called on people to take care of their health, hygiene and clean hands regularly based on the principles of eating clean, drinking clean and living clean, continue to work hard to grow rice, crops and occupations to improve livelihoods and family economy.
In addition, the Minister told the local people not to do dry rice for the second time this year because the water supply is not enough and the district, commune, village authorities, local authorities and working groups continue to inspect and find water sources and Pump water for irrigation and save people's rice from now until the next dry season, especially strictly implement the Royal Government's circular on water conservation measures.
At the same time, Minister Thong Khon handed over 1 million Riels to: Hun Sen Tang Kork High School, Mr. Ta Chi Yai Chi 100 students each received a piece of cloth and 10,000 Riels. Separately, Minister Thong Khon and Mrs. Nhek Sim Thong Khon also donated 10 million Riels for the construction of achievements in the pagoda. Ley Sopheap Leads Tens of Thousands of Network Marketing Businesses to Support Small and Medium Enterprise Development with the Royal Government
