Cambodian trade union leader: EU Commission decision to cut tariff preferences from Cambodia does not hurt the economy, but strengthens Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Som Aun, President of the National Assembly of the Cambodian Confederation of Unions and President of the Federation of Trade Unions of Cambodia, this morning, February 15, 2020, presided over a get-together with more than 100 local unions at the National Confederation of Trade Unions. Cambodia.
Mr. Som Oun added that requiring Cambodia to pay a 20 percent tariff on imported goods did not slow down or collapse the Cambodian economy, but instead strengthened Cambodia's ability to survive on its own. On the other hand, Cambodia has been preparing for a year to deal with this risk.
He added that the EU procedure now is a reminder that Cambodia must be prepared to live on its own, which in the future the EBA will automatically disappear when the Cambodian economy recovers from the status of a less developed country.
Mr. Som Oun confirmed that so far no factory has been closed due to the EBA. For some factories that have planned to suspend workers for a month or two, it is common practice that this problem occurs every year because some factories sew seasonal garments and some factories offer products by contract. Shorts that are sometimes made for an existing customer need to be suspended to wait for a new customer, etc.
He acknowledged that the recent outbreak of coronavirus in China was also part of the reason for some factories to be temporarily shut down in the near future. In China, work has been suspended, so about 70 percent of Cambodia's raw materials, which Cambodia relies on to import from China, will face temporary challenges in the short term.
Mr. Som Oun also welcomed the project of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which is in the process of negotiating a free trade agreement between Cambodia and China, when there is a free trade agreement, the Chinese market will be open for Cambodian goods and call on all workers. Must have confidence in the Royal Government of Cambodia to ensure responsibility for the stability and safety of workers.
