(Phnom Penh): If we look at the era of Democratic Kampuchea between 1975-1979, the lives of the people were collective and all the land was controlled by the Khmer Rouge.
Since the overthrow of the regime on January 7, 1979, the land has been under the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Agriculture, which is the property of the state. Land and / or hiring laborers and prohibiting the unauthorized occupation, clearing or clearing of forests until 1989, when the state decided to grant private ownership of land to Cambodians.
Although the state has given private ownership, the government continues to focus on improving people's livelihoods by providing state-owned private land to the poor who are homeless through social land concessions.
To better understand what social land concessions can be granted for? What are the qualifications and conditions for citizens to receive social land concessions?
Therefore, the legal awareness program of FRESH NEWS in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation would like to raise the topic of "Social Land Concessions" to present to the following students:
The policy of granting social land concessions was established through Sub-Decree No. 19 dated March 19, 2003. Social land concessions are legal mechanisms for the transfer of state private land for social purposes to the poor who lack land for housing and / or family farming.
Social land concessions may be granted for social purposes in accordance with one or more objectives, such as:
Provide land to poor homeless families to build houses for farming as a family, families displaced by the development of public infrastructure for resettlement, families affected by natural disasters, families repatriated, disbanded soldiers, and Families of disabled soldiers.
In addition to this social goal, it facilitates economic development and facilitates economic land concessions by providing plots of land to large plantation workers for housing or family farming, as well as developing undeveloped areas.
Social land concessions to be provided for residential construction are the largest at 1,200 square meters, but in areas with vacant land, social land concessions can be increased up to 3,600 square meters.
Social land concessions that can be provided for family farming are as large as 2 hectares, but in some areas the size of social land concessions can increase up to 5 hectares, depending on the nature of the land, the potential of the land or the type of crop and the type of labor and your family. Ask for land.
Applicants for social land concessions must have the following qualifications:
No one can deny the right to participate in the social land concession program of a female head of household, a disabled person, a disabled veteran and a disqualified military head.
In order to obtain a social land concession, the people who are the subject of the land recipient must respect the following conditions:
If the recipient of the social land concession fails to meet the conditions of possession and use of the land concession, the land will be returned to the state land for redistribution.
In short, social land concessions are a legal mechanism for the transfer of state-owned private land to provide people who lack land for housing and / or real family farming in order to improve their livelihoods. State public land is not the subject of a social land concession.
