Eight farming communities in Preah Vihear province have signed a contract to sell organic cassava to a happy company at a good price with a high price compared to the outside market
(Preah Vihear): Farmers in Preah Vihear province who have signed a contract to sell organic cassava to the company are happy because the market price sold to the company under the contract is higher than the market price that traders buy outside.
Mr. Peng Trida, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said on February 15, 2020 that in Preah Vihear Province, 8 agricultural communities have signed contracts to sell organic cassava to Thai Wha through community corporations. Cambodia Agriculture CACC.
As of mid-February 2020, the company has collected about 5,000 tons of cassava for export, he said. He said that by implementing contract farming, the people of Preah Vihear province are happy to sell fresh cassava at prices ranging from 374 riel to 390 riel per kilogram, compared to the price of foreign buyers is higher.
Mr. Peng Trida also pointed out that the implementation of contract farming is that farmers have an existing market and are not afraid of cocktail traders. On the other hand, farmers receive technical assistance and knowledge, as well as loans from financial institutions with reasonable interest rates, especially the sale of potatoes under this contract is not deducted as a percentage of 1 ton of potatoes to pay a budget of 1000kg different from Brokers now cut the weight percentage from 10-15%.
