In the opening ceremony of the final examination of training courses and regulations on labor regulations for labor inspectors at the National Employment Agency (NEA) on February 15, 2020, Mr. Prak Chanthoeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor introduced some recommendations. Includes:
* 1: Take the wisdom gained from this training course and improve the law enforcement and work efficiency to improve the capacity of the institution in order to meet the needs of the public in the rapid development of the system. National and international.
* 2: Continue to strengthen capacity and develop knowledge more widely in line with the evolution of legal rules and the development of digital technology, which is an important priority area for the development of the country.
* 3: Continue to disseminate and share knowledge related to regulations in this field to other officials through continuous training in each department or unit.
* 4: It is requested to the Secretariat of the Commission for the Development of Laws and Regulations in the field of labor to continue to cooperate with relevant units, especially the National Institute of Labor, which will operate in the near future to continue to organize this training and training for new chairpersons. Which is the progress of the legal documents in the field of labor in more detail, both in theory and practice.
This training course is designed to study 12 subjects, focusing on four basic laws in the field of labor, such as labor law, trade union law, minimum wage law and social security law, and with the participation of participants. A total of 756 officials are at the ministry level and at the capital-provincial level of the Department of Labor and Vocational Training.
Armed forces arrest a man on a warrant for the sale of nearly 58 hectares of wind land in Kampong Speu province, today sent to court for legal action
(Phnom Penh): A man was arrested by the National Gendarmerie in cooperation with the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie on the order of the Prosecutor's Office in connection with a case of fraud in the sale of nearly 58 hectares of wind land in the amount of nearly 3 million dollars To Chinese businessmen in Kampong Speu province.
According to the police, the suspect is Keo Moniroth, 55 years old, living in the 4th floor of LEGCY Business Center, Mao Tse Toung Blvd., Sangkat Toul Tum Poung, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
After the arrest on the morning of February 15, 2020, the police sent the suspect to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for processing.
Phnom Penh Municipal Court officials have revealed that the suspect was a senior police officer at the Ministry of Interior who was scrambling for the court to release him.
Police confirmed that the suspect, Keo Moniroth, was sued by the Chinese victim for defrauding him of $ 2,900,000 in connection with a 33-hectare land purchase case at Kilometer 32 along National Road. No. 41 is located in Prey Khle village, Por Meral commune, Bor Seth district, Kampong Speu province during October 2019.
The suspect and a senior police officer of the Ministry of Interior made a contract to buy and sell the land to the victim, claiming that the suspect was the owner of the land and had a police officer of the Ministry of Interior as a witness, but in fact they There was no land given to the victim according to the contract, so the victim complained to the court to help find justice.
Because the suspects and their accomplices used tricks to deceive both the people and the company, the victims decided to file a complaint against the suspects and their accomplices to the court to help find justice for the company and the people.
