Chip Mong continues to focus on human resource training programs in the construction sector
(Phnom Penh): Chip Mong Inc. Camel Cement Company and the National Polytechnic Institute of Cambodia (NPIC) this morning, February 15, 2020, co-organized a training course for 60 more builders in response to The request of the master craftsman and to contribute to building human resources, expertise in the field of construction and building trust from construction owners.
This training aims to provide real and better skills to the master builder. In one training course for 3 months, more than 30 masters will have the opportunity to learn the main subjects according to each stage, such as planning work, site preparation work, bricklaying work, cementing work, safety work, steel structure installation work, concrete pouring work, and printing work. As well as on-site practice.
These masters from Phnom Penh, Kandal and Kampong Cham have requested to Chip Mong Inc. Camel Cement to re-open the training course after successfully completing the training of more than 90 masters in the first phase.
He stressed that Chip Mong Inc. focuses on the production of quality cement, but more importantly, the use of cement to meet technical standards through the master builder on site.
Mr. Bun Phearin, Director of the National Polytechnic Institute, stressed the importance of training master builders in response to the development of the national economy and the construction sector directly, as this sector receives a lot of investment, both domestic and foreign investment. . In fact, Chip Mong Inc.'s investment in cement production has made Cambodia more independent in the construction sector, and this sector requires a lot of human resources.
Upon successful completion of the training, the master builder will receive a Certificate of Education from the National Polytechnic Institute of Cambodia and Chip Mong Inc. Camel Cement. In addition, the master craftsman receives an additional $ 15 in cash every Saturday for meals during the study period.
