Letter from readers: Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Khmer leader "Heart of the Ocean"!
While people are amazed to buy masks to wear until the price of masks goes up, the Cambodian Prime Minister set an example by refusing to wear a mask and telling Cambodians to be careful but not to wear a mask if it is not necessary.
As people around the world discriminate against the Chinese, the Cambodian Prime Minister has become very close to the Chinese people. This is an action to alleviate the fear of this virus and also to show solidarity in difficult times without having to run away alone.
For Prime Minister Hun Sen, the humanitarian heart is bigger than fear and discrimination. In this sense, the Cambodian leader not only allowed the giant ship to dock, but also greeted the tourists at the entrance of the ship, shaking their hands until a Western greeting. A country without a mask.
The gesture of this Cambodian leader was warmly applauded and appreciated by the President of the World Health Organization and the foreign embassies that had their nationals on board, and especially the appreciation and gratitude of Tourists aboard the ship. World-renowned newspapers also published extensively, praising Cambodia for its noble humanitarian spirit.
Through these latest decisions and actions, Cambodian leaders have shown the world the most outstanding example of the symbol of "solidarity", emergency assistance and the fight against discrimination with respect to human life. It is a right that must be respected first. Through this activity, Cambodia is being admired by the world. The world is also looking at Cambodia as a small country with a leader with a heart as big as the ocean.
As Cambodian children, we are very proud of our leaders who are not only bringing us happiness, but also sowing a culture of peace that is a source of happiness for people all over the world.
