Ministry of Land Management announces 5 results of the meeting of the National Committee for Coastal Management and Development of Cambodia
The meeting was attended by Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, Representative of Minister Say Sam Al, Mr. Kong Vimean, Deputy Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, Representative of Mr. Kouch Chamroeun and Representative of the Ministry of Institutions. Some other stakeholders who are members of the NCDD.
After the meeting, the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction announced the following five results: JC Airlines will officially launch a new route from "Phnom Penh-Chiang Mai".
Chiang Mai Province is located in the north of Thailand, a place with beautiful environment and nature due to its long history as well as rich landscapes, making Chiang Mai famous for its rich roses. This area is called the Rose of Northern Thailand.
Due to the beautiful scenery and green nature everywhere and the rapid development, the province ranks second after Bangkok, the capital of Thailand. In the past, Chiang Mai was the capital of Thailand. There are many ancient temples and monasteries here that showcase the great history and culture of northern Thailand.
At the same time, Chiang Mai silk products and textiles are famous all over the world, and they are exported to many countries every year. Through its glorious economic and cultural development, Chiang Mai has attracted many tourists from all over the world.
On the other hand, this new flight is the only direct flight from Phnom Penh to Chiang Mai.
