Royal Government allows Chinese companies to explore for oil in Block D off the coast of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to grant an oil exploration license to a Chinese company to explore for oil in Block D off the coast of Cambodia.
He added that at this stage, the company is conducting research on the amount of oil in Block D, whether there is potential for production. After the company studies to find out the amount of oil, the company will apply for oil production.
According to the director general, the oil exploration agreement in Block D is for 30 years, which is divided into two phases. The first phase is a research phase, which usually lasts seven years, and if the company finds it first, it can apply for production, but if the company is not yet able to find it, it can apply for another three years. The second stage is the production stage after the research in the first stage.
At the same time, Mr. Chiep Sour also confirmed that Block D oil field is close to Block A oil field with an area of more than 5,000 square kilometers in the waters of Cambodia.
He said that in the past, other companies have been granted exploration rights in the block, but due to falling oil prices and inability to pay, the company gave up.
Police officer car crashes into ABA Bank employee's motorbike, causing death in Svay Teap district, Svay Rieng province
(Svay Rieng): The car of a police officer collided with the motorcycle of an ABA Bank employee, causing the motorcycle owner to die on the road after being sent to emergency in Vietnam.
According to Svay Teap police, the victim was Prum Saron, 30, an ABA Bank employee living in Preah Ponlea village, Preah Ponlea commune, Kampong Ror district, while riding a black Honda C125 motorcycle with Prey Veng 1L license plate. -8090 Serious damage.
The provocative driver was identified as 51-year-old Kem Si Thmor, a police officer living in Ang Svay village, Prasot commune, Svay Teap district, Svay Rieng province.
According to witnesses, before the incident, they saw a golden Camry car with license plate Banteay Meanchey 2A-2060 on National Road No. 1, driving without respecting the right of way, suddenly hit a motorcycle riding alone. In the direction of avoiding each other completely, causing a surprise.
Later, the villagers reported to the local authorities to send the victim to Svay Teap District Referral Hospital with serious injuries, then sent to the hospital in Vietnam, died halfway through the family brought to celebrate. Meanwhile, the authorities measured and dragged the car and motorcycle exhibits to the Svay Teap District Police Inspectorate for legal action.
Police authorities confirmed that the reason is because the driver does not respect the right of way.
