A Cambodian agricultural company joins hands with a Norwegian company to help Cambodian farmers increase productivity and yields
(Phnom Penh): Angkor Green of Cambodia on the morning of February 14, 2020, signed a business partnership agreement with Yara International, originally from Norway, to contribute to the Royal Government and related partners to make Where Cambodian farmers can increase productivity, increase yields, be safer and be able to produce agricultural products in accordance with the standards of buyers, especially for export.
"At the same time, Angkor Green knows that the international company, which is a producer of special new generation fertilizers with high quality and has the support of farmers around the world, especially in developed countries and countries. Cambodia's neighbor is Yara International, headquartered in Norway. This content emphasizes further.
Because the two companies have similar visions and perceptions, the two companies decided to sign an agreement with the aim of bringing modern agricultural technology and world-class quality products that have been implemented in developed countries and neighboring countries. To farmers to Cambodia and to respond to the growth and good development of the agricultural sector in Cambodia.
To promote the implementation and achievement of the above goals, Angkor Green and Yara will work together to select a suitable distribution depot and meet the requirements of this world-class fertilizer distribution standard throughout Cambodia from now on. In addition, it will work with development partners working in the agricultural sector to support farmers to be able to use such high quality fertilizers and to use products that meet the needs and stages of the crop.
In addition, Angkor Green has been teaching industrial feed production techniques to farmers, using resources around their communities as raw materials to produce animal feed, and has been involved in the purchase of livestock and safe agricultural products from farmers. And is distributing safe pork, farm chicken and other safe agricultural products produced by Cambodian farmers.
Recently, the Export Department was established to contribute to the national market connection for Cambodian farmers and to increase the official export volume of Cambodian agricultural products abroad. Since the end of 2018, Angkor Green has exported turmeric (named Svay Angkor) to sell to customers as a Japanese company.
Chip Mong Bank launches new service "Chip Mong Bank Agent" to facilitate customer transactions quickly
