Senior Minister Sun Chanthol: Rehabilitation of 5 major streams in Sihanoukville is more than 50% complete
(Preah Sihanouk): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that as of January 2020, the rehabilitation of the five main streams in Sihanoukville has been completed 15,216 meters and equal to 51. 10% for the remaining length, the Ministry will cooperate with local authorities to expedite the restoration work to be completed before the rainy season.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol confirmed this on the afternoon of February 14, 2020, on the occasion of inspecting the progress of the restoration of streams and canals in Sihanoukville with the participation of government officials. Ministries and Departments of Public Works and Transport of Preah Sihanouk Province and local authorities.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthon stated that the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, as well as the Sihanoukville Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, has accelerated the restoration of some major streams in Sihanoukville to prevent and prevent flooding due to the rainy season. The coming rainy season as well as preparing the canal system in this city to be attractive and hygienic according to the plan of the Ministry.
At the same time, the Senior Minister also expressed his appreciation and gratitude to all the working groups and relevant authorities for their efforts to expedite the restoration of those streams.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also called on the people living in Sihanoukville, especially the people living along these canals to join and cooperate with the team of the Ministry and local authorities to speed up the restoration. Highly aware of any disturbances while restoring this as well.
