Sao Paulo: Scientists in Antarctica have registered a new temperature of 20.75 degrees Celsius, the first time above 20 degrees Celsius on the continent, amid growing concerns about melting. Glaciers and global warming. This was released by CNA on Friday evening, February 14, 2020.
On March 24, 2015, the temperature in Antarctica was 17.2 degrees Celsius, while 2019 was considered by the United Nations to be one of the hottest years ever since 2016. In 2020, temperatures will continue to be in this trend.
Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement to be Completed and Signed in 2020!
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia-China Bilateral Free Trade Agreement, initiated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Li Keqiang, Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China, aims to expand trade, investment, services and cooperation. Negotiations are scheduled to be completed and signed by the end of 2020.
This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Economy on the narrow meeting of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee on the results of the negotiations on the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement and the principles for further negotiations, which was received by Fresh News this afternoon. February 14, 2020
The inter-ministerial meeting was held on February 13, 2020 at the Ministry of Economy and Finance under the chairmanship of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Policy Committee. Economics and Finance (CSF).
The event was attended by Mr. and Mrs. Ministers and leaders of relevant ministries and institutions, as well as members of the Cambodian Negotiation Working Group to review and discuss the results of the first round of negotiations on the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement. On January 20-21, 2020 in Beijing, the People's Republic of China recently provided guidelines for the next round of negotiations.
The Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement was established with the aim of expanding trade, investment, services and deepening cooperation between the two countries.
The advancement of the FTA negotiations is a clear reflection of the rapid development of the close and strong relations and cooperation between the two countries in all fields, which have now reached the cooperation of the two countries. Strategic partners from all angles.
In addition, the agreement also shows the high level of consideration and concern of the two leaders on improving the lives of the people of the two countries by promoting trade and job creation.
The agreement will give Cambodia more diversity in exporting its products to the Chinese market, both in volume and in goods, by providing better tariff preferences.
In addition, the agreement will improve trade facilitation by facilitating and reducing unnecessary procedures and measures and obstructing the flow of trade in goods.
In terms of investment, this agreement will contribute to facilitating existing investors to expand their operations and attract more new investment to Cambodia, which will create new jobs for the people by improving the work related to Promote and facilitate investment.
All these factors will contribute to the development and support of national economic growth, as well as accelerate the process of economic integration of Cambodia into the region and the world.
The meeting noted and appreciated the progress of the first round of negotiations and provided guidelines to the negotiating team as a solid basis for the next round of negotiations aimed at concluding negotiations on the entire agreement as soon as possible in accordance with the guidelines. And the wishes of the heads of government of both countries.
In addition, the meeting also agreed on the plan to conclude negotiations on the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement in mid-2020 and to sign it by the end of 2020.
