Young Japanese Entrepreneur vows to attract more investors to Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tanaka Nubuiyuki, President of Young Entrepreneurs of the Japan Chamber of Commerce and Industry, expressed high optimism about the current economic growth of Cambodia and he pledged to attract more Japanese investors to invest in Cambodia as a testament. Better to serve the interests and growth of both countries.
The statement was made at a seminar on "The Next Generation of YEG Future in Cambodia - Doing Business in ASEAN Growth" hosted by the Young Entrepreneurs Group of the Japan Chamber of Commerce and Industry at the Cambodiana Hotel on February 13: Mr. Sam Sereyroth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce and Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Japan to Cambodia.
The head of the same entrepreneur said that Cambodia is an important base for Japanese companies to invest, while the Japanese economy is not growing due to the decline of its population. "Due to the high economic growth in Southeast Asia, especially Cambodia, which has a high economic growth rate of 7%, we are very interested and we hope to be able to cooperate with our Cambodian partners, as we hope to benefit both Japan and the United States," he said. And Cambodia.
On that occasion, Mr. Mikami Masahiro confirmed that currently more than 260 Japanese companies have been staying and investing in Cambodia, and many other Japanese enterprises and investors are interested. Therefore, Cambodia is still a good destination for Japanese and foreign investors as Cambodia has maintained a high economic growth rate of 7% and has a good geographical location in the center of ASEAN countries, especially peace.
