(Kampong Chhnang): Raising catfish as a family If we follow the technical characteristics of raising properly, whether small or large, it will give us a positive result for family resolution without Buy fish and meat from the market.
Mr. Chak Thoeun, 47 years old, a farmer living in Boeung Leach village, Sethy commune, Samaki Meanchey district, told reporters on the afternoon of February 13, 2020, that in the past 4 years, he has taken up the business of raising catfish. Family style In a plastic pond, only two small ponds can support the family's livelihood throughout the year, combined with growing vegetables and raising chickens in some homes, he does not have to go to the market to buy fish and meat.
The farmer stated that he actually raised catfish in two plastic ponds, each 20 to 30 square meters, 1 meter deep, and bought 5,000 catfish for 400,000. Riel by providing natural food with rice mixed with bran and daily kitchen waste. By now, it has been 3 months since the fish in his pond have grown, which is 5 to 7 fish per kilogram and can be eaten.
Mr. Chak Thoeun stated that the technique of making a plastic rubber pond is to put a plastic bag around it, with the top of the pond mouth covered with a wet cloth over the plastic rubber to prevent the plastic rubber from being exposed to sunlight and it will rot. It's fragile, obviously his plastic rubber pond is 4 years old and the plastic rubber is not rotten.
He also called on farmers not to leave their land vacant, but to try to raise catfish in plastic ponds as it is not difficult for them to easily support their daily lives without having to buy meat fish. The market, especially eating fish, natural foods and safe vegetables, is really healthy for the family.
