Islamic professor warns Khmer-Muslim youth not to be fooled on February 14
(Central): Professor of Islam, Mr. Musa Ahmad, warned all Cambodian Muslim youth not to forget Valentine's Day and practice it in the wrong way, contrary to the way of Islam to avoid any problems that may occur. In particular, it is different from religion, as this festival is a foreign festival, not related to religion.
He warned in an interview with Fresh News in Kandal province on February 14, 2020, as today is Valentine's Day.
He reminded that love is an important attribute that Allah (God) has instilled in everyone's heart, while love in Islam has many forms, such as:
"Muslims are used to fulfilling the role of their loved ones in accordance with the rights that they must receive faithfully on a regular basis, but this religion does not use them to take any day to celebrate the festival," he said. "Love, because true love is associated with the practice of regular acts of love, it is not just a performance."
At the same time, the Islamic professor, Mr. Mousa Ahmed, also encouraged all young Cambodian Muslims to increase their love for the country, society, community, dignity, especially the peace that is happening under the shadow of peace led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. 133 Cambodia-Vietnam border posts in Ratanakkiri province have been completed and handed over to the relevant authorities and institutions for maintenance
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Koy Pisey, Deputy Chairman of the Cambodian Boundary Commission, told Fresh News on February 14, 2020 that there are 133 Cambodian-Vietnamese border posts in Ratanakkiri, Cambodia and Yalai-Kantum provinces. Already built. The border posts have been handed over to the Tonkin Kiri provincial authorities and relevant institutions to manage and maintain.
According to Ms. Koy Pisey, in Ronkiri Province, Cambodia and Yalai-Kantum Province, Vietnam, there are more than 216 km of border lines with 40 major border posts, of which both sides have agreed to set up 31 major border posts and 82 additional border posts in the agreed area.
Cambodia and Vietnam share a 1,270-kilometer land border with 314 joint border posts. To date, the border demarcation between the two countries has reached about 84 percent.
The two sides pledged to work hard to complete the border post and develop the border area into a peaceful and prosperous area with mutual economic benefits.
