(Phnom Penh): General Touch Naroth, Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police and Director of the Bodyguard Department of the Ministry of Interior, and Ms. Yiv Narada, as well as the whole family, are now deeply saddened and unable to find a word to say. No, after the youngest son died at the age of 21.
Roth Pancharong, 21, died without saying goodbye to his parents and brother and sister last night on the night of February 13, 2020 due to illness.
The loss of the youngest son, a national police officer, has shocked General Touch Naroth, a former Phnom Penh police chief, and his wife, as well as their two children, almost with a heart attack. This friend did not leave a single word.
Before his death, during the day, Roth Pancharong had fun with his family and family, but a few hours later, he said goodbye forever.
The funeral of the National Police youth at the Department of Defense was traditionally held at the residence of General Touch Naroth on Concrete Road, Group 1, Prey Pring North 1 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Sen Chey.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen affirmed that now is not the time to be afraid and discriminate, but the time to unite to solve global challenges.
A meaningful message to the world by the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, was made on the morning of February 14, 2020, after Samdech Techo Hun Sen personally greeted the departing passengers. Westerdam tour at Sihanoukville port and flowers for tourists.
On the occasion of delivering an important message at the site of a large US cruise ship carrying more than 2,200 people docked in Sihanoukville, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stressed that this is an issue that needs to be addressed. Global Responsibility as well as Cambodia's Responsibility as a Member of the Responsible International Community.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister still claims that Samdech is here, even for a short time, but he will also send this message to the people of Cambodia across the country as well as to the international community that now is not the time to be afraid and not It is time to discriminate, but it is time to unite to address the challenges that have been plaguing not just one country, many countries have already experienced this.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed outrage and misunderstanding the words, "What should we say about respect for human rights if the right to life is not respected?" He stressed that Cambodia takes responsibility primarily on respect for human rights and must first respect the survival of the more than 2,200 people on board and of 41 nationalities.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia is now working on the process of respecting human rights: the right to life, the right not to be discriminated against, and the right to return safely to the country for travelers. More than 2,200 people were on board.
The Prime Minister stressed that the Cambodian people should understand and be proud when the Royal Government makes such a decision. In addition, the Prince thanked the Cambodian people for encouraging and supporting the Prince's decision to allow the ship to enter Cambodian territory, through which the 41 nationalities traveled back to Cambodia. Each country reunites families without fear.
