The following are the instructions of the Preah Vihear Provincial Administration, which are in full content: Announcing the implementation of the new structure of the Bakan District Administration, the Governor of Pursat Province prohibits officials from taking informal fees whenever the people come to rely on
(Pursat): After warning to take action against any official who continues to collect informal service fees from the people, Pursat Provincial Governor Mr. Mao Thunin has banned and banned all civil servants from taking fees on public services. From the people, on the contrary, all civil servants must work together to serve the people closely and quickly, in a timely, efficient and transparent manner.
Mr. Mao Thunin said this on February 14, 2020 at the launching ceremony of the new structure of 65 Bakan District Administration in accordance with Resolution No. 175 Pillar / NCDD of the National Committee. For democratic development at the sub-national level, with the participation of provincial councils, leaders of departments, units around the province, the three armed forces, district authorities, communes, teachers and a large number of people.
He said that based on the experience and positive results achieved at the sub-national level, the Royal Government is strongly committed to expand the process of decentralization and deconcentration reform in all capitals, provinces, districts and cities throughout the country through the amendment of the Constitution.
In the context of the implementation of this policy, there are three main objectives: 1-Strengthen and expand multi-party liberal democracy, 2-Improve the quality and efficiency of public services to meet local needs, 3-Participate And to be the owner of the people in making decisions related to management, leadership and local development.
He said that in order to achieve all these tasks, it is necessary for all officials who have been announced to take office to work hard to strengthen the spirit of internal unity on the basis of improving the efficiency of work and respecting the law. Adhere to the principle of strengthening the working system, ownership in fulfilling its roles and responsibilities for local development and responding to the needs of the people in its jurisdiction.
Mr. Mao Thunin also reminded that with the consideration and care of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia for the livelihood and well-being of the people, workers, civil servants have received many benefits of using the card. Equity Fund and the National Social Security Fund (NSSF) when you go to get health care services at public hospitals or private clinics that are registered free of charge.
