Three young men and women drowned in the Mekong River in Chhlong district, Kratie province
(Kratie): A group of young men and women went to visit the water, causing them to drown for about two hours before finding two dead bodies and another body has not been found. This incident happened on the evening of February 13, 2020 at Thmey 2 village, Khsach Andet commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province.
Chhlong Toran, Chhlong District Police Inspector, said that a group of six young people went to visit the Mekong River, which has sand and caused the six to drown, but three of them rode a car to escape drowning. Three others drowned, but no bodies have been found so far.
The first victim: Thin Pheaktra, a 19-year-old male living in the commune, died. The second victim: Le Chanreaksa, a 14-year-old Cambodian woman living in Chroy Thmor Krom village, Chhlong commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province, died. Separately, the third victim: Khon Theara, a 14-year-old female living in Prek Samrong village, Khsach Andet commune, Chhlong district, the body has not been found yet.
The inspector added that after receiving the information, the police immediately went to the scene to help find two bodies. Police examined the bodies of the victims and found that they really died from drowning, and the two bodies were handed over to their families for a traditional ceremony.
