New AFD Director Reaffirms Willingness to Provide Technical and Financial Support for Cambodia's Agricultural Development
Minister Veng Sakhon expressed his deep gratitude to the French Government through AFD for continuing to pay attention to and support the development of the agricultural sector in Cambodia with fruitful results as at present.
On this occasion, Ms. Ophelie BOURHIS confirmed to the Minister that AFD is committed to providing technical and financial support for the development of Cambodia's agricultural sector, emphasizing the development of agricultural development plans and policies related to the chain. Production costs and value added on rice, vegetable production, quality improvement of soil and household rubber.
Regarding the above-mentioned projects, Minister Veng Sakhon emphasized that the agricultural sector has played an important role in ensuring food security, promoting economic growth through exports, boosting domestic production, creating jobs, increasing incomes and reducing productivity. Poor in the country.
Not only that, development partners must also consider and review all project activities that have been implemented in the past to orient the goals of the Ministry as well as the Royal Government is the growth of the national economy and the family economy.
Separately, Minister Veng Sakhon also instructed AFD and the Working Group to consider the possibility of providing support for experiments and production of seeds, planting and harvesting techniques, warehousing, drying facilities on some other crops such as maize, cassava, mango and cashew. Has potential in domestic and foreign markets and provides good income to farmers.
At the same time, promote the organization of production communities to implement contract agricultural production in order to ensure the supply of quantity, quality and price stability, and especially the master plan and irrigation system that focuses on these crops.
In response to Minister Veng Sakhon's remarks, the Chair and the Working Group agreed with the Minister's remarks and will take those proposals into further consideration and incorporate them into a new project to be developed by AFD soon. This face.
In January, CMAC dropped 14 bombs from MK planes in 6 capitals and provinces
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Heng Ratana, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Cambodian Mine Action Center, recently confirmed that in January 2020, CMAC experts solved 14 bombs dropped from MK aircraft. Location in 6 capitals and provinces.
Heng Ratana said that of the 14 MK bombs, 13 had been detonated and were in explosive condition, and one had already exploded. The bombs were detonated in Phnom Penh, Kandal, Takeo, Kampong Cham, Prey Veng and Svay Rieng provinces, buried 5-7 meters deep.
He described the bombing as a serious threat to national security, especially to the construction of road infrastructure, irrigation, housing, bridges and other excavations that could be dangerous and damaging. Can also be large.
He also thanked Peace for creating an opportunity for the healing of the wounds of war gradually and to the point of complete destruction.
Please be informed that after the discovery of a bomb dropped from an MK81 aircraft, Sangkat Kork Roka, Khan Prek Pnov, on Friday, February 14, 2020, the CMAC Special Forces will work closely with the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority and the Armed Forces to prepare for the work. Destroy such bullets. At the same time, people should not be surprised by such explosions.
