Valentine's Day, February 14! Preah Vihear Youth and Provincial Women's Association for Peace and Development Volunteer to Donate Blood to 16 January Referral Hospital
Dr. Chou Ponina, Deputy Director of 16 Makara Referral Hospital in Preah Vihear Province, on behalf of Mr. Sok Veasna, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Hospital, stated that following the instructions of Preah Vihear Provincial Health Department, 16 Makara Provincial Referral Hospital has disseminated information to participating institutions in the province. Voluntary blood donation to save the lives of patients on the occasion of Valentine's Day, February 14.
Dr. Deputy Director of the Provincial Referral Hospital said that immediately after the announcement of the hospital on February 11, 2020, Ms. Chak Heng, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear and Chairman of the Association. Cambodian Women for Peace and Development of the province led a team of volunteers to donate blood to the hospital.
On the morning of February 13, 2020, Mr. Phon Tola led a total of 74 members to donate blood voluntarily to the 16th January Referral Hospital to save the lives of patients on the occasion of Valentine's Day on 14th February.
Mr. Juponina stated that volunteering to donate blood on the occasion of Valentine's Day on February 14 is to save the lives of patients who need blood to help the poor who are struggling. Hospitalization as well as contributing to society on humanitarian work.
He added that February 14 is not a Khmer tradition, so we young people should not be foolish to take foreign traditions and commit acts that should depart from our Khmer traditions. Instead, take this Valentine's Day as a tribute to love your parents, siblings, friends, especially to participate in good deeds such as donating blood to save the lives of patients is better.
