However, after requesting this land, which is located in Poi Char commune, Phnom Srok district, Banteay Meanchey province, Mr. Plan Dara did not use it for development to serve the common interests of the unit, instead he sold the land Some traders, 50 hectares, some nearly 10 hectares, quietly made hundreds of thousands of dollars without anyone knowing, sold from 2013 to 2016 and sold and took all the money.
Now, after the above documents are leaked to the public, the upper level is ordering a search to find out the truth.
As for the soldiers in the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Military Unit, after hearing about their former commander selling the unit's land quietly, they claimed that they did not agree with this case because they sold the unit's common land for money. Pockets alone.
(Phnom Penh): Two vehicles equipped with water pumps with the assistance of the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in Cambodia have been handed over to the Phnom Penh Capital Administration to pump flood water in various areas in Phnom Penh. Assistance in the project to prevent floods and improve the drainage system in Phnom Penh, Phase 4, which is a grant from Japan.
Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, said that the vehicles equipped with two water pumps are in the project to help prevent floods and improve the sewer system in Phnom Penh, Phase 4 under all districts. Japan's compensation.
He added that this is the second supply of machinery after the supply of 4 sewage trucks and 4 spray trucks in the flood protection project in Phnom Penh, Phase 3 under the grant financing. Of Japan in September 2015.
Mr. Yuji Sugano said that the fourth phase of the flood prevention and improvement project in Phnom Penh began in December 2018 and will be completed in October 2021.
"Although we have worked hard to release the floodwaters from Phnom Penh, the occurrence of flooding is still occurring, which requires the JICA team to continue to implement the project," he said. To do something to release water from Phnom Penh.
In addition to this work, JICA also provides training from technical officers to the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh. He confirmed that the two vehicles handed over are strong, fast and can pump water to relieve flooding in Phnom Penh and can be used for a long time.
Phnom Penh Governor Khuong Sreng said that each car equipped with a water pump received from Japan now has a capacity of 30 cubic meters per minute and a 300-meter-long drainage pipe for pumping rainwater. Flood and drain into a nearby lake canal to prevent damage to infrastructure in a vehicle equipped with six generators and pumps and a 50-meter drainage pipe for each pump.
For pump operation, all 6 pumps can be pumped in parallel or separately with 6 hoses, or 2 pumps can be pumped continuously with 3 hoses for a remote discharge location or a pumping station. Depth. France continues to help organize a number of irrigation projects in Siem Reap, Preah Vihear, Battambang, Kampong Thom and Kandal provinces with a budget of nearly $ 80 million
