During a working meeting with the Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia on the morning of February 12 yesterday at the Peace Palace, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, confirmed to the Japanese Ambassador that to facilitate investment in Cambodia in February. The Royal Government will reduce the price of electricity by 1 cent per kilowatt and will continue to improve transportation.
Regarding the reduction of 1 cent per kilowatt of electricity to support the industrial and agricultural sectors, Mr. Yim Viseth, President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia, told Fresh News on the afternoon of February 13, 2020 that starting from From February 1, 2020 onwards, the electricity bill issued at the end of February will implement the new price.
Mr. Yim Viseth stated that the consumers in the industrial and agricultural sectors received the discount up to 80% of the total number of consumers, and this discount is the consideration of the Royal Government of Cambodia in addition to the discount plan. Electricity bill according to the plan of each year.
The President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia stated, "The reduction of 1 cent per kilowatt is about 50-60 million dollars per year, which is a subsidy of the Royal Government to help the private sector in the sector. "Industries, including garment factories, footwear, as well as agriculture, to facilitate investment."
The Ministry of Mines and Energy claims that in 2020, as well as in subsequent years, Cambodia will no longer face electricity shortages. The highest demand for electricity in 2020 is 2,200 megawatts, while domestic supply and imports exceed demand. Cambodia has about 20-30% of energy reserves to meet the needs of new investment, so Cambodia has a total energy of about 2600-2700 megawatts.
