(Kandal): In order to make the implementation of the work in the new structure of the municipal-district administration to be easy and correct in the future, Dr. Mao Phirun, Governor of Kandal Province, said that the provincial administration will open the office. Skills at the municipal, district, specialized departments and councils to gain a deeper understanding of how to work with the new structure of the municipal administration successfully.
This was stated by the Provincial Governor at the 9th Ordinary Meeting of Kandal Provincial Council of the 3rd mandate on February 13, 2020 at Kandal Provincial Hall, which was also attended by Mr. Nuon Pha, Chairman of Provincial Council. And many other relevant officials.
Dr. Mao Phirun stated that the implementation of the new structure of the municipal administration is a historic reform in the sub-national administration, which requires officials to change the mindset and work attitude, so requires specialized units. Provincial, municipal, district and khan administrations, especially councils, need to find out more about this new structure in order to carry out the work easily and correctly.
(Tbong Khmum): Every year in February, the people of Choam Kravien commune, Memot district always celebrate fishing at Boeung Trapeang Kram resort, located in Satum village, Choam Kravien commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province. This "fishing ceremony" lasts for 3 days, from 13 to 15 February.
In 2019, Mr. Cheam Chan Sophoan and she, along with the provincial leaders, were invited to catch fish, cook, eat, dance and have fun with the people very happily and intimately.
The provincial governor, while visiting local people in the past, always called on people in that area, in the province or in the capitals and provinces to come and catch fish, cook and have fun together, especially this year. The prize money for the most accomplished winners is 1st, 2nd, 3rd and consolation prizes as well.
These are just as he promised to hold this ceremony every year so that people can enjoy gathering under the roof of peace, as well as continue to practice the ancestral traditions that have been held every year until now.
According to Mr. Ouch Yoeun, Chief of Choam Kravien Commune, the traditional fishing ceremony of the people of Choam Kravien Commune is after the harvest of agricultural crops and is an entertainment program for the people.
The commune chief said that on February 13, a program to visit the scenery around Boeung Trapeang Kram. On the night of the 13th and 14th, there will be a dance program against the light. In particular, the 15th is the day of the fishing celebration, starting at 9 am under the presidency of Mr. Cheam Chan Sophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum and Mrs. and the provincial leaders, along with people near and far.
Please be informed that before the fishing ceremony, the authorities do not allow people to fish in this lake to keep the fish for the fishing ceremony every year. For fishing, people can use only traditional equipment such as angrot chhnang and trak to catch fish in this ceremony, with the Boeung Kram area of about 30 hectares and the lake area of 1 hectare.
