(Kandal): On the morning of Wednesday, February 12, 2020, the Foreign Trade Bank of Cambodia held a grand opening ceremony for a new branch in Takhmao City, Kandal Province. .
The inauguration ceremony was presided over by Mr. Rath Sovannarak, Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, on behalf of Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, and Mr. Kim Rithy, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province, on behalf of Dr. Mao Phirun, Governor of Kandal Province. As well as the presence of Mr. Hun Manit.
Mr. Dith Sochol, Chief Executive Officer of Foreign Trade Bank of Cambodia (FTB), reported on the progress of FTB, the first strong and leading local commercial bank with over 40 years of operational experience. Since 1979, which has been highly trusted by customers and business partners in the country as well as internationally.
He added that the opening of a new branch in Takhmao will provide customers with a new option with modern banking services called quality digital banking, which will continue to contribute to improving the financial environment, investment activities, business, economy and market. Local finance, in particular, has directly contributed to improving the living standards of the people of Takhmao and Kandal provinces.
Mr. Kim Rithy mentioned the value of peace that led to the development of the country in almost all areas.
He also praised and congratulated the new branch of the Bank for Foreign Trade of Cambodia, which is present in the territory of Takhmao, the heart of Kandal province.
He also mentioned that the banking sector has contributed to reducing poverty and improving the family economy of our Cambodian people.
He also emphasized that bank employees are role models for the younger generation, as they have a high standard of professionalism and high responsibility, which is a role model for the younger generation.
Mr. Kim Rithy also wished the Bank for Foreign Trade of Cambodia to move forward successfully with the support of both domestic and foreign customers.
Mr. Rath Sovannarak said that financial institutions and banks are a factor that promotes economic growth and the environment, as well as social welfare. He also reminded the value of peace, as Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: "Thank you for peace!" Only with peace can we build and develop our country.
He also highlighted the recent establishment of a new branch of the Bank for Foreign Trade of Cambodia, which shows the Bank's commitment to providing efficient and fast financial services, as well as reflecting the trust of customers and Investors.
Please note that the Foreign Trade Bank of Cambodia was established in 1979 as a department of the National Bank of Cambodia to process foreign financial payments.
Koh Nheak Administrative Police Station Building in Koh Nhek District, Over $ 20,000 Donated by Philanthropists, was Officially Inaugurated
(Mondulkiri): Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Mondulkiri Province, officially inaugurated the Rayong Administrative Police Station, a precious gift from the General Director of Pacific Pacific Stock Company Limited.
The ceremony was also attended by Major General Lor Sokha, Provincial Police Commissioner, Representative of Pacific Company, relevant departments and units, as well as Mrs. Deputy Commissioner, District Inspector, Chief of Post and Deputy Chief of Post, which took place in Memum Village, Rayor Commune. Koh Nhek district, Mondulkiri province, on February 13, 2020.
Lieutenant Colonel Khlot Sokhea, Koh Nhek District Police Inspector, said that the newly constructed and inaugurated Rayon Administrative Police Station is now 8 meters wide, 12 meters long and has a bathroom, which is a precious gift. From the CEO of Pacific Pearl Stock Company Limited at a cost of $ 21,500.
He added that the construction of the administrative police station for 10 months from January 27, 2019 to October 7, 2019 has been completed and these achievements have been considered with care. From Major General Lor Sokha as well.
Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Provincial Governor, commended the Provincial Police Commissioner as well as the District Police Inspector, as well as all subordinate officers who cooperated with philanthropists in building achievements as well as the administrative police station in Koh Nhek District to facilitate the work of Police force to make it easier to provide public services to the people.
The provincial governor instructed all police forces and administrative posts to have good internal unity and to strive to perform their duties better in maintaining security and safety for the people, especially in the operation to crack down on various crimes. Time by providing warmth and increasing people's trust in law enforcement.
On that occasion, Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Provincial Governor, also donated 2,000 USD to the Rayo Administrative Police Station to be used as a seed in the administrative police station building and also brought 40 pieces of protective clothing donated by various donors. To 40 people in Rayor commune, Koh Nhek district.
