(Phnom Penh): Mr. Suy Serith, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh Capital Hall, warned not to appoint officials selected from the ranks of the powerful or their factions, but to judge the officials who need to be promoted in detail in order to Make sure that the officer really has the ability and knowledge to lead the unit or institution to work sustainably.
Such a warning by Mr. Suy Serith was made on February 13, 2020, on the occasion of the announcement of the new administrative structure of Khan Kampoul, Phnom Penh. Mr. Suy Serith warned that "officials who perform their duties well, competent, knowledgeable should be encouraged by asking for promotions and bonuses and must absolutely avoid appointing partisan officials, officials as descendants of officials or powerful people." .
At the same time, Mr. Suy Serith also advised the district administration before appointing any official should make a clear judgment in terms of age, current position, duration of work, ability, knowledge and qualifications that the officer has built in the past. .
Mr. Suy Serith said that it is the integration of officials from various offices under the district administration in order to reform the management and performance of duties in the sub-national administration to be better and more effective. In addition to serving the interests of the nation and the people to respond to the actual needs of the local people.
It should be noted that the appointment of a position to an official through a good evaluation that makes the institution progress, on the contrary, if the appointment by a faction or by a line of powerful people, it will have a negative effect in the unit. Or institutions cause emotional resentment and can also cause internal disunity.
