Japan currently has a total of 247 cases of coronavirus, including 28 on land and 219 on ships. 14 Families in Boeung Keng Kang District Urge Samdech Techo Hun Sen to Intervene After Court Decides to Demolish 16-Year-Old Homes
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of February 13, 2020, 14 families living in Village 4, Group 34, Sangkat Tumnup Teuk, Khan Boeung Keng Kang (north of Sovanna Market) came out with banners in order to insist on Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, intervened to solve the problem of their housing after the court decided to demolish it, even though they had lived in peace for 16 years.
On January 6, 2020, the court issued a voluntary enforcement order, requiring the 14 families to relocate on February 13, 2020. The person who asked the court to issue this order is named Lim Sunly.
According to residents, in 2004 they bought an apartment from a company called Kov Eang Lay and Ubon, checking that the site had a valid legal document issued by the authorities. They claim that Kov Eang Lay bought the land at the site from Ith Sarath.
A resident, Keo Srey Net, told reporters that she did not know why the house was demolished, because when her mother bought it from Kov Eang Lay, it was recognized by the authorities and even cadastral. Measure it, but there is no solid plan. She said that if she left this house, she would not know where to live, because this is the land that her parents gave her.
Speaking with a sad face, Ms. Keo Srey Net raised her hand in salute and requested, "Please help Samdech to see that the people living here are unjust. "I want a plan to be issued, because the 16 years I lived in peace, now there is no peace."
The resident said that the court's decision to affect her children, especially the study. His children raise the question of why they are safe to leave their homes.
Boeung Keng Kang district governor Them Sam An called the 14 families to solve this problem at the district hall immediately.
