(Kandal): On the evening of February 12, 2020, the police force of the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Office of Kandal Provincial Police released three fire trucks to spray water to clean National Road 21B in Takhmao City. Enhance the beauty of the national road and the image of Kring Takhmao, especially by wanting a good environment.
Deputy Fire Commissioner Ul Bonna said that after receiving an order from Brigadier General Chhoeun Socheat, the provincial police commissioner, he assigned the director of the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Office to lead the force to bring a large number of fire trucks. Three units sprayed water to clean National Road No. 21B from point A9 to the traffic light of Prek Samrong Bridge at the corner of Road 115 in Takhmao City.
The Deputy Commissioner confirmed that this road cleaning activity was led by the Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kandal Province and with the cooperation of Takhmao City Authority, Provincial Road Traffic Police and Takhmao City Traffic Police.
Mr. Moeng Youleng, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kandal Province, confirmed that the clean-up activities were not only carried out on National Road 21B, but also on major roads such as National Road 2 and Road 115. .. In the geography in Takhmao for a clean environment, easy to travel for the people and senior leaders.
Passengers and residents of houses next to the national road joined in the celebration and rejoiced to see the activities of the police and officers to clean the road again, because when the road was not cleaned, it was dusty due to the sandy soil. Much thicker. MG launches safe shopping campaign
