(Kampong Chhnang): The occupation of growing palm trees from ancient times to the present is still an important occupation of our Cambodian farmers in Sre Chamkar district. This business, too, has been left behind since ancient times, although now the market is rich in sugar or cane sugar.
In fact, the demand for natural brown sugar in Cambodia is still an indispensable need, which used to eat palm sugar in cooking and to make various desserts as well.
In the past, farmers in rural areas practiced this business almost everywhere, usually by tying palm trees and picking flowers during November and December, during the rainy season. It is not until May, the first rainy month of the year, that the palm trees are discarded and the plows and harrows are set up to start the rainy season, so the farmers in the farming districts, who are engaged in farming and growing palm trees, never have free time.
Mr. Ouk Mean said that although the business is a bit difficult, but he likes to take this business because this is a righteous business. This is also a business that he knows how to do from his father, and he will not give up for two reasons.
The two reasons are: First, he gets a daily allowance to support his family to have a decent life and second: He stays with his family, wife and children every day because he does not want to migrate to work in another country Far away from the family, wife, children. Senior official of the Ministry of Interior: Knowledge of intellectual property contributes to national economic growth
