General Miech Sophanna stated that the organization of this workshop is an effective mechanism because in this workshop, there is an invitation from all relevant actors to contribute to the protection of intellectual property as well as crackdown. Prevent all criminal offenses by dishonest businessmen who cheat the brand and so on.
Ms. Seng Vuoch Hun said that when intellectual property is protected by law, competition and innovation, she is active in society. In fact, the growth in intellectual property of small and medium-sized businesses is one of the reasons why Cambodia has maintained its economic growth rate of around 7% in recent years. In particular, it makes the consumption business more competitive, but requires legal protection.
The lawyer stated that intellectual property is being taken seriously by the Royal Government and has the support of relevant institutions. The perception that the food and pharmaceutical sector is an important part of the current impact on Cambodian society, and doing business in this field is very relevant and intellectual property.
(Rattanakiri): Officials from CamControl Rattanakiri Branch, in cooperation with the Department of Commerce and the working group of laboratory staff of General Department of CamControl, this morning, February 13, 2020, brought a mobile laboratory vehicle to inspect goods at Banlung Market. In Ratanakkiri province, garlic leaves were found to contain pesticide residues.
According to the Camcontrol branch in Ratanakkiri province, during the inspection operation at Banlung market, the team tested a total of 44 samples of food and seafood products to check for banned chemicals. One kilogram of garlic was found to contain 0.3 kg of banned chemicals, pesticide residues, and the team confiscated and destroyed it.
