Minister Thong Khon Chairs a Special Meeting to Review Upcoming Tourism Action Plan to Support Tourism in the New Coronavirus Crisis Stage (CoVid-19)
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of February 12, 2020 at the Ministry of Tourism, there was a special meeting chaired by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, with the participation of leaders and officials of tourism and leaders of the Tourism Industry Association. All.
The meeting agreed to set out an action plan with short-term and long-term measures, focusing on four strategic goals and 76 work activities.
According to the Minister, the four strategic goals are as follows:
First, to improve the image of Cambodia's tourism destination as a safe destination; second: to promote the local tourism movement; third: to increase tourism promotion and connectivity in the tourism market; Tourism industry
Through this guideline, the Ministry of Tourism will cooperate with the Ministry of Health to train at least one trainer at each tourism business base. Separately, the Ministry of Tourism will set up a crisis management team at the ministry level, a number of task forces led by the Secretary of State or Undersecretary of State and a code of professional officers, and a crisis management team in the capital and provinces.
According to the plan, the Ministry of Tourism will submit this action plan to the Economic and Financial Policy Committee for review and submission to the Royal Government for decision to support the tourism sector in Cambodia during the new coronavirus crisis (Covid-19). In time and after the crisis to be effective.
