Senior officials of the Ministry of Tourism urge tour operators to improve hygiene, cleanliness and greenery to celebrate the River Festival in Battambang
(Battambang): Ms. Hun Dany, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, on February 12, 2020, urged tourism operators to strengthen hygiene, cleanliness and greenery to celebrate the 6th River Festival to be held in Battambang Province from the 13th. March 15, 2020 coming soon.
Ms. Hun Dany said this on the occasion of the opening ceremony of the training course on women and clean cities, women and green development in tourism, which was held at the auditorium of Dewey International University with 126 participants.
This training course is organized by the Ministry of Tourism in order to promote the participation of women as well as the general public in clean city activities, hygiene, beauty and enhance the quality of products as well as services in the tourism sector.
She added that, as the host of the River Festival, tour operators in Battambang province, which are in the private sector, must also be involved in preparing to receive guests who will come to visit and be able to capture Opportunity to attract guests to miss Battambang and want to visit Battambang again and again through a smile, warmth, good service, good hygiene and reasonable prices.
(Phnom Penh): General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, responded to the people's question that the authorities only cracked down on petty drug traffickers, the mastermind behind the crackdown and the drug crackdown. Which?
For the question of where the seized drugs are taken? According to General Meas Virith, the general crackdown on drugs in accordance with the rule of law, drug evidence is very important in relation to punishment. In the operation of the crackdown, the quantity was first recorded through a clear record before being sent to court, and all the exhibits were properly kept by a committee.
General Meas Virith confirmed that the drug exhibits seized each year were kept in the court or in a safe place kept by the court because the drugs could be lost and deformed or could easily change. Items or defects of such quality must be carefully maintained in accordance with the technical specifications at the time of capture, sent to court, and the court has the right to dispose of the matter in a safe place.
The senior official of the National Anti-Drug Authority stressed that all drugs must be burned because the drugs are expensive and dangerous substances, so the authorities need to take time to maintain, so we have to burn. . He said that every year we celebrate the International Day Against Drug Abuse on June 26 every year.
General Meas Virith continued that on the occasion of the International Day, we always burn all the drugs, including chemicals, without leaving all those drugs to sit and watch like children. At the time, we set fire to it, but some people did not know when we organized this day.
General Meas Virith emphasized that the destruction of this organization must be given more attention with two measures:
First, the implementation of surrender measures that monitor drug trafficking, because criminals sometimes hire people to act on their behalf, which the person may or may not be aware of.
Second, direct repressive action, all law enforcement authorities use if they see a crime, in case it is found that it is not the implementation of measures to hand over surveillance, the authorities must crack down.
Minister of Commerce encourages and urges Thai businessmen to invest more in Cambodia
The seminar was attended by about 400 Thai businessmen from various large Thai companies, and the Minister encouraged and called on Thai businessmen to invest more in Cambodia.
In his keynote address, the Minister briefed on the progress of socio-economic development in Cambodia, especially the strong economic growth of around 7.1% in the last two decades, the increase in the average income of the population. Cambodians, as well as the rapid growth of foreign direct investment, including investment by Thai companies.
In addition, through the Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025, the Royal Government has already set a goal to transform Cambodian industry from unskilled labor to high-skilled industry by 2025. For the Ministry of Commerce itself, there is also the Cambodia Trade Integration Strategy 2019-2023, which emphasizes strengthening Cambodia's competitiveness and taking advantage of new sources of growth, including the Fourth Industrial Revolution.
Regarding investment, the Minister encouraged and called on Thai businesses to check and invest more in Cambodia.
The Minister also encouraged Thai companies through the Thai-Cambodian Business Council to fully participate in the Government and Private Sector Forum under the chairmanship of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, which will be held on April 1, 2020 to Raise concerns and challenges.
The announcement was made at a press conference on Tuesday evening ahead of the European Union's decision on the EBA on February 12, 2020.
"China has always adhered to the principle of non-interference in internal affairs," said Geng Shuang, a spokesman for the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs. "We oppose the use of trade to interfere in the internal affairs of other countries."
According to the spokesman, China supports the efforts of the Cambodian government and people in safeguarding the independence, sovereignty and dignity of the nation, and they are willing to provide positive assistance for sustainable development and promotion. The lives of the people of Cambodia and hope that the international community will contribute more constructively.
The European Union will make a decision on the evening of 12 February 2020 on whether to withdraw or continue to provide preferential tariffs on everything except arms (EBA) to Cambodia. Prior to this decision, the European Union demanded that Cambodia further promote human rights and democracy, as well as prohibit Cambodia from applying Cambodian law to opposition groups, which would be an interference in Cambodia's internal affairs.
The Royal Government of Cambodia considers the EU's excessive demands to be a violation of Cambodia's internal affairs and has repeatedly stated that it will not trade its national sovereignty with any foreign aid and will take action. Subsequently expand the possibilities to respond to the withdrawal of the EBA.
However, if a decision is made to remove parts of the EBA from Cambodia in February, it does not mean that the EU will have to immediately implement the Cambodian tariff, but will have to wait forever. It will take effect 6 months later.
