Economic and Financial Policy Committee meets to discuss and discuss the progress of the implementation of the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy for 2019
The Rectangular Strategy - Phase 4 was prepared and implemented during September 2018 and has become a basic document that reflects the political program of the Royal Government, the 6th legislature of the National Assembly and a solid basis for the preparation of policy documents. Strategies and action plans for development in various fields towards achieving the 2030 milestone and the 2050 vision that Cambodia expects to become a developed country.
Overall, the implementation of the Rectangular Strategy - Phase 4 for 2019 has made significant progress, with most of the key indicators being achieved and exceeding the set targets.
In fact, the progress of the strategic level indicator shows that the "growth" target for 2019 achieved 7.1% as planned, which is reflected in the continued increase in investment volume, the inflation rate is within a manageable level and the pace of growth. Economic diversification and so on.
At the same time, the goal of "employment" is in a better position through the continuous increase in the number of new jobs, the number of skilled workers, the participation rate of the workforce and the size of controllable civil servants.
