(Kampong Speu): A 10-year-old boy named Song Vuthy, a fifth-grade student at Wat Kak Primary School in Ta Reach village, Kak commune, Bor Seth district, Kampong Speu province, became the first millionaire of Echitan green tea for the fourth season of 2020. This.
Speaking to the team that handed over 100 million Riel to the house in the presence of Mr. Ichitan Pasaknathi in the above geographical area, Ms. Sim Sokrom, 36 years old, is a garment factory worker who is the mother of Song Vuthy. He said that every day when he went to school, Song Vuthy used to help sell his aunt's cakes at the school where he studied to get cakes or water to eat like other children.
Last weekend, after helping to sell cakes, my aunt asked for a bottle of Echitan green tea to eat, but when I opened the bottle cap, I saw a prize of 100 million riels. The boy immediately informed his aunt and handed the bottle cap to her at home.
She said that after receiving 100 million riel from Echitan green tea, she will use some to build bank debt and leave some to create a business to support the family and education of children in the future.
Ministry of Tourism Disseminates ASEAN Tourism Forum 2021 Ahead to Ministries, Institutions, Departments, Private Partners and Stakeholders
In order to mobilize and inspire the readiness to participate in the upcoming ASEAN Tourism Forum ATF 2021, the Ministry of Tourism on February 12, 2020 held an official launch ceremony "Cambodia hosts ASEAN Tourism Forum 2021 Presided over by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism at Sokha Residence Hotel, Phnom Penh.
The event was attended by leaders of relevant ministries and institutions, embassies in Cambodia, the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism and the inter-ministerial working group to manage and develop the tourism sector, the Association of Travel Agents (CATA), the Association of Asia-Pacific Travel Agents of Cambodia (PATACC) and the Tourism Federation. Cambodia (CTF) and the private sector involved in tourism, a total of about 900 people.
Minister Thong Khon called on all stakeholders in the tourism sector, both public and private, as well as the people of Cambodia to participate in promoting the hosting of the "ASEAN Tourism Forum 2021" and join the Royal Government in organizing Host this to receive guests who visit Cambodia with the concept of "clean city, clean resort, good service, good hospitality, provide warmth to tourists."
Mr. Thong Khon said that while the world is facing an outbreak of respiratory disease caused by the new coronavirus "Covid-19", Cambodia is still a safe tourist destination for all tourists. Cambodia's potential tourism is rich in cultural tourism products, heritage and ecotourism.
