Minister of Information warns journalists to report professionally, ethically and with clear sources of self-defense
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Information, Mr. Khieu Kanharith, reminded all journalists to disseminate their information professionally, ethically and with clear sources. .
Khieu Kanharith's remarks came as he presided over the closing ceremony of a workshop on "Professional and Ethical Dissemination of Information" for Journalists Working in the Media. In Cambodia, nearly 300 people on February 12, 2020 at the Ministry of Information.
Khieu Kanharith said: "Ethics is important. It is not a matter of coercion or crime, but ethics is like the wind in the first balloon: keep our dignity, journalists who show that we have "The right profession, we went through the second learning: it shows the value of people in society as a whole."
Mr. Khieu Kanharith continued that the use of dignified language and the maintenance of the dignity of journalists and information officers is to maintain the dignity, especially to show the level of education, understanding of journalists and stakeholders.
"Therefore, ethics through professional work First: As journalists, we must work ethically, must respect this ethics, speak and respect all people in the same society." More of Mr. Khieu Kanharith.
The Minister of Information added that as a journalist, one does not have to judge what is good or bad, but as a journalist, one has to stand in the middle, and journalists have to speak only about what has happened in society. But for a large number of jobs, it can also be a barrier for journalists' outreach work.
Mr. Khieu Kanharith said that professional media outlets need to know the code of ethics, understand the law on journalists and related laws, to know how much of their rights are in order to be able to publish this information. It's not just about shooting and advertising.
Mr. Sareth continued that as a professional journalist, it is necessary to disseminate information from all angles and not be able to get information just by hearing from the people and disseminating it, it will make this source of information. Incomplete corners. Thus, false information poses a risk and adversely affects the nation.
He hopes that the Ministry of Information and all relevant institutions will take further measures to punish those who spread false information.
It should be noted that any journalist who writes in accordance with professional ethics, but when published, will be sued by Samdech Techo Hun Sen's group of volunteer lawyers. Mr. Ky Tech, the head of the Samdech Techo Volunteer Lawyers Group, is responsible for defending journalists who adhere to the code of ethics. Chip Mong Bank opened two new branches on the same day.
