Opinion: Life-saving merits will make Mr. Jachin Ho remember Cambodia
A Chinese man from Wuhan, Ja Jin-ho, and his family, including his wife, daughter and son-in-law, left Cambodia on the night of February 11, 2020, after staying and receiving medical treatment. Respiratory tract caused by the "Corona" virus in Cambodia for more than half a month.
Life-saving merit is the greatest merit for everyone that makes it unforgettable. For Mr. Jachin Ho, the rescue of life, the liberation of life from the gates of death and the non-discrimination of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government, the leaders of the Ministry of Health, the doctors and the people are unforgettable merits in his life. He is like his family.
As he prepares to leave Cambodia, Mr. Jachin Ho and his family will never forget to say goodbye and express their deep gratitude to the Royal Government, the leadership of the Ministry of Health, the doctors and the Cambodian people for their attention. Try to treat him until he is healed and do not discriminate against him, even though he knows he has a disease that he is afraid of.
Although unable to speak in Khmer and express his heartfelt gratitude to the Cambodian people, through the gestures before leaving, Mr. Jachin Ho and his family showed and described that they were real. Thank you very much for the incomparable merit of saving his life by the Royal Government, the medical team and the non-discrimination of the Cambodian people.
Memories of this difficult time will surely be engraved in the hearts of Mr. Jaejoong and his family, and they will one day return to this precious land.
As a Cambodian citizen and as a scribe for this article, I wish Ja Jin Hoa a safe and healthy return from the "corona" respiratory disease that is invading his city. May the government, doctors and his people fight the coronavirus successfully.
Cambodians are looking forward to the return of him and his family, as well as the people of his city, with a smile on his face as the coronary heart disease is eradicated.
By Van Saray, a Chinese man who was cured of a new coronary heart disease left Cambodia tonight
(Phnom Penh): After recovering and leaving the Sihanoukville Provincial Referral Hospital, Mr. Jachin Ho, a Chinese national, a former former Corona patient, took his wife and children out of Cambodia on the night of February 11, 2020. This is according to the confirmation of the authorities.
The Chinese man was released from Sihanoukville Provincial Referral Hospital on the morning of February 10, 2020 after a third test, which showed he had no new coronary heart disease. The body no more.
Minister of Health Mr. Mam Bunheng and Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, accompanied by leaders of the Ministry of Health, Sihanoukville, representatives of the World Health Organization in Cambodia and the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, inspected the situation of Chinese men. In Sihanoukville before being allowed to leave the hospital.
Before leaving Cambodia, Mr. Jachin Ho thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Ministry of Health and the medical team for taking care of him and treating him until he was completely recovered and left the hospital.
Jachin Ho traveled from Wuhan with three other families to Sihanoukville, Cambodia on January 23, 2020. Two days after his arrival, he developed an abnormal cough and fever and was examined by a health officer for a throat swab test on January 27, 2020. To be treated at Sihanoukville Provincial Referral Hospital.
This is the first case of the new coronavirus in Cambodia as the virus has spread to many countries around the world. As of February 10, 2020, the death toll from the new coronary heart disease has risen to more than 1,000 and infected more than 40,000.
However, Cambodia, according to the Ministry of Health, so far, Cambodia continues to monitor the coronavirus closely, although now the new coronavirus has ended its presence in Cambodia.
