* First: Ensuring the sustainability of administrative work and providing services to the people by following administrative and financial procedures, letter negotiations and workplace arrangements * Second: Personnel management * Third: Management Documents and Assets * Fourth: Provision of OWSO services * Fifth: Support for Commune / Sangkat Administration * Sixth: Security, Public Order and Social Security * Seventh: District Council Meetings .
Cambodia will implement three goals in the World Covenant on Migration for Safe Migration
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia will take three of the 23 goals set out in the Global Convention for the Safe, Legal and Legal Migration (GCM) to implement the aim of facilitating the migration of Cambodians. Abroad, safe and legally in the destination country.
The Global Covenant on Safe, orderly and legal migration (GCM) is a joint statement that 193 countries around the world, including Cambodia, have jointly recognized as having the same issues related to migration. The Covenant raises all concerns over immigration, affecting tens of millions of people as a result of migration.
To select the three goals set out in the GCM this morning, February 12, 2020, Ms. Chou Bun Eng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Permanent Vice Chair of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking (NEC). Conducted an inter-ministerial meeting to prepare for the second national workshop in March on the selection of goals.
Speaking to reporters, Ms. Chou Bun Eng claimed that in the GCM, there are 23 key points that are all focused on legal migration, but Cambodia chose only three points. Only to apply to what is experiencing and is a priority.
Answer the question whether the selection of only 3 points is the determination of the relevant state parties or not? She said that the fact that Cambodia chose to implement only three points because it is all related to what Cambodia is experiencing now, but does not mean that other goals are thrown away, that is, will be implemented. Consecutive.
"In the 23 objectives of the Covenant, there are some things that are not related to us, but they are related to the migration issues of other countries, so Cambodia has to look at only a few priority tasks," she said. We can do it, and it's a start in action, not that we give up three more goals. "Whatever the purpose, it is important for Cambodia to start."
According to Ms. Chou Bun Eng, after the State Party accepted the GCM in 2018, it was determined that every four years, a meeting will be held to discuss which countries have chosen what goals and what has been achieved to share. Give each other experiences. Cambodia will also share these three selected goals on the international stage.
