Australia provides $ 10 million in additional assistance to Cambodia for demining (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Australian Government has decided to provide an additional $ 10 million in assistance to the Royal Government of Cambodia for demining. This is according to Mr. Koy Kuong, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia.
Australia's additional assistance in demining work was presented by the new Australian Ambassador to Cambodia, Pablo Chiho Kang, on the afternoon of February 11, 2020, on the occasion of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and Cooperation. International allowed to pay a courtesy call at the Ministry.
Koy Kuong said: "The two sides also discussed demining, which Australia has been helping to clear a lot of mines since 1994. "Australia has provided a lot of assistance to the demining sector, and this year Australia will provide another $ 10 million, because the ambassador said that the demining sector will achieve the government's plan to clear all mines by 2025." .
According to the spokesman on the occasion, Mr. Prak Sokhon extended a warm welcome and congratulations to the new Ambassador of Australia to Cambodia. The Deputy Prime Minister stated that the Cambodian leadership and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs will be ready to cooperate with the Ambassador to facilitate his successful diplomatic mission, which means that the relationship between Cambodia and Australia will be deeper and better.
The Deputy Prime Minister also thanked Australia for its assistance to Cambodia, including its efforts to bring peace to Cambodia. The Cambodian head of diplomacy also expressed his condolences to the Australian government and people, who have been hit hard by long-term wildfires that have wreaked havoc.
The Australian Ambassador expressed his pleasure at being appointed Ambassador to Cambodia. He thanked Prak Sokhon for his condolences to the Australian government and people affected by the wildfires.
"Furthermore, the Ambassador reminded and thanked the Cambodian people, the Cambodian community in Australia, as well as the alumni who had studied in Australia, as well as the Cambodian youth in Australia, who raised funds to alleviate the effects of the fire. "Forest fires in Australia." A spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs emphasized.
The Ambassador also expressed his condolences for the recent building collapses in Sihanoukville and Kep. He said that in the past, he had met with Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, where he initiated the construction safety code.
The Ambassador also began a study visit to Australia, taking officials from relevant ministries such as the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, the Ministry of Environment and some provincial authorities on a three-week study tour to complete construction on The future for more quality.
"The ambassador added that in 2020, our Cambodian students will register to study in Australia, both scholarship students and pay about 3,000." According to the spokesperson.
A senior foreign ministry official said the ambassador was also interested in Cambodia's transport sector, which he said would encourage Australian investors to invest in the sector. Regarding the agricultural sector, the two sides also discussed that Australia has helped the sector in the past to make our Cambodian farmers grow crops several times a year, as well as grow more crops.
The ambassador stressed that Australia will continue to provide assistance to Cambodia, but this time, Australia will work closely with the Royal Government, which means that if it provides assistance to the health sector, Australia will work closely with the Ministry of Health. The Human Resources Training Division will work closely with the Ministry of Education.
In addition, the two sides also discussed the ASEM Summit, which Cambodia will host later this year. The ambassador stated that Australia intends to work closely with Cambodia to assist Cambodia in organizing the summit.
