Cambodia, France vow to continue international adoption work for humanitarian goals
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and France continue to shake hands and show common ground in intermarriage with other countries for the humanitarian purpose of preventing human trafficking and to find good families for orphans.
The two sides made the remarks as Nim Thoth, Permanent Secretary of State and Representative of Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, received a courtesy call and discussed with the French delegation led by Denis Babet Ek. The Prime Minister in charge of inter-French adoption on February 11, 2020 at the Ministry of Social Affairs.
On that occasion, Mr. Nim Thoth stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia implements the policy to protect the rights of the child in accordance with the United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child enshrined in the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Mr. Nim Thoth added that the Royal Government of Cambodia considers international adoption as a policy for humanitarian purposes linked to respect for the rights and interests of children, preventing human trafficking through international adoption and seeking Good families give orphans who can not be adopted in the country.
In addition, Denis Babet, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of France, said that France continues to work with the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation on international adoption to help orphans in Cambodia. He has a better life.
In today's meeting, both the Cambodian and French sides expressed their friendship and closeness to each other as friendly countries and good partners in serving international adoption work in Cambodia.
It should be noted that in Cambodia, international adoption took place from 1987 until April 2011. Countries that cooperate with Cambodia include France, the United States, Belgium, Canada, Italy, the United Kingdom, Sanskrit, Poland, the Seychelles, Malta, Finland, Spain, Greece, and South Africa. Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara: We must all unite against traitors in order to maintain absolute peace
(Tbong Khmum): It has been almost 500 years since our country was peaceful and developed peacefully 41 years ago until today, so we must work together with Samdech Techo Hun Sen to protect and take care of it without cheating people Some biases and foreigners who try to destroy the political stability and peace of our country.
This was stated by Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara to about 3,000 civil servants on February 11, 2020 on the occasion of presiding over the representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprit Bun Rany Hun. Sen inaugurated various achievements in Wat Kiri Tekkenaram, also known as Wat Kbal Boeung Ses, in Kor commune, Tbong Khmum district, Tbong Khmum province.
The ceremony was also attended by a high-level delegation from the Ministry of Land Management, Mr. Seak Leng, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Mr. Cheam Chansophorn, Provincial Governor and leaders of all levels in Tbong Khmum.
Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara said that our country is growing day by day, both in the field of Buddhism and the empire that is going hand in hand, in which the Royal Government has built many infrastructures such as pagodas, schools, hospitals, roads, bridges, networks. Electricity, etc. to facilitate the execution of beliefs, living and meeting the basic needs of the people.
"However, there are still a small number of unscrupulous people and some countries who have repeatedly tried to cause unrest to destroy the peace, that is, they do not want to see our Cambodian people living happily under the roof of peace," he said. And development is not as fast as it is today. Therefore, we must all unite against those traitors in order to maintain absolute peace.
The Deputy Prime Minister emphasized that under the correct and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian People's Party, the country has been brought out of the flames of war, leading a prosperous and peaceful Cambodia. Pay close attention to the well-being of people from all walks of life, regardless of political affiliation or religious beliefs.
"We see that Cambodia has a large number of people practicing their respective religions, such as Buddhism, Islam and Christianity, but we can live in harmony with each other," he said.
It is important to maintain peace, political stability, such religious beliefs, based on the concern of the people across the country, so he called on all citizens to work together to maintain peace and development by continuing to vote in favor. Samdech Techo Hun Sen supports the Cambodian People's Party to continue to lead the country in every mandate.
