APSARA Authority completes the repair of 90 meters of Angkor Wat bank after 8 years of effort
(Siem Reap): A 90-meter-long bridge on the north side of Angkor Wat, on the north side of Angkor Wat, has been completely repaired by experts of APSARA Authority in 8 years in order to enhance the attractiveness of Angkor Wat temple landscape. Krasinthu River to be restored to its original shape and to help enhance the beauty of the bridge for national and international tourists to visit Angkor Wat to be stronger.
Mr. Mao Sokny, Technical Officer of the Department of Temple Conservation in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology of the APSARA Authority, said that the main reasons for the damage to the structure due to the age of the construction of termites on the stairs, lack of maintenance. The bedrock beneath the decay of the later limestone layer, and the large trees growing near the shoreline rooted into the rock, causing the rock to move from its original location on the bank.
Mr. Sokny added that in the past eight years, experts from the APSARA Authority have repaired the bank of Angkor Wat in the north of the bridge in stages, such as from 2013-2017, repaired 40 meters long. In 2019, 20 meters will be repaired, which is 10 meters at the point of the sewer system, and in 2020, 20 meters will be repaired.
In repairing, experts used traditional techniques to dig out old soil, replace it with new soil, and then compact the foundation with rock, sand, gravel, laterite and lime, especially the bottom of the foundation. Length to help hold the pressure and the clay to prevent water from entering the bottom, etc., so that the foundation is strong for a long time.
In the past, many international partners such as France, India, Italy have come to repair the banks of Angkor Wat, the stairs and the entrance in front of Angkor Wat, as well as help train many experts of the Apsara Authority to preserve this ancient structure. APSARA Authority starts construction of the road in front of the Terrace of the Elephants in early February
(Siem Reap): The construction of a new asphalt road on the old Dey Krahorm road, which dates back to 1912, located in front of the Sour Proth temple instead of the current rubber road in front of the Terrace of the Elephants, will begin construction at the beginning of the month. This February 2020, using a period of 5 months.
Mr. Yit Chanda, Deputy Director General of APSARA Authority, said that the bypass is to reduce the impact on the structure of the Elephant Terrace due to vibration from driving cars and toxic fumes from all kinds of vehicles, especially to maintain safety. When tourists pass by to visit the temple, avoid any dangers because this old rubber road is very close to the terrace of elephants.
He added that the construction of the new road has a total length of 1,427 meters, 6 meters wide, a kind of dark red rubber road, starting from the northeast corner of the Bayon temple to the gate of the pot, turning left before reaching Preah Pithu temple is connected to the old rubber road in front of Wat Tep Pranom.
After the construction of this road is completed, APSARA Authority will completely suspend the current use of the rubber road and improve the road as a garden to plant grass and trees to have a beautiful landscape and environment in front of the Terrace of the Elephants, as well as in the area of Angkor Thom. Round. APSARA Authority finds the gate of Tonle Snguot temple after finding the body 3 years ago
(Siem Reap): A fragment of a statue was found by the team working to repair the Tonle Snguot temple of the APSARA Authority at a location just 1 meter from the end of the gate, which was found in 2017.
After the discovery on the morning of February 10, 2020, to confirm that it was a foot fragment of the gate statue, the conservation and restoration work of the APSARA Authority made a replica of the gate statue at Angkor Conservation. Feet at the dry river temple. Through this comparison, the team confirmed that the foot piece is indeed part of the gate statue.
Currently, the team for the conservation and restoration of artefacts is preparing technical documents to assemble the statues at the gates that are being repaired at the Angkor Conservation.
(Kratie): Kratie Provincial Police in cooperation with Kratie Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport on the morning of February 11, 2020 held a meeting to review the results of road traffic safety work in 2019 and work direction for 2020 at the Theater. In the presence of Mr. Khan Chamnan, Deputy Governor and all relevant departments and institutions, including youth.
The main cause of traffic accidents is the driver disobeying traffic rules, which is a key issue that must be addressed.
Mr. Khan Chamnan said that across the country, traffic accidents are increasing and this accident causes millions of dollars in property damage per year, which is a high rate compared to other social accidents, with an average of 5 deaths per day. Four people were injured.
Factors that lead to an increase in the number of accidents First: due to the growth of vehicles, second: human factors and the spirit of law enforcement is still limited. And approving factors due to the faster growth of vehicles than the construction of road infrastructure, the development of roads are not yet balanced with the growth, and the management of roads, sidewalks and sidewalks is not yet thorough and narrow. Difficult to traffic.
The Deputy Governor also urged
* Continue to strengthen the mechanism for leading the traffic safety team at all levels, especially at the municipal, district, commune, and sangkat levels by organizing meetings to review, review, and gain experience, have regular reports, and increase cooperation in resolving all issues to ensure sustainable work processes in a spirit of responsibility. High responsibility.
* Continue to promote the monitoring and enforcement of the law in accordance with the action plan and work program that has been set out on a regular basis, day and night, with transparency and fairness in all targets throughout the province.
* Continue to promote the provision of public services in the provision of documents related to driving a vehicle and the transfer of rights to effectively serve the people, strengthen discipline, capacity, knowledge of all officials to pay high attention to fulfilling their duties and responsibilities. Reduce risk
* Continue to promote the technical inspection of vehicles, continue to install and repair safety poles, traffic signs, reflective stickers on the road at the head of the bridge.
* Continue to promote the dissemination of sub-decree law in all forms to reach homes in villages, communes, sangkats, community schools, remote areas and on social media.
* Continue to urge the traffic safety team of roads, cities, districts and communes to take action to organize order on the streets, towns, schools, parking lots in an orderly manner and to continue to monitor the reaction of the public to respond.
